<b>&#x27;γγιξα</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>first-person singular simple past of ’γγίζω</div><b>&#x27;γώ</b>
  <div><i>pron</i></div>
  <div class='def'>contraction of <a href="bword://εγώ">εγώ</a></div>
  <div class='ex'>Ξέρω <b>’γώ</b>; - How should I know?</div><b>&#x27;ναι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>contraction of <a href="bword://είναι">είναι</a></div>
  <div class='ex'>Αυτά θα <b>’ναι</b> προβλήματα τότε. - These will be problems then.</div><b>&#x27;συ</b>
  <div><i>pron</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Occasional, rare spelling of συ (sy) preceded with apostrophe — see: <a href="bword://εσύ">εσύ</a></div><b>&#x27;σύ</b>
  <div><i>pron</i></div>
  <div class='def'>contraction of <a href="bword://εσύ">εσύ</a></div><b>&#x27;χα</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>contraction of είχα</div>
  <div class='ex'>Να <b>’χα</b> τη δύναμη, θα το έκανα. - If I had the power, I’d do it.</div><b>&#x27;χαμε</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>contraction of είχαμε</div>
  <div class='ex'>Να <b>’χαμε</b> εκατομμύρια, καλά θα ’μασταν. - If we had millions, we’d be okay.</div><b>&#x27;χαν</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>contraction of είχαν</div>
  <div class='ex'>Τα <b>’χαν</b> ξοδέψει τα λεφτά όταν έγινε αυτό. - They&#x27;d spent the money when that happened.</div><b>&#x27;χατε</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>contraction of είχατε</div>
  <div class='ex'>Να <b>’χατε</b> λεφτά, όλα καλά θα ήταν. - If you had money, everything would be fine.</div><b>&#x27;χε</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>contraction of είχε</div>
  <div class='ex'>Μου <b>’χε</b> πει, αλλά ξέχασα τώρα. - He’d told me, but I’ve forgotten now.</div><b>&#x27;χες</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>contraction of είχες</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το <b>’χες</b> πει, όμως. - You’d said it, though.</div><b>&#x27;χουμε</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>contraction of έχουμε</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το <b>’χουμε</b> ξαναδεί το έργο αυτό. - We&#x27;ve seen that film before.</div><b>,η</b>
  <div><i>num</i></div>
  <div class='def'>The number 8000 in Greek numerals.</div><b>2η</b>
  <div><i>num</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation for δεύτερη, second (the ordinal number)</div><b>͵Α</b>
  <div><i>num</i></div>
  <div class='def'>The Greek numeral representing the number one thousand (1000); typically romanized as the Roman numeral M.</div><b>͵Β</b>
  <div><i>num</i></div>
  <div class='def'>The Greek numeral representing the number two thousand (2000); typically romanized as the Roman numeral MM.</div><b>͵Γ</b>
  <div><i>num</i></div>
  <div class='def'>The Greek numeral representing the number three thousand (3000); typically romanized as the Roman numeral MMM.</div><b>͵Δ</b>
