  <div class='def'>The Greek numeral representing the number ninety thousand (90,000).</div><b>͵ϟ</b>
  <div><i>num</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://͵Ϟ">͵Ϟ</a></div><b>͵Ϡ</b>
  <div><i>num</i></div>
  <div class='def'>The Greek numeral representing the number nine hundred thousand (900,000).</div><b>͵ϡ</b>
  <div><i>num</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://͵Ϡ">͵Ϡ</a></div><b>Άαλαντ</b>
  <div><i>name, neuter (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://Ώλαντ">Ώλαντ</a></div><b>Άαχεν</b>
  <div><i>name, neuter (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(indeclinable) Aachen (a city in Germany)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η ομαδα απο το <b>Άαχεν</b> συνέτριβε την Παναχαϊκή ήδη απο το πρώτο ημίχρονο. - The team from Aachen were crushing Panachaiki already from the first half.</div><b>Άβδηρα</b>
  <div><i>name, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Abdera (an ancient city in Thrace, in modern Greece)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Τα <b>Άβδηρα</b> ήταν πατρίδα του φιλοσόφου Δημόκριτου. - Abdera was the homecity of philosopher Democritus.</div><b>Άγαρ</b>
  <div><i>name, feminine (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(indeclinable) Hagar</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek Ἄγαρ, from Hebrew הגר (“Hagar”).</div><b>Άγγελος</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. a male given name, Angelos, equivalent to English Angelo</div>
  <div class='ex'>Οι <b>Άγγελοι</b> γιορτάζουν στις 8 Νοεμβρίου - [people called] Angelos celebrate their nameday on 8 November.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. a male surname, feminine equivalent <a href="bword://Αγγέλου">Αγγέλου</a></div>
  <div class='ex'>η βυζαντινή δυναστεία των <b>Αγγέλων</b> - the Byzantine dynasty of Angeloi</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Related to άγγελος. From Byzantine Greek Ἄγγελος, a male&#x27;s surname, from a male&#x27;s given name.</div><b>Άγγλος</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine (plural Άγγλοι, feminine Αγγλίδα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. Englishman (native or inhabitant of England) (usually male)</div>
  <div class='ex'>ένας 25χρονος <b>Άγγλος</b> […] - a 25-year-old Englishman […]</div>
  <div class='def'>2. and see: (plural) Άγγλοι the English, the English people</div><b>Άγια</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>offertory, offerings of bread and wine</div><b>Άγιε Βασίλειε</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>vocative singular of <a href="bword://Άγιος">Άγιος</a> <a href="bword://Βασίλειος">Βασίλειος</a></div><b>Άγιε Βασίλη</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>vocative singular of <a href="bword://Άγιος">Άγιος</a> <a href="bword://Βασίλης">Βασίλης</a></div><b>Άγιε Νικόλαε</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>vocative singular of <a href="bword://Άγιος">Άγιος</a> <a href="bword://Νικόλαος">Νικόλαος</a></div><b>Άγιες Τράπεζες</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative plural of Αγία Τράπεζα</div><b>Άγιο Όρος</b>
  <div><i>name, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Mount Athos (a Greek monastic centre)</div><b>Άγιο Βασίλειο</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>accusative singular of <a href="bword://Άγιος">Άγιος</a> <a href="bword://Βασίλειος">Βασίλειος</a></div><b>Άγιο Βασίλη</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>accusative singular of <a href="bword://Άγιος">Άγιος</a> <a href="bword://Βασίλης">Βασίλης</a></div><b>Άγιο Μύρο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>chrism, holy oil</div><b>Άγιο Μύρρο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of Άγιο Μύρο</div><b>Άγιο Νικόλαο</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>accusative singular of <a href="bword://Άγιος">Άγιος</a> <a href="bword://Νικόλαος">Νικόλαος</a></div><b>Άγιο Πνεύμα</b>
  <div><i>name, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Holy Ghost, Holy Spirit</div><b>Άγιοι Βασίληδες</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. nominative plural of <a href="bword://Άγιος">Άγιος</a> <a href="bword://Βασίλης">Βασίλης</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. vocative plural of <a href="bword://Άγιος">Άγιος</a> <a href="bword://Βασίλης">Βασίλης</a></div><b>Άγιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine Αγία, neuter Άγιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. names of churches or holy places</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η εκκλησία του <b>Αγίου</b> Δημητρίου είναι αφιερωμένη στον άγιο Δημήτριο. - The Church of Saint Demetrius is devoted to Saint Demetrius.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. placenames deriving from names of churches</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ο <b>Άγιος</b> Νικόλαος είναι πόλη στην Κρήτη. - Saint Nicholas is a city in Crete.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. see <a href="bword://άγιος">άγιος</a> for saints and formal address for priests, especially of high rank, in official correspondence</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>άγιος</b> Γεώργιος - Saint George</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> The adjective άγιος with uppercase first letter, for names of churches, places, and official use. Lowercase is used for referring to a Saint.</div><b>Άγιος Βασίλειος</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Saint Basil</div><b>Άγιος Βασίλης</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine (plural Άγιοι Βασίληδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>spelling and form of <a href="bword://αϊ">αϊ</a>-<a href="bword://Βασίλης">Βασίλης</a> as in verses of poems, literature</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Άγιος Βασίλης</b> έρχεται
κι όλους μας καταδέχεται - Santa Claus is coming
and condescends to all of us</div><b>Άγιος Βικέντιος και Γρεναδίνες</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Saint Vincent and the Grenadines (an archipelago and country in the Caribbean, comprising the islands of Saint Vincent and the island chain of the Grenadines)</div><b>Άγιος Γεώργιος</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine (usually uncountable, plural Άγιοι Γεώργιοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable, usually) placename (name of places or churches) after Saint George in both Greece and Cyprus.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable, usually) the saint, written as <a href="bword://άγιος">άγιος</a> <a href="bword://Γεώργιος">Γεώργιος</a> Saint George(person)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Άγιος from άγιος &amp; the name Γεώργιος.</div><b>Άγιος Γόρδιος</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Agios Gordios (a village in Corfu regional unit, Ionian Islands, Greece)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> By surface analysis, άγιος + Γόρδιος.</div><b>Άγιος Θωμάς και Πρίγκιπας</b>
  <div><i>name, neuter (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative term for of Σάο Τομέ <a href="bword://και">και</a> Πρίνσιπε</div><b>Άγιος Μαρίνος</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. San Marino (a landlocked microstate in Southern Europe, located within the borders of Italy)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. San Marino (the capital city of San Marino)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Calque of Italian San Marino</div><b>Άγιος Μαρτίνος</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Sint Maarten (a dependent territory and constituent country of the Netherlands, located on the southern half of the island of Saint Martin in the Caribbean Sea)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Calque of Dutch Sint Maarten.</div><b>Άγιος Νεκτάριος</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Agios Nektarios (a neighbourhood of Greece) usually near a church by the same name, or for the Saint by this name</div>
  <div class='ex'>e.g. Agios Nektarios at Poros island. Άγιος Νεκτάριος Πόρου on the Greek Wikipedia.Wikipedia ᵉˡ</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Άγιος &amp; Νεκτάριος from placenames Άγιος Νεκτάριος for «άγιος Νεκτάριος» (Saint Nektarios)</div><b>Άγιος Νικόλαος</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. Saint Nicholas (4th century Greek bishop from Anatolia and patron saint of the marines in the Orthodox tradition)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. Agios Nikolaos (large seaside town in Lasithi in Crete, Greece)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. Agios Nikolaos (municipality named for and containing the above town)</div>
  <div class='def'>4. Agios Nikolaos (any of the other so named towns in Greece)</div><b>Άγιος Χριστόφορος και Νέβις</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Saint Kitts and Nevis (a country comprising the islands of Saint Kitts and Nevis in the Caribbean)</div><b>Άγιους Βασίληδες</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>accusative plural of <a href="bword://Άγιος">Άγιος</a> <a href="bword://Βασίλης">Βασίλης</a></div><b>Άγκυρα</b>
  <div><i>name, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Ankara (the capital city of Turkey)</div><b>Άγναντα</b>
  <div><i>name, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Agnanta (a village in Arta regional unit, Epirus, Greece)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Related to Greek άγναντος.</div><b>Άδαμος</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine</i></div>
