  <div><i>name, masculine singular</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (Greek) Hades, the Underworld, the realm of the dead</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (Greek) Hades, god of the underworld and ruler of the dead</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) a dark and infernal place, the underworld</div>
  <div class='ex'>spelt with lowercase first letter: άδης (ádis)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> The figurative sense, usually with lowercase άδης, inherited from Ancient Greek ᾍδης. The ancient terms, learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ᾍδης.</div><b>Άδωνης</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine</i></div>
