  <div class='ex'>οι <b>Άνδεις</b> - the Andes</div><b>Άνδρος</b>
  <div><i>name, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Andros (a Greek island in the Cyclades)</div><b>Άνθιμος</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. a male given name</div>
  <div class='def'>2. Any of the saints whose feast day in the Greek Orthodox tradition is 3 September.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek Ἄνθιμος, from Ancient Greek ἄνθιμος, from ἄνθος.</div><b>Άννα</b>
  <div><i>name, feminine (plural Άννες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. Hannah</div>
  <div class='def'>2. a female given name, Anna, from Hebrew, equivalent to English Ann, Anne, or Hannah</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek Ἄννα, from Biblical Hebrew חַנָּה.</div><b>Άννυ</b>
  <div><i>name, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial, familiar) a female given name</div><b>Άνταμ</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(indeclinable) a male given name, equivalent to English Adam</div><b>Άνω Βαυαρία</b>
  <div><i>name, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Upper Bavaria (an administrative region of Bavaria; seat: Munich)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Calque of German Oberbayern. By surface analysis, άνω + Βαυαρία.</div><b>Άνω Κορακιάνα</b>
  <div><i>name, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Ano Korakiana (a village in Corfu regional unit, Ionian Islands region, Greece)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> By surface analysis, άνω + Κορακιάνα.</div><b>Άνω Πιτσά</b>
  <div><i>name, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Ano Pitsa (a village in Corinthia regional unit, Peloponnese, Greece)</div><b>Άξονας</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>the Axis, the Axis Powers</div><b>Άπω Ανατολή</b>
  <div><i>name, feminine singular</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(dated) Far East (a geographical region of Asia, consisting of East Asia (Korea, Japan, China, the Russian Far East, etc.) and Southeast Asia, taken as a whole)</div><b>Άπω Ανατολής</b>
  <div><i>name, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>genitive singular of Άπω <a href="bword://Ανατολή">Ανατολή</a></div>
  <div class='ex'>Older spelling: Ἄπω Ἀνατολῆς</div><b>Άραβας</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine (plural Άραβες, feminine Αράβισσα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (demonym) Arab (person)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Γνώρισα έναν <b>Άραβα</b> και γίναμε φίλοι. Ο άραβας φίλος μου … - I met an Arab and we became friends. My Arab friend …</div>
  <div class='def'>2. and see: (plural) Άραβες the Arab people</div><b>Άργος</b>
  <div><i>name, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Argos (a city in Argolis regional unit, Peloponnese, Greece)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek Ἄργος.</div><b>Άρειε Πάγε</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>vocative singular of Άρειος Πάγος</div><b>Άρειο Πάγο</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>accusative singular of Άρειος Πάγος</div><b>Άρειος Πάγος</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. Areopagus (a hill in Athens)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. supreme court, Court of Cassation</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek Ἄρειος Πᾰ́γος.</div><b>Άρης</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine</i></div>
