  <div><i>name, feminine (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(indeclinable) Vantaa (a city in Finland)</div><b>Βάραγγος</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine (plural Βάραγγοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (historical) Varangian; an ethnic Norseman with ancestral roots in medieval Scandinavia and other areas of Norse settlement during the Viking Age</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (historical) Varangian; a soldier of Nordic or Anglo-Saxon origin, most distinguished for forming the elite Varangian Guard army unit in the Byzantine Empire, serving as the personal bodyguard of the Byzantine Roman Emperor in Constantinople</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek Βάραγγος, from Medieval Latin Varingus, Waringus, from a Germanic origin, likely via Old Norse væringi (literally “oath sworn”), from vár (“pledge, oath”) + -ing (“suffix to form gerund noun”).</div><b>Βάρκιζα</b>
