  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Uncertain. Possibly from Byzantine Greek Γόλος, from Ottoman Turkish یولقاز (Yolkaz), یولقاس (Yolkas), from Ancient Greek Ἰωλκός. The change in consonants stems from a 19th century attempt by learned scholars to link the name with the Ancient Greek term βόλος or βῶλος.</div><b>Βόρεια Αμερική</b>
