  <div class='def'>(indeclinable) Zimbabwe (a country in Southern Africa)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Shona dzimba-dze-mabwe (“house of stones”), in reference to Great Zimbabwe.</div><b>Ζουλού</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. Zulu (An African ethnic group)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. Zulu (An individual member of the Zulu people)</div><b>Ζυγός</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. the constellation Libra</div>
  <div class='def'>2. the astrological sign Libra</div><b>Ζωή</b>
  <div><i>name</i></div>
  <div class='def'>a female given name, Zoi, equivalent to English Zoe</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek Ζωή.</div><b>Η</b>
  <div><i>num</i></div>
  <div class='def'>The number eight in Greek numerals.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>article</i></div>
  <div class='def'>the (feminine form; plural οι)</div><b>Η΄</b>
  <div><i>num</i></div>
  <div class='def'>The Greek numeral representing the number eight (8), typically romanized as the Roman numeral VIII.</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ο Ιωάννης Ηʹ Παλαιολόγος ήταν Βυζαντινός αυτοκράτορας που βασίλεψε από το 1425 μέχρι το θάνατό του το 1448.
John VIII Palæologus was a Byzantine emperor who ruled from 1425 until his death in 1448.</div><b>ΗΒ</b>
