  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek Ἡσίοδος.</div><b>Ησαΐας</b>
  <div><i>name</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. a male given name, Isaias, from Hebrew, equivalent to English Isaiah</div>
  <div class='def'>2. Isaiah (A prophet, the author of the Book of Isaiah).</div>
  <div class='def'>3. Isaiah, book of the Old Testament of Bible, and of the Tanakh.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek Ἠσαΐας, from Biblical Hebrew יְשַׁעְיָהוּ.</div><b>Ηωαρχαιοζωικός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) Eoarchean</div>
  <div class='ex'>ο <b>Ηωαρχαιοζωικός</b> αιώνας - the Eoarchean era</div><b>Θ΄</b>
  <div><i>num</i></div>
  <div class='def'>The Greek numeral representing the number nine (9), typically romanized as the Roman numeral IX.</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η Όγδοη Σταυροφορία αναλήφθηκε και πάλι από τον Λουδοβίκος Θʹ της Γαλλίας το 1270. Η Θʹ Σταυροφορία υπολογίζεται πολλές φορές σαν μέρος της όγδοης. - The Eighth Crusade was undertaken by Louis IX of France in 1270. The 9th Crusade is often considered part of the Eighth.</div><b>ΘΣ</b>
  <div><i>name</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. nomen sacrum form of <a href="bword://Θεός">Θεός</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. (Judaism) G-d)</div><b>Θάνατος</b>
