  <div class='def'>Thea (a village in West Attica regional unit, Attica, Greece)</div><b>Θέκλα</b>
  <div><i>name, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>a female given name, Thekla, equivalent to English Thecla</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek Θέκλα.</div><b>Θέουτα</b>
  <div><i>name, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Ceuta (an autonomous city of Spain and exclave at the edge of Morocco)</div><b>Θέρμο</b>
  <div><i>name, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Thermo (a town in Thermo, Aetolia-Acarnania, Greece).</div><b>Θέτις</b>
  <div><i>name, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (Greek) Thetis</div>
  <div class='def'>2. a female given name, Thetis</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek Θέτῐς.</div><b>Θήβα</b>
  <div><i>name, feminine</i></div>
