  <div class='def'>1. (indeclinable) Israel (a Biblical region of Western Asia roughly coextensive with the modern State of Israel, known in the Bible as the Land of Israel and considered the ancestral homeland of the Jewish people)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (historical, indeclinable) Israel (an ancient kingdom in Western Asia, roughly coextensive with the modern State of Israel and the Land of Israel)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (historical, indeclinable) Israel (an ancient kingdom that occupied the northern part of the Land of Israel and modern State of Israel, as distinct from Judah)</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (indeclinable) Israel (a name given to the Jewish patriarch Jacob)</div>
  <div class='def'>5. (indeclinable) the Hebrew people, the children of Israel</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek Ἰσρᾱήλ.</div><b>Ισραηλινή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural Ισραηλινές, masculine Ισραηλινός)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Israeli, female person from Israel or of Israeli nationality.</div><b>Ισραηλινός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural Ισραηλινοί, feminine Ισραηλινή)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Israeli, male person from Israel or of Israeli nationality.</div><b>Ιστία</b>
  <div><i>name, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Vela (a constellation)</div><b>Ιταλία</b>
  <div><i>name, feminine</i></div>
