  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek Ῑ̓τᾰλῐ́ᾱ.</div><b>Ιταλίδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural Ιταλίδες, masculine Ιταλός)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Italian (a female person from Italy or of Italian ethnicity)</div><b>Ιταλός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural Ιταλοί, feminine Ιταλίδα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Italian (a person, usually male, from Italy or of Italian ethnicity)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek Ἰταλός.</div><b>Ιχθείς</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://Ιχθύες">Ιχθύες</a></div><b>Ιχθύες</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. Pisces (constellation)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. Pisces (sign)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From ιχθύς, from Ancient Greek ἰχθύς.</div><b>Ιχθύς Ιπτάμενος</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Volans (a constellation)</div><b>Ιχθύς Νότιος</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Piscis Austrinus (the constellation)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> See ἰχθύς m &amp; νότιος.</div><b>Ιωάννα</b>
  <div><i>name, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. a female given name, Ioanna, from Hebrew, equivalent to English Joanna, Joan, or Jane</div>
  <div class='def'>2. A saint whose feast day in the Greek Orthodox tradition is 7 January.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek Ἰωάννα. Doublet of Γιάννα.</div><b>Ιωάννης</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. a male given name, Giannis, Yiannis, or Yannis, from Hebrew, equivalent to English John, Ian, or Iain</div>
  <div class='def'>2. Any of the religious figures named John in the Bible, such as the John the Apostle or John the Baptist.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. Any of the saints whose feast day in the Greek Orthodox tradition is 7 January.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek Ἰωάννης, from Biblical Hebrew יוֹחָנָן. Doublet of Γιάννης.</div><b>Ιωάννινα</b>
  <div><i>name, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. Ioannina (the capital and largest city of the regional unit of Ioannina and region of Epirus, Greece)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. Ioannina (a regional unit of Epirus, Greece)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Uncertain, but possibly after Άγιος Ιωάννης or after the feminine name Ιωαννίνα.</div><b>Ιωακείμ</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>a male given name, Ioakeim, from Hebrew, equivalent to English Joachim</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek Ἰωακείμ, from Biblical Hebrew יְהוֹיָקִים.</div><b>Ιόνια νησιά</b>
  <div><i>name, neuter plural</i></div>
