  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek Κύπρῐος, from Κύπρος + -ῐος. Compare Mycenaean Greek 𐀓𐀠𐀪𐀍 (ku-pi-ri-jo).</div><b>Κύπρος</b>
  <div><i>name, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Cyprus (an island and country in the Mediterranean Sea, normally considered politically part of Europe but geographically part of West Asia)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek Κύπρος, already with connections to Sumerian 𒌓𒅗𒁇 (ud-ka-bar /⁠zabar, kabar⁠/, “bronze, copper”) for the island&#x27;s copper mines at the time (see Latin Cyprius) and an Mycenaean Greek adjective 𐀓𐀠𐀪𐀍 (ku-pi-ri-jo, “Cypriot”). For more, see the etymology of ancient Κύπρος.</div><b>Κύριε ελέησον</b>
  <div><i>phrase</i></div>
  <div class='def'>O Lord, have mercy! (upon us)</div>
