  <div><i>name, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Ursa Major, Great Bear (constellation)</div><b>Μεγάλη Βρετανία</b>
  <div><i>name, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. Great Britain (a large island (sometimes also including some of the surrounding smaller islands) off the north-west coast of Western Europe, made up of England, Scotland, and Wales; abbreviation <a href="bword://ΜΒ">ΜΒ</a> (MV))</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) Great Britain (the United Kingdom, a kingdom and country in Northern Europe including the island of Great Britain as well as Northern Ireland on the northeastern portion of the island of Ireland; abbreviation <a href="bword://ΜΒ">ΜΒ</a> (MV))</div><b>Μεγάλη Εβδομάδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural Μεγάλες Εβδομάδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Holy Week (the week before Easter)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Μεγάλη + Εβδομάδα</div><b>Μεγάλη Παρασκευή</b>
  <div><i>name, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Good Friday (the Friday before Easter)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek Μεγάλη Παρασκευή. Μεγάλη + Παρασκευή.</div><b>Μεγάλη Τεσσαρακοστή</b>
  <div><i>name, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Lent</div><b>Μεγάλης Βρετανίας</b>
  <div><i>name, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>genitive singular of Μεγάλη <a href="bword://Βρετανία">Βρετανία</a></div><b>Μεγάλο Σάββατο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Holy Saturday, Easter Saturday</div><b>Μεγάλος Αδελφός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. Big Brother (character from &#x27;Nineteen Eighty-Four&#x27;)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. pervasive surveillance</div><b>Μεγάλος Αδερφός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of Μεγάλος Αδελφός</div><b>Μεγαλειοτάτη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural Μεγαλειοτάτες, masculine Μεγαλειότατος)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Your Majesty, ma&#x27;am (term of address for queens)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Semantic loan from English Majesty.</div><b>Μεγαλειότατος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural Μεγαλειότατοι, feminine Μεγαλειοτάτη)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Your Majesty, sire (title of address for kings and emperors)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Semantic loan from English Majesty.</div><b>Μεγαλόπολη</b>
  <div><i>name</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Megalopoli</div><b>Μεθόδιος</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>a male given name, Methodios, equivalent to English Methodius</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Koine Greek Μεθόδιος.</div><b>Μειόκαινο</b>
  <div><i>name, neuter</i></div>
