  <div><i>num</i></div>
  <div class='def'>The Greek numeral representing the number six (6), typically romanized as the Roman numeral VI.</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ο Πτολεμαίος ΣΤʹ Φιλομήτωρ ( 186 – 145 π.Χ. ) ήταν ο έκτος φαραώ της Δυναστείας των Πτολεμαίων.
Ptolemy VI the Mother-Lover (186–145 B.C.) was the sixth pharaoh of the Dynasty of the Ptolemies.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From the similarity of the stigma (Ϛ), a Byzantine ligature of the common Greek consonant cluster σ-τ using sigma&#x27;s lunate form ϲ, with the medieval variant of the numerical form of digamma (), employed in Greek numerals for the value six, its place in the epichoric Milesian Greek alphabet (where it was more often written Ϝ).</div><b>ΣΥΡΙΖΑ</b>
