  <div class='def'>1. Chania (a city, the capital of Chania regional unit, on the island of Crete, Greece)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. Chania (a regional unit of Crete, around the city)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek Χανιά, from Arabic الخان + -ιά, literally from ال (al-, “the, place of the”) + خان but possibly transliterating a neighborhood whose named derived from its former importance in the worship of the Minoan god Velchanos, whose Minoan name was transcribed into Ancient Greek as Ϝελχάνος.</div><b>Χαράλαμπος</b>
  <div><i>name, masculine (usually uncountable, plural Χαράλαμποι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable, usually) a male given name</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable, usually) A saint whose feast day in the Greek Orthodox tradition is 10 February.</div>
