  <div class='def'>1. star</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ο τίτλος της ταινίας «Ο Πόλεμος των <b>Άστρων</b>». - The film title Star Wars</div>
  <div class='def'>2. star (generally, any small dot in the night sky)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) fate, star (portent, omen - a sign of good luck)</div>
  <div class='def'>4. star (a flat figure with projecting points)</div>
  <div class='ex'>το <b>άστρο</b> του Δαβίδ - the Star of David</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἄστρον. The figurative sense of &quot;fate&quot; since Mediaeval times. The contemporary terms of the emblem or geometrical shape, semantic loan from French étoile. For &quot;Star Wars&quot;, semantic loan from English Star Wars</div><b>άστρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine άστρωτη, neuter άστρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unmade (bed), unlaid (table), unpaved (road), etc</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> α- (a-, “to make, cover, etc”) + στρώνω</div><b>άστυ</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural άστη or άστεα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>centre (UK), center (US) of town or city</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From the Ancient Greek ἄστυ.</div><b>άστυφτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine άστυφτη, neuter άστυφτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unsqueezed, not wrung</div><b>άσυλα ανιάτων</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative plural of <a href="bword://άσυλο">άσυλο</a> ανιάτων</div><b>άσυλο</b>
