  <div class='def'>1. asylum, shelter, sanctuary, haven, refuge</div>
  <div class='def'>2. asylum, hospice, home, hostel (for those in need, or in need of care or protection)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἄσυλον.</div><b>άσυλο ανιάτων</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural άσυλα ανιάτων)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>hospice</div><b>άσφαιρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine άσφαιρη, neuter άσφαιρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. blank (cartridge)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>άσφαιρο</b> φυσίγγιο - blank round</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) failed to achieve, ineffective, harmless</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (colloquial, derogatory, figuratively) infertile, barren</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From ά- + σφαίρα. Attested since 1887 in Katharevousa as ἄσφαιρος.</div><b>άσφαλτος</b>
