  <div class='def'>to see/face death</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> from άγγελο- m + βλέπω</div><b>αγγελοθωρώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial, intransitive) to be knocking on heaven&#x27;s door, be at death&#x27;s door, be on one&#x27;s deathbed (to be near death, to be dying)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Όταν <b>αγγελοθωρώ</b>, μάλλον θα μετανιώνω πολλά που δεν έκανα. - When I&#x27;m on my deathbed, I&#x27;ll probably be regretting not having done many things.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> άγγελος + θωρώ, referring to the angel of death.</div><b>αγγελοκρούομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to receive the knock announcing imminent death</div><b>αγγελοκρούω</b>
