  <div class='def'>to clean, purify</div><b>αγναντεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to scan, survey (the horizon, look from afar)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀγναντεύω, from the adverb ἀγνάντι or ἀγνάντια + -εύω.
The also modern Greek αγνάντια derives from the Ancient Greek phrase τά ἐναντία through the medieval forms τα ἐνάντια (with change of accent) &gt; *ταϊνάντια (crasis of the two vowels α + ε) &gt; ταγνάντια ([ι &gt; γ]). The adverbial form αγνάντι comes from the singular of the Ancient phrase *το ἐνάντι.</div><b>αγνεία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) chastity</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) purity</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἁγνεία.</div><b>αγνισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγνισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>purification, cleansing</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἁγνισμός.</div><b>αγνοημένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αγνοημένη, neuter αγνοημένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ignored</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αγνοούμαι, passive voice of αγνοώ (“not know; ignore”).</div><b>αγνοούμαι</b>
