  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) naivety, innocence</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἁγνότης. Equivalent to αγνός + -ότητα.</div><b>αγνώμονας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγνώμονες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ingrate, (ungrateful person)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀγνώμων, from the accusative singular ἀγνώμονα and see: αγνώμων.</div><b>αγνώμων</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγνώμων, neuter αγνώμον)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ungrateful (not thankful)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Αν και του έδωσαν αύξηση μισθού, ήταν εντελώς <b>αγνώμων</b>. - Even though they gave him a pay rise, he was completely ungrateful.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀγνώμων, from Ancient Greek ἀ- (a-, “un-”) (α- (a-) privative) + γνώμη. Semantic loan from French ingrat. Also substantivised.
:* The ancient neuter ἄγνωμον, with stress shift to αγνώμον.</div>
