  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀγνώμων, from Ancient Greek ἀ- (a-, “un-”) (α- (a-) privative) + γνώμη. Semantic loan from French ingrat. Also substantivised.
:* The ancient neuter ἄγνωμον, with stress shift to αγνώμον.</div><b>αγνώριστος</b>
