  <div class='def'>unyielding, unbowed, unwilling to kneel</div><b>αγονία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) sterility</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) barrenness</div><b>αγορά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγορές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (historical) agora, the ancient square or marketplace, the centre of public life</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η αρχαία <b>αγορά</b> στην Αθήνα είναι κάτω από την Ακρόπολη. - The ancient agora in Athens is just under the Acropolis.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. marketplace, market</div>
  <div class='ex'>Πάω στην <b>αγορά</b> να ψωνίσω. - I am going to the market to shop.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. purchase</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αγορά</b> τοις μετρητοίς - cash purchase</div>
  <div class='def'>4. commerce, trade</div>
  <div class='ex'>Οι <b>αγορές</b> κατέρρευσαν στο κραχ. - The markets collapsed during the crash.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀγορά.</div><b>αγοράζομαι</b>
