  <div class='def'>1. to ripen, approach ripeness</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to be not quite ripe</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From άγουρος + φέρνω.</div><b>αγουρωπός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγουρωπή, neuter αγουρωπό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>almost ripe, not quite ripe, semi-ripe</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> άγουρος + -ωπός</div><b>αγουρόλαδο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγουρόλαδα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. olive oil from unripe olives</div>
  <div class='def'>2. extra virgin olive oil</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> άγουρος + λάδι</div><b>αγουστιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγουστιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>lack of good taste, tastelessness (with reference to aesthetic properties such as beauty)</div><b>αγούπας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγούπες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αγιούπας">αγιούπας</a></div><b>αγράμματος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγράμματη, neuter αγράμματο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. illiterate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. ignorant</div>
  <div class='def'>3. uneducated</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From α- (a-, “lacking”) + γράμματα.</div><b>αγράμπελη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αγράμπελες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable, usually) flowering climbing plant; clematis</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable, usually) flowering climbing plant; wild woodbine</div><b>αγρίεμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγριέματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. wildness, fierceness, ferocity</div>
  <div class='def'>2. bullying</div><b>αγρίκησα</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>first-person singular simple past of αγρικάω and <a href="bword://αγρικώ">αγρικώ</a></div><b>αγρίμι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγρίμια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. wild animal</div>
  <div class='def'>2. agrimi, a wild goat from Crete</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) uncouth or unsociable person</div><b>αγρίως</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>wildly, savagely, fiercely</div><b>αγραμματισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγραμματισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>agrammatism</div><b>αγραμματοσύνη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγραμματοσύνες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>illiteracy</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγράμματος + -σύνη</div><b>αγρανάπαυση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγραναπαύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fallowing, allowing to lie fallow</div>
  <div class='ex'>χωράφι σε <b>αγρανάπαυση</b> - fallow field</div><b>αγρατσούνιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγρατσούνιστη, neuter αγρατσούνιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unscratched</div><b>αγρεργάτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγρεργάτες, feminine αγρεργάτρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>farmhand, agricultural worker</div><b>αγρεργάτρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγρεργάτριες, masculine αγρεργάτης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>farmhand, agricultural worker</div><b>αγρεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (dated) to hunt</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (dated) to canvass for votes</div><b>αγριάδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγριάδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. wildness, ferocity, fierceness</div>
  <div class='def'>2. agricultural weed</div>
  <div class='def'>3. agricultural weed; couch grass, twitch, quitch</div><b>αγριάμπελη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αγράμπελη">αγράμπελη</a></div><b>αγριάνθρωπος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγριάνθρωποι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. rough, savage or brutish man</div>
  <div class='def'>2. caveman</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From άγριος + άνθρωπος.</div><b>αγριελιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγριελιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative spelling of <a href="bword://αγριλιά">αγριλιά</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From άγριος + ελιά.</div><b>αγριεμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αγριεμένη, neuter αγριεμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. made wild</div>
  <div class='def'>2. scared</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αγριεύομαι, passive voice of αγριεύω (“make wild; scare”).</div><b>αγριεμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) wildness, fierceness, ferocity</div><b>αγριεύομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be frightened, be scared</div><b>αγριεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to make wild, taunt, bully</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to turn nasty, become wild</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to scare</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀγριεύω &lt; ἄγρι(ος), “wild; tough”) + affix -εύω. Ultimately from the ancient ἀγρός.</div><b>αγρικώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>variant of αγρικάω</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Simplified spelling of the inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀγροικῶ and see: γρικάω.</div><b>αγριλίσιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγριλίσια, neuter αγριλίσιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>olivewood</div><b>αγριλιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγριλιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>wild olive tree, oleaster</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀγριέλαιος. By surface analysis, άγριος + ελιά.</div><b>αγριοβούβαλο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγριοβούβαλα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>African buffalo (Syncerus caffer)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αγριο- (agrio-, “wild”) + βουβάλι.</div><b>αγριοβόρι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγριοβόρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>cold wild north wind</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριο- (agrio-, “wild”) + βοριάς</div><b>αγριοβότανο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγριοβότανα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>wild flower, weed</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριο- (agrio-, “wild”) + βότανο</div><b>αγριογούρουνο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγριογούρουνα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>wild boar, Sus scrofa</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριο- (agrio-, “wild”) + γουρούνι</div><b>αγριοδαμάσκηνο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγριοδαμάσκηνα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>bullace, wild plum, damson</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριο- (agrio-, “wild, uncultivated”) + δαμάσκηνο</div><b>αγριοκάστανο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγριοκάστανα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>horse chestnut, conker (UK)</div><b>αγριοκάτσικο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγριοκάτσικα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. ibex, wild goat</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) unsociable or ill behaved child or man</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριο- (agrio-, “wild”) + κατσίκι</div><b>αγριοκαστανιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγριοκαστανιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>horse chestnut tree</div><b>αγριοκερασιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγριοκερασιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. wild cherry tree (Prunus avium or Prunus serotina)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (metonymically) the wood of this tree.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> By surface analysis, αγριο- (agrio-, “wild”) + κερασιά.</div><b>αγριοκοίταγμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγριοκοιτάγματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>glare, scowl (fierce, frowning look)</div><b>αγριοκοιτάζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to glare, glare at (usually in the plural)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Οι δυο αντίπαλοι <b>αγριοκοιταζόντουσαν</b> πριν ορμήσουν ο ένας στον άλλον. - The two opponents glared at each other before starting the fight.</div><b>αγριοκοιτάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to glower, look angrily at</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριο- (agrio-, “wild”) + κοιτάζω</div><b>αγριοκοιταγμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αγριοκοιταγμένη, neuter αγριοκοιταγμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>who has been looked at angrily</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αγριοκοιτάζομαι and αγριοκοιτιέμαι, passive voices of αγριοκοιτάζω and αγριοκοιτάω / αγριοκοιτώ respectively. Morphologically, from αγριο- (agrio-, “wild”) + κοιταγμένος.</div><b>αγριοκόριτσο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγριοκόριτσα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>a girl acting in a wild manner.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριο- (agrio-, “wild”) + κορίτσι</div><b>αγριοκύμινο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) caraway (literally: wild cumin)</div><b>αγριολάχανο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγριολάχανα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>wild cabbage</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀγριολάχανον.</div><b>αγριολούλουδο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγριολούλουδα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>wild flower</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριο- (agrio-, “wild”) + λουλούδι</div><b>αγριομέλισσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγριομέλισσες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>wild bee, bumblebee</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριο- (agrio-, “wild”) + μέλισσα</div><b>αγριομιλάω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αγριομιλώ">αγριομιλώ</a></div><b>αγριομιλώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to speak harshly, angrily, etc</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to snap at</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριο- (agrio-, “wild”) + μιλώ</div><b>αγριοπερίστερο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγριοπερίστρα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>rock dove (IOC preferred term), rock pigeon (Columba livia)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριο- (agrio-, “wild”) + περιστέρι</div><b>αγριοράδικο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγριοράδικα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Any of various wild edible bitter plants; especially dandelion and hawkbit.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριο- (agrio-, “wild”) + ραδίκ(ι) (“radiccio”) + -ο (suffix for neuters).</div><b>αγριοραδίκι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγριοραδίκια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αγριοράδικο">αγριοράδικο</a></div><b>αγριοσυκιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγριοσυκιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>wild fig tree</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριο- (agrio-, “uncultivated”) + συκιά</div><b>αγριοτριαντάφυλλο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγριοτριαντάφυλλα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of άγριο <a href="bword://τριαντάφυλλο">τριαντάφυλλο</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριο- (agrio-, “wild”) + τριαντάφυλλο</div><b>αγριοτριανταφυλλιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγριοτριανταφυλλιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>dog rose</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριο- (agrio-, “wild”) + τριανταφυλλιά</div><b>αγριοφωνάρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγριοφωνάρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>bawl, angry shout</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριο- (agrio-, “wild”) + φωνάρα</div><b>αγριωπά</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>grimly, fiercely, in a growling manner</div><b>αγριωπός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγριωπή, neuter αγριωπό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. scowling, glowering</div>
  <div class='def'>2. grim, wild-looking, fierce-looking</div><b>αγριόγαλλος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγριόγαλλοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αγριόγαλος">αγριόγαλος</a></div><b>αγριόγαλος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγριόγαλοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>grouse, bustard (one of several terms for these game birds)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριο- (agrio-, “wild”) + γάλος</div><b>αγριόγατα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγριόγατες, masculine αγριόγατος)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>wildcat</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριό- + γάτα</div><b>αγριόγατος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγριόγατοι, feminine αγριόγατα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. wildcat</div>
  <div class='def'>2. bobcat</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριό- + γάτος</div><b>αγριόκοτα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγριόκοτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>grouse, pheasant (one of several terms for members of these families)</div><b>αγριόκοττα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγριόκοττες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative spelling of <a href="bword://αγριόκοτα">αγριόκοτα</a></div><b>αγριόκουρκος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγριόκουρκοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>western capercaillie (Tetrao urogallus), often more simply capercaillie</div><b>αγριόκρινο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγριόκρινα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. iris (flowering plant)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. wild lily</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αγριό- + κρίνο.</div><b>αγριόκυκνος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγριόκυκνοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (broadly) wild swan</div>
  <div class='def'>2. whooper swan, Cygnus cygnus</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριό- + κύκνος</div><b>αγριόπαπια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγριόπαπιες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. wild duck</div>
  <div class='def'>2. mallard (the common dabbling duck, Anas platyrhynchos)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From άγριος + πάπια.</div><b>αγριόρνιθα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγριόρνιθες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>grouse, bustard (one of several terms for members of these families)</div><b>αγριόσκυλο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγριόσκυλα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. savage, fierce or wild dog</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (specifically) any of various species of wild dog</div>
  <div class='ex'>αφρικανικό <b>αγριόσκυλο</b> - African wild dog</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριό- + σκύλος</div><b>αγριόσυκο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγριόσυκα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>wild fig</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριο- (agrio-, “uncultivated”) + σύκο</div><b>αγριότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγριότητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. savagery, brutality, ferocity</div>
  <div class='def'>2. atrocity</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀγριότης, equivalent to άγριος + -ότητα.</div><b>αγριότοπος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγριότοποι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>wild country, wilderness, uncultivated tract</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριό- + τόπος</div><b>αγριόχηνα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγριόχηνες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. wild goose</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) large wild birds: eg bustard, crane</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριό- + χήνα</div><b>αγριόχοιρος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγριόχοιροι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>wild boar, Sus scrofa</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριό- + χοίρος</div><b>αγριόχορτο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγριόχορτα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>weed (unwanted plant)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγριό- + χορτο (chorto, “plant”)</div><b>αγριώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(obsolete) to rile, to infuriate</div><b>αγροίκησα</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>first-person singular simple past of αγροικάω and <a href="bword://αγροικώ">αγροικώ</a></div><b>αγροίκος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγροίκοι, feminine αγροίκα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. boor, churl, roughneck</div>
  <div class='def'>2. yokel</div>
  <div class='def'>3. bounder</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγροίκα, neuter αγροίκο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. churlish, boorish</div>
  <div class='def'>2. rustic, coarse</div><b>αγροβακτήριο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγροβακτήρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>agrobacterium (Agrobacterium)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from translingual Agrobacterium. By surface analysis, αγρός + βακτήριο.</div><b>αγροβιολογία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγροβιολογίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>agrobiology</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγρο- (agro-) + βιολογία.</div><b>αγροδίαιτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγροδίαιτη, neuter αγροδίαιτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>rural, living in the countryside</div><b>αγροικία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγροικίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>farmhouse, country cottage</div><b>αγροικώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>variant of αγροικάω and see: <a href="bword://γρικάω">γρικάω</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀγροικῶ and see: γρικάω.</div><b>αγροκήπιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγροκήπια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>model farm, experimental farm</div><b>αγροκαλλιέργεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγροκαλλιέργειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>agriculture</div>
  <div class='ex'>αστική <b>αγροκαλλιέργεια</b> - urban agriculture</div><b>αγρονομία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) agronomy, rural economy</div><b>αγρονομικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγρονομική, neuter αγρονομικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>agronomic, relating to agronomy</div><b>αγρονόμος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural αγρονόμοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. farm manager</div>
  <div class='def'>2. agronomist</div>
  <div class='def'>3. a rank in the rural police</div><b>αγροτεμάχιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγροτεμάχια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>plot, parcel of land, small field</div><b>αγροτιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) peasantry, farmers, countrypeople (as a class)</div><b>αγροτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγροτική, neuter αγροτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. agrarian</div>
  <div class='def'>2. relating to a farm or farmer</div>
  <div class='def'>3. rural, relating to the countryside</div><b>αγροτοβιομηχανικός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγροτοβιομηχανικοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>agroindustry, industrialised farming</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αγροτικός + βιομηχανικός.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγροτοβιομηχανική, neuter αγροτοβιομηχανικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>agroindustry, industrialised farming</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αγροτικός + βιομηχανικός.</div><b>αγροτοδασικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγροτοδασική, neuter αγροτοδασικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(neologism) forest</div>
  <div class='ex'>αγροτοδασική πυρκαγιά - forest fire</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγροτο- (agroto-, “agrarian, rural”) + δασικός</div><b>αγροτοπατέρας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγροτοπατέρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(derogatory) carpetbagger (paternalistic political or union official who in public supports rural causes, but perhaps to further his own ends)</div><b>αγροτοπατερισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγροτοπατερισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(derogatory) carpetbaggery - the activities of a paternalistic political or union official who in public supports rural causes, but perhaps to further his own ends</div><b>αγροτόσπιτο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγροτόσπιτα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>farmhouse</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From the Ancient Greek κατοικία.</div><b>αγροφυλακή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) rural police service</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγρός + φύλακας</div><b>αγροφύλακας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγροφύλακες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>rural policeman, field warden</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγρός + φύλακας</div><b>αγρυπνάω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αγρυπνώ">αγρυπνώ</a></div><b>αγρυπνία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγρυπνίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. sleeplessness, night of watching</div>
  <div class='def'>2. vigilance, watchfulness</div>
  <div class='def'>3. vigil (church ceremony)</div><b>αγρυπνισμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αγρυπνισμένη, neuter αγρυπνισμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sleepless</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect passive participle of αγρυπνώ, a verb without passive forms.</div><b>αγρυπνώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to stay awake, be sleepless</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to keep watch, guard</div><b>αγρωστοειδή</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αγρωστώδη">αγρωστώδη</a></div><b>αγρωστώδη</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>The Poaceae, most grasses.</div><b>αγρόκτημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγροκτήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. farm</div>
  <div class='def'>2. country cottage or property</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from αγρο- (agro-) + κτήμα; see αγρός for more on the first component.</div><b>αγρός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγροί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. field</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (in plural) countryside</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀγρός.</div><b>αγρότης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγρότες, feminine αγρότισσα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>farmer, countryman</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀγρότης.</div><b>αγρότισσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγρότισσες, masculine αγρότης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>farmer, countrywoman</div><b>αγρύπνια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγρύπνιες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αγρυπνία">αγρυπνία</a></div><b>αγυάλιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγυάλιστη, neuter αγυάλιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unpolished, unvarnished</div>
  <div class='ex'>Έχει <b>αγυάλιστα</b> παπούτσια. - He has unpolished shoes.</div><b>αγυιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγυιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(archaic, dated, formal, often, sarcastic) lane, back street, side street (small and narrow street or alley)</div>
  <div class='ex'>informal, standard synonym: σοκάκι n (sokáki).</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Katharevousa ἀγυιά from Ancient Greek ἀγυιᾱ́, less common variant of ἄγυια. Loaned in the 19th century to substitute the Demotic σοκάκι which was a Turkish loanword.</div><b>αγυιοπαίδου</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. misconstruction of αγυιόπαιδος genitive singular of <a href="bword://αγυιόπαις">αγυιόπαις</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. misconstruction of αγυιόπαιδου genitive singular of <a href="bword://αγυιόπαιδο">αγυιόπαιδο</a></div><b>αγυιόπαιδο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγυιόπαιδα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>street urchin, guttersnipe, gamin</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Katharevousa ἀγυιόπαις coinage, from αγυιά + παιδ- (paid-, “child”). Compare γυμνασιόπαιδο.</div><b>αγυιόπαις</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγυιόπαιδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>monotonic spelling of ἀγυιόπαις (Katharevousa): See Modern Greek <a href="bword://αγυιόπαιδο">αγυιόπαιδο</a></div><b>αγυμνασία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) lack of physical exercise</div><b>αγυρντίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sprain, wrench, dislocate</div><b>αγυρτία</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>misspelling of <a href="bword://αγυρτεία">αγυρτεία</a></div><b>αγυρτεία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγυρτείες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>charlatanism, quackery (medical fraud)</div><b>αγχέμαχος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγχέμαχος, neuter αγχέμαχον)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(formal, literary) weapon or armor suitable for hand-to-hand fighting, close quarter combat</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀγχέμαχος</div><b>αγχίνοια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) sagacity, wisdom</div><b>αγχίνους</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγχίνους, neuter αγχίνουν)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. wise, sagacious</div>
  <div class='def'>2. intelligent</div>
  <div class='def'>3. perceptive</div><b>αγχιστεία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) relationship by marriage</div>
  <div class='ex'>Έχουν συγγένεια εξ αγχιστείας. - They are related by marriage.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀγχιστεία.</div><b>αγχολυτικό</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. inflection of <a href="bword://αγχολυτικός">αγχολυτικός</a>:; masculine accusative singular</div>
  <div class='def'>2. inflection of <a href="bword://αγχολυτικός">αγχολυτικός</a>:; neuter nominative/accusative/vocative singular</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγχολυτικά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anxiolytic, tranquilizer, antianxiety</div><b>αγχολυτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγχολυτική, neuter αγχολυτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anxiolytic, tranquilizing, antianxiety</div><b>αγχωμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αγχωμένη, neuter αγχωμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(stressed) stressed</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αγχώνομαι, passive voice of αγχώνω (“make anxious, stress”).</div><b>αγχωτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγχωτική, neuter αγχωτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. stressful, stress-inducing</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (of a person) anxious (having a feeling of anxiety or disquietude)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αγχώ(νω)) + -τικός with semantic loan from French angoissé.</div><b>αγχόνη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγχόνες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(rare) gallows, noose, gibbet</div><b>αγχώδης</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγχώδης, neuter αγχώδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>stressed, anxious, neurotic</div><b>αγχώνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to worry, be anxious, be stressed</div><b>αγχώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to make anxious, stress (induce stress in someone)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> άγχος + -ώνω.</div><b>αγωγή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγωγές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. education, training, upbringing</div>
  <div class='def'>2. treatment, regimen</div>
  <div class='def'>3. discipline</div>
  <div class='def'>4. lawsuit, action</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀγωγή.</div><b>αγωγιάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. hire, rent (an animal)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. hire out (an animal)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Koine Greek ἀγωγιάζω</div><b>αγωγιάτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγωγιάτες, feminine αγωγιάτισσα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>muleteer, mule driver</div><b>αγωγιάτισσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγωγιάτισσες, masculine αγωγιάτης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>muleteer, mule driver</div><b>αγωγιμότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγωγιμότητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. electrical conductivity, thermal conductivity</div>
  <div class='def'>2. conductance (electrical conductivity)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγώγιμος + -ότητα, calque of French conductivité. First attested 1890.</div><b>αγωγός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγωγοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. conductor, wire, lead</div>
  <div class='def'>2. pipe, conduit, channel</div>
  <div class='def'>3. duct</div><b>αγωνία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγωνίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. impatience, anxiety, suspense</div>
  <div class='ex'>Μια ενδιαφέρουσα πλοκή διατηρεί τον θεατή σε <b>αγωνία</b> σε όλη την ταινία. - An intriguing plot keeps the viewer in suspense throughout the film.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. agony, anguish</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀγωνία.</div><b>αγωνίζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to fight, contend</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to struggle</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to play, match</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀγωνίζομαι.</div><b>αγωνίστρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγωνίστριες, masculine αγωνιστής)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. fighter, contender</div>
  <div class='def'>2. campaigner</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) breadwinner</div><b>αγωνιστής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγωνιστές, feminine αγωνίστρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. fighter, contender</div>
  <div class='def'>2. campaigner</div>
  <div class='def'>3. agonist</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (figuratively) breadwinner</div><b>αγωνιστικά</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>competitively, agonistically</div><b>αγωνιστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγωνιστική, neuter αγωνιστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fighting, combative, competitive, fit for contest, debating, very active</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αγωνιστική</b> διάθεση - fighting spirit</div><b>αγωνιστικότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) militancy, aggression</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγωνιστικός + -ότητα.</div><b>αγωνιώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to be in agony</div>
  <div class='ex'>Οι σκύλοι μου <b>αγωνιούν</b> να σας γνωρίσουν. - My pups are dying to meet you.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to be anxious</div><b>αγωνιώδης</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγωνιώδης, neuter αγωνιώδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anxious, desperate, anguished</div><b>αγωνοδίκης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγωνοδίκες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. judge, umpire</div>
  <div class='def'>2. supervisor or administrator of an event</div><b>αγωνοθέτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγωνοθέτες, feminine αγωνοθέτρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>donor, sponsor, provider or organiser of a literary or arts prize</div><b>αγωνοθέτρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγωνοθέτριες, masculine αγωνοθέτης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>donor, sponsor, provider or organiser of a literary or arts prize</div><b>αγωνοθεσία</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) administration, adjudication</div><b>αγωνοθετώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to start a sporting competition</div><b>αγωροφέρνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>highly unorthodox spelling of <a href="bword://αγοροφέρνω">αγοροφέρνω</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αγοροφέρνω, but using the spelling αγώρι for αγόρι n at the dictionaries by Babiniotis, connecting the omega with Ancient Greek ἄωρος. See more at αγόρι.</div><b>αγόγγυστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγόγγυστη, neuter αγόγγυστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. uncomplaining (literal: without muttering)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. longsuffering, enduring</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From the adverb of Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀγογγύστως, a back-formation from αγογγύστως.</div><b>αγόρευση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγόρευσες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>speech, rhetoric, oration (public speaking)</div><b>αγόρι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγόρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. boy</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (informal) lad, laddie, sonny</div>
  <div class='def'>3. boyfriend, sweetheart (male)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀγόριν, ἀγούριν; diminutive of Koine Greek ἄγωρος, from Ancient Greek ἄωρος, from ὥρα. Compare with Byzantine Greek ἄγουρος.</div><b>αγύμναστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγύμναστη, neuter αγύμναστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unexercised, unfit (physical exercise)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. untrained, lacking practise (UK), lacking practice (US)</div><b>αγύρευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγύρευτη, neuter αγύρευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unsought, not looked for</div><b>αγύριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγύριστη, neuter αγύριστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unreturned, untraversed, not returned from</div>
  <div class='ex'>δανεικά κι <b>αγύριστα</b> - borrowed and not returned</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγύριστοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>place or setting no one returns from, i.e. hell; chiefly in the expression</div>
  <div class='ex'>Να πας στον <b>αγύριστο</b>! - Go to hell!</div><b>αγύρτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγύρτες, feminine αγύρτισσα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>charlatan, imposter, quack</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀγύρτης.</div><b>αγύρτικος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγύρτικη, neuter αγύρτικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>humbugging, behaving like a charlatan</div><b>αγύρτισσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αγύρτισσες, masculine αγύρτης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>charlatan, imposter</div><b>αγώγι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγώγια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. load, burden</div>
  <div class='def'>2. porterage, carriage</div>
  <div class='def'>3. porterage, carriage; porterage, carriage - the fare or charge for this</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (rare) conductivity</div><b>αγώγιμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αγώγιμη, neuter αγώγιμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. thermally or electrically conductive</div>
  <div class='def'>2. actionable</div><b>αγώι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγώγια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αγώγι">αγώγι</a></div><b>αγών</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγώνες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(archaic) monotonic spelling of ἀγών)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀγών. Compare inherited αγώνας.</div><b>αγώνας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αγώνες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. fight, efforts, struggle</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (capitalized) the Greek War of Independence</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ο <b>Αγώνας</b>, Ο <b>Αγώνας</b> του 1821</div>
  <div class='def'>3. race, game, match</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (in plural) the Games</div>
  <div class='ex'>οι ολυμπιακοί αγώνες (the Olympic Games)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀγών. Doublet of αγών, a borrowing.</div><b>αγώνισμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αγωνίσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>competition, contest, event</div><b>αδάκρυτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδάκρυτη, neuter αδάκρυτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unweeping, tearless, dry-eyed</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) unfeeling, without regrets</div><b>αδάμαντας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αδάμαντες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αδάμας">αδάμας</a></div><b>αδάμας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αδάμαντες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (dated, formal) diamond</div>
  <div class='def'>2. adamant, adamantine</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀδάμας, ancient sense: &quot;the hardest metal&quot;, from the accusative singular &quot;τόν ἀδάμαντα</div><b>αδάμαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδάμαστη, neuter αδάμαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>indomitable, untameable</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αδάμαστη</b> θέληση - indomitable will</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀδάμαστος.</div><b>αδάνειστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδάνειστη, neuter αδάνειστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. not loanable, unborrowable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unborrowable, unborrowed</div><b>αδάπανος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδάπανη, neuter αδάπανο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>free of charge, free, gratis, without charge</div><b>αδέκαρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδέκαρη, neuter αδέκαρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>penniless, without money, poor</div><b>αδέκαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδέκαστη, neuter αδέκαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. incorruptible</div>
  <div class='def'>2. impartial unbiased</div><b>αδέλφι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αδέλφια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. sibling</div>
  <div class='def'>2. a general term of close relationship</div>
  <div class='ex'>όλοι οι άνθρωποι είναι <b>αδέλφια</b> - all men are brothers</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀδελφός.</div><b>αδέλφωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αδελφώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. fraternisation, brotherhood</div>
  <div class='def'>2. tillering (production of multiple shoots)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αδελφώνω + -μα (-ma).</div><b>αδέλφωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αδελφώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(rare) brotherhood, fraternisation</div>
  <div class='ex'>Other forms: αδέρφωμα n (adérfoma)</div><b>αδένας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αδένες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>gland</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From the Ancient Greek ἀδήν.</div><b>αδένωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αδενώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>adenoma</div><b>αδέξια</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>awkwardly</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. nominative/accusative/vocative feminine singular of <a href="bword://αδέξιος">αδέξιος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αδέξιος">αδέξιος</a></div><b>αδέξιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδέξια, neuter αδέξιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>clumsy, awkward, uncoordinated</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀδέξῐος; by surface analysis, α- (a-, “un-, -less”) + δεξιός.</div><b>αδέρφι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αδέρφια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. alternative form of <a href="bword://αδέλφι">αδέλφι</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. Cretan dialect form of <a href="bword://αδέλφι">αδέλφι</a></div><b>αδέρφια</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of αδέλφια</div><b>αδέρφωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αδερφώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αδέλφωμα">αδέλφωμα</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αδερφώνω + -μα (-ma).</div><b>αδέσμευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδέσμευτη, neuter αδέσμευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unattached, unmarried</div>
  <div class='def'>2. non-aligned, neutral</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αδέσμευτες</b> χώρες - non-aligned countries</div><b>αδέσποτη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αδέσποτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>stray bullet, stray punch</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative feminine singular of <a href="bword://αδέσποτος">αδέσποτος</a></div><b>αδέσποτο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αδέσποτα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>stray, stray animal</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://αδέσποτος">αδέσποτος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://αδέσποτος">αδέσποτος</a></div><b>αδέσποτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδέσποτη, neuter αδέσποτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. stray, ownerless (of animal)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. random, stray, directionless (of bullet, ball, etc)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀδέσποτος.</div><b>αδέψητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδέψητη, neuter αδέψητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. raw</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unworked, crude</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) uneducated, uncultivated</div><b>αδήλωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδήλωτη, neuter αδήλωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>undeclared, unregistered, unreported</div>
  <div class='ex'>Θα δημοσίευσε μια λίστα από 1.747 πλούσιων φορολογουμένων που είχαν εντοπιστεί με <b>αδήλωτα</b> εισοδήματα. - It published a list of 1,747 wealthy taxpayers who were found to have undeclared income.</div><b>αδήμευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδήμευτη, neuter αδήμευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unconfiscated, unseized</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unseizable, non-confiscatable (not subject to seizure)</div><b>αδήριτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδήριτη, neuter αδήριτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>dire, of necessity, insurmountable</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αδήριτη</b> ανάγκη - dire necessity</div><b>αδήωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδήωτη, neuter αδήωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unlooted, unplundered</div><b>αδίαντο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αδίαντα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. maidenhair (Adiantum capillus-veneris)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. adiantum (Adiantum)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀδῐ́ᾰντον. For the second sense, semantic loan from translingual Adiantum.</div><b>αδίδακτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδίδακτη, neuter αδίδακτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>untaught, unseen</div><b>αδίδαχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδίδαχτη, neuter αδίδαχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αδίδακτος">αδίδακτος</a></div><b>αδίκαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδίκαστη, neuter αδίκαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unheard, untried</div><b>αδίκημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αδικήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>offence (UK), offense (US) (unjust or illegal act)</div><b>αδίπλωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδίπλωτη, neuter αδίπλωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unfolded, lacking folds</div><b>αδίστακτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδίστακτη, neuter αδίστακτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unscrupulous, ruthless (contemptuous of what is right or honourable)</div><b>αδίσταχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδίσταχτη, neuter αδίσταχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αδίστακτος">αδίστακτος</a></div><b>αδίψαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδίψαστη, neuter αδίψαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unthirsty, not thirsty</div><b>αδίωκτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδίωκτη, neuter αδίωκτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unsued, unprosecuted</div><b>αδαής</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. ignorant, inexperienced</div>
  <div class='def'>2. clumsy</div><b>αδαημοσύνη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) ignorance, inexperience</div><b>αδαμάντινος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδαμάντινη, neuter αδαμάντινο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. made of diamond</div>
  <div class='def'>2. adamantine</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) adamant, firm, unflinching</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀδαμάντινος and semantic loan from English adamantine &lt; Latin adamantinus &lt; Ancient Greek ἀδαμάντινος.</div><b>αδαμαντίνη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) tooth enamel</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Ultimately from Ancient Greek ἀδᾰμάντῐνος.</div><b>αδαμαντοκόλλητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδαμαντοκόλλητη, neuter αδαμαντοκόλλητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>set with diamonds, decorated with diamonds</div><b>αδαμαντοποίκιλτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδαμαντοποίκιλτη, neuter αδαμαντοποίκιλτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>set with diamonds, decorated with diamonds</div><b>αδαμαντοπωλείο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αδαμαντοπωλεία)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>jeweller&#x27;s, jewellery shop (UK), jeweler&#x27;s, jewelry store (US) (specializing in diamonds or other gemstones)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αδαμαντ- (adamant-) + -ο- (-o-) + -πωλείο.</div><b>αδαμαντοπώλης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αδαμαντοπώλες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>diamond dealer, jeweller (UK), jeweler (US)</div><b>αδαμαντοστόλιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδαμαντοστόλιστη, neuter αδαμαντοστόλιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>set with diamonds, decorated with diamonds</div><b>αδαμαντουργός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αδαμαντουργοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>diamond cutter</div><b>αδαμαντοφόρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδαμαντοφόρα, neuter αδαμαντοφόρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>diamond rich, land bearing diamonds</div><b>αδαμαντωρυχείο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αδαμαντωρυχεία)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>diamond mine</div><b>αδαμαντωρύχος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αδαμαντωρύχοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>diamond miner</div><b>αδαμαντόστικτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδαμαντόστικτη, neuter αδαμαντόστικτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>set with diamonds, decorated with diamonds</div><b>αδαμιαία περιβολή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(humorous, idiomatic, uncountable) birthday suit, nakedness (literally: Adamic clothes)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Εμφανίστηκε με <b>αδαμιαία περιβολή</b>. - He appeared in his birthday suit.</div><b>αδαμιαίος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδαμιαία, neuter αδαμιαίο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. of Adam, Adam&#x27;s</div>
  <div class='def'>2. naked</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> from Αδάμ</div><b>αδαπάνητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδαπάνητη, neuter αδαπάνητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unspent, not spent</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀδαπάνητος.</div><b>αδαπάνως</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>free of charge, free</div><b>αδασκάλευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδασκάλευτη, neuter αδασκάλευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. untutored, unschooled, uninstructed</div>
  <div class='def'>2. undomesticated</div><b>αδασμολόγητα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>duty-free</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αδασμολόγητος.</div><b>αδασμολόγητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδασμολόγητη, neuter αδασμολόγητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>duty-free</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From α- (a-, “not”) + δασμολογώ.</div><b>αδείλιαστα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fearlessly</div><b>αδείλιαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδείλιαστη, neuter αδείλιαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fearless, intrepid (not battle shy)</div><b>αδείπνητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδείπνητη, neuter αδείπνητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>undined, without supper</div><b>αδειάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (transitive) to empty (to make empty; to void; to remove the contents of)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Άδειασαν</b> τα ποτήρια τους. - They emptied their glasses.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (transitive) to empty, to clear out, to pour out, to decant, to unload (:contents)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Αδειάστε</b> το περιεχόμενο στην κατσαρόλα - Empty the contents into the pan.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (intransitive) to be empty</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το σχολείο <b>αδειάζει</b> το καλοκαίρι· τα παιδιά πάνε διακοπές. - The school is empty in the summer; the children are on vacation.</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (colloquial) to be available</div>
  <div class='ex'>Έλα να με βοηθήσεις. — Δεν <b>αδειάζω</b>, έχω πολλή δουλειά. - Come and help me. — I am not free, I have too much work.</div>
  <div class='def'>5. to unload (a weapon)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀδειάζω, formed from Ancient Greek ἄδει(α) f, “no fear; abundance”) + -άζω.</div><b>αδειανός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδειανός, neuter αδειανή)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://άδειος">άδειος</a></div><b>αδειασμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αδειασμένη, neuter αδειασμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>made empty</div>
  <div class='ex'>compare to άδειος (ádeios), αδειανός (adeianós, “empty”)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect passive participle of αδειάζω.</div><b>αδειοδοτώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>authorise (UK), authorize (US), license</div><b>αδειούχος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδειούχος or αδειούχα, neuter αδειούχο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. on leave, on furlough</div>
  <div class='def'>2. licensed</div><b>αδεκαρία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αδεκαρίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>poverty, pennilessness, penury, destitution</div><b>αδελέαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδελέαστη, neuter αδελέαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unseduced, not tempted</div><b>αδελφάτο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αδελφάτα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. brotherhood, sisterhood, fraternity, sorority (an association of people)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. board of management (usually of a charitable organisation)</div><b>αδελφή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αδελφές, masculine αδελφός)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. sister (female sibling)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η <b>αδελφή</b> μου σπουδάζει νομική. - My sister is studying law.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. sister (nurse)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Πάω να φωνάξω την <b>αδελφή</b> να σου αλλάξει την πάπια. - I&#x27;m going to get the sister to change your bedpan.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. sister (form of address for nuns)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η <b>Αδελφή</b> Ιωάννα είναι καλόγρια εδώ και επτά χρόνια. - Sister Ioanna has been a nun for seven years now.</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (colloquial, derogatory) queer, faggot (homosexual man)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το γκέι μπαρ είναι γεμάτο <b>αδελφές</b>. - The gay bar is full of queers.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀδελφή, feminine form of ἀδελφός; from Proto-Hellenic *hə- (“same, together”) from Proto-Indo-European *sm̥- (“together, one”) + *gʷelbʰ- (“womb”), equivalent to ἁ- (ha-, “same”, copulative prefix) + δελφύς.</div><b>αδελφικά</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. fraternally</div>
  <div class='def'>2. in a sisterly or brotherly manner.</div><b>αδελφικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδελφική, neuter αδελφικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>brotherly, fraternal</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αδελφική</b> αγάπη - brotherly love</div><b>αδελφικότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αδελφικότητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. brotherliness, sisterliness</div>
  <div class='def'>2. fraternity (the relationship)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αδελφικός + -ότητα. First attested 1893.</div><b>αδελφογαμία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) adelphogamy</div><b>αδελφοκτονία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) fratricide (killing of one&#x27;s brother)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) sororicide (killing of one&#x27;s sister)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀδελφοκτονία. By surface analysis, αδελφός + -κτονία.</div><b>αδελφοκτόνος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδελφοκτόνα, neuter αδελφοκτόνο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. fratricidal</div>
  <div class='def'>2. sororicidal</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀδελφοκτόνος. By surface analysis, ἀδελφός + κτόνος</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural αδελφοκτόνοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. brother killer, fratricide (the person)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. sister killer, sororicide (the person)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀδελφοκτόνος. By surface analysis, ἀδελφός + κτόνος</div><b>αδελφομάνα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αδελφομάνες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial, derogatory, sometimes) fag hag (woman who enjoys the company of gay men)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η Φωφώ είναι <b>αδελφομάνα</b>, διότι όλοι οι φίλοι της είναι γκέι. - Fofo is a fag hag, since all her friends are gay.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αδελφή + μάνα.</div><b>αδελφομίκτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αδελφομίκτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>incestuous person</div><b>αδελφομιξία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) incest between siblings</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From ἀδελφός + μίξις.</div><b>αδελφοποίηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αδελφοποιήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. fraternisation (UK), fraternization (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. twinning</div><b>αδελφοποιία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αδελφοποιίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fraternisation (UK), fraternization (US)</div><b>αδελφοποιτός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αδελφοποιτοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(dated) blood brother or a close friend</div>
  <div class='ex'>(folksy)</div><b>αδελφοσύνη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) brotherhood, brotherly love (the relationship between siblings)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) brotherhood (the love between friends)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (uncountable) brotherhood, confraternity (organisation)</div><b>αδελφωμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αδελφωμένη, neuter αδελφωμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fraternised (UK), fraternized (USA)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αδελφώνομαι, passive voice of αδελφώνω (“fraternise”).</div><b>αδελφός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αδελφοί, feminine αδελφή)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. brother</div>
  <div class='def'>2. monk</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀδελφός; from Proto-Hellenic *hə- (“same, together”) from Proto-Indo-European *sm̥- (“together, one”) + *gʷelbʰ- (“womb”), equivalent to ἁ- (ha-, “same”, copulative prefix) + δελφύς.</div><b>αδελφότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αδελφότητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. brotherhood, fellowship (the love of friends and/or brothers)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. brotherhood, fellowship, fraternity, sodality (the organisation or institution)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀδελφότης, equivalent to αδελφός + -ότητα.</div><b>αδελφώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to fraternise (UK), fraternize (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to reconcile</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to tiller (to produce multiple stems)</div><b>αδεμάτιαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδεμάτιαστη, neuter αδεμάτιαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unbundled, unbunched</div>
  <div class='def'>2. not sheaved, not gathered into sheafs (cereal crops)</div><b>αδενίτιδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αδενίτιδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>adenitis</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from French adénite.</div><b>αδενικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδενική, neuter αδενικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>glandular</div><b>αδενοειδής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδενοειδής, neuter αδενοειδές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>adenoid, glandular</div><b>αδενοπάθεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) glandular fever</div><b>αδενωματώδης</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>adenomatous</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αδένωμα + -ώδης.</div><b>αδεξιότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) clumsiness</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) tactlessness</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αδέξιος + -ότητα. First attested 1859.</div><b>αδερφάκι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αδερφάκια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of αδελφάκι</div><b>αδερφάτο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αδερφάτα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αδελφάτο">αδελφάτο</a></div><b>αδερφή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αδερφές or αδερφάδες, masculine αδερφός)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αδελφή">αδελφή</a></div><b>αδερφικά</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αδελφικά">αδελφικά</a></div><b>αδερφικάτα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. fraternally</div>
  <div class='def'>2. in a sisterly or brotherly manner.</div><b>αδερφικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδερφική, neuter αδερφικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αδελφικός">αδελφικός</a></div><b>αδερφικότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αδερφικότητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αδελφικότητα">αδελφικότητα</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αδερφικός + -ότητα. First attested 1893.</div><b>αδερφομεράδι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αδερφομεράδια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αδερφομοιράδι">αδερφομοιράδι</a></div><b>αδερφομοίρι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αδερφομοίρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial) brother&#x27;s share (of family inheritance)</div><b>αδερφομοιράδι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αδερφομοιράδια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial) brother&#x27;s share (of family inheritance)</div><b>αδερφοποίηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αδερφοποιήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αδελφοποίηση">αδελφοποίηση</a></div><b>αδερφοποιτός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αδερφοποιτοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>blood brother, spiritual brother</div><b>αδερφοσύνη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αδελφοσύνη">αδελφοσύνη</a></div><b>αδερφωμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αδερφωμένη, neuter αδερφωμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>a less formal variant of <a href="bword://αδελφωμένος">αδελφωμένος</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αδερφώνομαι, passive voice of αδερφώνω (“fraternise”), variant of αδελφώνω.</div><b>αδερφός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αδερφοί, feminine αδερφή)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αδελφός">αδελφός</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀδελφός.</div><b>αδερφώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αδελφώνω">αδελφώνω</a></div><b>αδηλητηρίαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδηλητηρίαστη, neuter αδηλητηρίαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unpoisoned</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ήθελε να βεβαιωθεί ότι το φαγητό του ήταν <b>αδηλητηρίαστο</b>. - He made sure that his food was not poisoned.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) unbitter</div><b>αδημιούργητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδημιούργητη, neuter αδημιούργητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not created, uncreated, not made</div><b>αδημονία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) impatience, anxiety</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀδημονία.</div><b>αδημονώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to fret, be impatient</div><b>αδημοσίευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδημοσίευτη, neuter αδημοσίευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unpublished</div><b>αδηφάγος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδηφάγος or αδηφάγα, neuter αδηφάγο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. greedy</div>
  <div class='def'>2. gluttonous, voracious</div>
  <div class='def'>3. insatiable</div><b>αδηφαγία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αδηφαγίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) gluttony, greed</div><b>αδιάβαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάβαστη, neuter αδιάβαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unread (book, paper, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unstudied (course, subject, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. unreadable, illegible</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (figuratively) buried without a priest (not read over)</div><b>αδιάβατος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάβατη, neuter αδιάβατο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>impassable, pathless</div><b>αδιάβλητο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) impartiality, fairness</div><b>αδιάβλητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάβλητη, neuter αδιάβλητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>impeccable, fair, unimpeachable, impartial</div><b>αδιάβροχο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αδιάβροχα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>raincoat, mackintosh, mac</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://αδιάβροχος">αδιάβροχος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://αδιάβροχος">αδιάβροχος</a></div><b>αδιάβροχος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάβροχη, neuter αδιάβροχο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>waterproof</div>
  <div class='ex'>αδιάβροχο μπουφάν (waterproof jacket)</div><b>αδιάβρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάβρωτη, neuter αδιάβρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>uncorroded</div><b>αδιάγνωστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάγνωστη, neuter αδιάγνωστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>undiagnosed</div><b>αδιάζευκτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάζευκτη, neuter αδιάζευκτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>undivorced, not divorced</div><b>αδιάθετος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάθετη, neuter αδιάθετο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unwell, indisposed, off-colour</div>
  <div class='def'>2. menstruating</div>
  <div class='def'>3. unsold</div>
  <div class='def'>4. unused</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀδιάθετος”). The &quot;ill, unwell&quot; sense is a semantic loan from French indisposé.</div><b>αδιάκοπος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάκοπη, neuter αδιάκοπο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. constant</div>
  <div class='def'>2. without interruption, uninterrupted, continuous</div>
  <div class='def'>3. perpetual</div><b>αδιάκριτα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>indiscreetly, tactlessly</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αδιάκριτος">αδιάκριτος</a></div><b>αδιάκριτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάκριτη, neuter αδιάκριτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>indiscreet (not discreet; wanting in discretion)</div><b>αδιάλειπτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάλειπτη, neuter αδιάλειπτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>incessant, continuous</div><b>αδιάλλακτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάλλακτη, neuter αδιάλλακτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>intransigent, adamant, unreconciled, irreconcilable</div><b>αδιάλλαχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάλλαχτή, neuter αδιάλλαχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αδιάλλακτος">αδιάλλακτος</a></div><b>αδιάλυτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάλυτη, neuter αδιάλυτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. insoluble, undissolvable, not dissolvable (will not dissolve in a solvent)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. indissoluble, undissolvable (of marriage)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. not broken up</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (figuratively) inscrutable</div><b>αδιάντροπος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάντροπη, neuter αδιάντροπο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>shameless, barefaced, without modesty</div><b>αδιάνυτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάνυτη, neuter αδιάνυτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>untravelled, not covered (distance)</div><b>αδιάπλαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάπλαστη, neuter αδιάπλαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>undeveloped</div><b>αδιάπλευστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάπλευστη, neuter αδιάπλευστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unnavigable</div><b>αδιάπτωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάπτωτη, neuter αδιάπτωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unfailing, unflagging, sustained, undiminished, unabated</div>
  <div class='def'>2. constant, unchanging, changeless</div><b>αδιάρρηκτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάρρηκτη, neuter αδιάρρηκτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unbreakable</div>
  <div class='ex'>αδιάρρηκτοι δεσμοί φιλίας (unbreakable bonds of friendship)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. intact, unbroken</div><b>αδιάσειστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάσειστη, neuter αδιάσειστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>irrefutable, undeniable</div><b>αδιάσπαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάσπαστη, neuter αδιάσπαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unbreakable, unbroken</div>
  <div class='def'>2. indissoluble</div><b>αδιάφθορος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάφθορη, neuter αδιάφθορο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. chaste, untouchable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. incorruptible, uncorrupted, unbribed</div>
  <div class='def'>3. whole, pristine, undamaged, undecayed</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αδιάφθοροι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>untouchable, incorruptible (law enforcer)</div><b>αδιάφορος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάφορη, neuter αδιάφορο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. indifferent (not interested, not caring)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Αυτός ο μαθητής είναι τελείως <b>αδιάφορος</b>. Δεν προσέχει καθόλου στο μάθημα. - This student is totally indifferent. He pays no attention whatseoever at lessons.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. uninteresting</div>
  <div class='ex'>Τα μαθήματα του καθηγητή Χ είναι <b>αδιάφορα</b>, δεν έχουν κανένα ενδιαφέρον. - Lessons by professor X are entirely uninteresting, they are of no interest at all.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. of no importance</div>
  <div class='ex'>μου είναι <b>αδιάφορο</b>, σου είναι <b>αδιάφορα</b>, ... - it is of no interest to me, they are of no interest to you, ...</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀδιάφορος, ancient sense: &quot;not different&quot;. By surface analysis, α- privative (a- privative) + διάφορος.</div><b>αδιάψευστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιάψευστη, neuter αδιάψευστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>indisputable, undeniable, irrefutable</div><b>αδιέξοδο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αδιέξοδα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. dead-end, cul-de-sac</div>
  <div class='def'>2. impasse, deadlock, stalemate</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://αδιέξοδος">αδιέξοδος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://αδιέξοδος">αδιέξοδος</a></div><b>αδιέξοδος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιέξοδη, neuter αδιέξοδο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. dead-end, with no exit</div>
  <div class='def'>2. stalemate</div><b>αδιήγητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιήγητη, neuter αδιήγητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>undescribable, untold, unspeakable</div><b>αδιήθητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιήθητη, neuter αδιήθητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unfiltered</div><b>αδιαίρετος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιαίρετη, neuter αδιαίρετο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. indivisible</div>
  <div class='def'>2. undivided</div>
  <div class='def'>3. atom</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> 4th century BC (Aristotle) Ancient Greek ἀδιαίρετος, from ἀ- (a-) + διαιρετός, the latter from δι- (di-) + αἱρέω + -τος (-tos).</div><b>αδιαβίβαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιαβίβαστη, neuter αδιαβίβαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>untransmitted</div><b>αδιαβατικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιαβατική, neuter αδιαβατικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>adiabatic</div><b>αδιαβροχοποιώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to waterproof</div><b>αδιαγούμητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιαγούμητη, neuter αδιαγούμητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αδιαγούμιστος">αδιαγούμιστος</a></div><b>αδιαγούμιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιαγούμιστη, neuter αδιαγούμιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unlooted, unplundered</div><b>αδιαθεσία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αδιαθεσίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>indisposition, malaise</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned formation from αδιάθε(τος), “indisposed”) + -σία, formed as a calque of French indisposition.</div><b>αδιαθετώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to be slightly unwell, be out of sorts, feel faint</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to menstruate, have a period</div><b>αδιαιρετότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) indivisibility</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αδιαίρετος + -ότητα. First attested 1786.</div><b>αδιακανόνιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιακανόνιστη, neuter αδιακανόνιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unpaid, unsettled (debt, bill, account, etc)</div><b>αδιακρίτως</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>indiscriminately</div><b>αδιακρισία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) indiscretion, a tactless or an indiscrete act</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) tactlessness, lack of discretion</div><b>αδιακόρευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδιακόρευτη, neuter αδιακόρευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unviolated</div><b>αδιακόσμητος</b>
