  <div class='def'>spindle (a rod used for spinning and then winding fibres)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek αδράχτι, from Koine Greek ἀδράκτιον, a diminutive of Ancient Greek ἄδρακτος, from Ancient Greek ἄτρακτος.
Compare Mariupol Greek дърахт.</div><b>αδρανής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδρανής, neuter αδρανές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. inactive, inert, sluggish</div>
