  <div class='def'>inactivated</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αδρανοποιούμαι, passive voice of αδρανοποιώ (“inactivate”).</div><b>αδρανοποιούμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be inactive</div><b>αδρανοποιώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to inactivate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to power down</div><b>αδρανώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be dormant, be inert, be inactivate, vegetate</div><b>αδρεναλίνη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) adrenaline (epinephrine, the hormone and neurotransmitter)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from French adrénaline. Suffix -ίνη.</div><b>αδριανή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αδριανές)</i></div>
