  <div class='def'>exceptionally large wage, salary or fee</div><b>αδροπληρώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to overpay, pay handsomely</div><b>αδρόμισθος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδρόμισθη, neuter αδρόμισθο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>exceptionally well paid</div><b>αδρός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδρή or αδρά, neuter αδρό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. ample, handsome, generous (of fee, money)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. broad, sizeable</div>
  <div class='def'>3. rugged, rough</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἁδρός.</div><b>αδρόσιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδρόσιστη, neuter αδρόσιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unrefreshed</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) unhappy</div><b>αδρότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αδρότητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>vigour (UK), vigor (US), strength, ruggedness</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἁδρότης, equivalent to αδρός + -ότητα.</div><b>αδυνάστευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδυνάστευτη, neuter αδυνάστευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. untyrannical, undomineering</div>
  <div class='def'>2. not domineered</div><b>αδυνάτισμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αδυνατίσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>slimming, weight loss</div><b>αδυναμία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αδυναμίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. weakness, inadequacy</div>
  <div class='def'>2. inability</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) soft spot, weakness</div><b>αδυνατίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to lose weight, become thin</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to weaken</div><b>αδυνατισμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αδυνατισμένη, neuter αδυνατισμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>emaciated, gaunt, weakened</div>
  <div class='ex'>also see αποστεωμένος (aposteoménos), αποσκελετωμένος (aposkeletoménos), κάτισχνος (kátischnos)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect passive participle of αδυνατίζω, a verb with no passive forms.</div><b>αδυνατιστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδυνατιστική, neuter αδυνατιστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>slimming, causing weight loss</div><b>αδυνατώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be incapable, be unable, be weak</div><b>αδυσώπητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδυσώπητη, neuter αδυσώπητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. implacable, inexorable, relentless</div>
  <div class='def'>2. harsh, fierce</div><b>αδωροδόκητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδωροδόκητη, neuter αδωροδόκητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unbribed</div><b>αδόκητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδόκητη, neuter αδόκητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unexpected, unforeseen</div>
  <div class='def'>2. sudden</div><b>αδόκιμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδόκιμη, neuter αδόκιμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unidiomatic</div>
  <div class='def'>2. inappropriate, indifferent, mediocre</div><b>αδόλωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδόλωτη, neuter αδόλωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unbaited</div><b>αδόνητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδόνητη, neuter αδόνητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unshaken, not vibrated</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unmoved, unshaken</div><b>αδόξαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδόξαστη, neuter αδόξαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unhonoured, unsung</div><b>αδύναμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδύναμη, neuter αδύναμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. weak, feeble (bodily, politically, economically, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. weak, pale (colour)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀδύναμος, from ἀ- (a-) + δύναμις.</div><b>αδύνατος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδύνατη, neuter αδύνατο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. weak, poor (health)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ο άνθρωπος έχει μια <b>αδύνατη</b> καρδιά. - The man has a weak heart.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. weak, poor (knowledge)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Αυτός ο μαθητής είναι <b>αδύνατος</b>. - This pupil is weak.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. weak, regular</div>
  <div class='ex'>Οι <b>αδύνατοι</b> τύποι της προσωπικής αντωνυμίας … - The weak forms of the personal pronoun …</div>
  <div class='def'>4. thin</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ο πελαργός έχει <b>αδύνατα</b> πόδια. - The stork has thin legs.</div>
  <div class='def'>5. impossible, unattainable</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η αδύνατη αποστολή. - The impossible mission.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ᾰ̓δῠ́νᾰτος. By surface analysis, α- (a-) + δυνατός.</div><b>αδώρητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αδώρητη, neuter αδώρητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. undonated</div>
  <div class='def'>2. not donatable</div><b>αε.</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://αρχαιοελληνικός">αρχαιοελληνικός</a>: related to Ancient Greece and its people</div><b>αεί</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>always, evermore, forever</div>
  <div class='ex'>ες <b>αεί</b> - for ever</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀεί.</div><b>αείμνηστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αείμνηστη, neuter αείμνηστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unforgotten, late lamented (of the dead)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀείμνηστος. By surface analysis, αεί- + μνηστός.</div><b>αείποτε</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>always</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αεί + ποτέ.</div><b>αειθαλής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αειθαλής, neuter αειθαλές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. evergreen (of plant which keeps its leaves)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) fresh, lively and young looking (of old person)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀειθαλής. By surface analysis, αει- (aei-, “ever”) + θάλλω.</div><b>αεικίνητο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αεικίνητα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>perpetual motion</div>
  <div class='ex'>Older form: ἀεικίνητον (aeikínēton) (Katharevousa)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Substantivised neuter singular of αεικίνητος &lt; Ancient Greek ἀεικίνητος, Semantic loan from New Latin perpetuum mobile.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://αεικίνητος">αεικίνητος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://αεικίνητος">αεικίνητος</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inflectional forms.</div><b>αεικίνητον</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Katharevousa form of <a href="bword://αεικίνητο">αεικίνητο</a></div><b>αεικίνητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αεικίνητη, neuter αεικίνητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>restless, energetic</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αει- (aei-, “ever”) + κινητός</div><b>αειφορία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) sustainability</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ᾱ̓εί + φέρω.</div><b>αειφόρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αειφόρα or αειφόρος, neuter αειφόρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sustainable</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αειφόρος</b> ανάπτυξη - sustainable development</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αει- (aei-, “ever”) + -φόρος</div><b>αενάως</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Katharevousa form of <a href="bword://αέναα">αέναα</a></div><b>αεράγημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αεραγήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>group of airborne troops, airborne detachment</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αερ- (aer-, “air”) + άγημα</div><b>αεράθλημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αεραθλήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>air sport</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αερ- (aer-, “air”) + άθλημα</div><b>αεράμυνα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) air defence (UK), air defense (US)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αερ- (aer-, “air”) + άμυνα</div><b>αεράτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αεράτη, neuter αεράτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. airy, open to the air (of a situation, room, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. graceful</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) breezy, airy (of someone&#x27;s manner)</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (figuratively) easygoing, cocky (of someone&#x27;s manner)</div><b>αερίζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to fart, break wind, blow off</div><b>αερίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>I ventilate, air, aerate</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀερίζω from ἀέρ(ας), “wind”) + -ίζω. Hellenistic sense of the verb: &quot;be thin as air&quot;.</div><b>αεραγωγός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αεραγωγοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>air-duct</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αερ- (aer-, “air”) + αγωγός</div><b>αεραθλητικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αεραθλητική, neuter αεραθλητικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>relating to air sport</div><b>αεραντλία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αεραντλίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>air-pump</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αερ- (aer-, “air”) + αντλία</div><b>αερασκός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αερασκοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(rare) airbag</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αερ- (aer-, “air”) + ασκός</div><b>αεργία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) inactivity, unemployment, idleness</div><b>αεριαγωγός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αεριαγωγοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>air duct</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αέρι + αγωγός</div><b>αερικό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αερικά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. sprite, pixie, elf, fairy, ethereal spirit</div>
  <div class='def'>2. demon (causing madness)</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://αερικός">αερικός</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://αερικός">αερικός</a></div><b>αερικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αερική, neuter αερικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>airy, well ventilated</div><b>αεριολογία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αεριολογίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>aerology</div><b>αεριοποίηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) gasification</div><b>αεριοποιώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to aerate, gasify</div><b>αεριοπροώθηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) jet propulsion</div><b>αεριοστροβιλωθητήρας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>jet engine</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αεριοστρόβιλος + ωθώ + -τήρας.</div><b>αεριοστρόβιλος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αεριοστρόβιλοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>gas turbine</div><b>αεριούχος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αεριούχος, neuter αεριούχο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>aerated, fizzy</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αεριούχο</b> νερό - fizzy water</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αέριο + -ούχος.</div><b>αερισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αερισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. ventilation, airing, aeration</div>
  <div class='def'>2. ventilation (mechanical)</div><b>αεριστήρας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αεριστήρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. aerator</div>
  <div class='def'>2. ventilator, fan</div><b>αεριτζής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αεριτζήδες, feminine αεριτζού)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. spiv, crook, black marketeer</div>
  <div class='def'>2. someone who playing in crooked gambling in order to tempt others in</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αέρας + -τζής.</div><b>αεριτζίδικος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αεριτζίδικη, neuter αεριτζίδικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>spivish, crooked</div><b>αεριωθούμενο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αεριωθούμενα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>jet, jet aircraft, jet aeroplane, jet airplane</div><b>αεριωθούμενος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αεριωθούμενη, neuter αεριωθούμενο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>jet propelled</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αέριος + ωθούμενος from ωθώ</div><b>αεριόφως</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) gaslight</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly, uncountable) gas, coal gas, town gas</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αεριό- + φως (fos) Calque of English gaslight</div><b>αεριώδης</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αεριώδης, neuter αεριώδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>gaseous</div><b>αεριώθηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αεριωθήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>jet propulsion</div><b>αεροβάμων</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αεροβάμων, neuter αεροβάμον)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(figuratively) fantasizing, daydreaming</div><b>αεροβάτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αεροβάτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. daydreamer, fantasist</div>
  <div class='def'>2. visionary</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀεροβάτης. By surface analysis, αερο (aero, “air”) + βάτης.</div><b>αεροβίωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) aerobics</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) aerobiosis</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From French aérobiose.</div><b>αεροβασία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αεροβασίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. daydream, fantasy</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (literally) a walk in the air</div><b>αεροβατώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to daydream, have one&#x27;s head in the clouds, build castles in the air</div><b>αεροβικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αεροβική, neuter αεροβικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>aerobic (used with exercises, etc)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αεροβική</b> γυμναστική - aerobic exercise</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From English aerobic.</div><b>αεροβόλο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αεροβόλα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>air gun</div><b>αερογέφυρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αερογέφυρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. airlift</div>
  <div class='ex'>η <b>αερογέφυρα</b> του Βερολίνου - the Berlin Airlift</div>
  <div class='def'>2. viaduct</div><b>αερογεφύρωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αερογεφυρώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>airhead</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αερο- (aero-, “air”) + γέφυρα + -ωμα (-oma).</div><b>αερογραμμή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αερογραμμές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. air route</div>
  <div class='def'>2. airline, airways</div><b>αεροδίνη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αεροδίνες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>dust devil (formal term)</div><b>αεροδίνητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αεροδίνητη, neuter αεροδίνητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>swirling (air)</div><b>αεροδιάδρομος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αεροδιάδρομοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>air corridor, air lane</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αερο- (aero-, “air”) + διάδρομος</div><b>αεροδιάστημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αεροδιαστήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) aerospace</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> By surface analysis, αερο- (aero-, “aero-, air”) + διάστημα.</div><b>αεροδιαστημικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αεροδιαστημική, neuter αεροδιαστημικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>aerospatial, related to aerospace</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αεροδιάστημα + -ικός.</div><b>αεροδικείο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αεροδικεία)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>airforce court martial</div><b>αεροδρομικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αεροδρομική, neuter αεροδρομικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>airport (referring to)</div>
  <div class='ex'>το <b>αεροδρομικό</b> μουσείο - the airport museum</div><b>αεροδρόμιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αεροδρόμια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>airport, aerodrome</div>
  <div class='ex'>Τα νησιά έχουν <b>αεροδρόμια</b>, μικρότερα από τον διεθνή αερολιμένα της πρωτεύουσας. - Islands have airports, smaller than the international airport of the capital.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from French aérodrome from ἀήρ, αερο- (aero-) + δρόμος. Different sense of the ancient ἀεροδρόμος.</div><b>αεροδυναμική</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) aerodynamics</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative feminine singular of <a href="bword://αεροδυναμικός">αεροδυναμικός</a></div><b>αεροδυναμικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αεροδυναμική, neuter αεροδυναμικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>aerodynamic</div><b>αεροελέγκτρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αεροελέγκτριες, masculine αεροελεγκτής)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>air traffic controller</div><b>αεροελεγκτής</b>
