  <div class='def'>eagle-eyed, sharp-eyed</div><b>αετονύχης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αετονύχηδες, feminine αετονύχισσα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. sharp operator, cunning cheat</div>
  <div class='def'>2. grasping person</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αετός + νύχι.</div><b>αετονύχισσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αετονύχισσες, masculine αετονύχης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sharp operator, cunning cheat</div><b>αετοράχη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αετοράχες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>steep mountain</div><b>αετοφωλιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αετοφωλιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>eyrie, eagle&#x27;s nest</div><b>αετόπουλο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αετόπουλα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>eaglet</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αετός + -πουλο (-poulo)</div><b>αετός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αετοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. eagle; kite (toy)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) eagle; a clever resourceful person</div>
  <div class='ex'>see: έξυπνος (éxypnos, “intelligent”)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. eagle ray</div>
  <div class='ex'>usually in the form αϊτός (aïtós)</div>
  <div class='def'>4. for the constellation see <a href="bword://Αετός">Αετός</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀετός.</div><b>αζάρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αζάρωτη, neuter αζάρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unwrinkled, wrinkle-free, smooth</div><b>αζήλευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αζήλευτη, neuter αζήλευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unenviable, unenvious</div><b>αζήμιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αζήμια, neuter αζήμιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>harmless</div><b>αζήτητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. something unwanted, undesired, unidentified</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unclaimed luggage</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αζήτητος">αζήτητος</a></div><b>αζήτητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αζήτητη, neuter αζήτητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unclaimed, undemanded, not in demand</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unsought, unlooked-for</div><b>αζαλέα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αζαλέες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>azalea</div><b>αζεμάτιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αζεμάτιστη, neuter αζεμάτιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unscalded, unblanched, unbasted</div><b>αζεριανά</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Azerbaijani, Azeri (the language of Azerbaijan and its people)</div><b>αζερικά</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Azerbaijani, Azeri (the language of Azerbaijan and its people)</div><b>αζερικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αζερική, neuter αζερικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Azerbaijani (relating to Azerbaijan or its people or language)</div><b>αζευγάριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αζευγάρωτη, neuter αζευγάρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unploughed (UK), unplowed (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unpaired, uncoupled, unyoked</div><b>αζευγάρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αζευγάρωτη, neuter αζευγάρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unpaired</div>
  <div class='def'>2. uncoupled</div>
  <div class='def'>3. unploughed (UK), unplowed (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>4. unmated, without a mate</div><b>αζημίωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αζημίωτη, neuter αζημίωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>without loss, lossless</div><b>αζιμούθιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) azimuth</div><b>αζουλένιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (usually uncountable, plural αζουλένια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) azulene</div><b>αζουρίτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αζουρίτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>azurite</div><b>αζούρ</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(indeclinable) openwork, cutwork</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from French ajour.</div><b>αζωγράφιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αζωγράφιστη, neuter αζωγράφιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unpainted (portrait not painted)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. undecorated (surface unadorned with painting)</div><b>αζωθαιμία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αζωθαιμίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>azotemia</div><b>αζωικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αζωική, neuter αζωικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>azoic</div><b>αζωτοδέσμευση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) nitrogen fixation</div>
  <div class='ex'>ατμοσφαιρική <b>αζωτοδέσμευση</b> - atmospheric (lightning-induced) nitrogen fixation</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From άζωτο + δέσμευση.</div><b>αζωτούχος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αζωτούζος, neuter αζωτούζο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nitrogenous</div><b>αζωϊκός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αζωϊκή, neuter αζωϊκό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αζωικός">αζωικός</a></div><b>αζύγιαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αζύγιαστη, neuter αζύγιαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αζύγιστος">αζύγιστος</a></div><b>αζύγιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αζύγιστη, neuter αζύγιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unweighed, untared</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) unconsidered</div><b>αζύμωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αζύμωτη, neuter αζύμωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unkneaded</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unfermented</div><b>αηδής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αηδής, neuter αηδές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(formal) disgusting, revolting, sickening, nauseating</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀηδής, from ἀ- (a-, “a-, un-”) + ἡδύς.</div><b>αηδία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αηδίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. disgust, revulsion, distaste (intense dislike or loathing someone feels for something bad or nasty)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Σβήσ’ την τηλεόραση – αυτός ο δημοσιογράφος μου προκαλεί <b>αηδία</b>! - Turn off the TV – that reporter makes me sick!</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively, in plural) nonsense, rubbish, trash, crap, bull, shit (words, actions, etc of no meaning)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Όλο κάθεται και λέει <b>αηδίες</b>. - All he does is sit and talk crap.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀηδία, from ἀηδής, from ἀ- (a-, “a-, un-”) + ἡδύς.</div><b>αηδιάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (transitive) to disgust, revolt, sicken, nauseate</div>
  <div class='ex'>Μ’ <b>αηδιάζει</b> η μυρωδιά του τόνου. - The smell of tuna disgusts me.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (intransitive) to be revolted, be disgusted, be sickened, be nauseated</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Αηδιάσαμε</b> από το θέαμα. - We were disgusted by the sight.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αηδία f.</div><b>αηδιασμένα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>in disgusted manner, disgustedly</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αηδιασμένος">αηδιασμένος</a></div><b>αηδιασμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αηδιασμένη, neuter αηδιασμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disgusted, repelled, revolted</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Passive perfect participle of αηδιάζω (a verb with active forms only).</div><b>αηδιαστικά</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. nominative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αηδιαστικός">αηδιαστικός</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. accusative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αηδιαστικός">αηδιαστικός</a></div>
  <div class='def'>3. vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αηδιαστικός">αηδιαστικός</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disgustingly, revoltingly, nauseatingly</div>
  <div class='ex'>Είναι <b>αηδιαστικά</b> τσιγκούνης. - He&#x27;s disgustingly miserly.</div><b>αηδιαστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αηδιαστική, neuter αηδιαστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disgusting, repulsive, revolting, sickening, nauseating (causing intense dislike)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Τι <b>αηδιαστικός</b> άνθρωπος! - What a disgusting person!</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αηδία f. First attested 1886.</div><b>αηδονολαλιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αηδονολαλιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. nightingale&#x27;s voice, nightingale&#x27;s song</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) a singing voice like a nightingale</div><b>αηδονολαλώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to sing sweetly, like a nightingale</div><b>αηδονοφωλιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αηδονοφωλιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nightingale&#x27;s nest</div><b>αηδόνα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αηδόνες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. female nightingale</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) woman with fine singing voice</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀηδόνα m, from ἀηδόν(ι) n) + augmentative -α (-a). From Ancient Greek ἀηδών, with stem ἀηδον-.</div><b>αηδόνι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αηδόνια, feminine αηδόνα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nightingale (Luscinia megarhynchos)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Byzantine Greek ἀηδόνι, from Koine Greek ἀηδόνιον n, from Ancient Greek ἀηδών f with stem ἀηδον-.</div><b>αηδόνισμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αηδονίσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nightingale&#x27;s song</div><b>αηδών</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Katharevousa form of <a href="bword://αηδόνι">αηδόνι</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀηδών.</div><b>αηδώς</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(formal) disgustingly, revoltingly, nauseatingly</div><b>αητομάτης</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αητομάτα, neuter αητομάτικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>hawk-eyed, sharp-eyed</div><b>αηχοποίηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αηχοποιήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>devoicing</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> άηχος + -ποίηση.</div><b>αθάλη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αιθάλη">αιθάλη</a></div><b>αθάμπωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αθάμπωτη, neuter αθάμπωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>undazzled, unblurred (of clear vision)</div><b>αθάνατος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αθάνατη, neuter αθάνατο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>immortal</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀθάνατος.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αθάνατοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. immortal</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (in plural) (the) immortals, (the) gods</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀθάνατος.</div><b>αθάρρετος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αθάρρετη, neuter αθάρρετο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αθάρρευτος">αθάρρευτος</a></div><b>αθάρρευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αθάρρευτη, neuter αθάρρευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>timid, shy</div><b>αθέατος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αθέατη, neuter αθέατο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>invisible, out of sight, secret, unseen</div>
  <div class='ex'>η αθέατη πλευρά της Σελήνης (the unseen side of the moon)</div><b>αθέλητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αθέλητη, neuter αθέλητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unintentional, unwilling, inadvertent</div><b>αθέμιτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αθέμιτη, neuter αθέμιτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. against established social custom, immoral, unfair</div>
  <div class='def'>2. illegal, unlawful</div><b>αθέρας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) awn (of wheat, barley, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) husk (of wheat, barley, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (uncountable) cutting edge (of blade)</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (figuratively, uncountable) acme, cream, best part</div>
  <div class='def'>5. (figuratively, uncountable) cutting edge, groundbreaking</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀθήρ.</div><b>αθέριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αθέριστη, neuter αθέριστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unreaped, unmown, standing</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From α- (a-, “un-”) + θερίζω.</div><b>αθέρμαντος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αθέρμαντη, neuter αθέρμαντο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unheated</div><b>αθέσπιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αθέσπιστη, neuter αθέσπιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not legislated, unenacted</div><b>αθέτηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αθετήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. breach, breaking of faith</div>
  <div class='def'>2. trespass</div><b>αθήλαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αθήλαστη, neuter αθήλαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unsuckled, unfed</div><b>αθήρ</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>awn (of wheat, barley, etc)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀθήρ.</div><b>αθήρωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αθηρώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>atheroma</div><b>αθίγγανος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αθίγγανοι, feminine αθίγγανη or αθιγγανίδα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://Αθίγγανος">Αθίγγανος</a></div><b>αθανασία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) immortality</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀθανασία.</div><b>αθανατίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to immortalise (UK), immortalize (US)</div><b>αθεΐα</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>atheism</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀθεΐᾱ from ancient ἄθεος. See άθεος.</div><b>αθεΐζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to become an atheist</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to become atheistic, tend towards atheism</div><b>αθεΐστρια</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>atheist</div><b>αθεάτριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αθεάτριστη, neuter αθεάτριστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not theatregoing, ignorant of the theatre, untheatrical</div><b>αθειάφιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αθειάφιστη, neuter αθειάφιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unsprayed, undusted</div><b>αθεμέλιωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αθεμέλιωτη, neuter αθεμέλιωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αθεμελίωτος">αθεμελίωτος</a></div><b>αθεμελίωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αθεμελίωτη, neuter αθεμελίωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. without foundation (of a building)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) without foundation, unfounded, unwarranted</div><b>αθεράπευτα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. incurably</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) incurably, hopelessly</div>
  <div class='ex'>Είναι <b>αθεράπευτα</b> αισιόδοξος. - He is incurably optimistic.</div><b>αθεράπευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αθεράπευτη, neuter αθεράπευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. incurable, cureless</div>
  <div class='def'>2. uncured</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) incurable, confirmed, hopeless</div><b>αθερίνα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αθερίνες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>smelt, Mediterranean sand smelt (Atherina hepsetus, Atherina boyeri)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀθερίνα. From Ancient Greek ἀθερῑ́νη + the suffix -α (-a).</div><b>αθεσμοθέτητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αθεσμοθέτητη, neuter αθεσμοθέτητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not legislated, unenacted</div><b>αθετώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to violate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to break your word, break trust</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to renege, go back on</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀθετῶ, contracted form of ἀθετέω, from adjective ἄθετος, from ἀ- (a-) privative + θετός. and the ancient τίθημι.)</div><b>αθεϊσμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>atheism</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From French athéisme &lt; athé(e) from Ancient Greek ἄθεος.</div><b>αθεϊστής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αθεϊστές, feminine αθεΐστρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>atheist</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From French athéiste.</div><b>αθεϊστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αθεϊστική, neuter αθεϊστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>atheistic</div><b>αθεόφοβος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αθεόφοβη, neuter αθεόφοβο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. impious, ungodly</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (noun) unholy person, rogue</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From α- (a-, “not”) + θεός + φόβος.</div><b>αθεώρητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αθεώρητη, neuter αθεώρητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unauthorised (UK), unauthorized (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unvalidated, unstamped, without a visa</div>
  <div class='def'>3. not officially examined</div><b>αθηλύκωτος</b>
