  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αιτία + -κρατία, calque of New Latin determinismus. Compare to the synonym ντετερμινισμός, a loanword of German Determinismus.</div><b>αιτιοκρατικά</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>deterministically</div><b>αιτιοκρατικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αιτιοκρατική, neuter αιτιοκρατικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>deterministic</div><b>αιτιολ.</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://αιτιολογικός">αιτιολογικός</a>: aetiological (UK), etiological (US)</div><b>αιτιολογία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αιτιολογίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. excuse</div>
  <div class='def'>2. aetiology (UK), etiology (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. explanation</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek αἰτιολογίᾱ. By surface analysis, αιτία + -λογία</div><b>αιτιολογικό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αιτιολογικά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>grounds, reason, explanation</div><b>αιτιολογικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αιτιολογική, neuter αιτιολογικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. aetiological (UK), etiological (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. explanatory, causative</div><b>αιτιολογώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to justify</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to rationalise, rationalize</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek αἰτιολογῶ, contracted form of αἰτιολογέω.</div><b>αιτιολόγηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αιτιολογήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>justification, rationale</div><b>αιτιοπαθογένεση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αιτιοπαθογενέσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) aetiopathogenesis</div><b>αιτιότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αιτιότητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>causation, causality</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αίτιος + -ότητα, calque of German Kausalität. First attested 1834.</div><b>αιτιώδης</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αιτιώδης, neuter αιτιώδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>causal</div><b>αιτιώμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (transitive) to blame</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (transitive) to justify</div><b>αιτούμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(formal) request, ask by petition, call for</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αιτούμαι</b> βοήθεια - I ask by petition (for) help</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek αἰτοῦμαι, contracted form of αἰτέομαι, mediopassive voice of αἰτέω.</div><b>αιτούσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αιτούσες, masculine αιτών)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(formal) applicant</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>first-person singular simple past of <a href="bword://αιτώ">αιτώ</a></div><b>αιτώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(archaic) chiefly used in the passive <a href="bword://αιτούμαι">αιτούμαι</a>: request petition</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> See the passive αιτούμαι. The rare modern active voice, learned borrowing from Ancient Greek αἰτῶ, contracted form of αἰτέω.</div><b>αιτών</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αιτώνες, feminine αιτούσα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(formal) applicant</div><b>αιφνίδια</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>suddenly</div><b>αιφνίδιος</b>
