  <div class='def'>1. point, spearhead</div>
  <div class='def'>2. tip of nose</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) jibe, barbed comment, banter</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek αἰχμή.</div><b>αιχμαλωσία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αιχμαλωσίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>captivity</div><b>αιχμαλωτίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to capture, take prisoner</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to captivate, fascinate</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η μουσική αυτή <b>αιχμαλωτίζει</b> τον ακροατή. - This music captivates the listener.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek αἰχμαλωτίζω. By surface analysis, αιχμαλωσία + -ίζω.</div><b>αιχμαλωτισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αιχμαλωτισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>captivity</div><b>αιχμηρός</b>
