  <div class='def'>small dinghy, skiff</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀκάτιον, probably a technical loanword from Pre-Greek, but sometimes connected to ἄκρος.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://ακάτιος">ακάτιος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://ακάτιος">ακάτιος</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀκάτιον, probably a technical loanword from Pre-Greek, but sometimes connected to ἄκρος.</div><b>ακάτιον</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
