  <div class='def'>real estate</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ἀκίνητος + περιουσία</div><b>ακίνητο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ακίνητα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>real estate; property or land</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://ακίνητος">ακίνητος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://ακίνητος">ακίνητος</a></div><b>ακίνητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακίνητη, neuter ακίνητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>immobile, motionless, fixed, static, immovable</div><b>ακαίρως</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>at the wrong time, out of time</div><b>ακαβούρντιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαβούρντιστη, neuter ακαβούρντιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unroasted</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) untormented</div><b>ακαγιού</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ακαζού">ακαζού</a></div><b>ακαδημία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ακαδημίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>see <a href="bword://Ακαδημία">Ακαδημία</a></div><b>ακαδημαϊκά</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>academically</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://ακαδημαϊκός">ακαδημαϊκός</a></div><b>ακαδημαϊκός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαδημαϊκή, neuter ακαδημαϊκό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. academic, scholarly</div>
  <div class='def'>2. theoretical (rather than practical)</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural ακαδημαϊκοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>academic (member of an academy, college, or university)</div><b>ακαδημαϊκότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) the property of being academic</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ακαδημαϊκός + -ότητα. First attested 1895.</div><b>ακαδημαϊκώς</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>academically</div><b>ακαδημαϊσμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>academicism (conventional, scholarly, formalism)</div><b>ακαζού</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(indeclinable) mahogany (red-brown colour)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Έβαψε τα μαλλιά της <b>ακαζού</b>. - She dyed hair mahogany.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from Portuguese acaju (“mahogany; cashew”), borrowed from Old Tupi acaju.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (indeclinable) mahogany colour</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (indeclinable, rare) cashew</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from Portuguese acaju (“mahogany; cashew”), borrowed from Old Tupi acaju.</div><b>ακαθάριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαθάριστη, neuter ακαθάριστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unclean, not cleaned, unwashed</div>
  <div class='def'>2. gross</div>
  <div class='def'>3. unweeded, unpeeled, etc</div><b>ακαθέλκυστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαθέλκυστη, neuter ακαθέλκυστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unlaunched</div><b>ακαθίδρυτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαθίδρυτη, neuter ακαθίδρυτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unestablished, not established (authority)</div><b>ακαθαρσία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ακαθαρσίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. impurity, dirt, filth</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (in plural) faeces, excrement</div><b>ακαθιέρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαθιέρωτη, neuter ακαθιέρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not established, unestablished</div><b>ακαθοδήγητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαθοδήγητη, neuter ακαθοδήγητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unguided</div>
  <div class='def'>2. untutored, uninstructed</div><b>ακαθόριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαθόριστη, neuter ακαθόριστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. vague, uncertain, indeterminate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. blurred, amorphous</div>
  <div class='def'>3. indefinable</div><b>ακακία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ακακίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>acacia (shrub or tree)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀκακία. Doublet of γαζία.</div><b>ακακοποίητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακακοποίητη, neuter ακακοποίητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. not interfered with</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unmolested</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) unadulterated</div><b>ακαλίγωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαλίγωτη, neuter ακαλίγωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unshoed, unshod</div><b>ακαλαίσθητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαλαίσθητη, neuter ακαλαίσθητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. tasteless, lacking good taste</div>
  <div class='def'>2. ill-mannered, inelegant</div><b>ακαλαισθησία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) bad taste, absence of aesthetic sense</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) inelegance</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From α- (a-, “un-, in-”) + καλαισθησία.</div><b>ακαλαφάτιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαλαφάτιστη, neuter ακαλαφάτιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. uncaulked, not caulked</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (colloquial, figuratively, vulgar) unfucked</div><b>ακαλλιέργητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαλλιέργητη, neuter ακαλλιέργητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. uncultivated (lacking culture, manners, education, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. uncultivated, fallow</div><b>ακαλλώπιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαλλώπιστη, neuter ακαλλώπιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ill-groomed, not smartened up</div><b>ακαλμάριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαλμάριστη, neuter ακαλμάριστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not calmed, unsoothed</div><b>ακαλόπιαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαλόπιαστη, neuter ακαλόπιαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unpersuadable, not to be cajoled</div><b>ακαμάτευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαμάτευτη, neuter ακαμάτευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>untilled, unploughed (UK), unplowed (US)</div><b>ακαμάτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ακαμάτηδες, feminine ακαμάτρα or ακαμάτισσα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sluggard, layabout, lazybones, loafer, slouch</div><b>ακαμάτισσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ακαμάτισσες, masculine ακαμάτης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ακαμάτρα">ακαμάτρα</a></div><b>ακαμάτρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ακαμάτρες, masculine ακαμάτης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sluggard, layabout, lazybones, loafer, slouch</div><b>ακαματεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to laze, loaf, idle</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to become lazy</div><b>ακαμψία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) rigidity, inflexibility</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) stiffness</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively, uncountable) intransigence, inflexibility</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἄκαμπτος.</div><b>ακανθεφύρα</b>
  <div><i>name, feminine (plural ακανθεφύρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Acanthephyra-genus shrimp.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from translingual Acanthephyra.</div><b>ακανθόχοιρος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ακανθόχοιροι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (as in terminology) porcupine</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (as in terminology or obsolete) archaic synonym of <a href="bword://σκαντζόχοιρος">σκαντζόχοιρος</a>: hedgehog</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀκανθόχοιρος, from ἄκανθος + χοῖρος. Doublet of σκαντζόχοιρος.</div><b>ακανθώδης</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακανθώδης, neuter ακανθώδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. thorny, prickly</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ακανθώδης</b> θάμνος - thorny shrub</div>
  <div class='def'>2. spinous</div>
  <div class='ex'>οι <b>ακανθώδεις</b> αποφύσεις των οσφυϊκών σπονδύλων - the spinous processes of the lumbar vertebrae</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) hazardous, dangerous</div>
  <div class='ex'>ένας <b>ακανθώδης</b> δρόμος - a dangerous road</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (figuratively) touchy, prickly, temperamental</div><b>ακανόνιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακανόνιστη, neuter ακανόνιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. irregular</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ακανόνιστοι</b> παλμοί καρδιάς - irregular heart beats</div>
  <div class='def'>2. asymmetric</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ακανόνιστα</b> χαρακτηριστικά - asymmetric features</div>
  <div class='def'>3. unsettled, not cleared up</div><b>ακαπάρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαπάρωτη, neuter ακαπάρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unsecured, without a deposit (of a transaction)</div><b>ακαπέλωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαπέλωτη, neuter ακαπέλωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. hatless, bareheaded</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) not overpriced</div><b>ακαπήλευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαπήλευτη, neuter ακαπήλευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. plain, honest,</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unexploited</div><b>ακαπίστρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαπίστρωτη, neuter ακαπίστρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unbridled, without a bridle or halter</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) unbridled, unchecked, without control</div><b>ακαρδία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural ακαρδίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable, usually) heartlessness</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively, uncountable, usually) heartlessness, lack of courage</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from French acardie. See Late Latin acardia &lt; a- privative + -cardia, formed on Ancient Greek ἀ- (a-, “-less”) + κᾰρδῐ́ᾱ + -ῐ́ᾱ. Equivalent to α- (a-) + καρδ(ιά)) + -ία.</div><b>ακαριαία</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>immediately, instantaneously</div><b>ακαριαίος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαριαία, neuter ακαριαίο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>instantaneous, immediate, spontaneous</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From the Ancient Greek ἀκαριαῖος.</div><b>ακαρπία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) fruitlessness, barrenness, seedlessness</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) crop failure</div><b>ακαρποφόρητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαρποφόρητη, neuter ακαρποφόρητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unfruitful, fruitless</div><b>ακαρτέρητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαρτέρητη, neuter ακαρτέρητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. rash</div>
  <div class='def'>2. impatient</div><b>ακαρύκευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαρύκευτη, neuter ακαρύκευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unseasoned, flavourless (UK), flavorless (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. plain, bland</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) unadorned</div><b>ακασσιτέρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακασσιτέρωτη, neuter ακασσιτέρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. untinned, not tin coated</div>
  <div class='def'>2. tinless, without tin</div><b>ακατάβλητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατάβλητη, neuter ακατάβλητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. indomitable, invincible</div>
  <div class='def'>2. sprightly</div>
  <div class='def'>3. unpaid</div><b>ακατάγγελτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατάγγελτη, neuter ακατάγγελτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unsued, unaccused</div><b>ακατάδεκτα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disdainfully, snobbishly, haughtily</div><b>ακατάδεκτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατάδεκτη, neuter ακατάδεκτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>a more formal variant of <a href="bword://ακατάδεχτος">ακατάδεχτος</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned influence on ακατάδεχτος with alteration [xt] &gt; [kt], itself inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀκατάδεκτος. Morphologically, α- (a-) + verb καταδέχομαι as: α- (a-, privative) + κατα- (kata-) + δεκτός from verb δέχομαι, stem δεκ-.</div><b>ακατάδεχτα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ακατάδεκτα">ακατάδεκτα</a></div><b>ακατάδεχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατάδεχτη, neuter ακατάδεχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disdainful, snobbish, snooty, haughty</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀκατάδεκτος with [kt] &gt; [xt]. Morphologically, α- (a-) + verb καταδέχομαι as: α- (a-, privative) + κατα- (kata-) + δεκτός &gt; δεχτός from verb δέχομαι. Doublet of ακατάδεκτος.</div><b>ακατάθετος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατάθετη, neuter ακατάθετο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unbanked, undeposited, cash in hand</div><b>ακατάκριτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατάκριτη, neuter ακατάκριτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. blameless</div>
  <div class='def'>2. uncriticised (UK), uncriticized (US)</div><b>ακατάκτητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατάκτητη, neuter ακατάκτητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unbeaten, unconquered</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unbeatable, unconquerable</div><b>ακατάληκτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατάληκτη, neuter ακατάληκτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>without ending, without termination</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀκατάληκτος.</div><b>ακατάληπτα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>jargon</div><b>ακατάληπτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατάληπτη, neuter ακατάληπτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>incomprehensible</div><b>ακατάλληλος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατάλληλη, neuter ακατάλληλο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. inappropriate, unsuitable, inconvenient</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unfit (for consumption)</div><b>ακατάλυτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατάλυτη, neuter ακατάλυτος)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. enduring, indissoluble</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unshakeable, firm</div><b>ακατάπαυστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατάπαυστη, neuter ακατάπαυστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unceasing, constant, continuous, ceaseless, incessant</div>
  <div class='def'>2. nonstop</div><b>ακατάπαυτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατάπαυτη, neuter ακατάπαυτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ακατάπαυστος">ακατάπαυστος</a></div><b>ακατάπειστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατάπειστη, neuter ακατάπειστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not persuaded, unconvinced</div><b>ακατάργητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατάργητη, neuter ακατάργητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unabolished, not abolished</div>
  <div class='def'>2. uncancelled</div><b>ακατάρτιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατάρτιστη, neuter ακατάρτιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unqualified, ignorant</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unprepared, not organised</div><b>ακατάσβεστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατάσβεστη, neuter ακατάσβεστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (figuratively) unquenchable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. burning, not extinguished, unquenchable</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀκατάσβεστος and semantic loan from French inextinguible. From privative ἀ- (a-) + κατασβέννυμι.</div><b>ακατάστατος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατάστατη, neuter ακατάστατο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. untidy, messy, disordered</div>
  <div class='def'>2. variable</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀκατάστατος, with semantic loan from French désordonné, en désordre, as well as semantic loan from German unordentlich. The Ancient Greek term is from ἀ- (a-, “a-, un-”) + an adjectival formation from καθίστημι.</div><b>ακατάσχετος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατάσχετη, neuter ακατάσχετο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unstemmable, unstaunchable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. nonstop</div>
  <div class='def'>3. not distrained</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek κατέχω.</div><b>ακατάτακτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατάτακτη, neuter ακατάτακτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unconscripted, unenlisted</div>
  <div class='def'>2. ungraded, unclassified</div><b>ακατάταχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατάταχτη, neuter ακατάταχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ακατάτακτος">ακατάτακτος</a></div><b>ακατάφερτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατάφερτη, neuter ακατάφερτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not feasible, unfeasible, unachievable</div><b>ακατέβατα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. at an unreduced price, without discount</div>
  <div class='def'>2. at a fixed price</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://ακατέβατος">ακατέβατος</a></div><b>ακατέβατος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατέβατη, neuter ακατέβατο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unreduced, not discounted, fixed price</div>
  <div class='def'>2. fixed, non-negotiable</div><b>ακατέργαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατέργαστη, neuter ακατέργαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>crude, untreated, unrefined, unprocessed, raw</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀκατέργαστος.</div><b>ακατήχητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακατήχητη, neuter ακατήχητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. not catechised (UK), not catechized (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. uninitiated</div><b>ακαταίσχυντος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακαταίσχυντη, neuter ακαταίσχυντο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unashamed, not feeling shame</div><b>ακαταβύθιστος</b>
