  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) walking stick, cane, armrest</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) rock (a person who provides security or support to another)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀκουμπιστήρι &lt; ἀκουμβιστήριον, from verb ἀκουμβίζω. By surface analysis, ακουμπάω/ακουμπώ, stem ακουμπισ- from ακουμπίζω (“to touch”) + -τήρι, following the example of similar tool nouns with that suffix such as σκαλιστήρι and ποτιστήρι.</div><b>ακουμπώ</b>
