  <div class='def'>coastal</div><b>ακτοπλοώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to coast, sail coastally</div><b>ακτοφυλακή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) coast guard service</div><b>ακτοφύλακας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ακτοφύλακες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>coast guard officer</div><b>ακτύπητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακτύπητη, neuter ακτύπητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αχτύπητος">αχτύπητος</a></div><b>ακυβέρνητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακυβέρνητη, neuter ακυβέρνητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. without government</div>
  <div class='def'>2. uncontrolled</div>
  <div class='def'>3. rudderless (watercraft)</div><b>ακυβερνησία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) lack of government, anarchy</div><b>ακυνήγητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακυνήγητη, neuter ακυνήγητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unchased, not pursued</div><b>ακυοφόρητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακυοφόρητη, neuter ακυοφόρητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. not full term (of gestation)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. of a foetus</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) not according to plan, half-baked</div><b>ακυρίευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακυρίευτη, neuter ακυρίευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>indomitable, impregnable, invincible</div><b>ακυριολεξία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ακυριολεξίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>misnomer</div><b>ακυρολεκτώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of ακυριολεκτώ: speak figuratively or metaphorically</div><b>ακυρολεξία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ακυρολεξίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ακυριολεξία">ακυριολεξία</a></div><b>ακυρωτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακυρωτική, neuter ακυρωτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>invalidating, annulling, reversing</div><b>ακυρότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) invalidity, voidness, nullity</div><b>ακυρώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to annul, revoke, quash, render null and void</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to abolish, repeal</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to punch or cancel a ticket</div><b>ακυρώσιμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακυρώσιμη, neuter ακυρώσιμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>voidable, annulable, reversible</div><b>ακωδικοποίητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακωδικοποίητη, neuter ακωδικοποίητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>uncodified</div><b>ακωκή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ακωκές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>tip, spike (a sharp extremity)</div><b>ακωμώδητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακωμώδητη, neuter ακωμώδητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>underided, unridiculed, unmocked</div><b>ακόλαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακόλαστη, neuter ακόλαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>lecherous, licentious, debauched, dissolute, dissipated</div><b>ακόλλητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακόλλητη, neuter ακόλλητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. not glued, not stuck</div>
  <div class='def'>2. not adhered to something</div>
  <div class='def'>3. not adhered to something; not soldered</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀκόλλητος.</div><b>ακόλουθος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακόλουθη, neuter ακόλουθο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>following, next, as follows</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀκόλουθος.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural ακόλουθοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. attendant, attaché</div>
  <div class='def'>2. acolyte</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀκόλουθος.</div><b>ακόμα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. yet, still</div>
  <div class='ex'>Είναι <b>ακόμα</b> ζωντανός. - He&#x27;s still alive.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. more, remaining, other</div>
  <div class='ex'>Χρειάζομαι <b>ακόμα</b> δύο μέρες. - I need two more days.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. even + <a href="bword://και">και</a> (kai)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Ακόμα και</b> η Ελένη είπε ναι! - Even Helen said yes!</div>
  <div class='def'>4. even if + <a href="bword://και">και</a> <a href="bword://αν">αν</a> (kai an), <a href="bword://και">και</a> να (kai na) or <a href="bword://και">και</a> <a href="bword://όταν">όταν</a>; when followed by a concessive clause</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Ακόμη και αν</b> συμφωνούν μεταξύ τους, συμπεριφέρονται άσχημα. - Even if they agree with each other, they behave badly.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> With stress shift, from Byzantine Greek ἀκομήν, anaptyctic form of Ancient Greek ἀκμήν, from ἀκμή.
Compare Mariupol Greek ако́ма.</div><b>ακόμα και αν</b>
  <div><i>phrase</i></div>
  <div class='def'>even if, even though</div>
  <div class='ex'>Δε θα τον ψηφίσω <b>ακόμα και αν</b> μου δώσουν 1.000.000 ευρώ. - I won&#x27;t vote for him even if they give me 1,000,000 euros.</div><b>ακόμα κι αν</b>
  <div><i>phrase</i></div>
  <div class='def'>even if, even though</div>
  <div class='ex'>Δεν θα τον ψηφίσω <b>ακόμα κι αν</b> μου δώσουν 1.000.000 ευρώ. - I won&#x27;t vote for him even if they give me 1,000,000 euros.</div><b>ακόμη</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ακόμα">ακόμα</a></div><b>ακόμη δε βγήκε απ&#x27; τ&#x27; αβγό</b>
  <div><i>phrase</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(idiomatic) just a kid, barely out of diapers, still wet behind the ears (referring to a young person believing themselves to be experienced)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Ακόμη δε βγήκε απ’ τ’ αβγό</b> και προσπαθεί να μας πει πώς να κάνουμε τη δουλειά μας. - He&#x27;s barely grown and he&#x27;s trying to tell us how to do our jobs.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Literally, “isn&#x27;t even out of the egg”.</div><b>ακόμη και αν</b>
  <div><i>phrase</i></div>
  <div class='def'>even if, even though</div>
  <div class='ex'>Δεν θα τον ψηφίσω <b>ακόμη και αν</b> μου δώσουν 1.000.000 ευρώ. - I won&#x27;t vote for him even if they give me 1,000,000 euros.</div><b>ακόμη κι αν</b>
  <div><i>phrase</i></div>
  <div class='def'>even if, even though</div>
  <div class='ex'>Δεν θα τον ψηφίσω <b>ακόμη κι αν</b> μου δώσουν 1.000.000 ευρώ. - I won&#x27;t vote for him even if they give me 1,000,000 euros.</div><b>ακόνι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ακόνια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>whetstone, grindstone</div><b>ακόνισμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ακονίσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sharpening, whetting, grinding</div><b>ακόντιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ακόντια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. spear (weapon)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. javelin (the object and the event)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. aligning pole, levelling staff</div><b>ακόντιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) throwing, hurling</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) throwing the javelin</div><b>ακόπιαστα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ακοπίαστα">ακοπίαστα</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://ακόπιαστος">ακόπιαστος</a></div><b>ακόπιαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακόπιαστη, neuter ακόπιαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ακοπίαστος">ακοπίαστος</a></div><b>ακόρεστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακόρεστη, neuter ακόρεστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. insatiable</div>
  <div class='ex'>Έχει μια <b>ακόρεστη</b> δίψα για γνώση. - She has an insatiable thirst for knowledge.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unsaturated (of a solution or a fat)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ακόρεστα</b> λιπαρά - unsaturated fat</div><b>ακόρντο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ακόρντα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>chord</div><b>ακόρυφος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακόρυφη, neuter ακόρυφο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. peakless, headless</div>
  <div class='def'>2. leaderless, without a ruler</div>
  <div class='def'>3. powerless, unguided</div><b>ακόσμητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακόσμητη, neuter ακόσμητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>plain, simple, unadorned</div><b>ακύκλωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακύκλωτη, neuter ακύκλωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unsurrounded, not encircled</div><b>ακύμαντος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακύμαντη, neuter ακύμαντο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. quiet, serene, unruffled</div>
  <div class='def'>2. calm, waveless, flat (sea)</div><b>ακύρωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ακυρώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. annulment, invalidation, cancellation</div>
  <div class='def'>2. punching (a ticket)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. vacating (of a legal opinion)</div><b>ακύρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακύρωτη, neuter ακύρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unratified, unconfirmed</div><b>ακώλυτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ακώλυτη, neuter ακώλυτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unobstructed, free, unchecked</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀκώλυτος.</div><b>αλά</b>
  <div><i>prep</i></div>
  <div class='def'>in the style of, in the manner of</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αλά</b> Τούρκα - in Turkish style</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from French à la.</div><b>αλά καρτ</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://α">α</a> <a href="bword://λα">λα</a> κάρτ</div><b>αλάβαστρος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αλάβαστροι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of αλάβαστρο (neuter)</div><b>αλάβωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλάβωτη, neuter αλάβωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unhurt, unwounded</div>
  <div class='def'>2. invulnerable</div><b>αλάδωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλάδωτη, neuter αλάδωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unoiled, oilless (food)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unlubricated, ungreased (machinery)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) unbribed</div><b>αλάθευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλάθευτη, neuter αλάθευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αλάνθαστος">αλάνθαστος</a></div><b>αλάθητο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) infallibility</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://αλάθητος">αλάθητος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://αλάθητος">αλάθητος</a></div><b>αλάθητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλάθητη, neuter αλάθητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αλάνθαστος">αλάνθαστος</a></div><b>αλάκερος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλάκερη, neuter αλάκερος)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ολάκερος">ολάκερος</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ὁλόκληρος.</div><b>αλάνης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αλάνηδες, feminine αλάνισσα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>carefree man of the streets, gadabout, bum</div><b>αλάνθαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλάνθαστη, neuter αλάνθαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unerring, infallible</div><b>αλάνι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλάνια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. alternative form of αλάνα</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly, colloquial) street urchin (child who lives, or spends most of his/her time, in the streets or in the above lot)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Έχουν μαζευτεί όλα τα <b>αλάνια</b> της γειτονιάς και κάνουν θόρυβο. - All the street urchins of the neighbourhood have gathered and are making noise.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ottoman Turkish آلاڭ.</div><b>αλάξευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλάξευτη, neuter αλάξευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unsculpted, unhewn</div><b>αλάργα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>remotely, far away</div><b>αλάργεμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλαργέματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>departure, going away</div><b>αλάτι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλάτια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>common salt, table salt</div>
  <div class='ex'>μαγειρικό <b>αλάτι</b> - cooking salt</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἁλάτιν, from Koine Greek ἁλάτιον, a diminutive of Ancient Greek ἅλας, from ἅλς, from Proto-Indo-European *séh₂l-, *séh₂ls. Compare the borrowed doublet άλας and Mariupol Greek а́лас.</div><b>αλάτινος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλάτινη, neuter αλάτινο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. salty, salt</div>
  <div class='def'>2. saltlike</div>
  <div class='def'>3. saline, salty (of water)</div><b>αλάτισμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) salting, corning, the process of preserving with salt</div><b>αλάφι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλάφια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ελάφι">ελάφι</a></div><b>αλάφιασμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλαφιάσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alarm, panic</div><b>αλάφρωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλαφρώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ελάφρωμα">ελάφρωμα</a></div><b>αλέ ρετούρ</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(indeclinable) round (trip) return (ticket)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from French aller-retour written in Greek alphabet.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(indeclinable) round trip (ticket/journey)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from French aller-retour written in Greek alphabet.</div><b>αλέα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλέες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>row of trees, avenue (usually in parks and gardens)</div><b>αλέγκρο</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>allegro (played in that manner)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from Italian allegro.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλέγκρα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>allegro (a piece in that manner)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from Italian allegro.</div><b>αλέγρα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>cheerfully, joyfully</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. nominative/accusative/vocative feminine singular of <a href="bword://αλέγρος">αλέγρος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αλέγρος">αλέγρος</a></div><b>αλέγρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλέγρα, neuter αλέγρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. cheerful, merry, breezy, chirpy, lively, buoyant</div>
  <div class='def'>2. allegro</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from Italian allegro.</div><b>αλέθω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to grind, mill, crush</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀλέθω, from Ancient Greek ἀλέω.</div><b>αλέκιαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλέκιαστη, neuter αλέκιαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. without stain, stainless, unstained</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unblemished, spotless</div><b>αλέκτορας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αλέκτορες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(rare) cock, rooster (male chicken)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀλέκτωρ, from ἀλέξω.</div><b>αλέκτωρ</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αλέκτορες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Katharevousa form of <a href="bword://αλέκτορας">αλέκτορας</a></div><b>αλέρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλέρωτη, neuter αλέρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. undirtied, unsoiled, unstained, spotless, clean</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) unstained (morally)</div><b>αλέστα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. quickly, sharply, at once</div>
  <div class='def'>2. immediately, readily</div><b>αλέτρι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλέτρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>plough</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀλέτριν, dissimilated variant of ἀρέτρι(ν)), from ἀρότρι(ν)), from Koine Greek ἀρότριον, from diminutive of Ancient Greek ἄροτρον. Doublet of άροτρο.</div><b>αλήθεια</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. really, truly</div>
  <div class='def'>2. by the way</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀλήθεια.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλήθειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>truth</div>
  <div class='ex'>Πες μου την <b>αλήθεια</b>. - Tell me the truth.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀλήθεια.</div><b>αλήστευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλήστευτη, neuter αλήστευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unrobbed, not cheated</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unpillaged</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀλῄστευτος.</div><b>αλήτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αλήτες, feminine αλήτισσα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. bum, roughneck, loafer</div>
  <div class='def'>2. delinquent, yobbo</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀλήτης.</div><b>αλήτικος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλήτικη, neuter αλήτικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. vagrant</div>
  <div class='def'>2. wandering, roaming</div><b>αλήτισσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλήτισσες, masculine αλήτης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. female bum, roughneck, loafer</div>
  <div class='def'>2. female delinquent, yobbo</div><b>αλί</b>
  <div><i>intj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>woe, alas</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αλί</b> και τρισ<b>αλί</b>! - woe and thrice woe!</div><b>αλίευμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλιεύματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>catch</div><b>αλίμενος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλίμενη, neuter αλίμενο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. harbourless (UK), harborless (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) inhospitable</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀλίμενος. See λιμήν.</div><b>αλίμονο</b>
  <div><i>intj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (followed by genitive weak personal pronoun) alas, woe expressing distress or misery</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Αλίμονό</b> του, τι έπαθε ο καημένος! - Alas, see what happened to the poor guy!</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (followed by genitive weak personal pronoun) Expresses a threat, God help</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Αλίμονό</b> σου αν σε πιάσει! - God help you if he catches you!</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Univerbation of the Byzantine Greek ἀλλ’ εἰ μόνον.</div><b>αλίπαντος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλίπαντη, neuter αλίπαντο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unlubricated, ungreased, oiled (machinery)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) unfertilised (field)</div><b>αλίπαστα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>salted foods, brined foods</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αλίπαστος">αλίπαστος</a></div><b>αλίπαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλίπαστη, neuter αλίπαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. salted, brined, pickled (food)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unfertilised, unmanured (land)</div><b>αλίπεδο</b>
