  <div class='def'>(colloquial) poor olive crop</div><b>αλαζονία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλαζονίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>a less common spelling of <a href="bword://αλαζονεία">αλαζονεία</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀλαζονία, a less common spelling ἀλαζονεία. See αλαζονεία.</div><b>αλαζονεία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλαζονείες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>arrogance, haughtiness, presumption</div>
  <div class='ex'>also a rare spelling: αλαζονία f (alazonía)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀλαζονεία, from ἀλαζών.
Also, a spelling ἀλαζονία.</div><b>αλαζονεύομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (rare) to swagger, be arrogant, be haughty</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (rare) to swank, boasts and lie</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀλαζονεύομαι, from ἀλαζών.</div><b>αλαζονικά</b>
