  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From the Ancient Greek ἀλείφω.</div><b>αλεγράδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) merriment, cheerfulness, joyfulness</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) liveliness</div><b>αλεγράρω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to cheer up, rejoice, enliven, liven up</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αλλεγράρω with simplified one &lt; λ &gt;. Borrowed from Italian allegrare, from allegro.</div><b>αλεηλάτητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλεηλάτητη, neuter αλεηλάτητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unlooted, unplundered</div><b>αλειμματοκέρι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλειμματοκέρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>tallow candle</div><b>αλειτούργητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλειτούργητη, neuter αλειτούργητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unconsecrated, unblessed, unused</div>
  <div class='def'>2. uncommunicated (having not attended mass or taken communion)</div><b>αλεξήλιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλεξήλια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(archaic) parasol</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αλεξ- (alex-, “protection, deflection”) + ήλιος, calque of French parasol.</div><b>αλεξήνεμο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλεξήνεμα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>windscreen (UK), windshield (US)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αλεξ- (alex-, “protection, deflection”) and άνεμος.</div><b>αλεξήνεμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλεξήνεμη, neuter αλεξήνεμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. shielding from the wind</div>
  <div class='def'>2. related to a windscreen</div><b>αλεξία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) alexia, word blindness</div><b>αλεξίπτωτο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλεξίπτωτα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>parachute</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αλεξι- (alexi-, “protection, deflection”) + πτώση, calque of French parachute. First attested 1874.</div><b>αλεξίπυρο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλεξίπυρα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>firescreen</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://αλεξίπυρος">αλεξίπυρος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://αλεξίπυρος">αλεξίπυρος</a></div><b>αλεξίπυρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλεξίπυρη, neuter αλεξίπυρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fireproof</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αλεξι- (alexi-, “protection, deflection”) + πυρ (pyr, “fire”), calque of French pare-feu. First attested 1861.</div><b>αλεξίσφαιρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλεξίσφαιρη, neuter αλεξίσφαιρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>bulletproof</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αλεξι- (alexi-, “protection, deflection”) + σφαίρα, calque of English bulletproof.</div><b>αλεξίφωτο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλεξίφωτα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>lampshade</div><b>αλεξανδρινισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αλεξανδρινισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>imitation of the behaviour or standards of the era when Alexandria flourished</div><b>αλεξανδρινός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλεξανδρινή, neuter αλεξανδρινό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Alexandrian</div><b>αλεξιβρόχιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλεξιβρόχια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(dated) umbrella</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αλεξι- (alexi-, “protection, deflection”) + βροχή, calque of French parapluie. Attested since 1897 in Katharevousa as ἀλεξιβρόχιον.</div><b>αλεξικέραυνο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλεξικέραυνα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>lightning conductor, lightning rod</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αλεξι- (alexi-, “protection, deflection”) + κεραυνός, calque of French parafoudre. First attested 1782.</div><b>αλεξιπτωτίστρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλεξιπτωτίστριες, masculine αλεξιπτωτιστής)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. parachutist</div>
  <div class='def'>2. paratrooper</div><b>αλεξιπτωτιστής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αλεξιπτωτιστές, feminine αλεξιπτωτίστρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. paratrooper</div>
  <div class='def'>2. parachutist</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) parachutist (someone dropped into an organisation from outside)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αλεξίπτωτο + -ιστής, calque of French parachutiste.</div><b>αλεποπορδή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλεποπορδές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>puffball</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αλεπού + πορδή</div><b>αλεπουδάκι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλεπουδάκια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fox cub</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αλεπού + -άκι</div><b>αλεπουδίσιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλεπουδίσια, neuter αλεπουδίσιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>vulpine, foxy (resembling or pertaining to foxes)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αλεπού.</div><b>αλεποφωλιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλεποφωλιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>foxhole, (fox&#x27;s) earth, fox&#x27;s hole, fox burrow</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αλεπού + φωλιά</div><b>αλεπού</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλεπούδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. fox</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) cunning or sly person</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀλωπού, ἀλωπώ, from Ancient Greek ἀλώπηξ, from Proto-Hellenic *alōpēkos), diminutive of Proto-Indo-European *h₂wl(o)p ~ *h₂ulp (“(red) fox”)).</div><b>αλεπότρυπα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλεπότρυπες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>foxhole, fox&#x27;s hole, fox burrow</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αλεπού + τρύπα</div><b>αλερετούρ</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of αλέ-ρετούρ</div><b>αλεσιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλεσιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial) the quantity that can be ground in one milling (corn, coffee, olives, etc)</div><b>αλεσμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλεσμένη, neuter αλεσμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ground, milled, powdered</div>
  <div class='ex'>πιπέρι <b>αλεσμένο</b> - ground pepper</div><b>αλεστικά</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>miller&#x27;s fee</div><b>αλεστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλεστική, neuter αλεστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>milling, relating to milling</div><b>αλετρίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to plough (UK), plow (US)</div><b>αλετροπόδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλετροπόδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ploughshare (UK), plowshare (US)</div><b>αλετροπόδι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλετρόδια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αλετροπόδα">αλετροπόδα</a></div><b>αλετροχέρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλετροχέρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ploughstaff (UK), plowstaff (US)</div><b>αλευθέρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλευθέρωτη, neuter αλευθέρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αλευτέρωτος">αλευτέρωτος</a></div><b>αλευράς</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αλευράδες, feminine αλευρού)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>flour merchant, flour dealer</div><b>αλευρέμπορος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αλευρέμποροι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>flour merchant, flour dealer</div><b>αλευροβιομήχανος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural αλευροβιομήχανοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>miller, flour manufacturer</div><b>αλευροβιομηχανία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλευροβιομηχανίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>flour industry</div><b>αλευρογυρίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to flour (dust with flour)</div><b>αλευροειδής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλευροειδής, neuter αλευροειδές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. floury</div>
  <div class='def'>2. mealy</div><b>αλευροκοσκινίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to sift flour</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to screen flour</div><b>αλευροπασπαλίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>spread flour</div><b>αλευροποίηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλευροποιήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>milling, flour production</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αλεύρι + -ποίηση</div><b>αλευροποιΐα</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>flour industry</div><b>αλευροποιώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to grind (to dust)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to mill</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αλεύρι + -ποιώ</div><b>αλευροσακιάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>bag flour</div><b>αλευροσταυρώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>bag flour</div><b>αλευρού</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλευρούδες, masculine αλευράς)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>flour merchant, flour dealer</div><b>αλευρωμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αλευρωμένη, neuter αλευρωμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>mealy (like meal or flour)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αλευρώνομαι, passive voice of αλευρώνω (“to dust with flour”).</div><b>αλευρόγαια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(Katharevousa, obsolete, uncountable) magnesium oxide, magnesia, a white powder (MgO) which is an ore of magnesium</div>
  <div class='ex'>εὑρίσκεται συχνάκις ἡ <b>ἀλευρόγαια</b> καὶ κομμάτια μικρὰ, λευκὰ, ἐλαφρὰ, καὶ εὔτριπτα, καὶ ὡς κόνις ἐλαφρὰ, καὶ λευκή - magnesium oxide is most often found as small, white, low density, easily pulverised pieces and as a low density white powder</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Of late 18th–early 19th c. as a neologism from άλευρον + γαία, in reference to the flour-like consistency of this alkaline earth oxide. The term was preferred by scholars of the Greek Enlightenment, who were reluctant to adopt μαγνησία, a calque of Late Latin magnesia, due to confusion with the region name Μαγνησία.</div><b>αλευρόκολλα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλευρόκολλες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. flour and water paste</div>
  <div class='def'>2. gluten</div><b>αλευρόμυλος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αλευρόμυλοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>flour mill</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αλεύρι + μύλος</div><b>αλευρώδης</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλευρώδης, neuter αλευρώδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αλευροειδής">αλευροειδής</a></div><b>αλευρώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (figuratively) to powder, apply makeup</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to flour (dust with flour)</div><b>αλευτέρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλευτέρωτη, neuter αλευτέρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unliberated, not freed</div><b>αλεύκαντος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλεύκαντη, neuter αλεύκαντο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unbleached</div><b>αλεύρι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλεύρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>flour (ground cereal grains, especially wheat)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Αυτή κοσκινίζει <b>αλεύρι</b> σε μια λεκάνη. - She sifts flour into a bowl.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek *ἀλεύριον, a diminutive of ἄλευρον).</div><b>αλεύρωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλευρώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. flouring, dusting with flour</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) smattering (of knowledge)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αλευρώνω + -μα (-ma).</div><b>αληθής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αληθής, neuter αληθές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(formal) true (in Boolean logic)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ᾰ̓ληθής.</div><b>αληθεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (in the present and imperfect tense) to come true, be realised</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (in the present and imperfect tense) to be true, be right</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (in other forms) to prove to be true</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (in other forms) to be realized</div><b>αληθινά</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>truly</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αληθινός">αληθινός</a></div><b>αληθινός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αληθινή, neuter αληθινό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>true, real</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀληθινός.</div><b>αληθοφάνεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) verisimilitude, believability, credibility, plausibility</div><b>αληθοφανής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αληθοφανής, neuter αληθοφανές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>credible, believable, plausible</div><b>αληθώς</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (Katharevousa, formal) really, truly</div>
  <div class='def'>2. used in set phrase for Easter greeting, as answer to Christ is risen</div>
  <div class='ex'>Χριστός ανέστη! — <b>Αληθώς</b> ανέστη! - Christ is risen! — Truly he is risen!</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ᾰ̓ληθῶς, adverb formed from adjective ᾰ̓ληθής.</div><b>αληθώς ανέστη</b>
  <div><i>intj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Truly he is risen (traditional Greek paschal (Easter) reply)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀληθῶς ἀνέστη.</div><b>αλησμονάω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αλησμονώ">αλησμονώ</a></div><b>αλησμονώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://λησμονώ">λησμονώ</a></div><b>αλησμόνητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. memorable, unforgettable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unforgotten</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀλησμόνητος. By surface analysis, α- (a-) + λησμονώ + -τος (-tos).</div><b>αλητάμπουρας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αλητάμπουρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. hooligan, yob, yobbo (UK)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. bum, roughneck, loafer, punk (US)</div><b>αληταράς</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αληταράδες, feminine αληταρού)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. hooligan, yob, yobbo (UK)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. bum, roughneck, loafer, punk (US)</div><b>αληταρία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) hooliganism, delinquency (behaviour)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) riffraff</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αλήτης + -αρία.</div><b>αληταριό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) riff-raff, yobbery, delinquents (collectively)</div><b>αλητεία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλητείες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>vagrancy, hooliganism, vagabondage</div><b>αλητεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(intransitive) loaf, bum around</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀλητεύω (“wonder around”).</div><b>αλητοπαρέα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλητόπαιδα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>bums, street urchins, guttersnipes (collectively)</div><b>αλητοτουρίστας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αλητοτουρίστες, feminine αλητοτουρίστρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>scruffy tourist with little money</div><b>αλητόπαιδο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλητόπαιδα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>street urchin, guttersnipe</div><b>αλιά</b>
  <div><i>intj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αλί">αλί</a></div><b>αλιάδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλιάδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>skordalia</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> A mediaeval borrowing from Italian agliata.</div><b>αλιάετος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αλιάετοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>osprey, sea eagle (Pandion haliaetus)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἁλιάετος.</div><b>αλιάνιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλιάνιστη, neuter αλιάνιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not cut up, unsplit</div><b>αλιβάνιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλιβάνιστη, neuter αλιβάνιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. uncensed</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) having not been to church</div>
  <div class='def'>3. unflattered</div><b>αλιγάτορας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αλιγάτορες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alligator</div><b>αλιεία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) fishing</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἁλιείᾱ.</div><b>αλιευτικό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλιευτικά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fishing boat</div>
  <div class='ex'>for smaller boats, less formal: ψαράδικο n (psarádiko), ψαρόβαρκα f (psaróvarka)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Substantivized neuter of adjective αλιευτικός by ellipsis of neuter noun σκάφος. As in Ancient Greek expression ἁλιευτικόν πλοῖον &quot;fishing vessel&quot;, from ἁλιευτικός, derived from ἁλιεύω, derived from ἁλιεύς, derived from ἅλς.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://αλιευτικός">αλιευτικός</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://αλιευτικός">αλιευτικός</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> See the etymology of the corresponding lemma form.</div><b>αλιευτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλιευτική, neuter αλιευτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fishing, fish</div><b>αλιεύς</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αλιείς)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fisherman</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἁλιεύς.</div><b>αλιεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to fish, angle</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to fish, search, hunt (for something)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Hellenistic Koine Greek ἁλιεύω. The figurative sense, semantic loan from Italian pescare or from French pêcher.</div><b>αλιμάριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλιμάριστη, neuter αλιμάριστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unsharpened, unfiled, unrasped</div>
  <div class='ex'>Άφησα τα νύχια μου <b>αλιμάριστα</b>. - I left my nails unfiled.</div><b>αλισάχνη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) spume, sea foam, seaspray</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) salt flakes, salt rime</div><b>αλισίβα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) lye (alkaline solution)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from Venetan lisiva, ultimately from Latin lixivus.</div><b>αλισβερίσι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλισβερίσια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>dealings, business</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from Ottoman Turkish آلیش ویریش.</div><b>αλισιβερίσι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλισιβερίσια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αλισβερίσι">αλισβερίσι</a></div><b>αλισματώδη</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>The Alismatales, an order of plants.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Calque of translingual Alismatales, as άλισμα + -ώδη.</div><b>αλισφακιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλισφακιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αλιφασκιά">αλιφασκιά</a></div><b>αλιτάνα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλιτάνες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αλτάνα">αλτάνα</a></div><b>αλιτήριος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλιτήρια, neuter αλιτήριο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. rascally, mischievous</div>
  <div class='def'>2. dishonest, villainous</div><b>αλιφασκιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλιφασκιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sage</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἐλελίσφακος.</div><b>αλκάλιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλκάλια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. alkali metal (lithium, sodium, potassium, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) alkali, alkali metal hydroxides (sodium hydroxide, etc)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η σόδα και η ποτάσα είναι <b>αλκάλια</b>. - Soda and potash are alkalis.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from French alcali, from Arabic اَلْقِلْي (al-qily, “alkali”).</div><b>αλκάνιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (usually uncountable, plural αλκάνια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) alkane</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From English alkane + -ιο (-io).</div><b>αλκίνιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλκίνια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alkyne (eg: acetylene)</div><b>αλκαλικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλκαλική, neuter αλκαλικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alkaline</div><b>αλκαλιμέταλλο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλκαλιμέταλλα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alkali metal (lithium, sodium, potassium, rubidium, cesium or francium)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αλκάλι(ο) n, “alkali”) + μέταλλο n.</div><b>αλκαλοειδές</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλκαλοειδή)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alkaloid</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from French alcaloïde.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative neuter singular of <a href="bword://αλκαλοειδής">αλκαλοειδής</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from French alcaloïde.</div><b>αλκαλοειδής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλκαλοειδής, neuter αλκαλοειδές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alkaloid</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from French alcaloïde.</div><b>αλκαϊκός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλκαϊκή, neuter αλκαϊκό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Alcaic</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek Ἀλκαϊκός from Ἀλκαῖος + -ικός.</div><b>αλκοολίκι</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αλκοολίκια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (colloquial) habitual alcoholism</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) similar addictions</div><b>αλκοολική</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλκοολικές, masculine αλκοολικός)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alcoholic, an abuser of alcohol</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative feminine singular of <a href="bword://αλκοολικός">αλκοολικός</a></div><b>αλκοολικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλκοολική, neuter αλκοολικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. Of or pertaining to alcohol</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αλκοολική</b> ζύμωση - alcoholic fermentation</div>
  <div class='def'>2. alcoholic, describing an abuser of alcohol</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αλκοολικοί, feminine αλκοολική)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alcoholic, an abuser of alcohol</div><b>αλκοολισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) alcoholism</div><b>αλκοολούχος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλκοολούχος or αλκοολούχα, neuter αλκοολούχο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alcoholic (containing alcohol)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αλκοολούχο</b> ποτό - alcoholic beverage</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned formation from αλκοόλ + -ούχος, a calque of German alkoolhaltig.</div><b>αλκοτέστ</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(indeclinable) breath test</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from French alcotest.</div><b>αλκοόλ</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (indeclinable) alcohol (component of intoxicating drinks)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (indeclinable) spirits (intoxicating drinks)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (indeclinable) ethanol, ethyl alcohol</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (indeclinable) surgical spirit</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from French alcool.</div><b>αλκοόλη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλκοόλες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alcohol (methanol, ethanol, etc)</div><b>αλκυονίδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλκυονίδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>a halcyon day (hot winter day), singular of αλκυονίδες, elliptical form of αλκυονίδες ημέρες</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀλκῠονίς f from the accusative singular &quot;τὴν ἀλκῠονίδα&quot;.
By ellipsis of ημέρα f.</div><b>αλκυονίδες ημέρες</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>halcyon days (warm, sunny periods in winter)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Οι χειμερινές κακοκαιρίες διακόπτονται συχνά κατά τον Ιανουάριο και το πρώτο δεκαπενθήμερο του Φεβρουαρίου από ηλιόλουστες ημέρες, τις γνωστές από την αρχαιότητα <b>&quot;Αλκυονίδες ημέρες&quot;</b>. - Winter bad weather days are often interrupted, during January and the first fortnight of February, with sunny days, well known as &quot;Alkion days&quot; in ancient times.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀλκῠονίδες ἡμέραι, plural of ἀλκῠονίς f &amp; Ancient Greek ἡμέρα f.</div><b>αλκυόνα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλκυόνες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αλκυόνη">αλκυόνη</a></div><b>αλκυόνη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλκυόνες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. kingfisher, common kingfisher, halcyon, Alcedo atthis</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (usually) kingfisher family</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (literary) halcyon</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀλκυών.</div><b>αλλά</b>
  <div><i>conj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>but</div>
  <div class='ex'>Είναι έξυπνος <b>αλλά</b> τεμπέλης. - He is clever but lazy.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀλλά.</div><b>αλλάζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be changed, be altered</div><b>αλλάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to change, alter (appearance, content or substance of something)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀλλάζω, from Ancient Greek ἀλλάσσω, ἀλλάττω, from ἄλλος.</div><b>αλλάσσω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αλλάζω">αλλάζω</a></div><b>αλλέγκρο</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative spelling of <a href="bword://αλέγκρο">αλέγκρο</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative spelling of <a href="bword://αλέγκρο">αλέγκρο</a></div><b>αλλέγρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλλέγρα, neuter αλλέγρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αλέγρος">αλέγρος</a></div><b>αλλέως</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αλλιώς">αλλιώς</a></div><b>αλλήθωρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλλήθωρη, neuter αλλήθωρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. cross-eyed, having a squint</div>
  <div class='def'>2. suffering from strabismus</div><b>αλλήλους</b>
  <div><i>pron</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(pronoun, reflexive) each other, one another</div>
  <div class='ex'>αγαπάτε <b>αλλήλους</b> - love one another</div><b>αλλήλων</b>
  <div><i>pron</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(pronoun, reflexive) each other, one another</div><b>αλλαγή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλλαγές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>change, differentiation, replacement (the action and the effect)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Έκανε μια <b>αλλαγή</b> στις ρυθμίσεις. - He made a change to the settings.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀλλαγή, from Ancient Greek ἄλλος.</div><b>αλλαγμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλλαγμένη, neuter αλλαγμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>changed, altered</div><b>αλλαντικό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλλαντικά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>charcuterie, processed and cured meats (bacon, chorizo, corned beef, salami, sausage, etc)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From άλλαντα + -ικός, in which άλλαντα is inherited from Ancient Greek ἀλλᾶντες, the plural of ἀλλᾶς, which is perhaps from dialectal *αλλᾱϝεντ-, from Proto-Italic *allā- (“garlic”), whence Latin ālium.</div><b>αλλαντοποιΐα</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αλλαντοποιία">αλλαντοποιία</a></div><b>αλλαντοποιία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) pork meats preparation, pork butchery</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) sausage making</div><b>αλλαντοποιείο</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλλαντοποιεία)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. pork meat factory</div>
  <div class='def'>2. sausage factory</div><b>αλλαντοποιός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αλλαντοποιοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>maker of sausages, charcuterie, salami, etc</div><b>αλλαντοπωλείο</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αλλαντοπωλεία)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>pork butcher&#x27;s selling sausages, charcuterie, salami, etc</div><b>αλλαντοπώλης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αλλαντοπώλες, feminine αλλαντοπώλισσα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>shopkeeper selling sausages, charcuterie, salami, etc</div><b>αλλαντοπώλισσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλλαντοπώλισσες, masculine αλλαντοπώλης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>shopkeeper selling sausages, salami, etc</div><b>αλλαξιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλλαξιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. change (of clothes)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Πήρε για <b>αλλαξιές</b> εσώρουχα. - He took three changes of underwear.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (colloquial) exchange</div><b>αλλαξιέρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλλαξιέρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>changing table (small raised platform designed to allow a person to change an infant&#x27;s nappy/diaper)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αλλαξ- (allax-, “change”) + -ιέρα</div><b>αλλαξοδρομώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to change direction</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αλλαξο- (allaxo-, “change”) + δρόμος</div><b>αλλαξοκαιριά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλλαξοκαιριές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unsettled weather, changeable weather</div>
  <div class='def'>2. a change in the weather</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αλλαξο- (allaxo-, “change”) + καιρός, καιρ(ός) + -ιά.</div><b>αλλαξοπίστισα</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>first-person singular simple past of αλλαξοπιστίζω</div><b>αλλαξοπιστία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλλαξοπιστίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>change of faith/religion</div><b>αλλαξοπιστώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to recant, change</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αλλαξο- (allaxo-, “change”) + πίστη</div><b>αλλαξόπιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλλαξόπιστη, neuter αλλαξόπιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. renegade, turncoat</div>
  <div class='def'>2. apostate</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αλλαξό- + πίστη</div><b>αλλαχού</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>elsewhere</div><b>αλλεπάλληλα</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>neuter nominative/accusative/vocative plural of <a href="bword://αλλεπάλληλος">αλλεπάλληλος</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>successively, in succession, one after the other</div><b>αλλεπάλληλος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλλεπάλληλη, neuter αλλεπάλληλο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. repeated, successive, sequential</div>
  <div class='def'>2. repetitious</div><b>αλλεπαλληλία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλλεπαλληλίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sequence, succession</div><b>αλλεργία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλλεργίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. allergy (condition)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) antipathy, repulsion</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from German Allergie. Coined by Austrian pediatrician Clemens von Pirquet in 1906 from Ancient Greek ἄλλος + ἔργον, on the model of Energie.</div><b>αλλεργικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλλεργική, neuter αλλεργικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>allergic</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αλλεργία + -ικός.</div><b>αλλεργιολογία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αλλεργιολογίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) allergology</div><b>αλληγορία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλληγορίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>allegory</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Koine Greek ἀλληγορία.</div><b>αλληγορικά</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>allegorically</div><b>αλληγορικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλληγορική, neuter αλληγορικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>allegorical</div><b>αλληγορώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to speak allegorically</div><b>αλληθωρίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to squint</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to suffer from strabismus</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) to examine closely</div><b>αλληθώρισμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλληθωρίσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>squint, strabismus</div><b>αλληλέγγυος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλληλέγγυα, neuter αλληλέγγυο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. joint, jointly</div>
  <div class='def'>2. solidary</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Koine Greek ἀλληλέγγυος.</div><b>αλληλένδετος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλληλένδετη, neuter αλληλένδετο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(in plural, mainly) intertwined, interconnected, intertwangled</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀλληλένδετος.</div><b>αλληλασφάλεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλληλασφάλειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>mutual insurance</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αλληλ- (allil-, “mutuality”) + ασφάλεια</div><b>αλληλεγγύη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) solidarity, fellowship (the mutual guarantee of support and friendship)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀλληλεγγύη &amp; semantic loan from French solidarité. Morphologically, αλληλ- (allil-, “mutuality: of each other”) + εγγύηση</div><b>αλληλεξάρτηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλληλεξαρτήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>interdependence, mutuality</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αλληλ- (allil-, “mutuality”) + εξαρτώμαι</div><b>αλληλεπίδραση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλληλεπιδράσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>interaction, mutual influence</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αλληλο- (allilo-) + επίδραση.</div><b>αλληλεπιδρώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to interact, act mutually</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αλληλ- (allil-, “reciprocal, mutual”) + επιδρώ</div><b>αλληλεπικοινωνία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλληλεπικοινωνίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>intercommunication (between two people, machines, etc)</div><b>αλληλεπικοινωνώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to intercommunicate</div><b>αλληλοαπάγομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to elope</div><b>αλληλοβοήθεια</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>mutual aid</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αλληλο- (allilo-, “reciprocal, mutual”) + βοήθεια, calque of French entraide.</div><b>αλληλοβοηθιέμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
