  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) alopecia</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀλωπεκία.</div><b>αλωπεκίαση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αλωπεκία">αλωπεκία</a></div><b>αλόγα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλόγες, masculine άλογο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (colloquial) female horse, mare</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (slang) large, clumsy woman</div><b>αλόγιαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλόγιαστη, neuter αλόγιαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αλόγιστος">αλόγιστος</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek *ἀλόγιαστος found as adverb ἀλόγιαστα, from ἀ- (a-) privative + λογιάζω, λογιασ-, a form of the ancient λογίζομαι + -τος (-tos). Doublet of αλόγιστος.</div><b>αλόγιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλόγιστη, neuter αλόγιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>rash, thoughtless</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀλόγιστος, from ἀ- (a-) privative +, λογισ- + -τος (-tos). Doublet of αλόγιαστος.</div><b>αλόη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλόες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>aloe</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀλόη.</div><b>αλύγιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλύγιστη, neuter αλύγιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>inflexible, stiff, unbending</div><b>αλύμαντος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλύμαντη, neuter αλύμαντο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unbroken, sealed (of a sealed letter or document)</div><b>αλύπητα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. mercilessly, pitilessly</div>
  <div class='def'>2. spend lavishly</div><b>αλύπητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλύπητη, neuter αλύπητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>merciless, pitiless</div><b>αλύτρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλύτρωτη, neuter αλύτρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. not freed, not liberated</div>
  <div class='def'>2. in bondage</div><b>αλύχτημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλυχτήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>synonym of <a href="bword://αλύχτισμα">αλύχτισμα</a></div><b>αλύχτισμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλυχτίσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>barking, bark, howling</div>
  <div class='ex'>το <b>αλύχτισμα</b> του σκύλου - the barking of the dog</div><b>αλώβητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλώβητη, neuter αλώβητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. undamaged, unharmed, unscathed</div>
  <div class='def'>2. undiluted</div><b>αλώνι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλώνια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. threshing floor (floor where grain is threshed)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) threshing</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἁλώνιν, from Koine Greek ἁλώνιον, from a diminutive of Ancient Greek ἅλως. Doublet of άλως.</div><b>αλώνισμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αλωνίσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>threshing</div><b>αλώνιτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλώνιτη, neuter αλώνιτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unthreshed</div><b>αλώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(rare) To dominate, to occupy, to conquer.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> By surface analysis, άλωση”) + -ώνω.</div><b>αλώπηξ</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αλώπεκες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(for taxonomic terms) Monotonic spelling of <a href="bword://ἀλώπηξ">ἀλώπηξ</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> The ancient Ancient Greek ἀλώπηξ.</div><b>αλώσιμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αλώσιμη, neuter αλώσιμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>pregnable, capturable, vulnerable</div><b>αμ</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of αστρονομική <a href="bword://μονάδα">μονάδα</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Abbreviation.</div><b>αμάγευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμάγευτη, neuter αμάγευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unbewitched, unenchanted</div><b>αμάδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αμάδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. quoit (a small round flat stone)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (in plural) a children&#x27;s game similar to quoits</div>
  <div class='ex'>παίζω <b>αμάδες</b> - to play quoits</div><b>αμάδητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμάδητη, neuter αμάδητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unplucked (without feathers, hair, leaves removed)</div><b>αμάζευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμάζευτη, neuter αμάζευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unpicked, unharvested (crops)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. untidy (room, house)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. uncollected (debts)</div>
  <div class='def'>4. ungathered</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From α- (a-, “un-”) + μαζεύω.</div><b>αμάθεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αμάθειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. ignorance</div>
  <div class='def'>2. illiteracy</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀμαθ(ία) with metaplasm to ‑εια, based on adjective αμαθής, as in the group of pairs of adjective-abstract nouns.</div><b>αμάθευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμάθευτη, neuter αμάθευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unknown, not known</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unlearned, not learnt</div><b>αμάθητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμάθευτη, neuter αμάθευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. not learnt, not studied</div>
  <div class='def'>2. inexperienced, unskilled</div><b>αμάκα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) cadging, sponging</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) begging</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from Italian macca.</div><b>αμάλαγος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμάλαγη, neuter αμάλαγο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. pure, uncontaminated</div>
  <div class='def'>2. untouched</div><b>αμάλακτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμάλακτη, neuter αμάλακτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αμάλαχτος">αμάλαχτος</a></div><b>αμάλαχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμάλαχτη, neuter αμάλαχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unkneaded (bread dough)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) untouched, unyielding</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) heartless</div><b>αμάλγαμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αμαλγάματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. amalgam (alloy of mercury)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. amalgam (tooth filling)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) amalgam, medley, mashup</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Reborrowing from French amalgame, from Medieval Latin amalgama, from Arabic مَلْغَم, from Ancient Greek μάλαγμᾰ. Doublet of μάλαμα.</div><b>αμάλλιαγος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμάλλιαστη, neuter αμάλλιαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unfledged, callow, hairless</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) callow, inexperienced</div><b>αμάλλιαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμάλλιαστη, neuter αμάλλιαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αμάλλιαγος">αμάλλιαγος</a></div><b>αμάλωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμάλωτη, neuter αμάλωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unrebuked, unscolded, not told off</div><b>αμάν</b>
  <div><i>intj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. wow, oh man, oh boy</div>
  <div class='def'>2. oh no</div>
  <div class='def'>3. gosh, blimey, whoa</div>
  <div class='def'>4. my God, for God&#x27;s sake</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from Ottoman Turkish آمان (aman).</div><b>αμάνικος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμάνικη, neuter αμάνικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sleeveless (of a garment, having no sleeves)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> α- (a-, “lacking”) + μανίκι</div><b>αμάντευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμάντευτη, neuter αμάντευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unguessed</div><b>αμάντριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμάντριστη, neuter αμάντριστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αμάντρωτος">αμάντρωτος</a></div><b>αμάντρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμάντρωτη, neuter αμάντρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>wallless, unwalled (not surrounded by a wall or hedge)</div><b>αμάξι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αμάξια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. horse carriage, trap</div>
  <div class='def'>2. car, automobile</div><b>αμάξωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αμαξώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>bodywork, coachwork, body (of car etc)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> άμαξα + -ωμα (-oma)</div><b>αμάραντη αγάπη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>love-lies-bleeding</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αμάραντος and αγάπη f.</div><b>αμάραντος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμάραντη, neuter αμάραντο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>undying, unwilting, unfading, eternal</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀμάραντος.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αμάραντοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. amaranth</div>
  <div class='def'>2. everlasting flower</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀμάραντος.</div><b>αμάρτημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αμαρτήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. sin</div>
  <div class='ex'>επτά θανάσιμα <b>αμαρτήματα</b> - seven deadly sins</div>
  <div class='def'>2. error, mistake</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From the Ancient Greek ἁμάρτημα.</div><b>αμάρτυρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμάρτυρη, neuter αμάρτυρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unattested</div><b>αμάσητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμάσητη, neuter αμάσητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unchewed, not chewed</div><b>αμάτιαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμάτιαστη, neuter αμάτιαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unaffected by the evil eye</div>
  <div class='def'>2. one who has not been cursed by the evil eye</div><b>αμάχη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αμάχες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. enmity, strife</div>
  <div class='def'>2. hostility, hatred</div><b>αμάχητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμάχητη, neuter αμάχητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>irrefutable (without argument)</div><b>αμέθοδος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμέθοδη, neuter αμέθοδο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unmethodical, disorderly, unsystematic</div><b>αμέθυστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμέθυστη, neuter αμέθυστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sober, not drunk</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αμέθυστοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>amethyst</div><b>αμέλγω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αρμέγω">αρμέγω</a></div><b>αμέλεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αμέλειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. negligence, carelessness inattention</div>
  <div class='def'>2. negligence</div><b>αμέλημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αμελήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>error, accident (caused by negligence)</div><b>αμέριμνος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμέριμνη, neuter αμέριμνο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unconcerned, insouciant</div>
  <div class='def'>2. nonchalant, light-hearted</div><b>αμέριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμέριστη, neuter αμέριστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. undivided</div>
  <div class='def'>2. undivisible</div>
  <div class='def'>3. complete, whole</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀμέριστος. By surface analysis, α- (a-) + μερίζω + -τος (-tos).</div><b>αμέρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμέρωτη, neuter αμέρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>undomesticated (largely of animals)</div><b>αμέστωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμέστωτη, neuter αμέστωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unripe (fruits, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. immature (people)</div><b>αμέσως</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. immediately, at once, straight away</div>
  <div class='ex'>Near-synonym: αμελλητί (amellití, “promptly”)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. synonym of <a href="bword://άμεσα">άμεσα</a> (without anything intervening; without intermediation)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀμέσως, from Ancient Greek ἄμεσος. By surface analysis, άμεσ(ος)) + -ως (-os).</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>intj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>right away!</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀμέσως, from Ancient Greek ἄμεσος. By surface analysis, άμεσ(ος)) + -ως (-os).</div><b>αμέταλλα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nonmetals</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αμέταλλος">αμέταλλος</a></div><b>αμέταλλος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμέταλλη, neuter αμέταλλο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. non-metallic</div>
  <div class='def'>2. non-metallic</div><b>αμέτε</b>
  <div><i>intj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (colloquial, idiomatic) second-person plural present active imperative of <a href="bword://πηγαίνω">πηγαίνω</a>, alternative form of <a href="bword://άμετε">άμετε</a>; go!</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Αμέτε</b> στο καλό! - Go [plural] to good (with good luck)!</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (colloquial, idiomatic) second-person plural present active imperative of <a href="bword://πηγαίνω">πηγαίνω</a>, alternative form of <a href="bword://άμετε">άμετε</a>; go!</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Αμέτε</b> στο διάβολο! - Go [plural] to the devil (to hell)!</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> See etymology of άμετε, άμε.</div><b>αμέτοχος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμέτοχη, neuter αμέτοχο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>uninvolved, not taking part</div><b>αμέτρητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμέτρητη, neuter αμέτρητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>innumerable, uncountable, countless</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀμέτρητος; by surface analysis, α- (a-, alpha privative) + μετρητός.</div><b>αμήν</b>
  <div><i>intj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(Judaism) amen</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀμήν.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(indeclinable) amen</div>
  <div class='ex'>ώσπου να πεις <b>αμήν</b> - before you could say Jack Robinson</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀμήν.</div><b>αμήνυτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμήνυτη, neuter αμήνυτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. not sued (law)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unannounced, unexpected</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀμήνυτος (“not denounced; unannounced”).</div><b>αμήχανος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμήχανη, neuter αμήχανο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. bewildered, awkward</div>
  <div class='def'>2. embarrassed</div>
  <div class='def'>3. helpless</div><b>αμίαντος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμίαντη, neuter αμίαντο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. made of asbestos</div>
  <div class='def'>2. pure, chaste</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀμίαντος.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) asbestos</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀμίαντος.</div><b>αμίκρυντος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμίκρυντη, neuter αμίκρυντο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(rare) <a href="bword://Α">Α</a> rarer form of <a href="bword://ασμίκρυντος">ασμίκρυντος</a></div><b>αμίλητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμίλητη, neuter αμίλητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. silent, quiet</div>
  <div class='def'>2. speechless</div><b>αμίμητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμίμητη, neuter αμίμητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. inimitable, (colloquial) priceless</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unrivalled, incomparable</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From the Ancient Greek ἀμίμητος.</div><b>αμίσθωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμίσθωτη, neuter αμίσθωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unhired, not hired</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unrented, unleased</div><b>αμαγάριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμαγάριστη, neuter αμαγάριστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. clean, pure</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unsoiled, uncontaminated, undefiled</div><b>αμαγείρευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμαγείρευτη, neuter αμαγείρευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>uncooked, raw</div><b>αμαδρυάδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αμαδρυάδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(Greek) hamadryad, wood-nymph</div><b>αμαζόνα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αμαζόνες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (Greek) Amazon (mythical female warrior)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. amazon (a strong, athletic woman)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek Ἀμαζών.</div><b>αμαζόνειος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμαζόνεια, neuter αμαζόνειο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αμαζόνιος">αμαζόνιος</a></div><b>αμαζόνιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμαζόνια, neuter αμαζόνιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. Amazonian (of the river)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. amazonian (of women)</div><b>αμαθής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμαθής, neuter αμαθές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ignorant, uneducated, illiterate</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀμαθής.</div><b>αμακαδόρος</b>
