  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://αμφίβιος">αμφίβιος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://αμφίβιος">αμφίβιος</a></div><b>αμφίβιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφίβια, neuter αμφίβιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>amphibious</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀμφίβιος. By surface analysis, αμφί- + βίος.</div><b>αμφίβολος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφίβολη, neuter αμφίβολο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. doubtful</div>
  <div class='def'>2. questionable, unsavory</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀμφίβολος. For sense &quot;questionable&quot;, semantic loan from French douteux. Morphologically, αμφι- (amfi-) + stem βολ- for which see αμφιβάλλω - αμφιβολία f &amp; βάλλω - βολή + suffix -ος (-os).</div><b>αμφίγνωμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφίγνωμη, neuter αμφίγνωμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>indecisive dithering, irresolute, wavering, hesitant</div><b>αμφίδρομος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφίδρομη, neuter αμφίδρομο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. two-way, bidirectional</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) ambiguous</div>
  <div class='def'>3. bisexual</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀμφίδρομος. By surface analysis, αμφί- + δρόμ(ος)) + -ος (-os).</div><b>αμφίεση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αμφιέσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>attire, dress, clothes, clothing</div><b>αμφίκοιλος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφίκοιλη, neuter αμφίκοιλο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>biconcave</div><b>αμφίκοπος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφίκοπη, neuter αμφίκοπο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. double-edged, two-edged</div>
  <div class='def'>2. ambiguous</div><b>αμφίκυρτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφίκυρτη, neuter αμφίκυρτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. biconvex, lenticular</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (of the moon) gibbous</div><b>αμφίλογος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφίλογη or αμφίλογος, neuter αμφίλογο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. contentious, equivocal</div>
  <div class='def'>2. ambiguous</div><b>αμφίπλευρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>The Bilateria.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αμφίπλευρος.</div><b>αμφίπλευρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφίπλευρη, neuter αμφίπλευρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>bilateral, two-sided</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀμφίπλευρος. By surface analysis, αμφί- + -πλευρος (-plevros).</div><b>αμφίπυρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αμφίπυρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Any owlet moth of the genus Amphipyra.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from translingual Amphipyra.</div><b>αμφίρροπος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφίρροπη, neuter αμφίρροπο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>hesitant, irresolute, wavering</div><b>αμφίσημος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφίσημη, neuter αμφίσημο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>describes ambiguous words or phrases</div><b>αμφίστομος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφίστομη, neuter αμφίστομο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. double-edged, two-edged</div>
  <div class='def'>2. with two openings, on two fronts</div>
  <div class='def'>3. ambiguous</div><b>αμφίχειρας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αμφίχειρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ambidextrous person</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from αμφί- + χειρ (cheir) + -ας (-as), modelled on Koine Greek μονόχειρ, whence μονόχειρας.</div><b>αμφίψωμο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αμφίψωμα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(neologism) sandwich</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αμφί- + ψωμί</div><b>αμφεταμίνη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αμφεταμίνες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>amphetamine</div><b>αμφιβάλλω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to doubt, have doubts</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀμφιβάλλω. Morphologically αμφι- (amfi-) + βάλλω.</div><b>αμφιβληστροειδής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αμφιβληστροειδείς)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>retina</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφιβληστροειδής, neuter αμφιβληστροειδές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>retinal, of the retina</div><b>αμφιβληστροειδίτιδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) retinitis</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αμφιβληστροειδής + -ίτιδα</div><b>αμφιβολία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αμφιβολίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>doubt, uncertainty</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀμφιβολία.</div><b>αμφιγνωμία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) indecision, hesitancy</div><b>αμφιδέξιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφιδέξια, neuter αμφιδέξιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (figuratively) deft</div>
  <div class='def'>2. ambidextrous</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αμφι- (amfi-, “both, in two sides (prefix)”) + δέξιος.</div><b>αμφιδεξιότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) ambidexterity, ambidextrousness</div><b>αμφιδρόμια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αμφιδρόμιες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(historical) amphidromia (an ancient post-natal ceremony)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀμφιδρόμια.</div><b>αμφιθέατρο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αμφιθέατρα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. amphitheatre (UK), amphitheater (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. lecture theatre, lecture hall</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αμφι- (amfi-, “both, in two sides (prefix)”) + θέατρο.</div><b>αμφιθαλής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφιθαλής, neuter αμφιθαλές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>german, describes siblings (having the same parents)</div><b>αμφιθεατρικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφιθεατρική, neuter αμφιθεατρικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>amphitheatrical</div><b>αμφικλινής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφικλινής, neuter αμφικλινές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. sloping on two sides, not level</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) vacillating</div><b>αμφικτίονες</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>representatives at an amphictyony</div><b>αμφικτιονία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αμφικτιονίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αμφικτυονία">αμφικτυονία</a></div><b>αμφικτιονικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφικτιονική, neuter αμφικτιονικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>amphictyonic, relating to the amphictyony</div><b>αμφικτυονία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αμφικτυονίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>amphictyony</div><b>αμφικτυονικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφικτυονική, neuter αμφικτυονικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αμφικτιονικός">αμφικτιονικός</a></div><b>αμφικτύονες</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αμφικτίονες">αμφικτίονες</a></div><b>αμφιλεγόμενος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αμφιλεγόμενη, neuter αμφιλεγόμενο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>controversial</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αμφιλεγόμενο</b> θέμα - a moot point</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Hellenistic Koine “τά ἀμφιλεγόμενα”, neuter plural of passive present participle ἀμφιλεγόμενος of Ancient Greek verb Ancient Greek ἀμφιλέγω.</div><b>αμφιλογία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αμφιλογίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. ambiguity</div>
  <div class='def'>2. disagreement</div><b>αμφιπρόστυλος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφιπρόστυλη, neuter αμφιπρόστυλο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>amphiprostyle</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Latin amphiprostȳlos.</div><b>αμφιρρέπω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to hesitate, vacillate, waver</div><b>αμφιρρεπής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφιρρεπής, neuter αμφιρρεπές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>hesitant, irresolute, wavering</div><b>αμφισβήτηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αμφισβητήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>contest, dispute, controversy</div><b>αμφισβητήσιμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφισβητήσιμη, neuter αμφισβητήσιμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>contestable, debatable, controversial</div><b>αμφισβητίας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural αμφισβητίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>dissenter</div><b>αμφισβητώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to doubt</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to dispute, contest, question</div><b>αμφισβιτιέμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of αμφισβητούμαι</div><b>αμφισεξουαλικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφισεξουαλική, neuter αμφισεξουαλικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>bisexual</div><b>αμφισημία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αμφισημίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ambiguous words or phrases</div><b>αμφιταλάντευση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αμφιταλαντεύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>hesitation, wavering</div><b>αμφιταλαντεύομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to hesitate, to vacillate, to waver</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀμφιταλαντεύω with semantic loan from French vaciller. By surface analysis, αμφι- (amfi-) + ταλαντεύομαι.</div><b>αμφιτρύωνας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αμφιτρύωνες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>host of a party or dinner, amphitryon</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From proper noun Αμφιτρύωνας. Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek Ἀμφιτρύων from the accusative singular &quot;τόν Ἀμφιτρύωνα&quot; from ἀμφί &amp; τρύω. Semantic loan from French amphitryon from the comedy by Molière Amphitryon, as in the verses:
: le véritable Amphitryon | Est l’Amphitryon où l’on dîne. ― The real Amphitryon is | the Amphitryon with whom one dines.</div><b>αμφιφυλόφιλος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφιφυλόφιλη, neuter αμφιφυλόφιλο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(of people) bisexual, bi (attracted to both sexes)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αμφι- (amfi-, “two, bi-”) + φύλο + -φιλος (-filos, “-friend, -phile”), calque of English bisexual.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αμφιφυλόφιλοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>bisexual (male bisexual)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αμφι- (amfi-, “two, bi-”) + φύλο + -φιλος (-filos, “-friend, -phile”), calque of English bisexual.</div><b>αμφορέας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αμφορείς)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>amphora, urn</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀμφορεύς.</div><b>αμφοτέρωθεν</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>bilaterally</div><b>αμφοτεροβαρής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμφοτεροβαρής, neuter αμφοτεροβαρές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>mutual, reciprocal</div><b>αμφότεροι</b>
  <div><i>pron, masculine (feminine αμφότερες, neuter αμφότερα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(in plural) both</div>
  <div class='ex'>Επιστρατεύει <b>αμφότερους</b> τους γιους του. - He employs both his sons.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Katharevousa.</div><b>αμωλώπιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμωλώπιστη, neuter αμωλώπιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unbruised</div><b>αμόκ</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(indeclinable) amok, amuck</div>
  <div class='ex'>με πιάνει <b>αμόκ</b> - to run amok</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from French amok, from Malay amuk (“to go on a killing spree”).</div><b>αμόλευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμόλευτη, neuter αμόλευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αμόλυντος">αμόλυντος</a></div><b>αμόλημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αμολήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unleashing, letting go</div>
  <div class='def'>2. slackening, loosening</div><b>αμόλυβδος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμόλυβδη, neuter αμόλυβδο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unleaded</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From α- (a-, “un-”) + μόλυβδος.</div><b>αμόλυντος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμόλυντη, neuter αμόλυντο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>pure, chaste</div><b>αμόνι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αμόνια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. anvil (for metal working)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. incus, anvil (bone in the ear)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Ancient Greek ἀκμόνιον, diminutive of ἄκμων.</div><b>αμόνοιαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμόνοιαστη, neuter αμόνοιαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>quarrelsome, difficult to get on with</div><b>αμόρε</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (dated, indeclinable) love (romantic)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (colloquial, indeclinable) lover, flame</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from Italian amore.</div><b>αμόρφωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμόρφωτη, neuter αμόρφωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unlettered, illiterate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. ignorant, uneducated, uncultured</div><b>αμύγδαλο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αμύγδαλα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>almond (nut)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀμύγδαλον, ἀμυγδάλη, of Pre-Greek origin.</div><b>αμύητοι</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/vocative masculine plural of <a href="bword://αμύητος">αμύητος</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>laity</div><b>αμύητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμύητη, neuter αμύητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. uninitiated</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) ignorant</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (as a noun) layperson</div><b>αμύθητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμύθητη, neuter αμύθητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>immeasurable, fabulous, immense</div><b>αμύνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to defend oneself</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to brush off, repel</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀμύνομαι, from the mediopassive voice of Ancient Greek ἀμύνω.</div><b>αμύριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμύριστη, neuter αμύριστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. odourless (UK), odorless (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unsmelled, unsmelt</div><b>αμύρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμύρωτη, neuter αμύρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unanointed (with myrrh)</div><b>αμώμητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αμώμητη, neuter αμώμητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>impeccable, unblemished</div><b>αν</b>
  <div><i>conj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. if</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Αν</b> μπορείτε να έρθετε σήμερα. - If you are able to come today.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. whether</div>
  <div class='ex'>Δεν ξέρω <b>αν</b> είστε στο σπίτι σας. - I don&#x27;t know whether you are at home.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἐάν.</div><b>αν βάζεις τον κώλο σου να σου κάνει δουλειά, σκατά δουλειά θα κάνει</b>
  <div><i>proverb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial, humorous, vulgar) if you pay peanuts, you get monkeys (if one gives a task to someone incompetent, they will receive results of the same standard)</div><b>αν δεν βρέξεις κώλο, ψάρι δεν τρως</b>
  <div><i>proverb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>the cat would eat fish but would not wet her feet (in order to achieve something, it is inevitable and necessary that some sacrifices must occur)</div><b>αν είναι δυνατόν</b>
  <div><i>intj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>you can&#x27;t be serious, you must be joking / kidding, good heavens (expression of shock and/or disbelief)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Αν είναι δυνατόν</b>! Αυτό θα παρουσιάσεις ως έργο τέχνης; - You can&#x27;t be serious! That&#x27;s what you&#x27;re presenting as a work of art?</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Literally, “if it&#x27;s possible”.</div><b>αν είσαι και παπάς, με την αράδα σου θα πας</b>
  <div><i>proverb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>You must wait your turn, no matter who you are.</div><b>αν η γιαγιά μου είχε αρχίδια θα τη φώναζα παππού</b>
  <div><i>proverb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial, humorous) if my aunt had balls, she&#x27;d be my uncle</div><b>αν και</b>
  <div><i>conj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>although, while, though (in spite of the fact that)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Αν και</b> δε συμφωνώ, θα το κάνω. - Although I don&#x27;t agree, I&#x27;ll do it.</div><b>ανά</b>
  <div><i>prep</i></div>
  <div class='def'>per, by, through, throughout</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ανά</b> δύο έτη - every two years</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνά.</div><b>ανάβαθος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάβαθη, neuter ανάβαθο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. shallow, not deep (of water, vessel, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. superficial, shallow</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From ανά- + α- (a-) + βάθος.</div><b>ανάβαθρο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναβάθρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. staircase, stair, steps</div>
  <div class='def'>2. platform, podium</div><b>ανάβαση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναβάσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. going up, ascent</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) ascending to a throne</div><b>ανάβλεμμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναβλέμματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. glance, look, stare</div>
  <div class='def'>2. expression (in the eyes)</div><b>ανάβλεψη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναβλέψεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>seeing again (recovery of vision)</div><b>ανάβλυση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναβλύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>spurt, gushing (upward flow of liquid)</div><b>ανάβολος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάβολη, neuter ανάβολο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>awkward, uncomfortable, inconvenient</div><b>ανάβομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to be lighted, be lit</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to be ignited, be set alight, be set on fire</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to be aroused (sexually), be turned on</div><b>ανάβρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανάβρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>gushing up, seething (as of a spring)</div><b>ανάβραση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναβράσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. ferment, boiling. ebullition</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) commotion, turmoil</div><b>ανάβροχος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάβροχη, neuter ανάβροχο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>rainless, not raining, dry</div><b>ανάβρυσμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναβρύσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>spurt, gushing (upward flow of liquid)</div><b>ανάβω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (transitive) to ignite, to set alight, to set on fire, to light up</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ανάβω</b> φωτιά - I start a fire</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (intransitive) to catch fire</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Άναψε</b> μεγάλη φωτιά στο δάσος. - A big (strong) fire started/began at the forest.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (transitive) to light, to switch on, to turn on (to activate a light)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ανάβω</b> το φως στο δωμάτιο - I switch on the light in the room</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (figuratively, intransitive) to get fired up (to become very emotional or excited)</div>
  <div class='def'>5. (figuratively, transitive) to arouse, to turn on (sexually)</div>
  <div class='def'>6. (figuratively, transitive) to excite, to arouse, to ignite (strong emotions)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀνάβω, from Ancient Greek ἀνάπτω with -πτω &gt; -βω based on the common aorist stem αναψ- in the pattern σκάπτω - aorist ἔσκαψα &gt; έσκαψα - σκάβω</div><b>ανάγκη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανάγκες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. necessity</div>
  <div class='ex'>Από <b>ανάγκη</b> πήγαμε μέσω Λονδίνου. - Out of necessity we went through London.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. need, want, demand</div>
  <div class='ex'>Δεν τον ενδιαφέρουν οι <b>ανάγκες</b> της γυναίκας του. - He is not interested in his wife&#x27;s needs.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (euphemistic) call of nature (need for urination or defecation)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Έχετε τουαλέτα; Πρέπει να κάνω την <b>ανάγκη</b> μου. - Do you have a toilet? I need to go.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀνάγκη.</div><b>ανάγλυφη γραφή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) braille</div><b>ανάγλυφο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανάγλυφα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. relief (the shape of terrain)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. relief, bas relief</div><b>ανάγλυφος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάγλυφη, neuter ανάγλυφο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. relief</div>
  <div class='ex'>ο <b>ανάγλυφος</b> χάρτης της Ελλάδας. - the relief map of Greece.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. in relief</div>
  <div class='def'>3. vivid</div><b>ανάγνωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναγνώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. reading; the oral presentation of a text</div>
  <div class='def'>2. reading; perusal (the activity of viewing and understanding text)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. reading; interpretation (what is understood from a passage of text)</div>
  <div class='def'>4. reading; class activity in school</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνάγνωσις.</div><b>ανάγνωσμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναγνώσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>text, passage (a section of text; especially one for study or which is easily read)</div><b>ανάγομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to originate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to set sail</div><b>ανάγραμμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναγράμματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anagram</div><b>ανάγω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to reduce</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to raise</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to source, reference (identify the origin)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀνάγω.</div><b>ανάγωγος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάγωγη, neuter ανάγωγο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. uncouth, ill-mannered, brusque</div>
  <div class='def'>2. irreducible</div><b>ανάδειξη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναδείξεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. distinction, eminence</div>
  <div class='def'>2. appointment, election</div><b>ανάδελφος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάδελφη, neuter ανάδελφο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>brotherless, sisterless</div><b>ανάδεμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναδέματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fidgetting (UK), fidgeting (US)</div><b>ανάδοση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναδόσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. growth, germination</div>
  <div class='def'>2. soil moisture</div><b>ανάδοχος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάδοχος or ανάδοχη, neuter ανάδοχο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sponsoring</div>
  <div class='ex'>η <b>ανάδοχος</b> εταιρεία - the concessionary (the company holding the concession)</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural ανάδοχοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. contractor</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (dated, formal) godparent, godfather, godmother</div>
  <div class='def'>3. sponsor</div><b>ανάδραση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) feedback (in an electrical or biological process)</div><b>ανάδρομος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάδρομη, neuter ανάδρομο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. backwards going backwards</div>
  <div class='def'>2. anticlockwise (UK), counterclockwise (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. anadromous, returning (of salmon, etc)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Ancient Greek ἀνάδρομος, from ἀνά + δρόμος.</div><b>ανάδυση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναδύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. surface, emerge (from water)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) surface, emerge, become apparent</div><b>ανάερα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>airily, ethereally</div><b>ανάερος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάερη, neuter ανάερο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. airy, ethereal, light, lightweight</div>
  <div class='def'>2. in the air, hovering</div><b>ανάθεμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναθέματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. curse (prayer or imprecation that harm may befall someone)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) anathema (something which is vehemently disliked by somebody)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Υπήρξε το <b>ανάθεμα</b> της οικογένειας όταν παντρεύτηκε αλλοδαπή. - He was anathema to his family when he married a foreigner.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. excommunication (in Orthodox contexts)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η Εκκλησία απήγγειλε το <b>ανάθεμα</b> εναντίον του Βενιζέλου το 1916. - The Church ordered the excommunication of Venizelos in 1916.</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (figuratively) cursed place, Hell</div>
  <div class='ex'>Άμε στ’ <b>ανάθεμα</b>! - Go to hell!</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνάθεμα, from ἀνατίθημι, from ἀνά + τίθημι.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>intj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>damn, curse (used to express anger, irritation, disappointment, annoyance, contempt)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ανάθεμα</b> το - damn it</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνάθεμα, from ἀνατίθημι, from ἀνά + τίθημι.</div><b>ανάθεση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναθέσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>assignment, dedication</div><b>ανάθημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναθήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. donation</div>
  <div class='def'>2. votive offering</div>
  <div class='def'>3. accompaniment or accessory</div><b>ανάθρεμμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναθρέμματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nurture, upbringing</div><b>ανάκαμψη</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανακάμψεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>recovery</div><b>ανάκατα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>in a disorderly way: topsy-turvy, higgledy-piggledy</div><b>ανάκατος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάκατη, neuter ανάκατο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. mingled, mixed</div>
  <div class='def'>2. mixed up, disorderly</div>
  <div class='def'>3. tangled, tousled</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀνάκατος, from an earlier unattested form *ἀνώκατος with phonetic influence from ἀνά, from a univerbation of ἄνω κάτω, literally “upwards downwards”.</div><b>ανάκλαση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακλάσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. reflection (heat, light, sound, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. response, reflex (to stimulus)</div><b>ανάκληση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) annulment, invalidation, cancellation</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) recall (ambassador)</div><b>ανάκλιντρο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανάκλιντρα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>chaise longue (UK), chaise lounge (US)</div><b>ανάκουστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάκουστη, neuter ανάκουστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανήκουστος">ανήκουστος</a></div><b>ανάκριση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακρίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. cross-examination, examination</div>
  <div class='def'>2. interrogation, questioning</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (broadly) interrogator, cross-examiner</div><b>ανάκρουση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακρούσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. recoil (of a gun)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. striking up, playing (especially of a rousing piece)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. backing off, backing out</div>
  <div class='def'>4. going astern</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνάκρουσις, from ἀνακρούω, from ἀνά + κρούω.</div><b>ανάκρουσμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανακρούσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. striking up, playing</div>
  <div class='def'>2. recoil (of a gun)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. reversing, backing, backing out</div><b>ανάκτηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακτήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>retrieval, recovery</div><b>ανάκτορο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανάκτορα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>palace</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀνάκτορα (plural form), from Ancient Greek ἀνάκτορον, from ἄνᾰξ.</div><b>ανάκυψη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακύψεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. straightening up (upright posture)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. straightening out, correcting</div><b>ανάλαδος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάλαδη, neuter ανάλαδο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. without oil</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unanointed</div><b>ανάλατος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάλατη, neuter ανάλατο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unsalted, without salt</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) bland, uninspiring</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀνάλατος. By surface analysis, αν- (an-, “un-”) + αλάτ(ι), “salt”) + -ος (-os, adjectival suffix).</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανάλατοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>red valerian</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Substantivised masculine of the [[#Adjective]].</div><b>ανάλαφρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάλαφρη, neuter ανάλαφρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>light, lightweight, lightsome, airy, ethereal</div><b>ανάλγητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάλγητη, neuter ανάλγητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. insensible</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) callous, insensitive</div><b>ανάλεκτα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>analects, analecta, chosen passages</div><b>ανάλεκτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάλεκτη, neuter ανάλεκτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>describing analects, chosen passages</div><b>ανάλεστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάλεστη, neuter ανάλεστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unground</div><b>ανάληψη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναλήψεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. withdrawal (from bank account)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. assumption, taking on, undertaking (the act of taking to or upon oneself)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. Ascension (the believed entry of Jesus Christ into heaven after his resurrection)</div>
  <div class='def'>4. alternative letter-case form of <a href="bword://Ανάληψη">Ανάληψη</a> (holiday celebrating the Ascension of Jesus)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀνάληψις with semantic loan from French prélèvement in the financial sense.</div><b>ανάλλαχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάλλαχτη, neuter ανάλλαχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unchanged, unaltered</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unchanged (clothes)</div><b>ανάλογα</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>neuter nominative/accusative/vocative plural of <a href="bword://ανάλογος">ανάλογος</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. proportionally, proportionately</div>
  <div class='def'>2. accordingly</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ανάλογα</b> με - according to, in accordance with, depending on</div>
  <div class='def'>3. analogously</div><b>ανάλογος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάλογη, neuter ανάλογο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. proportional, proportionate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. suitable, appropriate</div>
  <div class='def'>3. analogous</div><b>ανάλυση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναλύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. analysis, interpretation</div>
  <div class='def'>2. parsing</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνάλυσις.</div><b>ανάλωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναλώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>consumption, use, expenditure</div><b>ανάμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανάματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>communion wine, sacramental wine</div><b>ανάμεικτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάμεικτη, neuter ανάμεικτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>mixed, blended, mingled, assorted</div><b>ανάμειξη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναμείξεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. involvement, meddling</div>
  <div class='def'>2. mixture, blend, mingling</div><b>ανάμελα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>carelessly, nonchalantly</div><b>ανάμερος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάμερη, neuter ανάμερο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. secluded, remote</div>
  <div class='def'>2. out of the way</div><b>ανάμεσα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. among, amongst</div>
  <div class='def'>2. between, among</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το τοπίο <b>ανάμεσα</b> στα δυο χωριά είναι μαγευτικό. - The countryside between the two villages is spectacular.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. compared to</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (figuratively) between</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Ανάμεσα</b> στους δυο παλιούς φίλους υπάρχει τώρα ένα χάσμα. - There is now a gap between the two old friends.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀνάμεσα, from ἀνάμεσον, from Ancient Greek ἀνάμεσος, from ᾰ̓νᾰ- + μέσος.</div><b>ανάμεσος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάμεση, neuter ανάμεσο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>between, in between</div><b>ανάμικτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάμικτη, neuter ανάμικτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανάμεικτος">ανάμεικτος</a></div><b>ανάμιξη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναμίξεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανάμειξη">ανάμειξη</a></div><b>ανάμνηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναμνήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>memory</div><b>ανάμπαιγμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναμπαίγματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. laughing stock</div>
  <div class='def'>2. mocking</div><b>ανάνηψη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανανήψεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>recover, coming round, resuscitation</div><b>ανάντης</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάντης, neuter άναντες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. uphill, towards the top</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) problematic, unfavourable</div><b>ανάξια</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unworthily</div>
  <div class='def'>2. incompetently</div><b>ανάξιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάξια, neuter ανάξιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unworthy, inadequate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. shameful, undignified</div>
  <div class='def'>3. incompetent</div><b>ανάπαιστος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανάπαιστοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anapaest (UK), anapæst, anapest (US)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνάπαιστος.</div><b>ανάπαλση</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναπαλμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. swing, oscillation</div>
  <div class='def'>2. vibration</div><b>ανάπαυλα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) short break or rest, breather,</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) truce</div><b>ανάπαυση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) rest, sleep</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (euphemistic, uncountable) dead</div><b>ανάπαψη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανάπαυση">ανάπαυση</a></div><b>ανάπεμψη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) reference back, remittance (act and effect)</div><b>ανάπηρη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανάπηρες, masculine ανάπηρος)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>person with disability</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative feminine singular of <a href="bword://ανάπηρος">ανάπηρος</a></div><b>ανάπηρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάπηρη, neuter ανάπηρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>handicapped, disabled (by injury, illness, etc)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ανάπηρος</b> πολέμου - disabled serviceman</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανάπηροι, feminine ανάπηρη)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>person with disability</div><b>ανάπλαση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναπλάσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>regeneration, renewal</div><b>ανάπλευση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναπλεύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. sailing or going; upstream, upriver</div>
  <div class='def'>2. sailing or going; against the wind</div>
  <div class='def'>3. sailing or going; against the current</div><b>ανάπλους</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανάπλοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. going/sailing; upstream, upriver</div>
  <div class='def'>2. going/sailing; against the wind</div>
  <div class='def'>3. going/sailing; against the current</div><b>ανάπλωρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάπλωρη, neuter ανάπλωρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. sailing or going; upstream, upriver</div>
  <div class='def'>2. sailing or going; against the wind</div>
  <div class='def'>3. sailing or going; against the current</div><b>ανάποδα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. astern</div>
  <div class='def'>2. backwards, the wrong way</div>
  <div class='ex'>ολοταχώς <b>ανάποδα</b>! - full astern!</div>
  <div class='def'>3. upside down</div>
  <div class='ex'>Κρεμάστηκα <b>ανάποδα</b> από το δέντρο. - I hung down upside down from the tree.</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (of clothes) inside out</div>
  <div class='ex'>Είχα περάσει σχεδόν ολόκληρη την ημέρα προτού αντιλήφθηκα ότι φορούσα το πουκάμισο <b>ανάποδα</b>. - I had gone almost the entire day before I realised my shirt was on inside out.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀνὰ πόδα.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://ανάποδος">ανάποδος</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀνὰ πόδα.</div><b>ανάποδη</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανάποδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. wrong side, reverse side</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (colloquial) backhander (blow with the back of the hand)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Όταν με είπε γαϊδούρι του έδωσα μια <b>ανάποδη</b>. - When he called me a jackass I gave him a backhander.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative feminine singular of <a href="bword://ανάποδος">ανάποδος</a></div><b>ανάποδος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάποδη, neuter ανάποδο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. reverse, opposite, contrary (in the other direction or the exact inverse of something)</div>
  <div class='ex'>παίρνω <b>ανάποδες</b> - get pissed off, get very angry</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (of days) off (in which a person is not performing up to their usual level or ability)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ήταν μια από τις <b>ανάποδες</b> μέρες μου. - It was one of my off days.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (of people) awkward, crabbed, cantankerous, contrary (ill-tempered or strange in behaviour and relations with others)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η γιαγιά της είναι πολύ <b>ανάποδη</b> γυναίκα. - Her granny is a very cantankerous woman.</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (of items) awkward, unwieldy (difficult to use)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Δεν μπορώ να χρησιμοποιήσω αυτό το <b>ανάποδο</b> εργαλείο! - I can&#x27;t use this unwieldy tool!</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀνάποδος, from ἀνα- (ana-, “back, backwards”) + ποδός.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανάποδοι, feminine ανάποδη)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial) spoilsport, killjoy (person who is anti-fun, or prevents others from having fun)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Μην είσαι <b>ανάποδος</b>, έλα στο πάρτι! - Don&#x27;t be a spoilsport, come to the party!</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀνάποδος, from ἀνα- (ana-, “back, backwards”) + ποδός.</div><b>ανάπρυμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάπρυμη, neuter ανάπρυμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>having turned to obtain a tailwind or following current</div><b>ανάπρωρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάπρωρη, neuter ανάπρωρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανάπλωρος">ανάπλωρος</a></div><b>ανάπτυγμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναπτύγματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>expansion, development, growth</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek πτύγμα.</div><b>ανάπτυξη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναπτύξεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>growth, development, improvement</div>
  <div class='ex'>βιώσιμη <b>ανάπτυξη</b> - sustainable development</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνάπτυξις.</div><b>ανάρια</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. thinly, sparsely, loosely</div>
  <div class='def'>2. seldom</div><b>ανάριος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάρια, neuter ανάριο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. thin; watery, dilute</div>
  <div class='def'>2. thin; loosely woven</div>
  <div class='def'>3. thin; rare, spread thinly, sparse, scattered</div><b>ανάριχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάριχτη, neuter ανάριχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανάρριχτος">ανάρριχτος</a></div><b>ανάρκωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάρκωτη, neuter ανάρκωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. not anaesthetised (UK), not anesthetized (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. make (someone) sleepy</div><b>ανάρμεγος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάρμεγη, neuter ανάρμεγο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unmilked</div><b>ανάρμεχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάρμεχτη, neuter ανάρμεχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανάρμεγος">ανάρμεγος</a></div><b>ανάρμοστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάρμοστη, neuter ανάρμοστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>improper, indecorous, indecent</div><b>ανάρπαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάρπαστη, neuter ανάρπαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. readily saleable (UK), salable (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. attractive, snapped up</div><b>ανάρρηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναρρήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accession (to high office)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. rise (in rank)</div><b>ανάρριχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάρριχτη, neuter ανάρριχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>over one&#x27;s shoulder</div><b>ανάρρωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) recovery, recuperation, convalescence</div><b>ανάρτηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναρτήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. hanging, suspending (of a picture, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (plural normally) suspension (of machinery, motor vehicles, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) post (display message)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From the Ancient Greek ἀνάρτησις.</div><b>ανάσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανάσες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. breathing</div>
  <div class='def'>2. breath</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Nominal formation from ανασαίνω.</div><b>ανάσαση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) respite, relief</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) breather (time to take breath)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (uncountable) breathing</div><b>ανάσκελα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>supinely, on your back</div><b>ανάσκελος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάσκελη, neuter ανάσκελο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(rare) supine (on your back)</div><b>ανάσκητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάσκητη, neuter ανάσκητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>untrained</div><b>ανάσταση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναστάσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>revival, resurrection</div><b>ανάστατος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάστατη, neuter ανάστατο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>agitated, disturbed, flustered</div><b>ανάστερος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάστερη, neuter ανάστερο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. starless (cloudy)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) unlucky</div><b>ανάστημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναστήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. height, stature (of a person)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) stature (moral)</div><b>ανάστροφη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναστροφές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. blow with the back of the hand, backhander</div>
  <div class='def'>2. alternative form of <a href="bword://αναστροφή">αναστροφή</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative feminine singular of <a href="bword://ανάστροφος">ανάστροφος</a></div><b>ανάστροφος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανάστροφη, neuter ανάστροφο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. upside-down, inverted</div>
  <div class='def'>2. reversed, reverse</div><b>ανάσχεση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανασχέσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. halting, stopping</div>
  <div class='def'>2. containment</div>
  <div class='def'>3. interception</div><b>ανάταξη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανατάξεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. taxis, resetting</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) repositioning</div><b>ανάταση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανατάσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. buoyancy, uplift</div>
  <div class='def'>2. raising of the arms upwards and outwards in joy or exercise</div><b>ανάτυπο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανάτυπα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>offprint, reprint</div><b>ανάφαση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αναφάσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) anaphase</div><b>ανάφλεξη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναφλέξεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>combustion, ignition, the process of burning</div><b>ανάχωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναχώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. embankment, bank</div>
  <div class='def'>2. mound</div><b>ανέβασμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανεβάσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. climb, ascent, going up</div>
  <div class='def'>2. mounting, boarding, getting on</div>
  <div class='def'>3. mounting (production)</div><b>ανέγγιχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέγγιχτη, neuter ανέγγιχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>untouched, unwounded, intact</div><b>ανέγγυος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέγγυα, neuter ανέγγυο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unsecured, unguaranteed</div><b>ανέγερση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανεγέρσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>erection</div><b>ανέγκλητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέγκλητη, neuter ανέγκλητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unindictable</div><b>ανέγνιαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέγνιαστη, neuter ανέγνιαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανέγνοιαστος">ανέγνοιαστος</a></div><b>ανέγνοιαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέγνοιαστη, neuter ανέγνοιαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. carefree, unworried, untroubled</div>
  <div class='def'>2. easy-going</div><b>ανέγνωμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέγνωμη, neuter ανέγνωμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unopinionated</div><b>ανέγνωρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέγνωρη, neuter ανέγνωρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial) unrecognisable, unfamiliar</div><b>ανέκαθεν</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>always, all along, from the beginning</div><b>ανέκδοτο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανέκδοτα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. anecdote (a short, entertaining account of an incident)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. joke</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From the neuter singular nominative of ανέκδοτος, i.e. an &quot;unpublished account&quot; &gt; &quot;short entertaining account&quot;.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://ανέκδοτος">ανέκδοτος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://ανέκδοτος">ανέκδοτος</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From the neuter singular nominative of ανέκδοτος, i.e. an &quot;unpublished account&quot; &gt; &quot;short entertaining account&quot;.</div><b>ανέκδοτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέκδοτη, neuter ανέκδοτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unpublished</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Koine Greek ἀνέκδοτος.</div><b>ανέκκλητα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>irrevocably, irreversibly</div><b>ανέκκλητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέκκλητη, neuter ανέκκλητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. irreversible, irrevocable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unappealable</div><b>ανέκφραστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέκφραστη, neuter ανέκφραστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. expressionless, poker faced, with vacant look</div>
  <div class='def'>2. inexpressible, indescribable (happiness, joy, etc)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀνέκφρασστος.</div><b>ανέλεγκτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέλεγκτη, neuter ανέλεγκτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>uncontrolled, unchecked, unrestricted</div><b>ανέλιξη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανελίξεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>evolution</div><b>ανέλκυση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. raising, hoisting</div>
  <div class='def'>2. refloating</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀνέλκυ(σις)) + -ση (-si).</div><b>ανέλπιδος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέλπιδη, neuter ανέλπιδο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>hopeless, without hope</div><b>ανέλπιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέλπιστη, neuter ανέλπιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unhoped-for, unexpected</div><b>ανέμελος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέμελη, neuter ανέμελο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. negligent, careless, lackadaisical</div>
  <div class='def'>2. carefree, nonchalant, casual</div><b>ανέμη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανέμες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. yarn winder, weasel, swift, reel</div>
  <div class='def'>2. trawlnet, dragnet</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Koine Greek ἀνέμη, from Ancient Greek ἄνεμος m.</div><b>ανέμισμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανεμίσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. winnowing, airing</div>
  <div class='def'>2. waving, flapping</div><b>ανέμπιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέμπιστη, neuter ανέμπιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>untrustworthy, unreliable, suspicious</div><b>ανέμπνευστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέμπνευστη, neuter ανέμπνευστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(neologism) uninspired, unimaginative</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αν- (an-, “not”, negating prefix) + εμπνέω + -τος (-tos, adjectival suffix).</div><b>ανέμυαλος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέμυαλη, neuter ανέμυαλο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://άμυαλος">άμυαλος</a></div><b>ανένδοτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανένδοτη, neuter ανένδοτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>firm, inflexible, unyielding</div><b>ανέντακτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέντακτη, neuter ανέντακτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανένταχτος">ανένταχτος</a></div><b>ανένταχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανένταχτη, neuter ανένταχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not a member, unaffiliated (of party or organisation)</div><b>ανέντιμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέντιμη, neuter ανέντιμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>dishonest, untrustworthy</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from αν- (an-, α- privative) + έντιμος.</div><b>ανέξοδος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέξοδη, neuter ανέξοδο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. free, free of charge, costless, gratis</div>
  <div class='def'>2. inexpensive</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> According to Petrounias αν- (an-, α- privative) + έξοδο + -ος (-os), different from the Hellenistic ἀνέξοδος. According to Babiniotis, from ἀνέξοδος, the modern sense being attested since 4th century.</div><b>ανέπαφος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέπαφη, neuter ανέπαφο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. untouched, not used</div>
  <div class='def'>2. intact, unharmed</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνέπαφος.</div><b>ανέραστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέραστη, neuter ανέραστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unloved, loveless</div>
  <div class='def'>2. not lusted after</div><b>ανέρχεται σε</b>
  <div><i>phrase</i></div>
  <div class='def'>it amounts to</div><b>ανέρχομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to rise, move up</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to amount</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀνέρχομαι. By surface analysis, αν- (an-, “up”, from ανα- (ana-)) + έρχομαι.
For sense amount: semantic loan from French s&#x27;élever.</div><b>ανέρχομαι σε</b>
  <div><i>phrase</i></div>
  <div class='def'>total, add up to, amounts to</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ο συνολικός προϋπολογισμός <b>ανέρχεται</b> σε 500 εκατομμύρια ευρώ. - The total budget amounts to 500 million euros.</div><b>ανέρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέρωτη, neuter ανέρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. with no added water; unadulterated, unwatered</div>
  <div class='def'>2. with no added water; neat (UK), straight (US)</div><b>ανέσπερος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέσπερη, neuter ανέσπερο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>never-failing, never-setting</div>
  <div class='ex'>το <b>ανέσπερο</b> φως - the never-failing light</div><b>ανέστιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέστια, neuter ανέστιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (literally) hearthless</div>
  <div class='def'>2. homeless</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνέστιος. By surface analysis, αν- (an-, negationary prefix) + εστία + -ος (-os, adjectival suffix).</div><b>ανέτοιμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέτοιμη, neuter ανέτοιμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unready, unprepared</div>
  <div class='def'>2. slow (in response)</div><b>ανέφελος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέφελη, neuter ανέφελο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. cloudless</div>
  <div class='def'>2. cloudless, happy</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From νέφος.</div><b>ανέφικτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανέφικτη, neuter ανέφικτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unattainable, unachievable, impossible, infeasible, unfeasible</div><b>ανέχεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) poverty, neediness</div><b>ανέχομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>tolerate, put up with, bear</div><b>ανήθικος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανήθικη, neuter ανήθικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. immoral, obscene</div>
  <div class='def'>2. amoral</div><b>ανήκεστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανήκεστη, neuter ανήκεστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>irreparable, incurable (usually only found in the phrase indicated)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ανήκεστη</b>/<b>ανήκεστος</b> βλάβη - irreparable damage</div><b>ανήκουστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανήκουστη, neuter ανήκουστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unheard, unheard of, inaudible</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) unique</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) heard for the first time</div><b>ανήκω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to belong</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀνήκω, from Ancient Greek ἀνά + ἥκω.</div><b>ανήλιαγος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανήλιαγη, neuter ανήλιαγο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sunless</div><b>ανήλιαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανήλιαστη, neuter ανήλιαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανήλιαγος">ανήλιαγος</a></div><b>ανήλικος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανήλική, neuter ανήλικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>underage, minor</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀνήλικος.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανήλικοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>minor, underage</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀνήλικος.</div><b>ανήλιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανήλια, neuter ανήλιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sunless</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀνήλιος.</div><b>ανήμερα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>on the day, on the same day, on the actual day</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Ανήμερα</b> το Πάσχα ψήνεται το αρνί στη σούβλα. - On the day of Easter lamb is roasted on the spit.</div><b>ανήμερος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανήμερη, neuter ανήμερο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. fierce, wild, savage</div>
  <div class='def'>2. untameable</div><b>ανήμπορος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανήμπορη, neuter ανήμπορο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>poorly, groggy, seedy, indisposed</div><b>ανήξερος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανήξερη, neuter ανήξερο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ignorant, uninformed</div><b>ανήρ</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural άνδρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(archaic) the Ancient Greek ἀνήρ typed in monotonic script in modern texts</div>
  <div class='ex'>Standard Modern Greek: άνδρας (ándras)</div><b>ανήστευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανήστευτη, neuter ανήστευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(food) permitted whilst fasting</div><b>ανήσυχος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανήσυχη, neuter ανήσυχο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. worried, anxious, uneasy, concerned</div>
  <div class='def'>2. restless, uneasy</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀνήσυχος.</div><b>ανήφορος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανήφοροι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανηφόρα">ανηφόρα</a></div><b>ανήψι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανήψια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nonstandard spelling of <a href="bword://ανίψι">ανίψι</a></div><b>ανία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) boredom, tedium, ennui</div>
  <div class='ex'>[...] κι ο Μάνος, για να διασκεδάσει την <b>ανία</b> του άρχισε να περιεργάζεται τους δέκα ανθρώπους του σαλονιού. - … and Manos, in order to disperse his boredom, he began to scrutinize the ten people in the living room.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀνία &amp; Semantic loan from French ennui.</div><b>ανίατος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανίατη, neuter ανίατο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>incurable, cureless (of a disease)</div><b>ανίδεος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανίδεη, neuter ανίδεο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unsuspecting, naive</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το έκαναν για να καλύψουν το γεγονός πως είναι <b>ανίδεοι</b>. - They did it to cover up the fact that they are clueless.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. ignorant</div>
  <div class='ex'>Εννοούσες «θεαματικά <b>ανίδεος</b>» με την καλή έννοια; - Did you mean &quot;spectacularly ignorant&quot; in a nice way?</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (as a noun) ignoramus</div><b>ανίδρυση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανιδρύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(archaic, formal) rebuilding, reconstruction</div><b>ανίδρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανίδρωτη, neuter ανίδρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. without sweat, without sweating, without perspiration</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) without trying, without making an effort</div><b>ανίδωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανίδωτη, neuter ανίδωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. without being seen, invisible, unseen</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unmet, unseen</div><b>ανίερος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανίερη, neuter ανίερο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. profane, sacrilegious</div>
  <div class='def'>2. ungodly, impious</div>
  <div class='def'>3. unhallowed, unholy</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνίερος, from ἱερός.</div><b>ανίκανος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανίκανη, neuter ανίκανο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. incapable, incompetent, inept</div>
  <div class='def'>2. impotent (sexually)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. unfit (militarily)</div><b>ανίκητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανίκητη, neuter ανίκητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unconquerable, unbeatable</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνίκητος.</div><b>ανίσκιωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανίσκιωτη, neuter ανίσκιωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>shadowless, shadeless</div><b>ανίσταμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to get up, stand up, rise, arise</div>
  <div class='ex'>Χριστός <b>ανέστη</b>! - Christ is risen!</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνίσταμαι.</div><b>ανίσχυρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανίσχυρη, neuter ανίσχυρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. powerless, impotent, feckless</div>
  <div class='def'>2. invalid, null and void</div><b>ανίσως</b>
  <div><i>conj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>if</div><b>ανίχνευση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανιχνεύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>detection, scouting, tracing</div><b>ανίχνευση επαφών</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) contact tracing</div><b>ανίψι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανίψια, masculine ανιψιός, feminine ανιψιά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nephew or niece (son or daughter of one&#x27;s brother or sister)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνεψιός. Cognate with Pontic Greek ανέψ̌ι.</div><b>αναίδεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) lack of modesty and respect; shamelessness, immodesty</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) lack of modesty and respect; impudence, cheek, impertinence, effrontery</div><b>αναίμακτα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. bloodlessly</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) peaceably</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αναίμακτος">αναίμακτος</a></div><b>αναίμακτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναίμακτη, neuter αναίμακτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>bloodless, without bloodshed</div><b>αναίμαχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναίμαχτη, neuter αναίμαχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναίμακτος">αναίμακτος</a></div><b>αναίρεση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναιρέσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. annulment, cassation</div>
  <div class='def'>2. appeal</div>
  <div class='def'>3. retraction</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναίρεσις.</div><b>αναίσθητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναίσθητη, neuter αναίσθητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unconscious, insensible, senseless</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) callous, unfeeling</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναίσθητος. By surface analysis, αν- (an-, α- privative) + αισθητός.</div><b>αναίσχυντος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναίσχυντη, neuter αναίσχυντο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>shameless, effrontery</div><b>αναίτιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναίτια, neuter αναίτιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unjustified, causeless</div>
  <div class='def'>2. innocent, blameless</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀναίτιος. By surface analysis, αν- (an-, α- privative) + αίτιος.</div><b>αναβάθμιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναβαθμίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. upgrade, promotion</div>
  <div class='def'>2. improvement (technology)</div><b>αναβάθρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναβάθρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. gangway, companionway, gangplank</div>
  <div class='def'>2. upward slope into a temple</div>
  <div class='def'>3. rope ladder</div><b>αναβάλλομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be delayed, be postponed</div><b>αναβάλλω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to postpone, put off, delay, procrastinate</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Αναβάλλω</b> συνεχώς να του τηλεφωνήσω. Δεν ξέρω τι να του πω. - I keep postponing this phonecall. I do not know what to say to him.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀναβάλλω. Morphologically ανα- (ana-) + βάλλω.</div><b>αναβάπτιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναβαπτίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>rebaptism</div><b>αναβάπτισμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναβαπτίσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναβάπτιση">αναβάπτιση</a></div><b>αναβάτην</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Katharevousa form of <a href="bword://αναβάτης">αναβάτης</a></div><b>αναβάτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναβάτες, feminine αναβάτρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. rider, horseman</div>
  <div class='def'>2. climber, mountaineer</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αναβάτες</b> των Άλπεων - Alpine mountaineers</div><b>αναβάτου</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Katharevousa form of <a href="bword://αναβάτης">αναβάτης</a></div><b>αναβάτρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναβάτριες, masculine αναβάτης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. rider, horsewoman</div>
  <div class='def'>2. climber</div>
  <div class='ex'>αναβάτριες των Άλπεων (alpine climbers)</div><b>αναβίβαση</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναβιβάσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. mounting (throne)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. mounting (production)</div><b>αναβίωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναβιώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>revival, recovery, resurgence</div><b>αναβαθμίδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναβαθμίδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (formal) step (one to help someone mount somewhere, ie a train or car)</div>
  <div class='ex'>(standard)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. terrace</div>
  <div class='def'>3. terrace (by river)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀναβαθμίς, from ἀνα- (ana-, “up, upwards”) + βαθμίς, from Ancient Greek βαίνω.</div><b>αναβαθμίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to upgrade, promote</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to improve (technology)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From ανα- (ana-) + Ancient Greek βαθμίς + -ίζω. Apparently a calque of English upgrade.</div><b>αναβαθμολογώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to re-mark, regrade</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> By surface analysis, ανα- (ana-) + βαθμολογώ.</div><b>αναβαθμολόγηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναβαθμολογήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>re-marking, regrading</div><b>αναβαθμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναβαθμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>step, ramp</div><b>αναβαλλόμενος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναβαλλόμενοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reprimand, tirade telling off</div>
  <div class='ex'>Μου έψαλε τον <b>αναβαλλόμενο</b>. - [He/she] told me off (literally: He chanted the &#x27;Anavallomenos&#x27; psalm.)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Present participle of αναβάλλομαι, passive voice of αναβάλλω (“to postpone”).
For the noun: word quoted from an ecclesiastical psalm, in jesting manner.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αναβαλλόμενη, neuter αναβαλλόμενο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>being continuously postponed</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Present participle of αναβάλλομαι, passive voice of αναβάλλω (“to postpone”).
For the noun: word quoted from an ecclesiastical psalm, in jesting manner.</div><b>αναβαπτίζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be born again, to be rebaptised</div><b>αναβαπτίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to rebaptise, baptise again</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to rechristen, christen again</div><b>αναβαπτισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναβαπτισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>rebaptism</div><b>αναβαπτιστής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναβαπτιστές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anabaptist</div><b>αναβαστάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to uphold, hold up (high)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ανα- (ana-, “upward”) + βαστάζω</div><b>αναβατήρας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναβατήρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. goods lift, elevator, hoist</div>
  <div class='def'>2. ski lift</div>
  <div class='def'>3. running board, step (on carriage)</div>
  <div class='def'>4. stirrup</div><b>αναβαφτίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναβαπτίζω">αναβαπτίζω</a></div><b>αναβιβάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to lift up</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to increase</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to rise to power</div>
  <div class='def'>4. to move (the accent) to previous syllable</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀναβιβάζω. By surface analysis, ανα- (“re-”) + βιβάζω (“cause to mount”).</div><b>αναβιώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναβιώνω">αναβιώνω</a></div><b>αναβιώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to revive, recover, resurrect</div><b>αναβλέπω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. see again, recover sight</div>
  <div class='def'>2. look up, look towards</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀναβλέπω. By surface analysis, ανα- (ana-) + βλέπω.</div><b>αναβλητικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναβλητική, neuter αναβλητικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>procrastinating, dilatory, delaying</div><b>αναβλητικότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) procrastination, dilatoriness</div><b>αναβλύζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to well, well up, gush, spurt</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to ooze</div><b>αναβολέας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναβολείς)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. stirrup</div>
  <div class='def'>2. stapes, stirrup (bone in the ear)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναβολεύς.</div><b>αναβολή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναβολές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. postponement, delay</div>
  <div class='def'>2. adjournment</div><b>αναβολικά</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αναβολικός">αναβολικός</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anabolic steroid</div><b>αναβολικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναβολική, neuter αναβολικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anabolic</div><b>αναβολισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) anabolism</div><b>αναβοσβήνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to turn on and off (in rapid succession)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to flicker, flash</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Dvandva compound of ανάβ(ω) (“switch on”) + -ο- + σβήνω (“switch off”).</div><b>αναβοώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to shout, yell, yell out</div><b>αναβράζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (literary, past, rare) to boil again</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (literary, past, rare) to seethe, boil up, boil over</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀναβράζω from the ancient ἀναβράσσω.</div><b>αναβρασμός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναβρασμή, neuter αναβρασμό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. boiling up, boiling over, seething</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) boiling over, seething (with anger)</div><b>αναβροχιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) drought, aridity, dryness</div><b>αναβρυτήριο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναβρυτήρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (literary) fountain, water jet</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (literary) spring</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively, literary) gushing</div><b>αναβρύζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναβλύζω">αναβλύζω</a></div><b>αναγάλλια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναγάλλιες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(literary) exultation, joy, jubilation, rejoicing</div><b>αναγάλλιασμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) exultation, joy</div><b>αναγέλασμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναγελάσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ridicule, gibe, scoffing</div><b>αναγέννηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναγεννήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. renewal, rebirth, revival</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (capitalized) Renaissance</div><b>αναγέρνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to recline</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to lie down (for a short while)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek αναγέρνω, from Koine Greek ἀναγείρω, from Ancient Greek ἀνεγείρω.</div><b>αναγαλλίδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναγαλλίδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anagallis (Anagallis-genus plant)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀναγαλλίς, with a semantic loan from translingual Anagallis.</div><b>αναγαλλιάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (transitive) to delight, fill with joy, make happy</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (intransitive) to be joyful, rejoice, be happy</div><b>αναγγέλλομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be announced</div><b>αναγγέλλω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to announce</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to call</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀναγγέλλω. By surface analysis, αν- (an-, from ανα- (ana-)) + αγγέλλω.</div><b>αναγγέλω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>misspelling of <a href="bword://αναγγέλλω">αναγγέλλω</a></div><b>αναγγελία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναγγελίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>notice, announcement, notification</div><b>αναγγελμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αναγγελμένη, neuter αναγγελμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>already announced</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αναγγέλλομαι, passive voice of αγγέλλω (“announce”).</div><b>αναγελώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to mock, sneer at, ridicule</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to be glad</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to be mocked</div><b>αναγεννάω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναγεννώ">αναγεννώ</a></div><b>αναγεννήτρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναγεννήτριες, masculine αναγεννητής)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>regenerator</div><b>αναγεννημένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αναγεννημένη, neuter αναγεννημένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reborn, rejuvenated</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αναγεννώμαι or αναγεννιέμαι, passive voice forms of αναγεννώ, αναγεννάω (“rejuvenate”).</div><b>αναγεννησιακός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναγεννησιακή, neuter αναγεννησιακό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Renaissance</div><b>αναγεννητής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναγεννητές, feminine αναγεννήτρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>regenerator</div><b>αναγεννητικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναγεννητική, neuter αναγεννητικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>regenerative, revivalist</div><b>αναγεννώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to regenerate, rejuvenate</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀναγεννῶ, contracted form of ἀναγεννάω. Morphologically, from ανα- (ana-, “re-”) + γεννώ.</div><b>αναγεννώμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be born again, to be reborn, to be regenerated, to be rejuvenated</div>
  <div class='ex'>Polytonic spelling: ἀναγεννῶμαι</div><b>αναγερτός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναγερτή, neuter αναγερτό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. reclining, taking a lie-down</div>
  <div class='def'>2. taking a nap</div><b>αναγιγνώσκω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(Katharevousa) to read</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀναγιγνώσκω.</div><b>αναγκάζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be compelled</div><b>αναγκάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to compel, coerce</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to obligate</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναγκάζω. By surface analysis, ανάγκη + -άζω.</div><b>αναγκαία</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. nominative/accusative/vocative feminine singular of <a href="bword://αναγκαίος">αναγκαίος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αναγκαίος">αναγκαίος</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>necessities</div>
  <div class='ex'>τα απολύτως <b>αναγκαία</b> της ζωής - the bare necessities of life</div><b>αναγκαία κακά</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative plural of αναγκαίο <a href="bword://κακό">κακό</a>, necessary evils</div><b>αναγκαίο κακό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναγκαία κακά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>necessary evil</div><b>αναγκαίος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναγκαία, neuter αναγκαίο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. necessary, essential</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (as a plural noun) necessities</div>
  <div class='ex'>τα απολύτως <b>αναγκαία</b> της ζωής - the bare necessities of life</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀναγκαῖος, from ἀνάγκη + -ιος (-ios). By surface analysis, ανάγκ(η) + -αίος.</div><b>αναγκαιότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναγκαιότητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>necessity</div><b>αναγκασμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναγκασμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>compulsion, coercion</div><b>αναγκαστικά</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αναγκαστικός">αναγκαστικός</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to have to, to be forced to, perforce (by constraint of circumstances)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. necessarily, of necessity</div><b>αναγκαστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναγκαστική, neuter αναγκαστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>compulsory, obligatory</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αναγκαστική</b> προσγείωση - forced landing</div><b>αναγλείφομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to lick one&#x27;s lips</div><b>αναγνωρίζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to be recognised, be identified</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to be acknowledged</div><b>αναγνωρίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to recognise (UK), recognize (US):; to identify</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to recognise (UK), recognize (US):; to acknowledge, admit</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Αναγνωρίζω</b> τα λάθη μου. - I admit my mistakes.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀναγνωρίζω. From the sense &quot;admit&quot; Semantic loan from French reconnaître. Morphologically, from ανα- (ana-, “repeated”) + γνωρίζω.</div><b>αναγνωρίσιμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναγνωρίσιμη, neuter αναγνωρίσιμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>recognisable (UK), recognizable (US)</div><b>αναγνωρισμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αναγνωρισμένη, neuter αναγνωρισμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. identified, recognised (UK), recognized (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. acknowledged</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αναγνωρίζομαι, passive voice of αναγνωρίζω (“I recognize”).</div><b>αναγνωριστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναγνωριστική, neuter αναγνωριστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reconnoitring</div><b>αναγνωσεις</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of αναγνώσεις</div><b>αναγνωσιμότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναγνωσιμότητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. readability, legibility (property of being capable of being read)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Είναι ένα πολύ δύσκολο κείμενο που δεν έχει καθόλου σχεδόν <b>αναγνωσιμότητα</b>. - It&#x27;s a very difficult article that has almost no readability.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (Internet) readership, ratings (number of people who read a certain written publication)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η <b>αναγνωσιμότητα</b> των εφημερίδων συνεχίζει να πέφτει. - The readership of newspapers continues to fall.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αναγνώσιμος + -ότητα, calque of English readability.</div><b>αναγνωσματάριο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναγνωσματάρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. primer, reader (elementary reading book)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. school book</div><b>αναγνωστήρι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναγνωστήρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>lectern</div><b>αναγνωστήριο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναγνωστήρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reading room (usually in library or school)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναγνωστήριον.</div><b>αναγνωστικό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναγνωστικά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. primer, reader (elementary reading book)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. school book</div><b>αναγνωστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναγνωστική, neuter αναγνωστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reading</div>
  <div class='ex'>το <b>αναγνωστικό</b> κοινό - the reading public</div><b>αναγνώριση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναγνωρίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. recognition</div>
  <div class='def'>2. acknowledgment</div>
  <div class='def'>3. identification</div>
  <div class='def'>4. reconnaissance, recce, recon</div><b>αναγνώσιμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναγνώσιμη, neuter αναγνώσιμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. literate (able to read)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. legible, readable (able to be read)</div><b>αναγνώστης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναγνώστες, feminine αναγνώστρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (in plural) readership</div>
  <div class='def'>2. lay reader (person who is not ordained but is appointed to lead Church services)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (Internet) reader (someone who reads a written publication or website)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Δωρεάν CD για τους <b>αναγνώστες</b> μας σήμερα. - A free CD for our readers today.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀναγνώστης (1st century BC), from ἀνάγνωσ(ις), “recognition; reading, reading aloud”) + -της.
The ecclesiastic term, since the mediaeval times.</div><b>αναγνώστρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναγνώστριες, masculine αναγνώστης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(Internet) reader (someone who reads a written publication or website)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Μια εξοργισμένη <b>αναγνώστρια</b> έγραψε στην εφημερίδα να διαμαρτυρηθεί. - A furious reader wrote to the paper to complain.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αναγνώστης + -τρια (-tria). First attested 1851.</div><b>αναγομώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to reload, recharge (gun or cartridge)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to retread a tyre (UK), recap a tire (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to refill, recharge (eg fire exinguisher)</div><b>αναγορεύομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be nominated, be elected</div><b>αναγορεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to nominate, vote</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to appoint, proclaim</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Αναγορεύτηκε</b> διδάκτορας στο πανεπιστήμιο. - He was proclaimed doctor/professor at the university.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναγορεύω. Morphologically, from (ανα-) αν- (“re-”) + αγορεύω.</div><b>αναγουλιάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to nauseate, make queasy (make liable to vomit)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to disgust</div><b>αναγουλιαστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναγουλιαστική, neuter αναγουλιαστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. nauseating, sickening (causing nausea)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) loathsome</div><b>αναγούλα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναγούλες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. a stomach discomfort with a desire to vomit, nausea</div>
  <div class='def'>2. nausea (strong dislike or disgust)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. motion sickness, seasickness</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (figuratively) disgust, repugnance</div><b>αναγούλιασμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναγουλιάσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nausea</div><b>αναγράφομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be inscribed</div><b>αναγράφω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to inscribe, record, publish</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to insert, enter, record (make an entry, enter a record)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀναγράφω. Morphologically, from ανα- (“up”) + γράφω (“write”).</div><b>αναγραμματίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to anagram, make an anagram, anagrammatise (UK), anagrammatize (US)</div><b>αναγραμματισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναγραμματισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. anagrammatisation (UK), anagrammatization (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. anagram</div><b>αναγραφή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναγραφές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. record, entry</div>
  <div class='def'>2. writing</div><b>αναγυρίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to turn over, turn, invert</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to return</div><b>αναγωγή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. abstract reference to something well known</div>
  <div class='def'>2. reduction</div>
  <div class='def'>3. reduction</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀναγωγή.</div><b>αναγωγικό μέσο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reducing agent</div><b>αναγωγικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναγωγική, neuter αναγωγικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. reducing, reductive</div>
  <div class='def'>2. reducing</div>
  <div class='def'>3. converting</div><b>αναγόμωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναγομώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. retreading a tyre (UK)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. recapping a tire (US)</div><b>αναγόρευση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναγορεύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. nomination, election</div>
  <div class='def'>2. proclamation, acclamation</div><b>αναδάσωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναδασώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reforestation</div><b>αναδένω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to tie up, truss</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to attach a rope (to be taken in tow)</div><b>αναδέχομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to become a sponsor or godparent</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to stand surety</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to undertake an obligation</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ᾰ̓νᾰδέχομαι. Sense &quot;become godparent&quot; since mediaeval times. By surface analysis, ανα- (“re-, again”) + δέχομαι (“accept”).</div><b>αναδίδω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to give off steam, steam</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to smell</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to give off, emit</div>
  <div class='def'>4. to exhale, breathe out</div><b>αναδίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναδίδω">αναδίδω</a></div><b>αναδίπλωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναδιπλώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (rhetoric) anadiplosis</div>
  <div class='def'>2. retreat, fall back, withdrawal</div>
  <div class='def'>3. refolding</div><b>αναδίφηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναδιφήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>rummage, scrutiny</div><b>αναδαν.</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://αναδανεισμός">αναδανεισμός</a>: reborrowing</div><b>αναδανεισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναδανεισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>a more recent reborrowing of a term originating from the same language</div>
  <div class='ex'>abbreviation: αναδαν. (anadan.)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Calque of English reborrowing. Morphologically, ανα- (ana-, “re-”) + δανεισμός m. Literally: borrowing again.</div><b>αναδασμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναδασμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. redistribution (of land)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. redistribution (of wealth, etc)</div><b>αναδασωτέος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναδασωτέα, neuter αναδασωτέο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reforested (or due to be)</div><b>αναδασώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to reforest, reafforest</div><b>αναδείχνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναδεικνύομαι">αναδεικνύομαι</a></div><b>αναδείχνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναδεικνύω">αναδεικνύω</a></div><b>αναδεικνύομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to be emphasised, be shown off</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to be distinguished, gain distinction, make one&#x27;s mark</div><b>αναδεικνύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to reveal, show off, promote, emphasise</div>
  <div class='ex'>Tο απλό φόρεμα <b>αναδεικνύει</b> όλη την ομορφιά της. - The simple dress shows off all her beauty.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to distinguish, appoint</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀναδείκνυμι and ἀναδεικνύω.</div><b>αναδεκτή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναδεκτές, masculine αναδεκτός)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>goddaughter</div><b>αναδεκτός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναδεκτοί, feminine αναδεκτή)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>godson, godchild</div><b>αναδενδράδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναδενδράδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. arbour (UK), arbor (UK)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. bower, pergola</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀναδενδράς</div><b>αναδεξιμιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναδεξιμιές, masculine αναδεξιμιός)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>goddaughter</div><b>αναδεξιμιός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναδεξιμιοί, feminine αναδεξιμιά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>godson, godchild</div><b>αναδεχτή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναδεχτές, masculine αναδεχτός)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναδεκτή">αναδεκτή</a></div><b>αναδεχτός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναδεχτοί, feminine αναδεχτή)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναδεκτός">αναδεκτός</a></div><b>αναδεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to agitate (mix vigorously, particularly mechanically, to produce even mixture)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to stir (for example: coffee)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to fidget, stir</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀναδεύω. By surface analysis, ανα- (“re”) + δεύω.</div><b>αναδημιουργία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) regeneration; rebuilding, redevelopment</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) regeneration; recreation (of lost tissue)</div><b>αναδημιουργημένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αναδημιουργημένη, neuter αναδημιουργημένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>regenerated, recreated</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αναδημιουργούμαι, passive voice of αναδημιουργώ (“Ι recreate”). Morphologically, ανα- (ana-, “re-”) + δημιουργημένος.</div><b>αναδημιουργικά</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>recreatively</div><b>αναδημιουργικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναδημιουργική, neuter αναδημιουργικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>recreative, regenerative</div><b>αναδημιουργός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναδημιουργοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>recreator, regenerator</div><b>αναδημιουργώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to regenerate, recreate</div><b>αναδημοσίευση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναδημοσιεύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reissue, republication</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From the Ancient Greek ἔκδοσις.</div><b>αναδημοσιεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>No definition available</div><b>αναδιάρθρωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναδιαρθρώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>restructuring, reorganisation (UK), reorganization (US)</div><b>αναδιανέμω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to redistribute, distribute</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to share, share out</div><b>αναδιανομή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναδιανομές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>redeployment, redistribution</div><b>αναδιαρθρώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to restructure</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to reassemble</div><b>αναδιορίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to reappoint</div><b>αναδιοργάνωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναδιοργανώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reorganisation (UK), reorganization (US)</div><b>αναδιοργανώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to reorganise (UK), reorganize (US)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ανα- (ana-, “repeat”) + διοργανώνω.</div><b>αναδιοργανώτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reorganiser (UK), reorganizer (US)</div><b>αναδιορισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναδιορισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reappointment</div><b>αναδιπλασιάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to redouble</div><b>αναδιπλασιασμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναδιπλασιασμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>redoubling, reduplication</div><b>αναδιπλώνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to retreat, withdraw</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to withdraw into oneself</div><b>αναδιπλώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to faulter, wobble</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to refold</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to collapse</div><b>αναδιφώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to scrutinise (UK), scrutinize (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to rummage, search, turn over</div><b>αναδομώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to restructure, reshuffle</div><b>αναδουλειά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναδουλειές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unemployment, joblessness</div>
  <div class='def'>2. slack time, slack business</div><b>αναδοχή</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναδοχές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. the acceptance of:; responsibility</div>
  <div class='def'>2. the acceptance of:; an obligation</div><b>αναδρομή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναδρομές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. recursion, regression, retrospection</div>
  <div class='def'>2. flashback</div>
  <div class='def'>3. recursion</div><b>αναδρομικά</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>retrospectively</div><b>αναδρομικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναδρομική, neuter αναδρομικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. back, backwards</div>
  <div class='def'>2. retrospective, retroactive</div><b>αναδρομικότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) retrospectivity, retroactivity</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) retrospectivity</div><b>αναδόμηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναδομήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>restructuring, reform, reshuffle</div><b>αναδύομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to surface, emerge, rise to the surface</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to rise from obscurity</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ᾰ̓νᾰδύομαι, middle voice of ᾰ̓νᾰδύω (“surface”). Morphologically, from ανα- (“re-”) + δύομαι, passive of δύω (“sink, plunge”).</div><b>αναερόβιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναερόβια, neuter αναερόβιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anaerobic</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αναερόβια</b> άσκηση - anaerobic exercise</div><b>αναζήτηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναζητήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. search, quest</div>
  <div class='def'>2. investigation</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναζήτησις.</div><b>αναζήτηση στέγης</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>house-hunting</div><b>αναζητάω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to look for, seek, search for</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to rummage</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to pursue</div>
  <div class='def'>4. to long for</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From the modern αναζητ(ώ) + -άω, from Ancient Greek ἀναζητῶ, contracted form of ἀναζητέω. By surface analysis, ανα- (ana-, “re-”) + ζητάω.</div><b>αναζητημένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αναζητημένη, neuter αναζητημένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>searched for</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αναζητούμαι, passive voice of αναζητώ (“seek, search for”) and of αναζητιέμαι, passive voice of αναζητάω / αναζητώ. Morphologically, ανα- (ana-, “re-”) + ζητημένος.</div><b>αναζητητής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναζητητές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>searcher, seeker</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αναζητώ + -τής.</div><b>αναζητιέμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναζητούμαι">αναζητούμαι</a></div><b>αναζητούμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be sought, be looked for</div><b>αναζητώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναζητάω">αναζητάω</a></div><b>αναζωογονητικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναζωογονητική, neuter αναζωογονητικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>revitalising (UK), revitalizing (US), invigorating</div><b>αναζωογονούμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be revitalised, be revived</div><b>αναζωογονώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to revive, revitalise (UK), revitalize (US)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀναζωογονῶ. Semantic loan from French ranimer. Morphologically analysed as ανα- (ana-, “re-”) + ζωογονώ.</div><b>αναζωογόνηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναζωογόνησεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. revival, enlivening, animation</div>
  <div class='def'>2. revitalisation (UK), revitalization (US)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Calque of French réanimation. Morphologically, from αναζωογονη- (“stem from αναζωογονώ, revitilise”) + -ση (“from suffix -σις”)</div><b>αναζωπυρώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to rekindle (physically and figuratively)</div><b>αναζωπυρώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(transitive) to rekindle (physically and figuratively)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀναζωπυρῶ with -ώνω suffix, from Ancient Greek ἀναζωπυρέω.</div><b>αναζωπύρωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναζωπυρώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. resurgence</div>
  <div class='def'>2. rekindling</div><b>αναθάλλω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (formal, rare, verb) to bloom again, flower again</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively, formal) to flourish again, born again</div><b>αναθάρρηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) courage, regaining courage</div><b>αναθέρμανση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναθερμάνσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. revitalisation (UK), revitalization (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. revival, upturn</div>
  <div class='def'>3. rekindling</div><b>αναθέτομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>misconstruction of ανατίθεμαι, passive of <a href="bword://αναθέτω">αναθέτω</a></div><b>αναθέτω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to assign, allocate (duties and responsibilities)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to entrust, charge, dedicate</div><b>αναθαρρεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to feel encouraged, take courage, take heart</div><b>αναθαρρύνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(transitive) to encourage, hearten</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀναθαρρύνω.</div><b>αναθαρρώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to feel encouraged, take courage, take heart</div><b>αναθεματίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to curse, put a curse on</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to excommunicate</div><b>αναθεματισμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αναθεματισμένη, neuter αναθεματισμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. damned, accursed, cursed</div>
  <div class='def'>2. damned, blasted, bloody</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αναθεματίζομαι, passive voice of αναθεματίζω (“to curse”).</div><b>αναθεματισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναθεματισμός)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>curse, anathematisation</div><b>αναθεμελιώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to refound, re-establish</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to lay a new foundation</div><b>αναθερμαίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to reactivate, reanimate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to reheat, rewarm</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to rekindle, revitalise (UK), revitalize (US)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀναθερμαίνω with semantic loan from English warm up. By surface analysis, ανα- (ana-) + θερμαίνω.</div><b>αναθεωρήσιμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναθεωρήσιμη, neuter αναθεωρήσιμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>amendable, revisable</div><b>αναθεωρητής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναθεωρητές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. revisionist</div>
  <div class='def'>2. reviser</div><b>αναθεωρητικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναθεωρητική, neuter αναθεωρητικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>revisionary, revisional</div><b>αναθεωρητιμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναθεωρητιμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>revisionism</div><b>αναθεωρώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to reconsider, revise, review</div><b>αναθεώρηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναθεωρήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. revision, re-examination</div>
  <div class='def'>2. rehearing</div><b>αναθηματικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναθηματική, neuter αναθηματικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>dedicatory, votive</div><b>αναθρέφω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανατρέφω">ανατρέφω</a></div><b>αναθρεφτός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναθρεφτοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. foster son, stepson</div>
  <div class='def'>2. foster child, nursling</div><b>αναθυμάμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (literary) to remember</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (literary) to remember fondly, remember with nostalgia</div><b>αναθυμίαση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναθυμιάσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. exhalation, effluvium</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (in plural) fumes, vapours (UK), vapors (US)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναθυμίασις.</div><b>αναθυμίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to remind</div><b>αναθυμούμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναθυμάμαι">αναθυμάμαι</a></div><b>αναθύμηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) recollection, remembrance</div><b>αναιδής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναιδής, neuter αναιδές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. impudent, cheeky</div>
  <div class='def'>2. brash, saucy</div>
  <div class='def'>3. shameless, immodest</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναιδής.</div><b>αναιμία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναιμίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anaemia (UK), anemia (US)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀναιμίᾱ from ἄναιμος and semantic loan from French anémie from Ancient Greek ἀναιμίᾱ. By surface analysis, αν- (an-, α- privative) + Ancient Greek αἷμα.</div><b>αναιμικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναιμική, neuter αναιμικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anaemic, anemic</div><b>αναιρέσιμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναιρέσιμη, neuter αναιρέσιμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. reversible, revocable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. refutable</div><b>αναιρετικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναιρετική, neuter αναιρετικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>relating to appeals</div><b>αναιρώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to refute, revoke</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to sublate</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναιρῶ, contracted form of ἀναιρέω. Morphologically By surface analysis, αν- (an-) + Ancient Greek αἱρέω, αἱρῶ.</div><b>αναισθησία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναισθησίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. anaesthesia (UK), anesthesia (US), anæsthesia (obsolete)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. insensitivity, unfeelingness</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναισθησία.</div><b>αναισθησιολογία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) anaesthesiology (UK), anesthesiology (US)</div><b>αναισθησιολόγος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural αναισθησιολόγοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anaesthetist, anaesthesiologist (UK); anesthetist, anesthesiologist (US)</div><b>αναισθητικό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναισθητικά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anaesthetic (UK), anesthetic (US)</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://αναισθητικός">αναισθητικός</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://αναισθητικός">αναισθητικός</a></div><b>αναισθητικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναισθητική, neuter αναισθητικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anaesthetic (UK), anesthetic (US)</div><b>αναισθητοποίηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναισθητοποιήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anaesthetization (UK) anesthetisation (US)</div><b>αναισθητοποιώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to anaesthetize</div><b>αναισθητώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to anaesthetise (UK), anesthetize (US)</div><b>αναισχυντία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) impudence, shamelessness, brassiness</div><b>αναιτιολόγητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναιτιολόγητη, neuter αναιτιολόγητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unjustified, unjustifiable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. inexplicable, unexplainable</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀναιτιολόγητος. By surface analysis, αν- (an-, α- privative) + αιτιο-λογ(ώ)) + -(η)τος (-(i)tos, “justify”).</div><b>αναιτιότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) blamelessness</div><b>ανακάθησα</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>misspelling of ανακάθισα</div><b>ανακάθομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to sit up (from a lying position)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ανα- (ana-, “upwards”) + κάθομαι</div><b>ανακάλυψη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακαλύψεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>discovery, find (the process of discovery and the thing discovered)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀνακάλυψις f with ending -σις (-sis) &gt; modern suffix -ση (-si), from ἀνακαλύπτω &lt; ἀνά + καλύπτω. See ανα- (ana-) + κάλυψη.</div><b>ανακάμπτω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (intransitive) to reappear, recover, revive (after absence or after a recession)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η οικονομία ανέκαμψε.<b></b> - The economy has recovered.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (transitive) cause recovery</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνακάμπτω (“bend back”). Morphologically, from ανα- (“re-”) + κάμπτω (“bend”).</div><b>ανακάτεμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανακατέματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. blending, mixing, stirring</div>
  <div class='def'>2. shuffling, shuffle</div>
  <div class='def'>3. confusion, disorder</div>
  <div class='def'>4. muddle, mix-up</div>
  <div class='def'>5. nausea, queasiness, sickness</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ανακάτεμα</b> στο στομάχι - nausea, queasiness</div><b>ανακάτωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανακατώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. blending, mixing, stirring</div>
  <div class='def'>2. shuffling, shuffle</div>
  <div class='def'>3. confusion, disorder</div>
  <div class='def'>4. muddle, mix-up</div>
  <div class='def'>5. nausea, queasiness, sickness</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ανακάτωμα</b> στο στομάχι - nausea, queasiness</div><b>ανακάτωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) turbulence, storminess</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) nausea, sickness</div><b>ανακάτωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανακάτωτη, neuter ανακάτωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unblended, pure</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unadulterated</div><b>ανακήρυξη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακηρύξεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. nomination, election</div>
  <div class='def'>2. proclamation, acclamation</div><b>ανακίνηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακίνησεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. agitating, stirring up, stirring</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) bring to attention, bring up, raise</div><b>ανακαίνιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακαινίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>renovation, refurbishment</div><b>ανακαθίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to sit up (from a lying position)</div><b>ανακαθιστός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανακαθιστή, neuter ανακαθιστό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sitting up</div><b>ανακαινίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to renovate, refurbish (especially a building)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to recondition (engine, furniture, etc)</div><b>ανακαινίστρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακαινίστριες, masculine ανακαινιστής)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. restorer, renovator</div>
  <div class='def'>2. reformer</div><b>ανακαινιστής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανακαινιστές, feminine ανακαινίστρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. restorer, renovator</div>
  <div class='def'>2. reformer</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀνακαινιστής, equivalent to ανακαινίζω + -ιστής.</div><b>ανακαινιστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανακαινιστική, neuter ανακαινιστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>restorative, relating to restoration or renewal</div><b>ανακαλύπτομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be discovered, be unmasked</div><b>ανακαλύπτω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to discover, uncover</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to invent, discover</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνακαλύπτω. By surface analysis, ανα- (“re-”) + καλύπτω (“cover”).</div><b>ανακαλώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to revoke, rescind</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to recall</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνακαλέω. By surface analysis, ανα- (ana-) + καλώ.</div><b>ανακαμπτίδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακαμπτίδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Any of genus Anacamptis of orchids</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from translingual Anacamptis. By surface analysis, ανακάμπτω + -ίδα.</div><b>ανακαούρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακαούρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(rare) heartburn</div><b>ανακατάληψη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακαταλήψεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>recapture, retaking</div><b>ανακατάταξη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακατατάξεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. rearrangement, reclassification, reassignment</div>
  <div class='def'>2. reorganisation (UK), reorganization (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. re-enlistment</div>
  <div class='def'>4. realignment</div><b>ανακαταλαμβάνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to recapture, retake</div><b>ανακατανέμω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to redistribute, reallocate</div><b>ανακατανομή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακατανομές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>redeployment, redistribution</div><b>ανακατασκευάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to reconstruct, rebuild</div><b>ανακατασκευή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακατασκευές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reconstruction, rebuilding</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From ανα- (ana-) + κατασκευή f.</div><b>ανακατατάσσω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to rearrange, reclassify, reassign</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to reorganise (UK), reorganize (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to re-enlist</div>
  <div class='def'>4. to realign</div><b>ανακατεύθυνση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακατευθύνσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(Internet) redirection</div><b>ανακατεύομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to interfere, meddle</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to get involved, mingle</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to retch, heave, feel queasy</div><b>ανακατεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to mix, mingle, mix up, stir</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to stir up, disrupt, involve</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From ανάκατ(ος) (“mixed up”) + -εύω (“suffix for verbs”). Prefix ανα- (“re-”). Also see ανακατώνω.</div><b>ανακατωσούρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακατωσούρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>confusion, turmoil, upset, agitation, chaos</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative feminine singular of <a href="bword://ανακατωσούρης">ανακατωσούρης</a></div><b>ανακατωσούρης</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανακατωσούρα, neuter ανακατωσούρικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. meddlesome, interfering</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (as a noun) busybody, meddlesome person</div><b>ανακατωτά</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>used only in the expression <a href="bword://απέξω">απέξω</a> κι <a href="bword://ανακατωτά">ανακατωτά</a></div>
  <div class='ex'>Θα το έχετε μάθει <b>απέξω κι ανακατωτά</b>. - You will have learnt it by heart / forwards and backwards / inside out.</div><b>ανακατώνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανακατεύομαι">ανακατεύομαι</a></div><b>ανακατώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανακατεύω">ανακατεύω</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀνακατώνω; by surface analysis, ανάκατος + -ώνω. Prefix ανα- (ana-, “re-”). Also see ανακατεύω, a modern formation from adjective ανάκατος.</div><b>ανακαψίλα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακαψίλες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(rare) heartburn</div><b>ανακεφαλαίωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακεφαλαιώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>summary, synopsis, summing up</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνακεφαλαίωσις.</div><b>ανακεφαλαιωτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανακεφαλαιωτική, neuter ανακεφαλαιωτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>recapitulative</div><b>ανακεφαλαιώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to sum up</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to summarise (UK), summarize (US)</div><b>ανακηρύσσω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to declare, to announce, to proclaim</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀνακηρύσσω. By surface analysis, ανα- (ana-) + κηρύσσω.</div><b>ανακινώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to shake, agitate (bottle contents)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to agitate, stir up</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to raise, bring up (for discussion)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀνακινῶ, contracted form of ἀνακινέω. By surface analysis, ανα- (“re-”) + κινώ (“move”).</div><b>ανακλάδισμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανακλαδίσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. stretch (body, limbs, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. crossed legs</div>
  <div class='def'>3. burgeoning (of plant)</div><b>ανακλαδίζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (colloquial) to stretch, stretch out</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to squat</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to burgeon, form shoots</div><b>ανακλαδιστός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανακλαδιστή, neuter ανακλαδιστό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>cross-legged</div><b>ανακλασμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine ανακλασμένη, neuter ανακλασμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reflected</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of ανακλώμαι, passive voice of ανακλώ (“reflect”).</div><b>ανακλαστικά</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://ανακλαστικός">ανακλαστικός</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reflexes</div><b>ανακλαστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανακλαστική, neuter ανακλαστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reflective</div><b>ανακλητήριο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανακλητήρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. recall (bugle call)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. recall</div><b>ανακλητήριος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανακλητήρια, neuter ανακλητήριο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>recall</div><b>ανακλητικό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανακλητικά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. the recall, a bugle call</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (often) reflex</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://ανακλητικός">ανακλητικός</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://ανακλητικός">ανακλητικός</a></div><b>ανακλητικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανακλητική, neuter ανακλητικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>revocatory, revocative, recalling</div><b>ανακλητός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανακλητή, neuter ανακλητό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. revocable, recallable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. reversible</div><b>ανακλώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to reflect (heat, light, sound, etc)</div><b>ανακλώμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be reflected</div><b>ανακλώμενος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine ανακλώμενη, neuter ανακλώμενο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>being reflected</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Present participle of ανακλώμαι, passive voice of ανακλώ (“reflect”). Learned form, as in Ancient Greek ἀνακλώμενος.</div><b>ανακοίνωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακοινώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>announcement</div>
  <div class='ex'>επίσημη ανακοίνωση (official announcement)</div><b>ανακοινωθέν</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανακοινωθέντα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. bulletin</div>
  <div class='def'>2. communique</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνακοινωθέν, the neutral form of the aorist passive participle of the verb ἀνακοινοῦμαι.</div><b>ανακοινώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to announce, declare (make people aware of something)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Τις νέες διοικήσεις σε νοσοκομεία <b>ανακοίνωσε</b> το Υπουργείο Υγείας. - New administrations in hospitals have been announced by the Ministry of Health.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> from ανα- (ana-) + Ancient Greek κοινόω to communicate</div><b>ανακοινώσιμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανακοινώσιμη, neuter ανακοινώσιμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>communicable, suitable to be announced</div><b>ανακολουθία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακολουθίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. inconsistency, contradiction</div>
  <div class='def'>2. non sequitur</div>
  <div class='def'>3. incoherency</div><b>ανακομιδή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακομιδές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. the removal of bones from a grave and their transfer to an ossuary or charnel house</div>
  <div class='def'>2. the transfer of saintly relics</div><b>ανακοπή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. check, curb, restraint</div>
  <div class='def'>2. arrest, stoppage (medical: of an organ&#x27;s function)</div><b>ανακουνώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανακινώ">ανακινώ</a></div><b>ανακουφίζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be relieved, to feel relieved</div><b>ανακουφίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to alleviate, relieve</div><b>ανακουφιστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανακουφιστική, neuter ανακουφιστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>soothing, alleviatory</div><b>ανακούρκουδα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. squatting (in a squatting position)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. sitting cross-legged</div>
  <div class='def'>3. sitting on your heels</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Byzantine Greek ἀνακούρκουδα</div><b>ανακούφιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) relief, comfort, solace (from anxiety)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνακούφισις.</div><b>ανακράζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to exclaim, shout out, cry out</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνακράζω. Morphologically, from ανα- + κράζω.</div><b>ανακρίβεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακρίβειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>inexactness, inaccuracy, inexactitude, imprecision</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from ανακριβής + -εια (-eia), a calque of French inexactitude.</div><b>ανακρίνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be cross-examined, interrogated</div><b>ανακρίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to interrogate, question</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀνακρίνω. By surface analysis, ανα- (“re-”) + κρίνω (“judge, examine”).</div><b>ανακρίτρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακρίτριες, masculine ανακριτής)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>interrogator, inquisitor</div><b>ανακρεμνώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανακρεμώ">ανακρεμώ</a></div><b>ανακρεμώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to suspend, hang, hang up</div><b>ανακρεόντειος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανακρεόντεια, neuter ανακρεόντειο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. relating to the poet Anacreon (notable for Bacchanalian poetry)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) Bacchanalian (of poetry)</div><b>ανακριβής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανακριβής, neuter ανακριβές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>inaccurate, inexact, imprecise</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Byzantine Greek ανακριβής. By surface analysis, αν- (an-, α- privative) + ακριβής.</div><b>ανακριβολογία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακριβολογίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>evasion, prevarication</div><b>ανακριβολογώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be inaccurate (with the truth), prevaricate</div><b>ανακριτής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανακριτές, feminine ανακρίτρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>interrogator, inquisitor</div><b>ανακριτική</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) investigative/forensic methodology</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative feminine singular of <a href="bword://ανακριτικός">ανακριτικός</a></div><b>ανακριτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανακριτική, neuter ανακριτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>interrogatory, examining, fact-finding</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ανακριτικό</b> γραφείο - interview room</div><b>ανακρούομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be played (of music pieces)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ο εθνικός ύμνος <b>ανακρούστηκε</b> από την ορχήστρα. - The national anthem was played by the orchestra.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Ancient Greek ἀνακρούομαι</div><b>ανακρούω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to strike up, play (especially a rousing piece)</div>
  <div class='ex'>H ορχήστρα <b>ανέκρουσε</b> τον εθνικό ύμνο. - The orchestra played the national anthem.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (used in active voice) to back off, back out</div>
  <div class='ex'>in the formal set phrase: ανακρούω πρύμναν (anakroúo prýmnan) or ανακρούω πρύμνη (anakroúo prýmni)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (used in active voice) to back off, back out; to reverse, go astern</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ᾰ̓νᾰκρούω (“push back”). Sense 1 since Hellenistic times. By surface analysis, ανα- + κρούω (“strike”).</div><b>ανακτημένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine ανακτημένη, neuter ανακτημένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>retrieved, recovered, regained</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of ανακτώμαι, passive voice of ανακτώ (“retrieve”).</div><b>ανακτοβούλιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανακτοβούλια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>privy council</div><b>ανακτορικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανακτορική, neuter ανακτορικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. palace, palatial</div>
  <div class='def'>2. royal</div><b>ανακτοσύμβουλος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανακτοσύμβουλοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>privy councillor (UK), privy councilor (US)</div><b>ανακτώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to regain, recover</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to regain</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Ανακτώ</b> τις αισθήσεις μου μετά από λιποθυμία. - I regained my senses after fainting.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to restore, recover (data)</div><b>ανακυκλώνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be recycled</div><b>ανακυκλώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to recycle</div><b>ανακυκλώσιμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανακυκλώσιμη, neuter ανακυκλώσιμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>recyclable</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From ανακυκλώ(νω)) + -σιμος (-simos).</div><b>ανακωχή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακωχές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>truce, ceasefire, armistice</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Koine Greek ἀνακωχή, late form of Ancient Greek ἀνοκωχή with analogical restoration to the &lt; ἀν(α)- (an(a)-) compounds + ὀκωχή f.</div><b>ανακόλουθο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανακόλουθα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anacoluthon</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνακόλουθον.</div><b>ανακόλουθος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανακόλουθη, neuter ανακόλουθο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>inconsistent, incoherent</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνακόλουθος.</div><b>ανακόπτομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be halted</div><b>ανακόπτω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to check, stem, halt, arrest, withstand (the flow of something)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ανακόπτω</b> την πορεία, την άνοδο, την εξέλιξη - I halt the course, the rise, the development</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀνακόπτω. By surface analysis, ανα- (“thoroughly”) + κόπτω (“cut”).</div><b>ανακύκληση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακυκλήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. revolving, cycling</div>
  <div class='def'>2. turning (the wheel of life)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. recycling</div><b>ανακύκλωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανακυκλώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. recycling</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ανακύκλωση</b> συσκευασιών - recycling of packaging</div>
  <div class='def'>2. looping (the loop)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ᾰ̓νᾰκῠ́κλωσῐς. In the modern sense of &quot;recycling&quot;, semantic loan from English recycling.</div><b>ανακύπτω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to arise, crop up (difficulties, issues)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνακύπτω. Morphologically, from ανα- (“re-”) + κύπτω (“bend”).</div><b>αναλάμπω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to gleam, flash, shine</div><b>αναλήθεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναλήθειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>lie, falsehood</div><b>αναλίσκομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(no past) to be consumed</div><b>αναλίσκω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(formal) to spend, use</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedely, from Ancient Greek ἀναλίσκω.</div><b>αναλαβαίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναλαμβάνω">αναλαμβάνω</a></div><b>αναλαμβάνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be taken on</div><b>αναλαμβάνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to undertake, take on, shoulder (responsibility, task)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to recover, regain (health)</div><b>αναλαμπή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναλαμπές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. gleam, flash</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) gleam, flare</div><b>αναλγησία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) analgesia</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively, uncountable) callousness, insensitivity</div><b>αναλγητικό</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. inflection of <a href="bword://αναλγητικός">αναλγητικός</a>:; masculine accusative singular</div>
  <div class='def'>2. inflection of <a href="bword://αναλγητικός">αναλγητικός</a>:; neuter nominative/accusative/vocative singular</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναλγητικά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>analgesic, painkiller</div><b>αναλγητικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναλγητική, neuter αναλγητικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>analgesic, painkilling</div><b>αναληθής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναληθής, neuter αναληθές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. untrue, false</div>
  <div class='def'>2. mendacious</div><b>αναληπτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναληπτική, neuter αναληπτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>restorative, tonic, analeptic</div><b>αναλλοίωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναλλοίωτη, neuter αναλλοίωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unchanged, unaltered, unchangeable</div><b>αναλογία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναλογίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. analogy</div>
  <div class='def'>2. proportion, ratio</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναλογίᾱ.</div><b>αναλογίζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to consider, dwell on, think about, brood, brood on</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ανα- (“re-”) + λογίζομαι (“think, consider”).</div><b>αναλογική</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) shortened form of <a href="bword://αναλογική">αναλογική</a> <a href="bword://αντιπροσώπευση">αντιπροσώπευση</a></div><b>αναλογική αντιπροσώπευση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) proportional representation</div><b>αναλογικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναλογική, neuter αναλογικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. proportional, proportionate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. analogue (UK), analog (US)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αναλογικό</b> ρολόι - analogue watch</div><b>αναλογιστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναλογιστική, neuter αναλογιστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. actuarially calculated</div>
  <div class='def'>2. proportional, proportionate</div><b>αναλογιστικώς</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>actuarially</div><b>αναλογώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to be proportionate, be in proportion</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to be analogous</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to correspond</div><b>αναλυτά</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αναλυτός">αναλυτός</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>loosely, slackly</div><b>αναλυτής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναλυτές, feminine αναλύτρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. analyst (occupation)</div>
  <div class='ex'>πολιτικός <b>αναλυτής</b> - political analyst</div>
  <div class='def'>2. analyser, analyzer (instrument)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αναλυτής</b> αμινοξέων - amino acid analyser</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>genitive feminine singular of <a href="bword://αναλυτός">αναλυτός</a></div><b>αναλυτικά</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αναλυτικός">αναλυτικός</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>analytically, in detail</div><b>αναλυτική μηχανή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναλυτικές μηχανές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>analytical engine</div><b>αναλυτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναλυτική, neuter αναλυτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>analytical, analytic</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αναλυτικό</b> μυαλό - analytical mind</div><b>αναλυτός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναλυτή, neuter αναλυτό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. molten, melted</div>
  <div class='def'>2. runny (of a honey)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. thin, watery (of a liquid)</div>
  <div class='def'>4. loose, untied (of a hair)</div><b>αναλφάβητη</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative masculine/feminine/neuter singular of <a href="bword://αναλφάβητος">αναλφάβητος</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναλφάβητες, masculine αναλφάβητος)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>illiterate person</div><b>αναλφάβητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναλφάβητη, neuter αναλφάβητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. illiterate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (as a noun) illiterate person</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναλφάβητοι, feminine αναλφάβητη)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>illiterate person</div><b>αναλφαβητισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) illiteracy</div><b>αναλόγια μουσικής</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>plural of <a href="bword://αναλόγιο">αναλόγιο</a> μουσικής</div><b>αναλόγια μουσικών</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>plural of <a href="bword://αναλόγιο">αναλόγιο</a> μουσικής</div><b>αναλόγιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναλόγια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. music stand</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αναλόγιο</b> μουσικής - music stand (formally, in full)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. lectern</div><b>αναλόγιο μουσικής</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναλόγια μουσικής)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>music stand</div><b>αναλόγως</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. proportionally, proportionately</div>
  <div class='def'>2. accordingly</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αναλόγως</b> με - according to, in accordance with, depending on</div>
  <div class='def'>3. analogously</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀναλόγως. By surface analysis, ανάλογ(ος)) + -ως (-os).</div><b>αναλύομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to be analysed (UK), to be analyzed (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to be parsed</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to burst into tears</div><b>αναλύτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναλύτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>analyte (substance being determined)</div><b>αναλύτρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναλύτριες, masculine αναλυτής)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>female analyst (occupation)</div><b>αναλύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to analyse (UK), analyze (US), assay</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to parse</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (broadly) to dilute</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (broadly) to psychoanalyse (especially in the passive)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναλύω (“unloose; resolve into its elements”). For modern senses, semantic loan from French analyser and English analyse. Morphologically, from ανα- + λύω.</div><b>αναλώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (Demotic, rare) to melt (make something liquid by heat)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (Demotic, figuratively, rare) to be exhausted, discourage</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (Demotic, rare) to dissolve</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναλῶ, contracted form of ἀνᾱλόω, a form of ἀνᾱλίσκω. The mediaeval form is ἀναλώνω, contemporary script, αναλώνω.</div><b>αναλώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to spend, consume, use</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀναλώνω from ancient Ancient Greek ἀναλόω, ἀναλῶ, alternative of ἀναλίσκω.</div><b>αναλώσιμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>writing materials, stationery</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αναλώσιμος">αναλώσιμος</a></div><b>αναλώσιμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναλώσιμη, neuter αναλώσιμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>consumable, expendable</div><b>αναμάλλιασμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναμαλλιάσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ruffling tousling, rumpling</div><b>αναμάρτητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναμάρτητη, neuter αναμάρτητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sinless, innocent</div><b>αναμάσημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναμασήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>rumination, chewing the cud, regurgitating</div><b>αναμένονται</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>third-person plural present indicative of αναμένομαι, the passive of <a href="bword://αναμένω">αναμένω</a></div><b>αναμένω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to expect</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to await, anticipate</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀναμένω, from ἀνα- (ana-) + μένω, with semantic loan from French s&#x27;attendre and Semantic loan from English is expected.</div><b>αναμέτρηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναμετρήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>contest, contention</div><b>αναμίσθωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναμισθώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>renewal of a lease</div><b>αναμαλλιάζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be tousled, to be dishevelled</div><b>αναμαλλιάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to tousle, dishevel</div><b>αναμαλλιάρης</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναμαλλιάρης, neuter αναμαλλιάρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. ruffled</div>
  <div class='def'>2. dishevelled (UK), disheveled (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. touselled (UK), touseled (US)</div><b>αναμαλλιασμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αναμαλλιασμένη, neuter αναμαλλιασμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. dishevelled (UK), disheveled (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. touselled (UK), touseled (US)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αναμαλλιάζομαι, passive voice of αναμαλλιάζω.</div><b>αναμασάω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναμασώ">αναμασώ</a></div><b>αναμασώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to chew the cud, ruminate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to repeat, go on (verbally)</div><b>αναμειγνύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to mix (paint, cement, etc.)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to mix up with; to mix up in (scandal, crime, etc)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀναμειγνύω or ἀναμιγνύω. By surface analysis, ανα- (ana-, “re”) + μειγνύω.</div><b>αναμενόμενος</b>
  <div><i>verb, masculine (feminine αναμενόμενη, neuter αναμενόμενο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>passive present participle of αναμένομαι, the passive of <a href="bword://αναμένω">αναμένω</a>: expected, anticipated</div><b>αναμερίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (intransitive, transitive) to move out of the way</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to push aside</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to stand aside</div><b>αναμετάδοση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναμεταδόσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. rebroadcast, retransmission</div>
  <div class='def'>2. broadcast</div><b>αναμεταδίδω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to retransmit, rebroadcast</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to recommunicate, communicate again</div><b>αναμεταδότης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναμεταδότες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>transmission mast, radio mast</div><b>αναμεταξύ</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://μεταξύ">μεταξύ</a></div><b>αναμετράω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναμετρώ">αναμετρώ</a></div><b>αναμετριέμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to contend, vie</div><b>αναμετρούμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναμετριέμαι">αναμετριέμαι</a></div><b>αναμετρώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to weigh up, assess</div><b>αναμηρυκάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (no past) to chew the cud, ruminate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively, no past) to ruminate, ponder</div><b>αναμηρυκασμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναμηρυκασμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>rumination</div><b>αναμηρυκαστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναμηρυκαστική, neuter αναμηρυκαστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ruminating</div><b>αναμιγνύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative spelling of <a href="bword://αναμειγνύω">αναμειγνύω</a></div><b>αναμισθώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to re-lease, lease or rent again</div><b>αναμμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αναμμένη, neuter αναμμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. burning, alight, incandescent, emitting flame</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) enraged, angry, fiery</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of ανάβομαι, passive voice of ανάβω</div><b>αναμνηστικό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναμνηστικά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>souvenir, memento, keepsake</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://αναμνηστικός">αναμνηστικός</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://αναμνηστικός">αναμνηστικός</a></div><b>αναμνηστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναμνηστική, neuter αναμνηστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. commemorative</div>
  <div class='def'>2. repetitious, iterative</div><b>αναμονή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναμονές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. wait</div>
  <div class='ex'>η πολύωρη <b>αναμονή</b> στο αεροδρόμιο - the long wait at the airport</div>
  <div class='def'>2. waiting, expectation</div>
  <div class='ex'>λίστα <b>αναμονής</b> - waiting list</div>
  <div class='def'>3. that part of a reinforced concrete column with its steel reinforcement protrude on a building&#x27;s roof</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (in plural) sleep, hibernation (of a computer in an incomplete state of closure)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναμονή, derived from Ancient Greek ἀναμένω. Can be synchronically analyzed as ανα- (ana-, “re-, above”) + μένω.</div><b>αναμορφωτήριο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναμορφωτήρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. young offenders institution, approved school, borstal (UK)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. reform school, reformatory (US)</div><b>αναμορφωτής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναμορφωτές, feminine αναμορφώτρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reformer (person who seeks to reform)</div><b>αναμορφωτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναμορφωτική, neuter αναμορφωτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reforming, reformative</div><b>αναμορφώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to reform</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to change radically, improve</div><b>αναμορφώτρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναμορφωτές, masculine αναμορφωτής)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reformer (person who seeks to reform)</div><b>αναμοχλεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to stir up, rake up (old passions, forgotten scandals)</div><b>αναμπαίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial, passive) to mock, tease, ridicule</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀνεμπαίζω, from ἀνα- (ana-) + ἐν- (en-) + παίζω.</div><b>αναμπαίχτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναμπαίχτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>teaser, mocker</div><b>αναμπουμπούλα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναμπουμπούλες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fuss, mayhem, hubbub, hurlyburly, turmoil, upheaval</div><b>αναμφίβολα</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αναμφίβολος">αναμφίβολος</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>undoubtedly, indubitably, unquestionably, without doubt</div><b>αναμφίβολος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναμφίβολοη, neuter αναμφίβολο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unquestionable, indubitable, undoubted</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀναμφίβολος. By surface analysis, αν- (an-, α- privative) + αμφίβολος.</div><b>αναμφίλεκτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναμφίλεκτη, neuter αναμφίλεκτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>undeniable, unmistakable, incontestable (universally accepted)</div><b>αναμφιβόλως</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναμφίβολα">αναμφίβολα</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀναμφιβόλως. By surface analysis, αναμφίβολ(ος)) + -ως (-os).</div><b>αναμφισβήτητα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>undeniably, unquestionably, indisputably</div><b>αναμφισβήτητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναμφισβήτητη, neuter αναμφισβήτητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unquestionable, undeniable</div><b>αναμόλυνση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναμολύνσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reinfection; fresh infection (after recovery)</div><b>αναμόρφωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναμορφώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reformation, reform</div><b>αναμόχλευση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναμοχλεύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (figuratively) search, rummage</div>
  <div class='def'>2. stirring up, turning up, raking up (old passions, forgotten scandals)</div><b>ανανάς</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανανάδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. pineapple (fruit)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Αγόρασα έναν <b>ανανά</b> από την αγορά. - I bought a pineapple from the market.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. pineapple (plant)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Portuguese ananás (“pineapple”).</div><b>ανανέωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανανεώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. renewal, renovation</div>
  <div class='def'>2. rejuvenation, revitalisation</div><b>ανανήφω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (literary) to come round, recover (consciousness especially after surgery)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively, literary) to recant, come round, recover (one&#x27;s senses)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀνανήφω (“become sober again, come to oneʼs senses”). Morphologically, from ανα- (“again”) + the ancient νήφω</div><b>ανανδρία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) cowardice, unmanliness</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνανδρίᾱ. By surface analysis, άνανδρος + -ία.</div><b>ανανεωμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανανεωμένη, neuter ανανεωμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>renewed, refreshed, restored</div><b>ανανεωτής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανανεωτές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>renovator</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Koine Greek ἀνανεωτής, from Ancient Greek ἀνανεόω / ἀνανεῶ. By surface analysis, ανανεώνω + -τής.</div><b>ανανεωτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανανεωτική, neuter ανανεωτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>renewing, refreshing</div><b>ανανεώνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to be renewed, be rejuvenated</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to find new interests</div><b>ανανεώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to renew, renovate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to replenish</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to revive, refresh</div><b>ανανεώσιμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανανεώσιμη, neuter ανανεώσιμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(of a resource) renewable</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ανανεώσιμες</b> πηγές ενέργειας - renewable energy sources</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from ανανεώ(νω)) + -σιμος (-simos), a calque of English renewable.</div><b>ανανογιέμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to remember, become aware, realise</div><b>ανανούριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανανούριστη, neuter ανανούριστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unlulled</div><b>αναντάν μπαμπαντάν</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>from the beginning</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ottoman Turkish انادن بابادن (anadan babadan, “from the origin, from the source”, literally “from mother from father”).</div><b>αναντίλεκτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναντίλεκτη, neuter αναντίλεκτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>undeniable, indisputable, certain</div><b>αναντίρρητα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>undeniably, unquestionably</div><b>αναντίρρητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναντίρρητη, neuter αναντίρρητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>undeniable, unmistakable, incontestable (universally accepted)</div><b>ανανταπόδοτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανανταπόδοτη, neuter ανανταπόδοτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unrequited, unreciprocated</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unrewarded, without reward</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ανανταπόδοτος</b> έρωτας - unrequited love</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (rhetoric) descriptive of anapodoton</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνανταπόδοτος.</div><b>ανανταπόκριτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανανταπόκριτη, neuter ανανταπόκριτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unanswered</div><b>αναντικατάστατος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναντικατάστατη, neuter αναντικατάστατο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. irreplaceable</div>
  <div class='ex'>Κανείς δεν είναι <b>αναντικατάστατος</b>. - Nobody is irreplaceable.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unreplaced</div><b>αναντιπροσώπευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναντιπροσώπευτη, neuter αναντιπροσώπευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unrepresented</div><b>αναντιστοιχία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disparity, inconsistency, lack of correspondence</div><b>αναντρία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανανδρία">ανανδρία</a></div><b>αναξέω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to scratch old wounds (stir up sleeping passions)</div><b>αναξαίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to card again, recomb (repeated wool treatment)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to rake up (old scandals, etc); reopen (old wounds)</div><b>αναξιοκρατία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>cronyism, favouritism (UK), favoritism (US), nepotism</div><b>αναξιοκρατικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναξιοκρατική, neuter αναξιοκρατικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nepotistic, nepotistical</div><b>αναξιοπάθεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναξιοπάθειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>undeserved suffering or misery</div><b>αναξιοπαθής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναξιοπαθής, neuter αναξιοπαθές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. suffering due to misfortune, suffering undeserved misery</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) unfortunate</div><b>αναξιοπαθώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to suffer (through no fault of your own)</div><b>αναξιοπιστία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) unreliability, untrustworthiness</div><b>αναξιοποίητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναξιοποίητη, neuter αναξιοποίητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unexploited</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αν- (an-, α- privative) + αξιοποι(ώ), “develop”) + -τος (-tos, adjectival suffix)</div><b>αναξιοπρέπεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) lack of dignity, indignity</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) shamefulness</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αν- (an-, α- privative) + αξιοπρέπεια</div><b>αναξιοπρεπής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναξιοπρεπής, neuter αναξιοπρεπές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. undignified, lacking dignity</div>
  <div class='def'>2. disreputable</div>
  <div class='def'>3. shameful</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αν- (an-, α- privative) + αξιοπρεπής.</div><b>αναξιοσύνη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) unworthiness, incompetence</div><b>αναξιόλογος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναξιόλογη, neuter αναξιόλογο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unimportant, insignificant</div>
  <div class='def'>2. trifling, piffling</div>
  <div class='def'>3. unworthy, unimportant</div><b>αναξιόπιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναξιόπιστη, neuter αναξιόπιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>untrustworthy, unreliable</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αναξιόπιστος</b> αφηγητής - unreliable narrator</div><b>αναξιότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) worthlessness, unworthiness, incompetence</div><b>αναξιόχρεο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναξιόχρεα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>insolvency, bankruptcy</div><b>αναξιόχρεος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναξιόχρεη, neuter αναξιόχρεο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. insolvent</div>
  <div class='def'>2. untrustworthy</div><b>αναπάλλομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to be oscillated, moved upwards</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to be moved</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η ψυχή μου <b>αναπάλλεται</b> στο άκουσμα αυτής της μουσικής. - My soul is exalted when I listen to this music.</div><b>αναπάλλω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to move or swing upwards, oscillate, vibrate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to be moved, stirred psychologically</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀναπάλλω. By surface analysis, ανα- (ana-) + πάλλω</div><b>αναπάντεχα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unexpectedly</div><b>αναπάντεχος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπάντεχη, neuter αναπάντεχο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unexpected, not anticipated, unanticipated</div>
  <div class='def'>2. sudden</div><b>αναπάντητα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>without unanswering</div><b>αναπάντητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπάντητη, neuter αναπάντητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unanswered, unacknowledged, (telephone calls): unreturned</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η ερώτηση εκείνη παρέμεινε <b>αναπάντητη</b>. - That question remained unanswered.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) unanswerable</div><b>αναπέμπω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to refer back, remit</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to offer</div><b>αναπήδημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναπηδήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>bound, leap</div><b>αναπήδηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναπηδήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>bounding forward, leaping up</div><b>αναπαιστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπαιστική, neuter αναπαιστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anapaestic (UK), anapestic (US)</div><b>αναπαλαίωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναπαλαιώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>restoration</div><b>αναπαλαιώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to restore, renovate, refurbish</div><b>αναπαλλοτρίωτο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) inalienability</div><b>αναπαλλοτρίωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπαλλοτρίωτη, neuter αναπαλλοτρίωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. inalienable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unalienated</div><b>αναπαλμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναπαλμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>swing, oscillation</div><b>αναπαμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναπαμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. rest, respite, relaxation</div>
  <div class='def'>2. quiet, peace</div><b>αναπαράγω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to reproduce (offspring)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to reproduce, duplicate (image,etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to reproduce (performance, music)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Calque of French reproduire. Morphologically ανα- (ana-) + παράγω.</div><b>αναπαράσταση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναπαραστάσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>re-enactment, representation</div><b>αναπαραγωγή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναπαραγωγές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. biological reproduction</div>
  <div class='def'>2. typographical reproduction</div>
  <div class='def'>3. reproduction by video, film, etc</div><b>αναπαραγωγικά συστήματα</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>plural of αναπαραγωγικό <a href="bword://σύστημα">σύστημα</a></div><b>αναπαραγωγικά όργανα</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>plural of αναπαραγωγικό <a href="bword://όργανο">όργανο</a></div><b>αναπαραγωγικό σύστημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναπαραγωγικά συστήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reproductive system</div><b>αναπαραγωγικό όργανο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναπαραγωγικά όργανα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reproductive organ, sex organ</div><b>αναπαραγωγικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπαραγωγική, neuter αναπαραγωγικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reproductive</div><b>αναπαραδιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) pennilessness, penury; poverty</div><b>αναπαραδιάρης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναπαραδιάρες, feminine αναπαραδιάρισσα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>penniless person</div><b>αναπαραδιάρισσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναπαραδιάρισσες, masculine αναπαραδιάρης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>penniless person</div><b>αναπαρασταίνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναπαριστάνομαι">αναπαριστάνομαι</a></div><b>αναπαρασταίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναπαριστάνω">αναπαριστάνω</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αναπαριστώ, as παρασταίνω from παριστώ. See etymologies of παριστάνω &amp; παρασταίνω.</div><b>αναπαριστάνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be portrayed</div><b>αναπαριστάνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to re-enact</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to depict, portray</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Calque of French représenter, from ανα- (ana-) + παριστάνω. Ultimately from Ancient Greek ἀνα- (ana-) + παρα- (para-) + ἵστημι.</div><b>αναπαριστώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναπαριστάνω">αναπαριστάνω</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned, archaic Katharevousa ἀναπαριστῶ. Calque of French représenter, from ἀνα- + παριστῶ with components ἀνα- (ana-) + παρα- (para-) + ἵστημι.</div><b>αναπασχόλητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπασχόλητη, neuter αναπασχόλητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unemployed, idle</div><b>αναπαυτήριο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναπαυτήρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. retreat, resting place</div>
  <div class='def'>2. snug, snuggery</div>
  <div class='def'>3. rest home</div><b>αναπαυτικά</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αναπαυτικός">αναπαυτικός</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>restfully, comfortably, cosily</div><b>αναπαυτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπαυτική, neuter αναπαυτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. snug, cosy</div>
  <div class='def'>2. comfortable, restful</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀναπαυστικός, with semantic loan from English comfortable and French confortable.</div><b>αναπαύομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to have a siesta, take a rest</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to die</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to neglect duties</div><b>αναπαύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to give comfort, give a rest</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (euphemistic) to die</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀναπαύω. By surface analysis, ανα- (“thoroughly, re-”) + παύω (“pause”).</div><b>αναπεπταμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπεπταμένη, neuter αναπεπταμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unfurled (sails, flags, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. open, wide, extended (stretch of countryside)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) far-reaching</div><b>αναπεσμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπεσμένη, neuter αναπεσμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>supine, on your back</div><b>αναπετάρισμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναπεταρίσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>twict, tic</div><b>αναπεταρίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to flutter</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to flinch, twitch</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to flirt</div><b>αναπετώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to jump, twitch (nervously)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to leap, jump up, fly</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to flee, fly, go</div>
  <div class='def'>4. to unfurl, open wings</div><b>αναπηδάω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναπηδώ">αναπηδώ</a></div><b>αναπηδώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to spring, jump up, leap</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to recoil, bounce</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to spurt (liquid)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναπηδῶ.</div><b>αναπηρία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναπηρίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disability</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned form from ανα- (ana-) + πηρός + -ία.</div><b>αναπηρικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπηρική, neuter αναπηρικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. invalid, for a person with a disability</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αναπηρικό</b> καροτσακι - wheelchair</div>
  <div class='def'>2. badly injured, maimed, crippled</div><b>αναπιάνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to knead dough</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to gossip</div><b>αναπλάθω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to remodel, reshape, reform</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to recreate</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to regenerate, transform</div>
  <div class='def'>4. to rescind, recall</div><b>αναπλάσσω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναπλάθω">αναπλάθω</a></div><b>αναπλέκω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(rare) to knit, braid</div><b>αναπλέω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to sail, go; to upstream, upriver</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to sail, go; to against the wind</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to sail, go; to against the current</div>
  <div class='def'>4. to sail into the offing; set sail (going out to sea)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναπλέω. Morphologically, from ανα- (ana-, “upward”) + πλέω.</div><b>αναπλήρωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναπλήρωματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>substitute</div><b>αναπλήρωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναπληρώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>substitution, replacement (action or its effect)</div><b>αναπλαστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπλαστική, neuter αναπλαστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reconstructive, regenerative</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αναπλαστική</b> χειρουργική - reconstructive surgery</div><b>αναπλειστηριάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to reauction, re-auction</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ανα- (“again”) + πλειστηριάζω (“auction”)</div><b>αναπλειστηριασμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναπλειστηριασμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reauction, repeat auction</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Calque of French nouvelle enchère. Morphologically, from ανα- (“again”) + πλειστηριασμός (“auction”).</div><b>αναπληρωματικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπληρωματική, neuter αναπληρωματικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. replacement, supplementary, alternate, surrogate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. nonvoting</div><b>αναπληρωτής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναπληρωτές, feminine αναπληρώτρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. deputy</div>
  <div class='def'>2. substitute, replacement (person)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αναπληρωτής</b> καθηγητής - supply teacher</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from αναπληρώ(νω)) + -τής, a calque of French suppléant.</div><b>αναπληρωτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπληρωτική, neuter αναπληρωτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. replacement, supplementary, alternate, surrogate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. nonvoting</div><b>αναπληρώνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be replaced</div><b>αναπληρώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to substitute, replace</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to compensate for, take the place of</div>
  <div class='ex'>Πρέπει ν’ <b>αναπληρώσουμε</b> το χαμένο καιρό. - We must make up for lost time.</div><b>αναπληρώτρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναπληρώτριες, masculine αναπληρωτής)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>substitute, replacement (person)</div><b>αναπνέω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to breathe</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to inhale, live</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) to relieve, relax</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναπνέω.</div><b>αναπνευστήρας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναπνευστήρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. snorkel</div>
  <div class='def'>2. breathing tube</div>
  <div class='def'>3. respirator</div>
  <div class='def'>4. ventilator, louvre</div><b>αναπνευστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπνευστική, neuter αναπνευστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>respiratory, breathing</div><b>αναπνοή</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>breath, breathing, respiration</div><b>αναποδίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(intransitive) to go backwards, reverse, go astern (mainly of ships, engines, machines)</div>
  <div class='ex'>&quot;anapodízo&quot;: i diadikasía apelefthérosis pagidevménon delfinión, thétontas ti michaní(-es) tou skáfous anápoda [...]
&quot;backdown&quot; means the procedure for releasing captured dolphins by shifting the vessel&#x27;s engine(s) into reverse …
eur-lex-europa.eu: Annex VIII (in English) retr:2019.01.17.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀναποδίζω.</div><b>αναποδιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναποδιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>bad luck, misfortune, adversity</div><b>αναποδιάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(familiar) to become ill-tempered, cantankerous, irritable</div>
  <div class='ex'>Όποτε τον βλέπω, <b>αναποδιάζω</b>· με εκνευρίζει. - Whenever I see him, I get irritated; he annoys me.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From ανάποδ(ος)) (sense: cantankerous) + -ιάζω.</div><b>αναποδιάρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναποδιάρες, masculine αναποδιάρης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>spoilsport, killjoy</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative feminine singular of <a href="bword://αναποδιάρης">αναποδιάρης</a></div><b>αναποδιάρης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (feminine αναποδιάρα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>spoilsport, killjoy</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναποδιάρα, neuter αναποδιάρικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ill-natured, spoilsport</div><b>αναποδογυρίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to overturn, turn upside down, turn over</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to capsize, upset</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From ανάποδα + Koine Greek γυρίζω.</div><b>αναποδογύρισμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναποδογυρίσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. overturning, inversion, upsetting</div>
  <div class='def'>2. knocking over</div><b>αναποζημίωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναποζημίωτη, neuter αναποζημίωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>uncompensated</div><b>αναποθήκευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναποθήκευτη, neuter αναποθήκευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unstorable</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> By surface analysis, αν- (an-, “not”) + αποθηκεύω + -τος (-tos, adjectival suffix).</div><b>αναποκατάστατος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναποκατάστατη, neuter αναποκατάστατο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. insolvent (bankrupt)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unreformed (sinner)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. unrehabilitated (criminal)</div>
  <div class='def'>4. unrestored</div>
  <div class='def'>5. (obsolete) not settled down (man)</div>
  <div class='def'>6. (obsolete) unmarried (woman)</div><b>αναπολόγητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπολόγητη, neuter αναπολόγητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. undefended</div>
  <div class='def'>2. without a hearing</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναπολόγητος.</div><b>αναπολώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to recall, recollect</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to reminisce, look back</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀναπολῶ, contracted form of ἀναπολέω.</div><b>αναποσφράγιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναποσφράγιστη, neuter αναποσφράγιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unopened, with unbroken seals</div><b>αναποτελεσματικά</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ineffectually, ineffective</div><b>αναποτελεσματικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναποτελεσματική, neuter αναποτελεσματικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ineffectual, ineffective</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from αν- (an-, α- privative) + αποτελεσματικός, a calque of French ineffectif (rare) and English ineffective.</div><b>αναποφάσιστα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>hesitantly, indecisively</div><b>αναποφάσιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναποφάσιστη, neuter αναποφάσιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. undecided</div>
  <div class='def'>2. indecisive, irresolute, hesitant</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αν- (an-, α- privative) + αποφάσισα + -τος (-tos), a calque of French indécis. First attested 1888.</div><b>αναποφασιστικότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) indecisiveness, indecision</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) irresolution, irresoluteness</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αναποφάσιστος + -ότητα, calque of French indécision. First attested 1877.</div><b>αναποχώριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναποχώριστη, neuter αναποχώριστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>inseparable</div><b>αναπροσανατολισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναπροσανατολισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reorientation</div><b>αναπροσαρμογή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναπροσαρμογές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. readjustment</div>
  <div class='def'>2. mark up, mark down (prices)</div><b>αναπροσαρμόζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to readjust (prices, wages, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to mark up, mark down</div><b>αναπτέρωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) boost, raising (morale, spirits)</div><b>αναπτήρας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναπτήρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>cigarette lighter</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ανάβω + -τήρας, calque of English lighter</div><b>αναπτερώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to raise, boost (morale, spirits)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Τα λόγια του μου <b>αναπτέρωσαν</b> το ηθικό. - His words boosted my morale.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to kindle</div><b>αναπτυγμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπτυγμένη, neuter αναπτυγμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. developed</div>
  <div class='def'>2. fully developed</div><b>αναπτυξιακός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπτυξιακή, neuter αναπτυξιακό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>developmental, development (to do with development)</div><b>αναπτύσσομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to mature, develop</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to deploy</div><b>αναπτύσσω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to unfold</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to develop, evolve, expand upon, expound</div><b>αναπυρώνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be relit)</div><b>αναπυρώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to reignite, relight</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to reignite (old arguments)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) to recall (old memories)</div><b>αναπόδεικτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπόδεικτη, neuter αναπόδεικτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unproven, unproved, unsubstantiated</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ᾰ̓νᾰπόδεικτος. See ἀποδείκνῡμι and ἀποδεικνύω. By surface analysis, αν- (an-, α- privative) + απόδειξη + -τος (-tos).</div><b>αναπόδειχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπόδειχτη, neuter αναπόδειχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναπόδεικτος">αναπόδεικτος</a></div><b>αναπόδοτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπόδοτη, neuter αναπόδοτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. untranslatable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unreturned, unreciprocated</div>
  <div class='def'>3. unmatched, unattributable</div><b>αναπόδραστα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>inevitably, unavoidably</div><b>αναπόδραστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπόδραστη, neuter αναπόδραστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. inevitable, inescapable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unavoidable</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναπόδραστος, from ἀν- (an-, “not”) + ἀποδιδράσκω.</div><b>αναπόκριτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπόκριτη, neuter αναπόκριτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unanswered</div><b>αναπόληση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναπολήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. contemplation</div>
  <div class='def'>2. reminiscence, recollection</div><b>αναπόσβεστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπόσβεστη, neuter αναπόσβεστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. still owing</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unliquidated</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀναπόσβεστος. By surface analysis, αν- (an-, α- privative) + αποσβεσ- (aposves-, “to erase, amortize”) + -τος (-tos), from ἀποσβέννῡμι.</div><b>αναπόσπαστα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>inseparably</div><b>αναπόσπαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπόσπαστη, neuter αναπόσπαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. integral (of one piece)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. inseparable, nondetachable</div><b>αναπότρεπτα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>inevitably, unavoidably</div><b>αναπότρεπτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unpreventable, unavoidable</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀναπότρεπτος -Late Koine in a papyrus Scholion-. By surface analysis, αν- (an-, α- privative) + αποτρέπ(ω)) + -τος (-tos).</div><b>αναπόφευκτα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>inevitably, unavoidably</div><b>αναπόφευκτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναπόφευκτη, neuter αναπόφευκτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unavoidable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unpreventable</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αν- (an-, α- privative) + αποφεύγω + -τος (-tos). See άφευκτος.</div><b>αναπύρωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναπυρώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. reignition</div>
  <div class='def'>2. resurgence</div><b>αναρίθμητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναρίθμητη, neuter αναρίθμητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>innumerable, countless</div><b>αναρθρία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) severe inarticulacy, severe weakness of pronunciation/articulation</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) anarthria</div><b>αναριγάω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναριγώ">αναριγώ</a></div><b>αναριγώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to shiver (with cold)</div><b>αναριεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to dilute, thin out, thin, spread out</div><b>αναριθμητισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναριθμητισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>renumbering</div><b>αναρμοδίως</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(formal) incompetently</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ποιος την άφησε να μιλήσει <b>αναρμοδίως</b> σ’ αυτό το θέμα; - Who let her speak incompetently on that subject?</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀναρμοδίως.</div><b>αναρμοδιότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναρμοδιότητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>incompetence, lack of jurisdiction (lack of legal authority to deal with a matter)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η <b>αναρμοδιότητα</b> του δικαστηρίου να εκδικάσει την υπόθεση. - The court&#x27;s lack of jurisdiction to try the case.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αν- (an-, α- privative) + αρμοδιότητα. First attested 1809 as αρμοδιότης.</div><b>αναρμόδια</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. nominative/accusative/vocative feminine singular of <a href="bword://αναρμόδιος">αναρμόδιος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αναρμόδιος">αναρμόδιος</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>incompetently</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ποιος την άφησε να μιλήσει <b>αναρμόδια</b> σ’ αυτό το θέμα; - Who let her speak incompetently on that subject?</div><b>αναρμόδιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναρμόδια, neuter αναρμόδιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. incompetent, unqualified (not having sufficient skill, knowledge or ability)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Αυτή είναι εντελώς <b>αναρμόδια</b> να κρίνει τέτοια θέματα. - She is completely unqualified to judge such matters.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. not responsible, irresponsible (not answerable for an act performed or for its consequences)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Αυτή η υπηρεσία είναι <b>αναρμόδια</b> για το θέμα που σε απασχολεί. - That service is not responsible for the area that you&#x27;re interested in.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀναρμόδιος. By surface analysis, αν- (an-, α- privative) + αρμόδιος.</div><b>αναρπάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to plunder (take violently)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to grab, snatch</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to snap up</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναρπάζω. By surface analysis, ανα- (ana-) + αρπάζω.</div><b>αναρρίπιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναζωπυρώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>enlivening, rekindling (especially a fire by blowing)</div><b>αναρρίχηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναρριχήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>climbing, clambering (an action or process)</div>
  <div class='ex'>η ορεινή <b>αναρρίχηση</b> - mountain climbing</div><b>αναρριγώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναριγώ">αναριγώ</a></div><b>αναρριπίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to blow on, fan, use bellows (to make a fire burn brightly)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to excite, stir up</div><b>αναρριχητικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναρριχητική, neuter αναρριχητικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>climbing, clambering</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αναρριχητικό</b> φυτό - climbing plant</div><b>αναρριχιέμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναρριχώμαι">αναρριχώμαι</a></div><b>αναρριχτός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναρριχτή, neuter αναρριχτό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανάρριχτος">ανάρριχτος</a></div><b>αναρριχώμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to climb, climb up, clamber up</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to creep</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) to crawl (to obtain promotion, etc)</div><b>αναρροφητήρας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναρροφητήρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>aspirator</div><b>αναρροφητικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναρροφητική, neuter αναρροφητικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>suction</div><b>αναρροφώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to suck, suck up, aspirate</div><b>αναρρούσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναρρούσες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>receding, recession (of a wave away from the shore)</div><b>αναρρυθμίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to amend, adjust, restore to order</div><b>αναρρωτήριο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναρρωτήρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>convalescent home, sanatorium, infirmary</div><b>αναρρωτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναρρωτική, neuter αναρρωτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>convalescent, recuperative</div><b>αναρρόφηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναρροφήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>suction</div><b>αναρρύθμιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναρρυθμίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>adjustment, readjustment, amendment</div><b>αναρρώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to recover, get better, convalesce</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀναρρώννυμι &lt; ἀνά + ῥώννυμι with metaplasm to -ώνω. Ultimately from Ancient Greek ῥώμη.</div><b>αναρτήρας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναρτήρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. trapeze (bar for patient to pull themselves up)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (literary) hanger, sling (something to suspend from)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (literary) earring</div><b>αναρτημένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αναρτημένη, neuter αναρτημένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>hung, suspended</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η ανακοίνωση είναι <b>αναρτημένη</b> στον πίνακα ανακοινώσεων. - The memo is hung on the notice board.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αναρτώμαι, passive voice of αναρτώ (“hang, suspend”).</div><b>αναρτώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to hang, hang up, suspend</div><b>αναρχία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) anarchy</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) lawlessness</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀναρχίᾱ. By surface analysis, αν- (an-, α- privative) + αρχή + -ία.</div><b>αναρχική</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναρχικές, masculine αναρχικός)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anarchist (female)</div><b>αναρχικιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναρχικιές, masculine αναρχικός)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναρχική">αναρχική</a></div><b>αναρχικός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναρχικοί, feminine αναρχική or αναρχικιά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anarchist (male)</div><b>αναρχικότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) anarchism (situation, condition)</div><b>αναρχισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) anarchism (ideology, philosophy)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From French anarchisme (“anarchism”).</div><b>αναρχοαυτόνομος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναρχοαυτόνομοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anarchist (behaving autonomously - as an in dividual)</div><b>αναρχούμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to govern anarchically</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to behave anarchically</div><b>αναρωτιέμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to wonder, ponder, contemplate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to ask yourself</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to wonder if or whether</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀναρωτῶ + -ιέμαι; see αναρωτώ for more.</div><b>αναρωτώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to enquire (UK) inquire (US) (with special interest)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to ask again, reask</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀναρωτῶ, from Ancient Greek ἀνερωτῶ, ἀνερωτάω; by surface analysis, ανα- (ana-, “re-”) + ρωτάω.</div><b>ανασάλεμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανασαλέματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>stirring</div><b>ανασέρνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to retract; to pull out, pull up</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to retract; to draw, draw out, draw up</div><b>ανασήκωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανασηκώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>raising, lifting, turning up (eyebrow, skirt)</div><b>ανασαίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to breathe, sigh</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to sigh with relief</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀνασαίνω, from earlier ἀνεσαίνω, from Ancient Greek ᾰ̓́νεσῐς + -αίνω. By surface analysis, άνεση + -αίνω.</div><b>ανασαιμιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανασαιμιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>breath, breathing, respiration</div><b>ανασαλεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (transitive) to move something gently, stir</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (intransitive) to move gently, waft, drift</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from the Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀνασαλεύω. By surface analysis, ανα- (“upward”) + σαλεύω (“move lightly”).</div><b>ανασασμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανασασμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. breathing</div>
  <div class='def'>2. breather (time to get breath)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. respite, relief</div><b>ανασηκωμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανασηκωμένη, neuter ανασηκωμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>raised, rolled up, turned up</div><b>ανασηκώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to raise (higher)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to lift, sit up, rise up</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to roll up, turn up, tuck up (sleeves, collar, hem of dress, etc)</div><b>ανασκάβομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανασκάπτομαι">ανασκάπτομαι</a></div><b>ανασκάβω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανασκάπτω">ανασκάπτω</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> As ανασκάπτω, with ανα- (“thoroughly”) + σκάβω (“dig”), metaplasm of the ancient σκάπτω.</div><b>ανασκάλεμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανασκαλέματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>rummaging, raking up</div><b>ανασκάπτομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to be dug, dug up, excavated</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (formal) to be razed to the ground</div><b>ανασκάπτω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to dig, dig up, excavate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (formal) to raze to the ground</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀνασκάπτω. By surface analysis, ανα- (“thoroughly”) and the ancient σκάπτω.</div><b>ανασκάφθηκα</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of ανασκάφτηκα</div><b>ανασκάφτομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανασκάπτομαι">ανασκάπτομαι</a></div><b>ανασκάφτω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανασκάπτω">ανασκάπτω</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> As ανασκάπτω, with ανα- (“thoroughly”) + σκάφτω (“dig”), dissimilation of σκάβω, itself a metaplasm of the ancient σκάπτω.</div><b>ανασκίρτημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανασκιρτήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. jump, start (the result of a sudden shock)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. leap (with joy)</div><b>ανασκίρτηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) jump, start (the result of a sudden shock)</div><b>ανασκαλεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to rummage, rake, rake through, rootle</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Ανασκαλεύω</b> τη φωτιά και τα κάρβουνα στο τζάκι. - I rake the fire and coals at the fireplace.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀνασκαλεύω.</div><b>ανασκαφέας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανασκαφείς)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. excavator, digger (machine)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. archaeologist, excavator, digger</div><b>ανασκαφή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανασκαφές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. excavation</div>
  <div class='def'>2. digging</div><b>ανασκαφικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανασκαφική, neuter ανασκαφικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>excavational, excavation (relating to an excavation or an excavation site)</div><b>ανασκευάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to rebut, refute</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνασκευάζω. By surface analysis, ανα- (ana-) + σκευάζω.</div><b>ανασκευάσιμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανασκευάσιμη, neuter ανασκευάσιμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>rebuttable, refutable</div><b>ανασκευή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανασκευές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>rebuttal, disproof, refutation</div><b>ανασκευαστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανασκευαστική, neuter ανασκευαστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>rebutting, refutatory</div><b>ανασκιρτάω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανασκιρτώ">ανασκιρτώ</a></div><b>ανασκιρτώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to start, be startled, jump with surprise</div><b>ανασκολοπίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to impale</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to destroy, kill</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) to ravage, maltreat</div><b>ανασκολοπισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανασκολοπισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>impalement</div><b>ανασκολοπιστής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανασκολοπιστές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>impaler</div>
  <div class='ex'>Βλαντ ο <b>Ανασκολοπιστής</b> - Vlad the Impaler</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀνασκολοπιστής, equivalent to ανασκολοπ- (anaskolop-, “to impale”) + -ιστής.</div><b>ανασκολόπιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανασκολοπίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>impalement</div><b>ανασκολόπισμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανασκολοπίσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>impalement</div><b>ανασκοπώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to survey, review, go over, scrutinise (UK), scrutinize (US)</div><b>ανασκουμπώνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to roll up one&#x27;s sleeves</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to get ready, prepare (for a task), gird one&#x27;s loins</div><b>ανασκουμπώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to roll up</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly, figuratively) to roll up one&#x27;s sleeves, prepare for work</div><b>ανασκούμπωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανασκουμπώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>the rolling up of sleeves, preparation for a task</div><b>ανασκόπηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανασκοπήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>review, survey</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from ανασκοπώ + -ση (-si), a calque of French révision and English review.</div><b>ανασπάζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(literary) to kiss, touch with the lips</div><b>ανασπώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to extort, extract</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to pull out</div><b>αναστάσιμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναστάσιμη, neuter αναστάσιμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Easter</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αναστάσιμα</b> τροπάρια - Easter hymn</div><b>αναστάτωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναστατώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>confusion, turmoil, disorder, chaos</div><b>αναστάτωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναστατώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>confusion, turmoil, upset, agitation, chaos</div><b>αναστέλλομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be suspended</div><b>αναστέλλω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to suspend (halt process temporarily)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Αναστέλλεται</b> η λειτουργία της υπηρεσίας εξυπηρέτησης πελατών. - The operation of customer service is suspended.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to suspend temporarily by law, or decree</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η κυβέρνηση <b>αναστέλλει</b> την εφαρμογή του νόμου. - The government suspends the implementation of the Act/law.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀναστέλλω. Morphologically, from ανα- (“back, backwards”) + the ancient στέλλω (“send”)</div><b>αναστέναγμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναστενάγματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sigh, groan</div><b>αναστένω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανασταίνω">ανασταίνω</a></div><b>αναστήλωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναστηλώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>restoration, reconstruction</div><b>αναστήνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανασταίνω">ανασταίνω</a></div><b>ανασταίνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to come back to life, resurrect</div><b>ανασταίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to resurrect, revive, revitalise (UK), revitalize (US), bring back to life</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνίστημι.</div><b>ανασταλτικό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανασταλτικά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>inhibition</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From ανασταλτικός.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://ανασταλτικός">ανασταλτικός</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://ανασταλτικός">ανασταλτικός</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From ανασταλτικός.</div><b>ανασταλτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανασταλτική, neuter ανασταλτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. inhibitory, inhibiting, deterring</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ανασταλτικός</b> παράγοντας - inhibiting factor, inhibitor</div>
  <div class='def'>2. checking, restraining</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ανασταλτικό</b> βέτο - restraining veto</div><b>ανασταλτός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανασταλτή, neuter ανασταλτό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(formal) suspendable (able or eligible to be suspended)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η ποινή του είναι <b>ανασταλτή</b>. - His sentence is suspendable.</div><b>αναστατικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναστατική, neuter αναστατικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anastatic</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> By surface analysis, ανάσταση + -ικός.</div><b>αναστατώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to disturb, disarrange</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to put in a panic</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) to disturb (emotions)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναστατέω + -ώνω; see ἄνω + ἵστημι for more on the components.</div><b>αναστενάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to sigh (with relief, grief, etc)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναστενάζω. Morphologically, from ανα- + στενάζω.</div><b>αναστενάρης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναστενάρηδες, feminine αναστενάρισσα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>firewalker (especially at Nestinarstvo)</div><b>αναστενάρια</b>
  <div><i>name, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Nestinarstvo (a traditional Greek/Bulgarian firewalking festival)</div><b>αναστενάρισσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναστενάρισσες, masculine αναστενάρης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>firewalker</div><b>αναστενάριων</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of αναστεναρίων</div><b>αναστεναγμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναστεναγμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sigh, groan</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀναστεναγμός. Morphologically, from ανα- (ana-) + στεναγμός.</div><b>αναστεναριών</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of αναστεναρίων</div><b>αναστηλωτής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναστηλωτές, feminine αναστηλώτρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>restorer, rebuilder</div><b>αναστηλώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to restore, reconstruct, rebuild</div><b>αναστηλώτρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναστηλώτριες, masculine αναστηλωτής)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>restorer, rebuilder</div><b>αναστολέας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναστολείς)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. inhibitor, inhibiting factor</div>
  <div class='ex'>ένας <b>αναστολέας</b> ενζύμου - an enzyme inhibitor</div>
  <div class='def'>2. stopper, gripe (short rope used for securing something)</div><b>αναστολή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναστολές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. suspension, abeyance, postponement</div>
  <div class='def'>2. suspended sentence</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (in plural) inhibitions</div><b>αναστομώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to make or enlarge a hole, ream</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to anastomose</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to sharpen, whet</div>
  <div class='def'>4. to smooth</div><b>αναστρέφω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to reverse, flip, turn over</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀναστρέφω. Morphologically from ανα- (“re-”) + στρέφω (“turn”).</div><b>αναστρέψιμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναστρέψιμη, neuter αναστρέψιμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reversible, correctable</div><b>αναστροφέας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναστροφείς)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>inverter, power inverter</div><b>αναστροφή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναστροφές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. anastrophe; inversion of word order</div>
  <div class='def'>2. anastrophe; inversion of stress position</div>
  <div class='def'>3. lying on the back with legs raised</div>
  <div class='def'>4. tack</div>
  <div class='def'>5. lateral reversal of organ position</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναστροφή.</div><b>αναστυλώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to support (a column)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to restore</div><b>αναστόμωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναστομώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. anastomosis (the hole or its creation)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. anastomosis</div><b>αναστύλωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναστυλώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναστήλωση">αναστήλωση</a></div><b>ανασυγκροτώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to rebuild, reconstruct</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to re-form, regroup, reorganise</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ανα- (“again, re-”) + συγκροτώ (“form, compose”)</div><b>ανασυγκρότηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανασυγκροτήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. reconstruction, reorganisation (UK), reorganization (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. regrouping, re-formation</div><b>ανασυνδέω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to reconnect, renew</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ανα- (ana-, “re”) + συνδέω</div><b>ανασυνθέτω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to recompose, to restructure, rearrange</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from ανα- (ana-) + συνθέτω, a calque of French recomposer.</div><b>ανασυνιστώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to reconstitute, re-establish, rebuild</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ανα- (“re-”) + συνιστώ (“establish”) from the ancient verb συνιστῶ, συνίστημι. Calque of French reconstituer. First attested in 1833.</div><b>ανασυντάσσω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to reorganise (UK), reorganize (US), regroup, rearrange, restructure</div><b>ανασυρτός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανασυρτή, neuter ανασυρτό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>retractable, retracted</div><b>ανασυστήνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to reconstitute, re-establish, rebuild</div><b>ανασυσταίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανασυστήνω">ανασυστήνω</a></div><b>ανασφάλεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανασφάλειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>insecurity (sense or feeling)</div><b>ανασφάλιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανασφάλιστη, neuter ανασφάλιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. insecure</div>
  <div class='def'>2. uninsured</div><b>ανασφαλής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανασφαλής, neuter ανασφαλές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>insecure</div><b>ανασχετικό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανασχετικά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>deterrent</div><b>ανασχετικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανασχετική, neuter ανασχετικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>deterring, deterrent</div><b>ανασχηματίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to reassemble, re-form</div><b>ανασχηματισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανασχηματισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. reassembly, reformation</div>
  <div class='def'>2. reshuffle</div><b>ανασόνι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανασόνια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anise (Pimpinella anisum)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ottoman Turkish آناصون (anason), ultimately a reborrowing from Ancient Greek ἄνισον.</div><b>ανασύνδεση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανασυνδέσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. reconnection</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) renewal</div><b>ανασύνθεση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανασυνθέσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>recomposition, reconstitution, restructuring, rearrangement</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from ανασυνθέ(τω)) + -ση (-si), a calque of French recomposition.</div><b>ανασύνταξη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανασυντάξεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. reorganisation (UK), reorganization (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. regrouping, recategorisation</div><b>ανασύρω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to retract; to pull out, pull up</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to retract; to draw, draw out, draw up</div><b>ανασύσταση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανασυστάσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reconstitution, re-establishment</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from ανασυστή(νω)) + -ση (-si), a calque of French reconstitution.</div><b>ανατ.</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://ανατολικός">ανατολικός</a>: Anatolian, of Asia Minor</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://ανατομία">ανατομία</a>: anatomy</div><b>ανατάραξη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναταράξεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disturbance, turmoil (the effect or the result)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αναταράξεις</b> του αεροπλάνου λόγω κενών αέρος - disturbances in the aircraft due to air turbulence</div><b>ανατάσσω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to reset</div><b>ανατέλλω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to rise, appear (celestial objects, especially the sun)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Ανατέλλει</b> ο ήλιος! - The sun rises!</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to dawn</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Ανατέλλει</b> μια νέα εποχή. - A new era is dawning.</div><b>ανατέμνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to dissect</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to dissect, pull apart (an opinion, theory, etc)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνατέμνω. By surface analysis, ανα- (ana-) + τέμνω.</div><b>ανατίμηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανατιμήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. increase in prices, price rise</div>
  <div class='def'>2. revaluation (of a currency)</div><b>ανατίναγμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανατινάγματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>jolt, bump, jerk</div><b>ανατίναξη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανατινάξεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>blowing up, blasting (act and result)</div><b>αναταράζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to shake, agitate, stir</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ᾰ̓νᾰτᾰράσσω / ᾰ̓νᾰτᾰράττω, in the pattern of change of ταράσσω &gt; ταράζω. Morphologically, from ανα- (“re-”) + ταράζω (“shake”).</div><b>αναταράσσω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναταράζω">αναταράζω</a></div><b>αναταραχή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναταραχές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unrest, disturbance</div>
  <div class='ex'>Οι απολύσεις προκάλεσαν <b>αναταραχή</b> μεταξύ των εργατών. - The layoffs caused unrest among the workers.</div><b>ανατείνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to list, raise (especially of the hands)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to stretch, stretch up</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀνατείνω. By surface analysis, ανα- (“re-”) + τείνω (“stretch”).</div><b>ανατιμητικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανατιμητική, neuter ανατιμητικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>upwards, upward</div><b>ανατιμώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to increase, appreciate, mark up (prices, financial value)</div><b>ανατινάζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be blown up</div><b>ανατινάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to explode, blow up</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνᾰτῐνάσσω. Morphologically, from ανα- + τινάζω.</div><b>ανατινάσσω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανατινάζω">ανατινάζω</a></div><b>ανατοκίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to add interest compoundly, capitalise interest (UK), capitalize interest (US)</div><b>ανατοκισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανατοκισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>compound interest</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνατοκισμός.</div><b>ανατολή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανατολές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. east, East</div>
  <div class='ex'>από την <b>ανατολή</b> ως την δύση - from east to west</div>
  <div class='def'>2. sunrise, dawn; moonrise</div>
  <div class='ex'>από την <b>ανατολή</b> ως την δύση - from sunrise to sunset</div>
  <div class='def'>3. Orient, (the) East</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνατολή, from ἀνατέλλω, from ἀνά + τέλλω.</div><b>ανατολίστρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανατολίστριες, masculine ανατολιστής)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>orientalist</div><b>ανατολίτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανατολίτες, feminine ανατολίτισσα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. Anatolian (a person, usually male, from Anatolia or of Anatolian ethnicity)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. Oriental (a person, usually male, from the East)</div><b>ανατολίτικος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Oriental, Levantine</div><b>ανατολίτισσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανατολίτισσες, masculine ανατολίτης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. Anatolian (a female person from Anatolia or of Anatolian ethnicity)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. Oriental (a female person from the East)</div><b>ανατολικά</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>in the east, east</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://ανατολικός">ανατολικός</a></div><b>ανατολικά-βορειοανατολικά</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>east-northeast</div><b>ανατολικά-νοτιοανατολικά</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>east-southeast</div><b>ανατολικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανατολική, neuter ανατολικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>eastern, of the east</div><b>ανατολιστής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανατολιστές, feminine ανατολίστρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>orientalist</div><b>ανατομ.</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://ανατομία">ανατομία</a>: anatomy</div><b>ανατομή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανατομές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>dissection (for anatomical study)</div><b>ανατομία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anatomy</div><b>ανατομείο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανατομεία)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anatomy theatre (UK), anatomy theater (US), anatomy laboratory, anatomy room</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ανατομία + -είο</div><b>ανατομικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανατομική, neuter ανατομικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anatomical</div><b>ανατοποθέτηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανατοποθετήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>repositioning</div><b>ανατοποθετώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to replace, restore, put back</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to place again (somewhere else)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from ανα- (ana-) + τοποθετώ.</div><b>ανατρέπω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to defeat, thwart</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to overrule, overturn</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to overturn, capsize</div>
  <div class='def'>4. to refute</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned. From Ancient Greek ἀνατρέπω. By surface analysis, ανα- (“upward”) + τρέπω (“turn”).</div><b>ανατρέφω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to bring up, raise, nurture</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to foster, mother</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνατρέφω. Morphologically from ανα- (ana-) + τρέφω.</div><b>ανατρέχω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to go back</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to backdate</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀνατρέχω</div><b>ανατρέψιμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανατρέψιμη, neuter ανατρέψιμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reversible, correctable</div><b>ανατρίχιασμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανατριχιάσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. shivering, trembling,</div>
  <div class='def'>2. giving: horror, goosebumps</div><b>ανατραπήκανε</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>colloquial variation of ανατραπήκαν, third-person plural simple past of <a href="bword://ανατρέπω">ανατρέπω</a></div><b>ανατρεπτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανατρεπτική, neuter ανατρεπτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. subversive, revolutionary, seditious</div>
  <div class='def'>2. refuting, annulling</div><b>ανατρεπόμενο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανατρεπόμενα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>dumper truck, dump truck, dumper, tipper lorry</div><b>ανατρεπόμενος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανατρεπόμενη, neuter ανατρεπόμενο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. tipping, dumping</div>
  <div class='def'>2. reversible, reversed</div>
  <div class='def'>3. overthrown</div><b>ανατριχίλα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανατριχίλες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. shivering, trembling</div>
  <div class='def'>2. dread, goosebumps</div><b>ανατριχιάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to tremble, shiver, shudder, quiver</div><b>ανατριχιαστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανατριχιαστική, neuter ανατριχιαστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. terrifying, frightening</div>
  <div class='def'>2. gruesome, ghastly</div><b>ανατροπέας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural ανατροπείς)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. equipment or apparatus for tipping</div>
  <div class='def'>2. subverter, subversive person</div><b>ανατροπή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανατροπές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. upsetting, turning over</div>
  <div class='def'>2. reversing, reverting</div>
  <div class='def'>3. knocking over, knocking down</div><b>ανατροφή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) upbringing, education</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) nurture, breeding</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀνατροφή. Morphologically ανα- (ana-) + τροφή.</div><b>ανατροφοδοτώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to supply, provision</div>
