  <div class='def'>unbuilt</div><b>αναυτολόγητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναυτολόγητη, neuter αναυτολόγητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unemployed</div>
  <div class='def'>2. not on the ship&#x27;s register/muster roll</div><b>αναφ.</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://αναφορικός">αναφορικός</a>: referential, relating to a reference</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://αναφορά">αναφορά</a>: reference</div><b>αναφέρομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to come up, refer to, relate to (in conversation)</div><b>αναφέρω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to mention, present, announce</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to cite, refer</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναφέρω. By surface analysis, ανα- (“re-, again”) + φέρω (“bear, carry”).</div><b>αναφαίνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to appear, emerge</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to look again</div><b>αναφαίρετος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>inalienable</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αναφαίρετο</b> ανθρώπινο δικαίωμα - inalienable human right</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀναφαίρετος. By surface analysis, αν- (an-, α- privative) + αφαιρώ + -τος (-tos).</div><b>αναφαγιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναφαγιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fasting, dieting</div><b>αναφανδόν</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>overtly, in plain view</div><b>αναφιλητό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναφιλητά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sobbing, sobs, intense weeping</div><b>αναφιλυτό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναφιλυτά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναφιλητό">αναφιλητό</a></div><b>αναφλέγομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to catch fire, be ignited</div><b>αναφλέγω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to set light to, ignite, kindle</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to flare up</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) to excite, arouse, incense</div><b>αναφλεκτήρας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναφλεκτήρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>spark plug, sparking plug</div><b>αναφομοίωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναφομοίωτη, neuter αναφομοίωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unassimilated, unassimilatable</div><b>αναφορ.</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://αναφορικός">αναφορικός</a>: referential, relating to a reference</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://αναφορά">αναφορά</a>: reference</div><b>αναφορά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναφορές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. reference</div>
  <div class='def'>2. report</div>
  <div class='def'>3. account</div>
  <div class='def'>4. mention</div>
  <div class='def'>5. petition</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναφορά.</div><b>αναφορικά</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>concerning, with regard to</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αναφορικός">αναφορικός</a></div><b>αναφορικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναφορική, neuter αναφορικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. relative</div>
  <div class='def'>2. referential</div><b>αναφουφουλιάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to fluff up, plump up (cushion, mattress, etc)</div><b>αναφροδισία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναφροδισίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>lack of sexual desire/urge, frigidity</div><b>αναφροδισιακός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναφροδισιακή, neuter αναφροδισιακό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. anaphrodisiac, antaphrodisiac, anaphrodisiacal (reducing the sex drive)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. frigid</div><b>αναφρόδιτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναφρόδιτη, neuter αναφρόδιτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>lacking a sexual urge, unlibidinous</div><b>αναφτερουγίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to flutter, flap (wings)</div><b>αναφτερώνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of αναπτερώνομαι</div><b>αναφτερώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναπτερώνω">αναπτερώνω</a></div><b>αναφτός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναφτή, neuter αναφτό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>lit, lighted</div><b>αναφυλακτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναφυλακτική, neuter αναφυλακτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anaphylactic</div><b>αναφυλαξία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) anaphylaxis</div><b>αναφυλλητό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναφυλλητά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναφιλητό">αναφιλητό</a></div><b>αναφυσώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to blow (so as to kindle)</div><b>αναφυτεύομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be replanted</div><b>αναφυτεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(formal) to replant</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Katharevousa ἀναφυτεύω, from Ancient Greek ἀναφυτεύω. Morphologically, from ανα- (“re-, again”) + φυτεύω (“I plant”).</div><b>αναφωνητό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναφωνητά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>cry, shout, yell</div><b>αναφωνώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to exclaim, ejaculate, cry out</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀναφωνῶ, from Ancient Greek ἀναφωνέω.</div><b>αναφύομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (figuratively, formal, intransitive) to spring up, arise (e.g. of problems, new issues)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το πρόγραμμα εκτελείτο απρόσκοπτα, αλλά ξαφνικά <b>ανεφύησαν</b> προβλήματα - The programme was running smoothly, but suddenly, problems have sprung up.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively, intransitive, literally) to grow again</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ᾰ̓νᾰφῠ́ομαι of active ᾰ̓νᾰφῠ́ω. The figurative sense, a semantic loan from French surgir. Morphologically, from ανα- (“again”) + φύομαι.</div><b>αναφύτευση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναφυτεύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. replanting</div>
  <div class='def'>2. transplanting</div><b>αναφώνηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναφωνήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>exclamation, interjection, cry, ejaculation</div><b>αναχαίτιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναχαιτίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>restraint, curbing, checking</div><b>αναχαιτίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to curb, restrain, repel (an enemy)</div><b>αναχαράζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to ruminate, chew the cud</div><b>αναχλός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναχλή, neuter αναχλό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. loose</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αναχλό</b> χώμα - loose earth</div>
  <div class='def'>2. shallow</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) relaxed</div><b>αναχρονισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναχρονισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anachronism</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναχρονισμός.</div><b>αναχρονιστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναχρονιστική, neuter αναχρονιστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anachronistic</div><b>αναχωμάτωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναχωματώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>heaping up or accumulation of earth during the formation of a trench or embankment</div><b>αναχωματίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to heap soil (forming an embankment or trench)</div><b>αναχωματώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to heap soil (forming an embankment or trench)</div><b>αναχωνεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to recast, refound; melt down</div><b>αναχωρήτρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναχωρήτριες, masculine αναχωρητής)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>hermit, recluse, anchorite (anachorite), eremite</div><b>αναχωρητήριο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναχωρητήρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>hermitage</div><b>αναχωρητής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αναχωρητές, feminine αναχωρήτρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>hermit, recluse, anchorite (anachorite), eremite</div><b>αναχωρητισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναχωρητήρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anachoresis (the way of life of an anchorite)</div><b>αναχωρώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to depart, leave (bus, train, etc.)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to depart from the everyday world, become a recluse</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναχωρῶ.</div><b>αναχόρταγος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναχόρταγη, neuter αναχόρταγο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανεχόρταγος">ανεχόρταγος</a></div><b>αναχώνευση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναχωνεύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>recasting, refounding; melting down</div><b>αναχώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to cover with earth, bury</div><b>αναχώρηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναχωρήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>departure, leaving, sailing</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀναχώρησις + -ση. For the modern meaning of &quot;departure&quot;, semantic loan from French depart.</div><b>αναψηλάφηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναψηλαφήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>review (the re-opening and re-examination of a closed case)</div><b>αναψηλαφώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to review (to re-opening and re-examination of a previous case)</div><b>αναψοκοκκίνησα</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>frequent misspelling of αναψοκοκκίνισα, first-person singular simple past of <a href="bword://αναψοκοκκινίζω">αναψοκοκκινίζω</a></div><b>αναψοκοκκινίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to become red in the face (through exercise or anger)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfective stem αναψ- of ανάβω + κοκκινίζω</div><b>αναψυκτήριο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναψυκτήρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. coffee bar, milk bar, etc (outlet for soft drinks, coffee, ice cream, etc.)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. refreshment room</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀναψυκτήριον, from the past stem ἀναψυκ- (anapsuk-) of ἀναψύχω + -τήριον, with semantic loan from German Εrfrischungsraum.</div><b>αναψυκτικό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αναψυκτικά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. soft drink (non-alcoholic, often fizzy)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. refreshment (drink, ice cream, ext)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned formation from the nominalized neuter of αναψυκτικός, with semantic loan from French rafraîchissement.</div><b>αναψυκτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναψυκτική, neuter αναψυκτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>relating to soft drinks</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned formation from αναψυκ- (anapsyk-), combining form of αναψύχω, + -τικός, with semantic loan from French rafraîchissant.</div><b>αναψυχή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) recreation, amusement, entertainment; rest, diversion, pastime, relaxation</div><b>αναψυχώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to give courage again, cheer up</div><b>αναψύχω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to make cool again</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to refresh (through rest or activity)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) to give fresh vigour, entertain</div><b>αναψύχωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αναψυχώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>cheering up, reinvigoration</div><b>αναύλωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναύλωτη, neuter αναύλωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unchartered</div><b>αναύξητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αναύξητη, neuter αναύξητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unincreasable, unincreased</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unaugmented (of verbs)</div><b>ανγκολέζικος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανγκολέζικη, neuter ανγκολέζικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αγκολέζικος">αγκολέζικος</a></div><b>ανδαλουσιανός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανδαλουσιανή, neuter ανδαλουσιανό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Andalusian (relating to Andalusia or its people)</div><b>ανδράδελφος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανδράδελφοι, feminine ανδραδέλφη)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sister-in-law (the sister of one&#x27;s spouse)</div><b>ανδράποδο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανδράποδα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. slave</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) creep (a grovelling or obsequious person)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνδράποδον.</div><b>ανδράχλη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αντράκλα">αντράκλα</a></div><b>ανδρίκειος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανδρίκεια, neuter ανδρίκειο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αντρίκειος">αντρίκειος</a></div><b>ανδρίκιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανδρίκια, neuter ανδρίκιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αντρίκειος">αντρίκειος</a></div><b>ανδραγάθημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανδραγαθήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>heroic feat, act of prowess</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Fom Ancient Greek ἀνδραγάθημα.</div><b>ανδραγαθία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) bravery, valour (UK), valor (US), prowess (ability to be brave)</div><b>ανδραγαθώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to fight bravely/valiantly</div><b>ανδραδέλφη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανδραδέλφες, masculine ανδράδελφος)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sister-in-law (the sister of one&#x27;s spouse)</div><b>ανδραποδίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of εξανδραποδίζω</div><b>ανδραποδισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανδραποδισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>enslavement, bondage</div><b>ανδρεία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανδρείες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>virtue, bravery, courage, valor</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνδρεία.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. nominative/accusative/vocative feminine singular of <a href="bword://ανδρείος">ανδρείος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://ανδρείος">ανδρείος</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> See the etymology of the corresponding lemma form.</div><b>ανδρείκελο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανδρείκελα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. puppet, marionette</div>
  <div class='def'>2. manikin, mannequin, dummy</div>
  <div class='def'>3. model, manikin, mannequin</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (figuratively) puppet, stooge</div>
  <div class='ex'>κυβέρρνηση <b>ανδρεικέλων</b> - a puppet government</div><b>ανδρείος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανδρεία, neuter ανδρείο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>brave, courageous, valorous, valiant</div><b>ανδρειεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αντρειεύω">αντρειεύω</a></div><b>ανδρειοσύνη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) bravery, valour (UK), valor (US), prowess (ability to be brave)</div><b>ανδρειωμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανδρειωμένη, neuter ανδρειωμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>brave, courageous, valorous, valiant</div><b>ανδρειώνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to be brave, to be courageous, to be a man</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to mature, reach manhood</div><b>ανδρειώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to make brave, fill with courage</div><b>ανδριάντας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανδριάντες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>statue</div><b>ανδριαντοποιΐα</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανδριαντοποιία">ανδριαντοποιία</a> (&#x27;incorrectly&#x27; accented)</div><b>ανδριαντοποιία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανδριαντοποιίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>statuary, sculpture</div><b>ανδριαντοποιός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural ανδριαντοποιοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sculptor, sculptress (of statues)</div><b>ανδρικό μόριο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανδρικά μόρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(euphemistic) penis (male member)</div><b>ανδρικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανδρική, neuter ανδρικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. men&#x27;s, for men</div>
  <div class='def'>2. masculine, male, not effeminate.</div><b>ανδρισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανδρισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. manliness, manhood, virility, masculinity</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (euphemistic) manhood (male genitalia)</div><b>ανδρογυνία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) androgyny</div><b>ανδρογυναίκα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανδρογυναίκες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αντρογυναίκα">αντρογυναίκα</a></div><b>ανδρογυνισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανδρογυνισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>androgyny</div><b>ανδρογόνο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανδρογόνα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. androgen (hormone)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (in plural, often) any of a group of compounds (anabolic steroids, male hormones, etc) which stimulate male characteristics.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From French androgène.</div><b>ανδροκοίτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανδροκοίτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sexual activity between men: anal sex, buggery</div><b>ανδροκρατία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) domination by men, androcracy</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From άνδρας + -κρατία, Calque of English androcracy.</div><b>ανδροκρατικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανδροκρατική, neuter ανδροκρατικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>androcratic</div><b>ανδροκρατούμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to be male dominated, dominated by a man or men</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to be patriarchal</div><b>ανδροκρατούμενος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανδροκρατούμενη, neuter ανδροκρατούμενο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>male dominated, dominated by a man or men</div><b>ανδρολογία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) andrology</div><b>ανδρολόγος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανδρολόγοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>andrologist</div><b>ανδροπρέπεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανδροπρέπειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>manliness, mannishness, masculinity, machismo</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀνδροπρέπεια.</div><b>ανδροπρεπής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανδροπρεπής, neuter ανδροπρεπές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>manly, masculine (in appearance and behaviour)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ανδροπρεπής &lt; άνδρας + -πρεπής</div><b>ανδροφέρνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αντροφέρνω">αντροφέρνω</a></div><b>ανδρων.</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://ανδρωνυμικό">ανδρωνυμικό</a>: andronym</div><b>ανδρωνίτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανδρωνίτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>rooms for men, men&#x27;s quarters</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀνδρών.</div><b>ανδρωνυμικό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανδρωνυμικά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>andronym</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀνήρ + ὄνυμα.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://ανδρωνυμικός">ανδρωνυμικός</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://ανδρωνυμικός">ανδρωνυμικός</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀνήρ + ὄνυμα.</div><b>ανδρωνυμικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανδρωνυμική, neuter ανδρωνυμικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>relating to an andronym</div><b>ανδρόγυνος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανδρόγυνοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. androgyne</div>
  <div class='def'>2. hermaphrodite</div><b>ανδρόπαυση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) andropause, male menopause</div><b>ανδρώνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to become a man, reach manhood</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to become stronger, complete, to develop</div><b>ανδρώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to make mature (literally, make a youth become a man)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to develop, make complete</div><b>ανείπωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανείπωτη, neuter ανείπωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unspeakable, inexpressible, ineffable, untold</div><b>ανείσπρακτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανείσπρακτη, neuter ανείσπρακτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>uncollected, unpaid</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ανείσπρακτοι</b> φόροι - unpaid taxes</div><b>ανείσπραχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανείσπραχτη, neuter ανείσπραχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανείσπρακτος">ανείσπρακτος</a></div><b>ανεβάζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (rare) passive of <a href="bword://ανεβάζω">ανεβάζω</a> used in expressions for</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το πιάνο <b>ανεβάστηκε</b> στον πέμπτο όροφο με γερανό. - The piano was lifted up to the tenth floor by a crane.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (rare) passive of <a href="bword://ανεβάζω">ανεβάζω</a> used in expressions for</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ο «Άμλετ» <b>ανεβάστηκε</b> από τρεις θιάσους πέρσι. - Hamlet was produced by three different companies last year.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (rare) passive of <a href="bword://ανεβάζω">ανεβάζω</a> used in expressions for</div>
  <div class='ex'>Τα αρχεία <b>ανεβάστηκαν</b> πολύ γρήγορα. - The files were uploaded very fast.</div><b>ανεβάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (with rare passive) to take up</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (with rare passive) to lift, carry up</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (with rare passive) to raise</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (with rare passive) to increase</div>
  <div class='def'>5. (with rare passive) to upload</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το αρχείο <b>ανεβάστηκε</b> πέρσι. Θα πρέπει να <b>ανεβάσω</b> ένα καινούριο. - The file was uploaded last year. I should upload a new one.</div>
  <div class='def'>6. (of theatrical performances, with rare passive) to produce</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀνέβαζω, from Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀναβάζω. The ⟨ε⟩ based on the augments from the past tense stem ανεβασ- or past ἀνέβασα). From the Ancient Greek ἀναβιβάζω.</div><b>ανεβαίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (transitive) to go up, climb</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Ανεβαίνω</b> τις σκάλες. - I climb the stairs.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (intransitive) to ascend</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ο ήλιος έχει <b>ανέβει</b> ψηλά στον ουρανό. - The sun has risen high in the sky.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (intransitive) to board, get in, get on (bus, ship, car, bicycle)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Ανεβαίνουμε</b> στο πλοίο. - We board the ferry.</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (intransitive) to be promoted, move up (qualification, job grade)</div>
  <div class='def'>5. (intransitive) to increase (temperature, blood pressure, atmospheric pressure)</div>
  <div class='def'>6. (intransitive) to rise (water level)</div>
  <div class='def'>7. (intransitive) to be uploaded)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το αρχείο <b>ανέβηκε</b> πέρσι. - The file was uploaded last year.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀνεβαίνω from the Ancient Greek ἀναβαίνω. The epsilon ανε-, from the aorist ἀνέβην.</div><b>ανεβασιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανεβασιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (colloquial) ascent</div>
  <div class='def'>2. going uphill</div><b>ανεβατός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεβατή, neuter ανεβατό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>rising</div><b>ανεβοκατέβασμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανεβοκατεβάσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ups and downs, going up and down</div><b>ανεβοκατεβάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to pick up and put down, raise and lower</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ανεβ(αίνω), “to go up”) + -ο- (infix) + κατεβάζω.</div><b>ανεβοκατεβαίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to bob up and down, go up and down</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to rock, heave</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ανεβ(αίνω), “ascend”) + -ο- (infix) + κατεβαίνω.</div><b>ανεγγύητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεγγύητη, neuter ανεγγύητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unguaranteed</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αν- (an-, α- privative) + εγγυ- (engy-, “guarantee”) + -τος (-tos, adjectival suffix).</div><b>ανεγείρω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(literary) to erect</div><b>ανεγκέφαλος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεγκέφαλη, neuter ανεγκέφαλο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. anencephalic</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (derogatory, figuratively) silly, brainless</div><b>ανεγκαινίαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεγκαινίαστη, neuter ανεγκαινίαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not inaugurated, uninaugurated, without an official opening</div><b>ανεγκεφαλία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) anencephaly</div><b>ανεγκλιμάτιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεγκλιμάτιστη, neuter ανεγκλιμάτιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unacclimatised, not acclimatised (UK), unacclimatized, not acclimatized (US)</div><b>ανεγκωμίαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεγκωμίαστη, neuter ανεγκωμίαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unpraised, without praise, not praised</div><b>ανεγνωρισμένος</b>
  <div><i>verb, masculine (feminine ανεγνωρισμένη, neuter ανεγνωρισμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>dated, formal variant of <a href="bword://αναγνωρισμένος">αναγνωρισμένος</a>: recognized</div><b>ανεγνώριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεγνώριστη, neuter ανεγνώριστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανέγνωρος">ανέγνωρος</a></div><b>ανεγχείρητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεγχείρητη, neuter ανεγχείρητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unusable, out of order, inoperable, u/s</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unused, not operated</div><b>ανεδαφικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεδαφική, neuter ανεδαφικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. irrational, unrealistic</div>
  <div class='def'>2. undoable, unimplementable (impossible to implement)</div><b>ανεδαφικότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) irrationality, groundlessness</div><b>ανειδίκευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανειδίκευτη, neuter ανειδίκευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unskilled, inexpert</div><b>ανειδοποίητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανειδοποίητη, neuter ανειδοποίητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unwarned, unadvised, uninformed</div><b>ανεικονικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεικονική, neuter ανεικονικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abstract, nonrepresentational</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from αν- (an-, α- privative) + εικονικός.</div><b>ανειλημμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανειλημμένη, neuter ανειλημμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>committed to, undertaken</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ανειλημμένες</b> υποχρεώσεις - undertaken commitments</div><b>ανειλικρίνεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) insincerity</div><b>ανειλικρινής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανειλικρινής, neuter ανειλικρινές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>insincere, disingenuous, deceitful, shifty</div><b>ανειρήνευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανειρήνευτη, neuter ανειρήνευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>without rest, ceaseless</div><b>ανεκδήλωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεκδήλωτη, neuter ανεκδήλωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unrevealed, secret, hidden</div><b>ανεκδίκαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεκδίκαστη, neuter ανεκδίκαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>untried, unheard (case)</div><b>ανεκδίκητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεκδίκητη, neuter ανεκδίκητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unrevenged, unavenged</div><b>ανεκδιήγητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεκδιήγητη, neuter ανεκδιήγητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>indescribable</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ανεκδιήγητα</b> βάσανα - indescribable suffering</div><b>ανεκδοτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεκδοτικη, neuter ανεκδοτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anecdotal</div><b>ανεκδοτογράφος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανεκδοτογράφοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>a writer of anecdotes</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> from ανέκδοτο</div><b>ανεκδοτογραφία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανεκδοτογραφίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>the writing of anecdotes</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> from ανέκδοτο</div><b>ανεκδοτογραφικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεκδοτογραφική, neuter ανεκδοτογραφικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anecdotal, relating especially to the writing of anecdotes.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> from ανέκδοτο</div><b>ανεκδοτολογία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανεκδοτολογίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>the telling of anecdotes</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> from ανέκδοτο</div><b>ανεκδοτολογικά</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anecdotally</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From ανεκδοτολογικός, from ανέκδοτο.</div><b>ανεκδοτολογικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεκδοτολογική, neuter ανεκδοτολογικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anecdotal, relating to anecdotes</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> from ανέκδοτο</div><b>ανεκδοτολόγος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανεκδοτολόγοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>raconteur, anecdotist, storyteller</div><b>ανεκκαθάριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεκκαθάριστη, neuter ανεκκαθάριστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unsettled, unpaid (bill) uncleared (account)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unliquidated (company)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αν- (an-, α- privative) + εκκαθαρισ- (ekkatharis-) + -τος (-tos, adjectival suffix).</div><b>ανεκλάλητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεκλάλητη, neuter ανεκλάλητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(literary) inexpressible, indescribable (eg joy)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Literally a synonym, but with negative connotations: ανεκδιήγητος (anekdiígitos).</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀνεκλάλητος. By surface analysis, αν- (an-, α- privative) + Ancient Greek ἐκλαλέω + -τος (-tos, adjectival suffix).</div><b>ανεκμετάλλευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεκμετάλλευτη, neuter ανεκμετάλλευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unexploited, not utilised, untapped (resources, wealth, etc)</div><b>ανεκμυστήρευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεκμυστήρευτη, neuter ανεκμυστήρευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(literary) unconfided, close (with information, etc)</div><b>ανεκπαίδευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεκπαίδευτη, neuter ανεκπαίδευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>untrained</div><b>ανεκπλήρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεκπλήρωτη, neuter ανεκπλήρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unfulfilled, unrealised (UK), unrealized (US) — (aspirations, desires, hopes)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unfulfillable, unrealisable (UK), unrealizable (US) — (aspirations, desires, hopes)</div><b>ανεκποίητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεκποίητη, neuter ανεκποίητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(literary) not disposed of, unsold</div><b>ανεκρίζωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεκρίζωτη, neuter ανεκρίζωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. ineradicable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. not eradicated</div><b>ανεκτέλεστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεκτέλεστη, neuter ανεκτέλεστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. priceless, inestimable, invaluable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unperformed (music)</div><b>ανεκτίμητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεκτίμητη, neuter ανεκτίμητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>priceless, inestimable, invaluable</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αν- (an-, α- privative) + εκτιμώ + -τος (-tos). Calque of French inestimable, inappréciable.</div><b>ανεκτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεκτική, neuter ανεκτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>tolerant, lenient, broadminded, permissive</div>
  <div class='ex'>Στο σπίτι μας, ήμασταν πάντοτε <b>ανεκτικοί</b> στις απόψεις των άλλων. - In our house, we&#x27;ve always been tolerant of others&#x27; views.</div><b>ανεκτικότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) tolerance, lenience, broadmindedness, permissiveness</div>
