  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αναπάντεχος">αναπάντεχος</a></div><b>ανεπάρκεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) insufficiency, inadequacy, scarcity (quality of not enough being available)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Λόγω της <b>ανεπάρκειας</b> του φαγητού, πόλοι πέθαναν στον λιμό. - Due to the scarcity of food, many died in the famine.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) deficiency, failure (lack of ability or function)</div>
  <div class='ex'>διανοητική <b>ανεπάρκεια</b> - mental deficiency</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (uncountable) incompetency, incompetence (inability to do something well)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η <b>ανεπάρκεια</b> της σ’ αυτό το θέμα ήταν καθαρή. - Her incompetence in this subject was clear.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αν- (an-, α- privative) + επάρκεια; calque of English insufficiency. First attested 1863.</div><b>ανεπίβλεπτος</b>
