  <div class='def'>1. unashamed</div>
  <div class='def'>2. blameless</div><b>ανεπαισθήτως</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(formal) imperceptibly, unperceived</div>
  <div class='ex'>Konstantinos Kavafis (1863‑1933) poem: &quot;Walls&quot;
Χωρίς περίσκεψιν, χωρίς λύπην, χωρίς αιδώ
μεγάλα κι υψηλά τριγύρω μου έκτισαν τείχη.
[...] Αλλά δεν άκουσα ποτέ κρότον κτιστών ή ήχον.
Ανεπαισθήτως μ’ έκλεισαν από τον κόσμον έξω.
Chorís perískepsin, chorís lýpin, chorís aidó
megála ki ypsilá trigýro mou éktisan teíchi.
[...] Allá den ákousa poté króton ktistón í íchon.
Anepaisthítos m’ ékleisan apó ton kósmon éxo.
With no consideration, no pity, no shame,
they have built walls around me, thick and high.
… But I never heard the builders, not a sound.
Imperceptibly they have closed me off from the outside world.
English translation by Edmund Keeley and Philip Sherrard @cavafy.com</div>
