  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀνεπανόρθωτος.</div><b>ανεπαρκής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανεπαρκής, neuter ανεπαρκές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. insufficient, inadequate, scarce (not as much as meets requirements)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ο αριθμός ενδιαφερόμενων ήταν <b>ανεπαρκής</b> για να δημιουργηθεί νέο θέμα στο πανεπιστήμιο. - The number of those interested was insufficient for a new subject to be created in the university.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. insufficient, inadequate, scarce (not as much as meets requirements); lame, feeble (excuse)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. incompetent, unable, unfit (not as good as necessary)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Οι δύο τους ήταν <b>ανεπαρκείς</b> γονείς. - They were both unfit parents.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αν- (an-, α- privative) + επαρκής; calque of English insufficient. First attested 1856.</div><b>ανεπαρκώς</b>
