  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial) to tumble, suddenly realise, get wind of</div><b>ανθίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to flower, bloom</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to flourish, bloom</div>
  <div class='ex'>Στα Κυκλαδονήσια <b>άνθισε</b> κατά την τρίτη χιλιετία π.Χ. ένας ιδιαίτερος και πρωτότυπος πολιτισμός. - An original culture flourished in the Cyclades in the 3rd millennium BC.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ᾰ̓νθῐ́ζω, with semantic shift.</div><b>ανθίσταμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to resist</div><b>ανθεκτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανθεκτική, neuter ανθεκτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. resilient, tough (having the ability to endure adversity, stress, trauma, etc.)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. durable, hard-wearing, resilient, tough (able to resist wear or decay)</div>
