  <div class='def'>to bewilder, bother, confuse</div><b>αντραλεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αντραλίζω">αντραλίζω</a></div><b>αντραλώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αντραλίζω">αντραλίζω</a></div><b>αντρεία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αντρείες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανδρεία">ανδρεία</a></div><b>αντρείος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αντρεία, neuter αντρείο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανδρείος">ανδρείος</a></div><b>αντρειά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αντρειές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανδρεία">ανδρεία</a></div><b>αντρειεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to strengthen, grow, mature (into a man)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to become braver</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) to intensify (heat, cold, storm, etc)</div><b>αντρειοσύνη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανδρειοσύνη">ανδρειοσύνη</a></div><b>αντρειωμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αντρειωμένη, neuter αντρειωμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>brave, courageous, valorous, gallant</div><b>αντρειώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αντρειεύω">αντρειεύω</a></div><b>αντρικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αντρική, neuter αντρικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>masculine, male, not effeminate.</div><b>αντρογυναίκα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αντρογυναίκες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. manly woman</div>
  <div class='def'>2. amazon (a strong, athletic woman)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) virago (a militant woman)</div><b>αντροκαλώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to challenge, confront</div><b>αντροκρατούμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανδροκρατούμαι">ανδροκρατούμαι</a></div><b>αντρομίδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αντρομίδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ενδρομίδα">ενδρομίδα</a></div><b>αντροπαρέα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αντροπαρέες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>group/party of men, stag party</div><b>αντροσύνη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial, uncountable) manliness, manhood, virility, masculinity</div><b>αντροφέρνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to look mannish, behave mannishly</div><b>αντρόγυνο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αντρόγυνα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of ανδρόγυνο</div><b>αντρόπιαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αντρόπιαστη, neuter αντρόπιαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>undishonoured, not dishonoured (UK), undishonored, not dishonored (US)</div><b>αντρώνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to become a man, reach manhood</div><b>αντρώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανδρώνω">ανδρώνω</a></div><b>αντσούγια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αντσούγιες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αντζούγια">αντζούγια</a></div><b>αντων.</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://αντωνυμία">αντωνυμία</a>: pronoun</div><b>αντωνυμία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αντωνυμίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. pronoun</div>
  <div class='def'>2. antonymy</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀντωνυμία cognate with Katharevousa ἀντωνυμία.</div><b>αντωνυμικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αντωνυμική, neuter αντωνυμικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(pronominal) pronominal</div><b>αντώνυμο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αντώνυμα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>antonym</div><b>ανυδρία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανυδρίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>drought, dryness, aridity</div><b>ανυμνώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to praise</div><b>ανυπάκουος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυπάκουη, neuter ανυπάκουο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. disobedient</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unruly</div>
  <div class='def'>3. insubordinate, rebellious</div>
  <div class='def'>4. indisciplinable, indocile, refractory</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανυπάκουοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disobedient person, rebel</div><b>ανυπέρβλητα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>insuperably, unsurpassably</div><b>ανυπέρβλητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυπέρβλητη, neuter ανυπέρβλητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>insuperable, unsurpassable; unsurpassed, unexcelled; unmatched, unequalled</div><b>ανυπέρθετος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυπέρθετος, neuter ανυπέρθετον)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unchangeable</div><b>ανυπαίτιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυπαίτια, neuter ανυπαίτιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not guilty, not responsible</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> α- (a-) + υπαίτιος</div><b>ανυπακοή</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) disobedience, insubordination</div><b>ανυπαρξία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) nonexistence, nothingness</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) nothingness, void (vacuum, outer space)</div><b>ανυπεράσπιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυπεράσπιστη, neuter ανυπεράσπιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. defenceless (UK), defenseless (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unprotected</div><b>ανυπερθέτως</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>without fail, unfailingly</div><b>ανυποθήκευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυποθήκευτη, neuter ανυποθήκευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unmortgaged</div><b>ανυποκρισία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) lack of hypocrisy, sincerity</div><b>ανυποληψία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) discredit, disrepute</div><b>ανυπολόγιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυπολόγιστη, neuter ανυπολόγιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>incalculable, inestimable, immeasurable</div><b>ανυπομονησία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) impatience, lack of patience</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From ανυπόμονος.</div><b>ανυπομονώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be impatient, look forward with impatience</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Ανυπομονώ</b> να έρθει το καλοκαίρι. - I can&#x27;t wait for summer to come.</div><b>ανυπομόνευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυπομόνευτη, neuter ανυπομόνευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>impatient, eager, anxious</div><b>ανυποστήρικτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυποστήρικτη, neuter ανυποστήρικτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unsupported, unpropped</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) unsupported, not seconded</div><b>ανυποστήριχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυποστήριχτη, neuter ανυποστήριχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανυποστήρικτος">ανυποστήρικτος</a></div><b>ανυποταγή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) disobedience, insubordination</div><b>ανυποταξία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανυποταξίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disobedience, insubordination</div><b>ανυποχώρητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυποχώρητη, neuter ανυποχώρητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>tenacious, inflexible, unyielding</div><b>ανυποψίαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυποψίαστη, neuter ανυποψίαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unsuspecting, unaware, oblivious, unwitting</div>
  <div class='ex'>Είναι <b>ανυποψίαστα</b> πιόνια στο παιχνίδι. - They are unwitting pawns in the game.</div><b>ανυπόγραφος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυπόγραφη, neuter ανυπόγραφο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unsigned</div><b>ανυπόδητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυπόδητη, neuter ανυπόδητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>barefoot, barefooted, shoeless, unshod</div><b>ανυπόδυτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυπόδυτη, neuter ανυπόδυτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανυπόδητος">ανυπόδητος</a></div><b>ανυπόθηκος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυπόθηκη, neuter ανυπόθηκο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unmortgaged</div><b>ανυπόκριτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυπόκριτη, neuter ανυπόκριτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. frank, undisguised, unfeigned</div>
  <div class='def'>2. sincere, frank, genuine</div><b>ανυπόληπτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυπόληπτη, neuter ανυπόληπτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not respectable, disreputable</div><b>ανυπόμονα</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://ανυπόμονος">ανυπόμονος</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>impatiently, eagerly</div><b>ανυπόμονος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυπόμονη, neuter ανυπόμονο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>impatient, eager, anxious</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀνυπόμονος. By surface analysis, αν- (an-, from α- privative) + υπομον(ή), “patience”) + -ος (-os).</div><b>ανυπόνιαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυπόνιαστη, neuter ανυπόνιαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unsuspecting, unsuspicious</div><b>ανυπόστατος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυπόστατη, neuter ανυπόστατο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. groundless, unsubstantiated, unfounded</div>
  <div class='ex'>Αυτά είναι <b>ανυπόστατα</b> ψεύδη. - These are unsubstantiated lies.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. imaginary, unreal</div><b>ανυπόσχετος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυπόσχετη, neuter ανυπόσχετο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>with no promise, unpromising (of a person)</div><b>ανυπότακτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυπότακτη, neuter ανυπότακτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. draft dodger</div>
  <div class='def'>2. undisciplined, unruly, insubordinate</div>
  <div class='def'>3. rebellious, refractory</div>
  <div class='def'>4. draft dodging</div><b>ανυπόταχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυπόταχτη, neuter ανυπόταχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανυπότακτος">ανυπότακτος</a></div><b>ανυπόφερτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυπόφερτη, neuter ανυπόφερτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανυπόφορος">ανυπόφορος</a></div><b>ανυπόφορος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυπόφορη, neuter ανυπόφορο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unbearable, intolerable, insufferable, unendurable</div><b>ανυσματικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυσματική, neuter ανυσματικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>vectorial, vectoral (less common)</div><b>ανυστέρητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυστέρητη, neuter ανυστέρητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>inaustere, without austerity, without privations</div><b>ανυστεροβουλία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) selflessness, lack of selfishness</div><b>ανυστερόβουλα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disinterestedly, selflessly</div><b>ανυστερόβουλος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυστερόβουλη, neuter ανυστερόβουλο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sincere, disinterested</div><b>ανυφάντρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανυφάντριες, masculine ανυφαντής)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://υφάντρια">υφάντρια</a></div><b>ανυφαίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://υφαίνω">υφαίνω</a></div><b>ανυψωτήρας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ανυψωτήρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. hoist, lift (for lifting heavy items off the ground)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. derrick</div><b>ανυψωτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανυψωτική, neuter ανυψωτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>raising, hoisting, lifting</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ανυψωτικό</b> ψαλίδι - scissor lift</div><b>ανυψώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to lift, raise, hoist</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ο γερανός <b>ανυψώνει</b> φορτία. - The crane lifts loads.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to boost, improve (someone&#x27;s situation)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) to exalt, extol</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from Koine Greek ἀνυψ(ῶ)) + -ώνω. By surface analysis, αν- (an-, from ανα- (ana-)) + υψώνω.</div><b>ανφάν-γκατέ</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (indeclinable) the cream of youngsters</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (indeclinable) the crème de la crème of society (also as feminine)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (as in French) spoilt/spoiled child</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From French enfant gâté (spoilt/spoiled child).</div><b>ανφάς</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>from the front, in front of</div><b>ανχης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://αντισυνταγματάρχης">αντισυνταγματάρχης</a></div><b>ανχος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://αντιναύαρχος">αντιναύαρχος</a></div><b>ανωμαλία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανωμαλίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. anomaly</div>
  <div class='def'>2. perversion</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From the Ancient Greek ἀνωμαλία.</div><b>ανωμεριά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανωμεριές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. upper, the upper part</div>
  <div class='def'>2. an upward slope</div><b>ανωμοτί</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>without oath</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνωμοτί.</div><b>ανωνυμία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) anonymity</div><b>ανωνυμογράφος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural ανωνυμογράφοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anonymous writer</div><b>ανωνυμογραφία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανωνυμογραφίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anonymous letter, anonymous article</div><b>ανωνυμογραφώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to write anonymously</div><b>ανωριμότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) immaturity (quality of not being mature)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Δεν υποφέρεται η <b>ανωριμότητα</b> αυτού του ανθρώπου. - This man&#x27;s immaturity can&#x27;t be tolerated.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αν- (an-, α- privative) + ωριμότητα; a calque of French immaturité.</div><b>ανωτέρω</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>above</div><b>ανωτερότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) superiority (the state of being superior)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ανώτερος + -ότητα, calque of French supériorité. First attested 1886.</div><b>ανωφέλετος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανωφέλετη, neuter ανωφέλετο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ανωφέλευτος">ανωφέλευτος</a></div><b>ανωφέλευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανωφέλευτη, neuter ανωφέλευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>useless, in vain</div><b>ανωφέρεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανωφέρειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ascent</div><b>ανωφελής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανωφελής, neuter ανωφελές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>useless, in vain</div><b>ανωφερής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανωφερής, neuter ανωφερές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>uphill</div><b>ανόητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανόητη, neuter ανόητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>foolish, stupid</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνόητος, from ἀ- (a-) + νοητός.</div><b>ανόθευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανόθευτη, neuter ανόθευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unadulterated, pure</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unalloyed (metals)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. honest, not fiddled (business, elections)</div><b>ανόμημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ανομήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. offence, transgression</div>
  <div class='def'>2. sin</div><b>ανόμοιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine όμοια, neuter όμοιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>different, unalike</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀνόμοιος.</div><b>ανόπτηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανοπτήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>annealing, tempering</div><b>ανόργανος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανόργανη, neuter ανόργανο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>inorganic</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ανόργανη</b> χημεία - inorganic chemistry</div><b>ανόργωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανόργωτη, neuter ανόργωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unploughed (UK), unplowed (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. uncultivated, untilled</div><b>ανόρεχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανόρεχτη, neuter ανόρεχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. having a lost appetite</div>
  <div class='def'>2. dispirited</div><b>ανόρθωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανορθώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. restoration</div>
  <div class='def'>2. rectification</div>
  <div class='def'>3. recovery</div><b>ανόρυξη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ανορύξεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>excavation, digging (footings, etc)</div><b>ανόσιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανόσια, neuter ανόσιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. impious, godless</div>
