  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>on</div><b>απάγκιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απάγκια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>lee, leeward, a place of shelter</div><b>απάγκιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απάγκιη, neuter απάγκιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>lee, leeward</div><b>απάγω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to kidnap, abduct</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπάγω. By surface analysis, απο- (apo-) + άγω.</div><b>απάγωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απάγωτη, neuter απάγωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>uniced, not iced, unfrozen</div><b>απάδω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to not be in time, out of time</div><b>απάθεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) impassivity, impassiveness, apathy, indifference</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀπάθεια.</div><b>απάλειψη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απαλείψεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>deletion, removal, erasure, crossing out, striking out</div><b>απάλιωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απάλιωτη, neuter απάλιωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>still working (in spite of age)</div><b>απάλυνση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απαλύνσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>softening, alleviating, easing</div><b>απάμβλυνση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απαμβλύνσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>weakening, bluntening, blunting</div><b>απάνεμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απάνεμη, neuter απάνεμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>leeward, leewards, lee</div><b>απάνθισμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απανθίσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>anthology, selection, collection, compendium (especially the best)</div><b>απάνθρωπος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απάνθρωπη, neuter απάνθρωπο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>inhuman, inhumane</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural απάνθρωποι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. cruel or inhuman person</div>
  <div class='def'>2. alien, non-human</div><b>απάντηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απαντήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>answer, response</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ᾰ̓πᾰ́ντησῐς.</div><b>απάντρευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απάντρευτη, neuter απάντρευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unmarried, single</div><b>απάνω</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://πάνω">πάνω</a></div><b>απάρθενος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απάρθενη, neuter απάρθενο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (colloquial) virgin, chaste</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) not tampered with</div><b>απάρνηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απαρνήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>renunciation, rejection, abandonment</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀπάρνησις.</div><b>απάστρευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απάστρευτη, neuter απάστρευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. not cleaned, unclean</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unpeeled</div><b>απάστωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απάστωτη, neuter απάστωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unpreserved, not salted, uncured</div><b>απάτη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απάτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. deceit</div>
  <div class='def'>2. deception</div>
  <div class='def'>3. fraud, hoax</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπάτη.</div><b>απάτητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απάτητη, neuter απάτητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. inaccessible, untrodden (mountain top)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. trackless</div>
  <div class='def'>3. untrodden (grapes)</div><b>απάτωρ</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural απάτορες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>a fatherless person</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπάτωρ.</div><b>απάχης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural απάχηδες, feminine απάχισσα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(obsolete) hoodlum, apache, street criminal</div><b>απάχικος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απάχικη, neuter απάχικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>roguish, criminal</div><b>απάχισσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απάχισσες, masculine απάχης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(obsolete) apache, street criminal</div><b>απάχυντος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απάχυντη, neuter απάχυντο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unfattened</div><b>απέ</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>then; next</div><b>απέθαντος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απέθαντη, neuter απέθαντο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>immortal, deathless, undying</div><b>απέκκριση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απεκκρίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>excretion</div><b>απέλαση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απελάσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>deportation, expulsion</div><b>απέλλα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(historical, uncountable) a Spartan people&#x27;s assembly</div><b>απέναντι</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>opposite, on the other side, across, over the way from</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀπέναντι.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>prep</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(with genitive) opposite to, across</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀπέναντι.</div><b>απένθητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απένθητη, neuter απένθητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unmourned</div><b>απένταρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απένταρη, neuter απένταρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>penniless, destitute, down-and-out</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> from α- (a-) + πεντάρα</div><b>απέξω</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. outside, from outside</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) (recite) by heart</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(indeclinable) outside, exterior</div><b>απέξω κι ανακατωτά</b>
  <div><i>phrase</i></div>
  <div class='def'>by heart, inside out, from top to bottom</div>
  <div class='ex'>Θα το έχετε μάθει <b>απέξω κι ανακατωτά</b>. - You will have learnt it by heart.</div><b>απέραντος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απέραντη, neuter απέραντο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>vast, endless, boundless</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπέραντος.</div><b>απέραστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απέραστη, neuter απέραστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unsurpassable, unsurmountable, impassable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. not unsurpassed, not unsurmounted</div>
  <div class='def'>3. waterproof, watertight</div><b>απέριττος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απέριττη, neuter απέριττο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>plain, simple, unadorned, not embellished</div><b>απέρχομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(formal) to depart, go away from</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀπέρχομαι. By surface analysis, απ- from απο- (“from”) + έρχομαι (“come”).</div><b>απέταλος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απέταλη, neuter απέταλο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unpetalled, without blossom</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (definition, rare) unshoed, unshod</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Either Learned borrowing from Katharevousa ἀπέταλος, attested since 1873, from Koine Greek ἀπέτηλος with change to πεταλ- from Ancient Greek πέταλον
Or learned borrowing from French apétale &lt; a- + pétale from Ancient Greek πέταλον, Morphologically, α- (a-, alpha privative) + Ancient Greek πέταλ(ον)) + suffix for adjectives -ος (-os).
Or, related to the unattested Ancient Greek ᾱ̓πέτᾰλος.
For the taxonomic term απέταλα see the New Latin apetala (example, Nestegis apetala.</div><b>απέχθεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απέχθειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abhorrence, disgust, loathing, repugnance</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπέχθεια. See etymology of απεχθάνομαι.</div><b>απέχω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (used with <a href="bword://από">από</a>) to be distant from, be far away</div>
  <div class='ex'>Πόσο <b>απέχει</b> η Αθήνα από εδώ; - How far away is Athens from here?</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (used with <a href="bword://από">από</a>) abstain from, refrain from</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (used with <a href="bword://από">από</a>) be absent</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀπέχω, from ἀπό απ- (ap-) + ἔχω, έχω</div><b>απήγανος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural απήγανοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>rue (herb)</div><b>απήδητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απήδητη, neuter απήδητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απήδηχτος">απήδηχτος</a></div><b>απήδηχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απήδηχτη, neuter απήδηχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unjumpable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unscrewed, unfucked, unmounted, unmated</div><b>απήχηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απηχήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. sensation, impression</div>
  <div class='def'>2. echo, resonance</div><b>απίδι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απίδια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial) pear (fruit)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀπίδιον, diminutive of ἄπιον.</div><b>απίεστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απίεστη, neuter απίεστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. incompressible, uncompressed</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) unpersuadable, intransigent</div><b>απίθανος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απίθανη, neuter απίθανο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unlikely, improbable, implausible</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From the Ancient Greek ἀπίθανος.</div><b>απίθωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απιθώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(literary, vernacular) touch, touching, abutment, leaning against (action &amp; effect)</div><b>απίκο</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (colloquial) anchor apeak (cable vertical and about to be raised)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. vertical</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) about to leave, on the alert, ready for action</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from Italian a picco.</div><b>απίκου</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απίκο">απίκο</a></div><b>απίκραντος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απίκραντη, neuter απίκραντο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>without sorrows/bitterness</div><b>απίστευτα</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://απίστευτος">απίστευτος</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>incredibly, unbelievably</div><b>απίστευτο</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://απίστευτος">απίστευτος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://απίστευτος">απίστευτος</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>intj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>well, I never!</div><b>απίστευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απίστευτη, neuter απίστευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>incredible, unbelievable</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀπίστευτος; by surface analysis, α- (a-) + πιστεύω + -τος (-tos).</div><b>απίστομα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial) prone, face down</div><b>απίστωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απίστωτη, neuter απίστωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>uncredited, not credited</div><b>απίσχανση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απισχάνσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. losing weight, slimming</div>
  <div class='def'>2. emaciation</div><b>απίσχνανση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) thinning out, reducing</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) emaciation; slimming</div><b>απαέρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>exhaust gas, exhaust, emission</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> By surface analysis, απ- (ap-, “from, ex-”) + αέρια.</div><b>απαίδευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαίδευτη, neuter απαίδευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>uneducated, ignorant</div><b>απαίνευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαίνευτη, neuter απαίνευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unpraised, unlauded</div><b>απαίσια</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. nominative/accusative/vocative feminine singular of <a href="bword://απαίσιος">απαίσιος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://απαίσιος">απαίσιος</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>awfully, terribly, dreadfully</div>
  <div class='ex'>Περάσαμε <b>απαίσια</b> σ’ αυτές τις διακοπές. - We had a dreadful time on this holiday.</div><b>απαίσιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαίσια, neuter απαίσιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>awful, dreadful, horrible appalling, terrible</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀπαίσιος, from ἀπό + αἴσιος; see αίσιος for the latter.</div><b>απαίτηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απαιτήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. demand</div>
  <div class='def'>2. claim, pretence</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (in plural) requirements, needs</div><b>απαγίδευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαγίδευτη, neuter απαγίδευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not trapped, untrapped, unsnared</div><b>απαγγέλλω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to recite, express</div><b>απαγγελία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απαγγελίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. recitation, declamation, recital</div>
  <div class='def'>2. diction, elocution</div><b>απαγγελλία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απαγγελίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>A rare form of <a href="bword://απαγγελία">απαγγελία</a></div><b>απαγγελμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine απαγγελμένη, neuter απαγγελμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. indicted</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>απαγγελμένες</b> κατηγορίες - indicted charges</div>
  <div class='def'>2. recited, delivered</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>απαγγελμένα</b> ποιήματα - poems that have been recited</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of απαγγέλλομαι, passive voice of απαγγέλλω. Also see απηγγελμένος, ἀπηγγελμένος.</div><b>απαγγελτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαγγελτική, neuter απαγγελτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>recitational, declamatory</div><b>απαγκίστρωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απαγκιστρώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. breaking off, disengagement</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unhooking, unhitching</div><b>απαγκειάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to find shelter (weather), give shelter</div><b>απαγκιάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απαγκειάζω">απαγκειάζω</a></div><b>απαγκιστρώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to unhook, to unhitch</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to disengage, to break off</div><b>απαγορευμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine απαγορευμένη, neuter απαγορευμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. prohibited, forbidden</div>
  <div class='ex'>«Ο <b>Απαγορευμένος</b> Πλανήτης» ήταν περιοδικό επιστημονικής φαντασίας. - The Forbidden Planet was a science-fiction magazine.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. banned (book, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. taboo (word, practice)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of απαγορεύομαι, passive voice of απαγορεύω (“forbid”).</div><b>απαγορευτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαγορευτική, neuter απαγορευτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>prohibitive, prohibitory</div><b>απαγορεύομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be forbidden</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>απαγορεύεται</b> το κάπνισμα - no smoking</div><b>απαγορεύσεις κυκλοφορίας</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>plural of <a href="bword://απαγόρευση">απαγόρευση</a> κυκλοφορίας</div><b>απαγορεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to forbid, ban, prohibit</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπᾰγορεύω. Morphologically, from απ- (απο-) (ap- (apo-), “reversal/negation”) + αγορεύω. From the ancient ᾰ̓γορᾱ́.</div><b>απαγχονίζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be hanged</div><b>απαγχονίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to hang (execute by hanging)</div><b>απαγχονισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural απαγχονισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>execution by hanging</div><b>απαγχόνιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απαγχονίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>hanging</div><b>απαγωγέας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural απαγωγέας)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>kidnapper, abductor</div><b>απαγωγή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απαγωγές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. kidnapping, abduction</div>
  <div class='def'>2. shanghaiing</div>
  <div class='def'>3. abduction</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀπαγωγή.</div><b>απαγόρευση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απαγορεύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ban, prohibition, interdiction</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀπαγόρευσ(ις) + -ση, from ἀπαγορεύω.</div><b>απαγόρευση κυκλοφορίας</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απαγορεύσεις κυκλοφορίας)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>curfew (legal restriction)</div><b>απαζάρευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαζάρευτη, neuter απαζάρευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>without haggling or bargaining</div><b>απαθής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. dispassionate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. cool, indifferent, impassive</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπαθής.</div><b>απαθανάτιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) immortalisation (UK), immortalization (US)</div><b>απαθανατίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to immortalise (UK), immortalize (US)</div><b>απαθλίωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) impoverishment (the action and its result)</div><b>απαιδαγωγησία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) illiteracy, ignorance</div><b>απαιδαγώγητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαιδαγώγητη, neuter απαιδαγώγητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>uneducated, ill-bred</div><b>απαιδευσία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) illiteracy, ignorance</div><b>απαισιοδοξία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) pessimism</div><b>απαισιοδοξώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be pessimistic</div><b>απαισιόδοξος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαισιόδοξη, neuter απαισιόδοξο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. pessimistic</div>
  <div class='ex'>Είμαι γενικά <b>απαισιόδοξος</b>. - I am generally pessimistic.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. pessimist</div><b>απαισιόμορφος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαισιόμορφη, neuter απαισιόμορφο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>of awful / horrible form, deformed, misformed</div><b>απαισιότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απαισιότητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>awfulness, dreadfulness, horribleness, terribleness</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From απαίσιος + -ότητα. First attested 1887.</div><b>απαιτητής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural απαιτητές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>claimant</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>genitive feminine singular of <a href="bword://απαιτητός">απαιτητός</a></div><b>απαιτητικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαιτητική, neuter απαιτητικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. demanding, exacting</div>
  <div class='def'>2. a persistant demander</div><b>απαιτητικότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) demandingness</div><b>απαιτητός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαιτητή, neuter απαιτητό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. due, demanded</div>
  <div class='def'>2. demandable, claimable</div><b>απαιτούμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be demanded</div><b>απαιτούμενος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine απαιτούμενη, neuter απαιτούμενο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. necessary, required, requisite</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (in plural) necessary funds see απαιτούμενα</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Present participle of απαιτούμαι, passive voice of απαιτώ</div><b>απαιτώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to demand, to call for, to require</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Απαιτώ</b> μηδενική ανοχή της βίας των ανδρών κατά των γυναικών. - I demand zero tolerance for men&#x27;s violence against women.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to necessitate</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπαιτέω.</div><b>απακετάριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απακετάριστη, neuter απακετάριστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not packeted, unpacked, loose</div><b>απαλαίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απαλύνω">απαλύνω</a></div><b>απαλείφομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be deleted</div><b>απαλείφω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(literary) delete, wipe off</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπαλείφω. Morphologically, from απ- (απο-) (“from”) + αλείφω (“spread”).</div><b>απαλειπτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαλειπτική, neuter απαλειπτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(rare) one who deletes, wipes off</div><b>απαλλάσσομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to rid oneself of, get rid of</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to be relieved of, be exempted from</div><b>απαλλάσσω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to release, absolve, deliver of, relieve, exempt</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from Ancient Greek ἀπαλλάσσω - ἀπαλλάττω. Morphologically απ- (ap-) + αλλάσσω.</div><b>απαλλαγή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απαλλαγές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. exemption, remission</div>
  <div class='def'>2. acquittal, absolution</div>
  <div class='def'>3. discharge (from service)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπαλλαγή. Morphologically, from απ- (απο-) (“from”) + αλλαγή (“change”).</div><b>απαλλαγμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine απαλλαγμένη, neuter απαλλαγμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>free from, clear of (without obligations)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of απαλλάσσομαι, passive voice of απαλλάσσω.</div><b>απαλλακτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαλλακτική, neuter απαλλακτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not guilty, exonerating, exonerative</div><b>απαλλαχτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαλλαχτική, neuter απαλλαχτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απαλλακτικός">απαλλακτικός</a></div><b>απαλλοτρίωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) expropriation, alienation (of property)</div><b>απαλλοτριώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to alienate (property)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to expropriate, embezzle (steal property or money)</div><b>απαλλοτριώσιμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαλλοτριώσιμη, neuter απαλλοτριώσιμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alienable, capable of being expropriated</div><b>απαλοιφή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απαλοιφές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. cancellation, cancelling, cancelling out, elimination</div>
  <div class='def'>2. cancellation, elimination, abolition</div><b>απαλυντικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαλυντική, neuter απαλυντικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>softening, ameliorating, emollient</div><b>απαλός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαλά, neuter απαλό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>smooth, soft</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἁπαλός.</div><b>απαλότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απαλότητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. softness</div>
  <div class='def'>2. pallor, paleness</div>
  <div class='def'>3. gentleness</div>
  <div class='def'>4. smoothness</div><b>απαλύνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be moderated</div><b>απαλύνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to soften, make soft, ameliorate, moderate, tone down</div><b>απαμβλύνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to weaken, ease, blunten, blunt</div><b>απανεμιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απανεμιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>lee, leeward</div><b>απανθράκωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. burning up, burning down</div>
  <div class='def'>2. charring, carbonisation (UK), carbonization (US)</div><b>απανθρακώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to burn, burn down, burn up</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to char</div><b>απανθρωπία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απανθρωπίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Katharevousa form of <a href="bword://απανθρωπιά">απανθρωπιά</a></div><b>απανθρωπιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απανθρωπιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>inhumanity, savagery</div><b>απαντάω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to reply, answer (in conversation, letter, email)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to find (in a text))</div>
  <div class='ex'>Αυτή η έκφραση <b>απαντά</b> μόνον σε κείμενα του 19ου αιώνα. - This expression is found only in 19th century texts.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Modern απαντώ, contracted form of ἀπαντάω) + modern suffix -άω</div><b>απαντέχω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to wait, expect</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to hope, hope for</div><b>απανταχού</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://πανταχού">πανταχού</a></div><b>απανταχούσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απανταχούσες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. encyclical (from the patriarchate)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively, humorous) exorbitant bill or invoice</div><b>απαντημένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine απαντημένη, neuter απαντημένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. answered, already answered</div>
  <div class='ex'>antonym: αναπάντητος (anapántitos, “unanswered”)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. encountered, met</div>
  <div class='ex'>synonym: συναντημένος (synantiménos)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of απαντιέμαι &amp; απαντώμαι, passive voices of απαντάω / απαντώ (“answer”).</div><b>απαντητικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαντητική, neuter απαντητικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>responsive</div><b>απαντικρύ</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>opposite</div><b>απαντοχή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) expectation, hope</div><b>απαντώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απαντάω">απαντάω</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπαντῶ, contracted form of ἀπαντάω. Also see the modern απαντάω.</div><b>απανωτά</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>successively, repeatedly</div><b>απανωτός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απανωτή, neuter απανωτό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>successive, in quick succession</div><b>απαξάπας</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαξάπασα, neuter απαξάπαν)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>entire, everything without exception</div><b>απαξία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απαξίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. demerit</div>
  <div class='def'>2. the absence of aesthetic or spiritual values</div><b>απαξιώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to refuse</div><b>απαξιώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to disdain, to refrain from condescension</div><b>απαπούτσωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαπούτσωτη, neuter απαπούτσωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>shoeless, barefoot</div><b>απαρ.</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://απαρέμφατο">απαρέμφατο</a>: infinitive</div><b>απαράβατος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαράβατη, neuter απαράβατο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. inviolable, binding, nonnegotiable; not subject to violation, mandatory</div>
  <div class='def'>2. inviolable, binding, nonnegotiable; fixed, unchangeable</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπαράβατος, from ἀ- (a-) (“not”) + παραβαίνω (“to transgress, violate”).</div><b>απαράβλαπτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαράβλαπτη, neuter απαράβλαπτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>A rare form of <a href="bword://απαράβλεπτος">απαράβλεπτος</a></div><b>απαράβλαφτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαράβλαφτη, neuter απαράβλαφτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>A rare form of <a href="bword://απαράβλεπτος">απαράβλεπτος</a></div><b>απαράβλεπτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαράβλεπτη, neuter απαράβλεπτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncommon) unprejudiced, not overlooked</div><b>απαράβλητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαράβλητη, neuter απαράβλητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unrivalled (UK), unrivaled (US)</div><b>απαράγγελτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαράγγελτη, neuter απαράγγελτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. not ordered, not requested</div>
  <div class='def'>2. uninvited</div><b>απαράγραπτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαράγραπτή, neuter απαράγραπτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. inalienable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. imprescriptible</div><b>απαράγραφτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαράγραφτή, neuter απαράγραφτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απαράγραπτος">απαράγραπτος</a></div><b>απαράδεκτα</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. nominative neuter plural of <a href="bword://απαράδεκτος">απαράδεκτος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. accusative neuter plural of <a href="bword://απαράδεκτος">απαράδεκτος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>3. vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://απαράδεκτος">απαράδεκτος</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unacceptably, inadmissibly</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ήρθε στη δουλειά <b>απαράδεκτα</b> αργά. - He came to work unacceptably late.</div><b>απαράδεκτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαράδεκτη, neuter απαράδεκτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unacceptable, objectionable</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το φαγητό που σερβίρουν εδώ είναι εντελώς <b>απαράδεκτο</b>. - The food they serve here is completely unacceptable.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. inadmissible</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀπαράδεκτος, equivalent to α- (a-, “not, un-, a-”) + παραδεκτός.</div><b>απαράδοτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαράδοτη, neuter απαράδοτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. undelivered, not delivered (mail, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. not surrendered, unsurrendered</div><b>απαράθετος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαράθετη, neuter απαράθετο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unlisted, not cited</div>
  <div class='def'>2. without quotation marks</div><b>απαράκαμπτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαράκαμπτη, neuter απαράκαμπτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. not bypassable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. without detour</div><b>απαράκλητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαράκλητη, neuter απαράκλητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unasked, unrequested, unsolicited</div><b>απαράλειπτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαράλειπτη, neuter απαράλειπτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not omitted, not omittable</div><b>απαράληπτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαράληπτη, neuter απαράληπτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unreceived</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀπαράληπτος.</div><b>απαράλλακτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαράλλακτη, neuter απαράλλακτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. identical</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unchangeable, immutable</div><b>απαράλλαχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαράλλαχτη, neuter απαράλλαχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απαράλλακτος">απαράλλακτος</a></div><b>απαράμιλλος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαράμιλλη, neuter απαράμιλλο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. incomparable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unrivalled (UK), unrivaled (US)</div><b>απαράσκευος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαράσκευη, neuter απαράσκευο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unprepared, not ready, unready, disorganised</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπαράσκευος. By surface analysis, α- (a-) + παρασκευή + -ος (-os).</div><b>απαράτσικ</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(indeclinable) apparatchik</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Russian аппара́тчик.</div><b>απαρέγγλιτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαρέγγλιτη, neuter απαρέγγλιτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>A rare form of <a href="bword://απαρέγκλιτος">απαρέγκλιτος</a></div><b>απαρέγκλιτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαρέγκλιτη, neuter απαρέγκλιτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unswerving, undeviating, inexorable</div><b>απαρέμφατο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απαρέμφατα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(infinitive) infinitive</div>
  <div class='ex'>ένα ρήμα στο <b>απαρέμφατο</b> - a verb in the infinitive</div><b>απαρένθετος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαρένθετη, neuter απαρένθετο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unparenthesised, not parenthesised</div>
  <div class='def'>2. not inserted</div><b>απαρέσκεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) dislike, displeasure</div><b>απαρέσκω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(formal) to dislike</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, and only for 3rd presons of present, from Ancient Greek ἀπαρέσκω.</div><b>απαρίθμηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απαριθμήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>enumeration, listing, recitation</div><b>απαραίτητα</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://απαραίτητος">απαραίτητος</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>necessarily</div><b>απαραίτητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαραίτητη, neuter απαραίτητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>needed, necessary, required, indispensable</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπαραίτητος, with semantic loan from French inévitable, indispensable.</div><b>απαραβίαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαραβίαστη, neuter απαραβίαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>inviolate</div><b>απαραδέκτως</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(formal) unacceptably, inadmissibly</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το φαγητό μας ήταν <b>απαραδέκτως</b> άνοστο. - Our food was unacceptably tasteless.</div><b>απαραδειγμάτιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απαραδειγμάτιστη, neuter απαραδειγμάτιστο)</i></div>
