  <div class='def'>(indeclinable) apartheid</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From English apartheid, from Afrikaans apartheid (literally “separateness”).</div><b>απαρχή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απαρχές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. beginning, origin</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) threshold</div><b>απαρχής</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>originally, from the beginning</div><b>απαρχαιωμένος</b>
