  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://απατηλός">απατηλός</a></div><b>απατηλός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απατηλή, neuter απατηλό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>deceptive</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπατηλός.</div><b>απατημένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine απατημένη, neuter απατημένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. cheated, whose spouse is unfaithful, deceived</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>απατημένος</b> σύζυγος - deceived husband</div>
  <div class='def'>2. tricked, deceived</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of απατιέμαι and απατώμαι, passive voices of απατώ, απατάω (“deceive; mistake”).</div><b>απατιέμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be mistaken, be wrong</div><b>απατός</b>
  <div><i>pron, masculine (feminine απατή, neuter απατό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial) only (used with the genitive personal pronouns: <a href="bword://μου">μου</a> (mou), <a href="bword://σου">σου</a> (sou) <a href="bword://του">του</a> (tou))</div><b>απατός μου</b>
  <div><i>pron, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>myself</div><b>απατός σου</b>
  <div><i>pron, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>yourself</div><b>απατώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. ) to cheat, scam, defraud, deceive, swindle, bamboozle</div>
  <div class='def'>2. ) to cheat on, deceive, two-time (spouse or partner)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η γυναίκα του τον <b>απατούσε</b> δύο χρόνια. - His wife was cheating on him for two years.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. ) be mistaken, err, be deceived by</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η μνήμη μου ποτέ δεν με <b>απατά</b>. - My memory is never wrong.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀπατῶ, contracted form of ἀπατάω.</div><b>απατώμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(formal) to be mistaken, be wrong</div><b>απαυγάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to glow, to shine</div><b>απαυδίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απαυδώ">απαυδώ</a></div><b>απαυδώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (literally) to render speechless</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to grow weary, to tire</div><b>απαυτός</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter or masculine or feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. whatshisname, whatshername thingummy</div>
  <div class='def'>2. thingy, thingummy, thingamajig</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (colloquial) penus, backside, arse</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (colloquial, in plural) genitals, privates</div><b>απαυτώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(vulgar) to copulate: fuck, screw</div><b>απαύγασμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απαυγάσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (figuratively) conclusion, result</div>
  <div class='def'>2. brilliance, glow, radiance</div><b>απείθαρχος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απείθαρχη, neuter απείθαρχο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>undisciplined, disobedient, insubordinate</div><b>απείθεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) disobedience, indiscipline, insubordination</div><b>απείθεια κατά της αρχής</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>civil disobedience</div><b>απείκασμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απεικάσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. image</div>
  <div class='def'>2. eidolon</div>
  <div class='def'>3. simulacrum</div><b>απείραγος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απείραγη, neuter απείραγο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(rare) unteased, not teased</div><b>απείραχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απείραχτη, neuter απείραχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unteased, not teased</div>
  <div class='def'>2. untouched</div><b>απείρως</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>infinitely</div><b>απεγκατάσταση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απεγκαταστάσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>deinstallation, uninstallation</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Morphologically from απ- (“removal-”) + εγ- (“within-”) + κατα- (“against-”) + στάση (“position”).</div><b>απεγκλωβίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to free, to set free</div><b>απεγκλωβισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural απεγκλωβισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. freedom</div>
  <div class='def'>2. setting free, freeing</div><b>απεγνωσμένα</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://απεγνωσμένος">απεγνωσμένος</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>desperately, frantically</div><b>απεγνωσμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απεγνωσμένη, neuter απεγνωσμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. desperate, undaunted, frantic</div>
  <div class='def'>2. a desperate man</div><b>απεθνικοποίηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απεθνικοποιήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. denationalisation, privatisation (UK)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. denationalization, privatization (US)</div><b>απεθνικοποιώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to denationalise, privatise (UK), denationalize, privatize (US)</div><b>απειθάρχητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απειθάρχητη, neuter απειθάρχητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>undisciplined, disobedient, insubordinate</div><b>απειθής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απειθής, neuter απειθές)</i></div>
