  <div class='def'>3. emancipation, release, liberation</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀπελευθέρωσις; see απελευθερία for more.</div><b>απελευθερία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) liberty, freedom</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπελευθερία, from ἀπελεύθερος + -ία, the former component from ἀπ- (ap-) + ἐλεύθερος.</div><b>απελευθερωμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine απελευθερωμένη, neuter απελευθερωμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. released, freed, liberated</div>
  <div class='def'>2. emancipated</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of απελευθερώνομαι, passive voice of απελευθερώνω.</div><b>απελευθερωτής</b>
