  <div class='def'>1. condescending, patronising</div>
  <div class='def'>2. affable</div><b>απεριέργεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) incuriosity, insouciance</div><b>απεριγέλαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απεριγέλαστη, neuter απεριγέλαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not mocked, unmocked, not ridiculed, not laughed at</div><b>απεριποίητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απεριποίητη, neuter απεριποίητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. neglected, uncared-for, untended</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unkempt, untidy</div><b>απερισκεψία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural απερισκεψίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) recklessness, rashness, imprudence, thoughtlessness</div><b>απεριτίφ</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(indeclinable) aperitif</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From French apéritif.</div><b>απεριτείχιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απεριτείχιστη, neuter απεριτείχιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>without walls, unwalled, unfenced</div><b>απεριτοίχιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απεριτοίχιστη, neuter απεριτοίχιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απεριτείχιστος">απεριτείχιστος</a></div><b>απεριόριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απεριόριστη, neuter απεριόριστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unlimited</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unconstrained</div><b>απερπάτητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απερπάτητη, neuter απερπάτητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unwalked, untrodden</div><b>απεσταλμένος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural απεσταλμένοι, feminine απεσταλμένη)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. emissary, envoy, delegate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. correspondent</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αποστέλλομαι, passive voice of αποστέλλω (“send, dispatch”). Learnedly, from Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀπεσταλμένος, participle of the ancient verb ἀποστέλλω &amp; semantic loan from French envoyé. Also substantivised.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine απεσταλμένη, neuter απεσταλμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sent, dispatched (acting as) an emissary</div>
  <div class='ex'>rare modern form: αποσταλμένος (apostalménos), near-synonym: σταλμένος (stalménos)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αποστέλλομαι, passive voice of αποστέλλω (“send, dispatch”). Learnedly, from Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀπεσταλμένος, participle of the ancient verb ἀποστέλλω &amp; semantic loan from French envoyé. Also substantivised.</div><b>απετάλωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απετάλωτη, neuter απετάλωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unshoed, unshod</div><b>απευαισθητοποίηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) desensitisation (UK), desensitization (US)</div><b>απευαισθητοποιώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to desensitise (UK), to desensitize (US)</div><b>απευθείας</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>directly, immediately, straight</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>απευθείας</b> από τους κατασκευαστές - straight from the manufacturers</div><b>απευθείας μετάδοση</b>
  <div><i>phrase</i></div>
  <div class='def'>live (broadcast)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From απευθείας + μετάδοση.</div><b>απευθυσμένο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απευθυσμένα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>rectum</div><b>απευθύνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to write to</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to address, apply to, appeal to</div><b>απευθύνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (transitive) to address, to deliver (a written or oral communication to)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to address, to speak to, appeal to</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀπευθύνω with semantic loan from French (s&#x27;)adresser.</div><b>απευκταίο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απευκταία)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>misfortune, misadventure, mishap</div><b>απευκταίον</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Katharevousa form of <a href="bword://απευκταίο">απευκταίο</a></div><b>απευκταίος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απευκταία, neuter απευκταίο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>undesired, undesirable</div><b>απευχή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απευχές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>something said to avoid evil</div><b>απεχθάνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(transitive) to abominate, detest, abhor</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπεχθάνομαι also with transitive sense since Hellenistic times. From ἀπεχθής from ἀπ(ό) (“with emphasizing sense”) + ἔχθος n. Morphologically απ- + εχθ‑ + ‑άνομαι.</div><b>απεχθής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απεχθής, neuter απεχθές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>repugnant, heinous, abhorrent, odious, loathsome</div><b>απεψία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) indigestion, dyspepsia</div><b>απεύχομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to wish away, wish it may not happen</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ᾰ̓πεύχομαι.</div><b>απηγγελμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine απηγγελμένη, neuter απηγγελμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(dated) (having been) recited, derlivered, older form of <a href="bword://απαγγελμένος">απαγγελμένος</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of απαγγέλλομαι, passive voice of απαγγέλλω, learnedly, with internal augment as in the older form Ancient Greek ἀπηγγελμένος of the ancient verb ἀπαγγέλλω.</div><b>απηγορευμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine απηγορευμένη, neuter απηγορευμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(dated) older form of <a href="bword://απαγορευμένος">απαγορευμένος</a>, as in the ancient ἀπηγορευμένος</div><b>απηλιώτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) the Levant, levanter (an easterly Mediterranean wind)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπηλιώτης.</div><b>απηλλαγμένος</b>
  <div><i>verb, masculine (feminine απηλλαγμένη, neuter απηλλαγμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>dated or formal form of <a href="bword://απαλλαγμένος">απαλλαγμένος</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from the Ancient Greek ἀπηλλαγμένος, perfect passive participle of ἀπαλλάσσω. Form of απαλλαγμένος, retaining the ancient combining forms (ἀπό) ἀπ- ap-) and the participle ἠλλᾰγμένος</div><b>απηνής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απηνής, neuter απηνές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>pitiless, relentless</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>απηνής</b> διώκτης - relentless pursecutor</div><b>απηρχαιωμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine απηρχαιωμένη, neuter απηρχαιωμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(dated) old form of <a href="bword://απαρχαιωμένος">απαρχαιωμένος</a></div>
  <div class='ex'>older spelling: ἀπηρχαιωμένος (apērkhaiōménos)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀπηρχαιωμένος, perfect participle of the passive verb ἀπαρχαιόομαι / ἀπαρχαιοῦμαι. And see απαρχαιωμένος.</div><b>απηχώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to echo, repeat, speak for, be a mouthpiece</div><b>απιδιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απιδιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial) pear tree</div><b>απιθανότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απιθανότητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unlikelihood, impossibility, improbability</div><b>απιθώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial) to touch</div><b>απιοειδής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απιοειδής, neuter απιοειδές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>pearlike, pear-shaped, piriform (of the fruit)</div><b>απιστία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απιστίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. infidelity</div>
  <div class='def'>2. breach of trust</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ᾰ̓πῐστῐ́ᾱ.</div><b>απιστοποίητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απιστοποίητη, neuter απιστοποίητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unattested, uncertified</div>
  <div class='def'>2. not vouched for</div><b>απιστώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to be unfaithful/disloyal</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to betray</div><b>απισχναίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to emaciate, make thin or skinny</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to reduce</div><b>απισχναντικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απισχvαντική, neuter απισχvαντικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>thinning down, causing to emaciate</div><b>απισχνασμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine απισχνασμένη, neuter απισχνασμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(formal) extremely thin, emaciated, scrawny, skinny</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect passive participle of απισχναίνω.</div><b>απλά</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>simply</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://απλός">απλός</a></div><b>απλά εισιτήρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative plural of απλό <a href="bword://εισιτήριο">εισιτήριο</a></div><b>απλάγιαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλάγιαστη, neuter απλάγιαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>stayed out of bed, stayed up, been up</div><b>απλάδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απλάδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. centrepiece — dish, charger, platter</div>
  <div class='def'>2. alternative form of <a href="bword://άπλα">άπλα</a></div><b>απλάκωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλάκωτη, neuter απλάκωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unpaved (eg courtyard)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. not pressed down</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (colloquial) not screwed, unfucked</div><b>απλάνευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλάνευτη, neuter απλάνευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unseduced</div><b>απλάνιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλάνιστη, neuter απλάνιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unplaned, rough (timber)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) uncouth, unrefined (person)</div><b>απλέρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλέρωτη, neuter απλέρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απλήρωτος">απλήρωτος</a></div><b>απλή αρμονική ταλάντωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απλής αρμονικής ταλάντωσης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>simple harmonic motion</div><b>απλήγιαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλήγιαστη, neuter απλήγιαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unwounded</div>
  <div class='def'>2. without sores</div><b>απλήγωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλήγωτη, neuter απλήγωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unwounded, uninjured</div><b>απλήθυντος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλήθυντη, neuter απλήθυντο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not increased, not multiplied, unaugmented</div><b>απλήρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλήρωτη, neuter απλήρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unsettled, unpaid, outstanding (bill, account)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. not paid for (work, goods)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. dishonoured, bounced (cheque)</div><b>απλής αρμονικής ταλάντωσης</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>plural of απλή αρμονική <a href="bword://ταλάντωση">ταλάντωση</a></div><b>απλίκα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απλίκες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>wall light, sconce, bracket lamp</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From French applique (“wall light”), from Latin applicare (“to attach”).</div><b>απλαισίωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλαισίωτη, neuter απλαισίωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unframed, without frame</div><b>απλανής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλανής, neuter απλανές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. fixed, glassy, blank, expressionless (stare)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. fixed</div>
  <div class='def'>3. star</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπλανής.</div><b>απλανιάριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλανιάριστη, neuter απλανιάριστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απλάνιστος">απλάνιστος</a></div><b>απλειστηρίαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλειστηρίαστη, neuter απλειστηρίαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unauctioned, not auctioned</div><b>απλεύριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλεύριστη, neuter απλεύριστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. not confronted, unaccosted</div>
  <div class='def'>2. not drawn alongside (ship)</div><b>απλημμύριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλημμύριστη, neuter απλημμύριστ)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unflooded, not inundated</div><b>απληροφόρητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απληροφόρητη, neuter απληροφόρητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>uninformed</div><b>απλησίαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλησίαστη, neuter απλησίαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. inaccessible, unapproachable (place)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unapproachable, forbidding, aloof (person)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. forbidding, prohibitive (price)</div><b>απληστία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) greed, avarice, strong desire</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀπληστία.</div><b>απλοέπεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) clear, simple, understandable writing or speech</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> απλο- (aplo-) + έπεια</div><b>απλογραφία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απλογραφίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. single-entry bookkeeping</div>
  <div class='def'>2. haplography</div><b>απλοελληνικά</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>in plain/demotic/simple Greek</div><b>απλοελληνικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλοελληνική, neuter απλοελληνικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>plain/demotic Greek</div><b>απλοελληνιστί</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>in plain/demotic/simple Greek</div><b>απλοικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλοική, neuter απλοικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απλοϊκός">απλοϊκός</a></div><b>απλοικότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απλοικότητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απλοϊκότητα">απλοϊκότητα</a></div><b>απλολ.</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://απλολογία">απλολογία</a>: haplology</div><b>απλολογία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απλολογίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>haplology</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from French haplologie (“haplology”), from Ancient Greek ἁπλόος + -λογία.</div><b>απλοποίηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απλοποιήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>simplification</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From απλοποιώ + -ση (-si), a calque of French simplification. Also analyzable as απλ(ός)) + -ο- (-o-) + -ποίηση.</div><b>απλοποιώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to simplify</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> απλός + -ποιώ</div><b>απλουστεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to simplify</div><b>απλοχέρης</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλοχέρα, neuter απλοχέρικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>generous, openhanded</div><b>απλοχεριά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απλοχεριές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>generosity, openhandedness, largesse</div><b>απλοχωριά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απλοχωριές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>space, spaciousness</div><b>απλοϊκός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλοϊκή, neuter απλοϊκό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>naive, simple, simple-minded, innocent, uncomplicated</div><b>απλοϊκότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απλοϊκότητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>simple-mindedness, naivety</div><b>απλούμιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλούμιστη, neuter απλούμιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unadorned, unembroidered, unornamented</div><b>απλούστατα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>simply</div><b>απλούστευση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απλουστεύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>simplification</div><b>απλυσιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) dirtiness, filthiness</div><b>απλωσιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απλωσιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>expanse, space</div><b>απλωτή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απλωτές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>stroke</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative feminine singular of <a href="bword://απλωτός">απλωτός</a></div><b>απλωταριά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απλωταριές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>drying area (for washing)</div><b>απλωτός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλωτή, neuter απλωτό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. flat, plain, even</div>
  <div class='def'>2. outspread, spread out</div><b>απλό εισιτήριο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απλά εισιτήρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>single ticket, one-way ticket</div><b>απλός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλή, neuter απλό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. plain, simple, uncomplicated</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>απλό</b> νερό - still water</div>
  <div class='def'>2. plain, unadorned</div>
  <div class='def'>3. single, one-way</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>απλό</b> εισιτήριο - one-way ticket</div>
  <div class='def'>4. naive</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἁπλοῦς.</div><b>απλότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>simplicity, plainness</div><b>απλόχερα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>generously, liberally</div><b>απλόχερος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλοχέρη, neuter απλοχέρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>generous, openhanded</div><b>απλόχωρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απλόχωρη, neuter απλόχωρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>roomy, spacious</div><b>απλώνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to spread</div><b>απλώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to spread, spread out</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Άπλωσε</b> το χέρι του και τη χάιδεψε απαλά στον ώμο. - He reached out his hand and patted her on the shoulder.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to hang out (washing)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to diffuse</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek απλώνω, from Ancient Greek ἁπλῶ, ἁπλόω + -ώνω, the former from ᾰ̔πλόος + -όω, thus &quot;to make (a folded object) onefold, unfold&quot; &gt; &quot;to spread out, diffuse&quot;.</div><b>απλώς</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>just, only</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> See απλός.</div><b>απλώστρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απλώστρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. drying area/yard/loft (for produce: tobacco, currants, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. clothes airer, drying rack, clothes horse</div><b>απνευστί</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>non-stop, without stopping</div><b>αποίητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποίητη, neuter αποίητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>uncreated, uninitiated, unformed</div><b>αποίκηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποικήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>emigration</div><b>αποίκιλτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποίκιλτη, neuter αποίκιλτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unadorned, plain, unembellished, unembroidered</div><b>αποίκιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποικίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>emigration</div><b>αποίμαντος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποίμαντη, neuter αποίμαντο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. bishopless</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (literary) shepherdless</div><b>αποβάθρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποβάθρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>quay, wharf, pier, platform</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀποβάθρα. απο- (apo-) from ἀπό + βαθρ- + suffix -α (-a) from the ancient βάθρον n, βα- stem from verb βαίνω.</div><b>αποβάλλω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to expel, reject</div>
  <div class='ex'>Πάντοτε <b>αποβάλλω</b> τις φοβίες μου. - I always get rid of my phobias.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to bring up, vomit</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to miscarry (baby)</div>
  <div class='def'>4. to send off (footballer)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀποβάλλω. Morphologically απο- (apo-) + βάλλω.</div><b>αποβίβαση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποβιβάσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. landing, unloading, disembarking, disembarkation</div>
  <div class='ex'>δελτίο <b>αποβίβασης</b> - landing card</div>
  <div class='def'>2. cathode</div><b>αποβαίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to prove, conclude</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀποβαίνω. Morphologically, from απο- (apo-) + βαίνω.</div><b>αποβατικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποβατική, neuter αποβατικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. landing</div>
  <div class='def'>2. amphibious</div><b>αποβδόμαδα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>last week</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From από + εβδομάδα.</div><b>αποβιβάζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to disembark, debark</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to debus, alight</div><b>αποβιβάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to put ashore</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to drop off, alight</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀποβιβάζω. By surface analysis, απο- (“de-”) + βιβάζω (“cause to mount”)</div><b>αποβιβαστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποβιβαστική, neuter αποβιβαστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disembarkation</div><b>αποβιομηχάνιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(neologism, uncountable) deindustrialisation (UK), deindustrialization (US)</div><b>αποβιομηχανίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(neologism) to deindustrialise (UK), deindustrialize (US)</div><b>αποβιώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποβιώνω">αποβιώνω</a></div><b>αποβιώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to die, decease, pass away</div><b>αποβλάκωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποβλακώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>stultification, stupefaction, daze</div><b>αποβλάκωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποβλακώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>stultification, stupefaction, daze</div><b>αποβλέπω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to aspire, aim at, aim to, look to</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Αποβλέπουν</b> στην εξάλειψη των ορυκτών καυσίμων. - They aim to eliminate fossil fuels.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> απο- (apo-) + βλέπω. From Ancient Greek ἀποβλέπω.</div><b>αποβλακωτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποβλακωτική, neuter αποβλακωτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>stupefying</div><b>αποβλακώνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to become stupid</div><b>αποβλακώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to stupefy, stultify</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to daze, stun</div><b>αποβολή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποβολές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. expulsion</div>
  <div class='def'>2. miscarriage, spontaneous abortion</div><b>αποβολιμαίος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποβολιμαία, neuter αποβολιμαίο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>due to be expelled, about to be aborted</div><b>αποβορβόρωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποβορβορώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (literary, rare) becoming completely unethical</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (in Katharevousa ἀποβορβόρωσις) clean up, removal of filth</div><b>αποβουτυρωμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποβουτυρωμένη, neuter αποβουτυρωμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>skimmed (especially milk)</div><b>αποβουτυρώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to cream off, to cream, to skim</div><b>αποβουτύρωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποβουτυρώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>creaming off, skimming, skimming off</div><b>αποβραδίς</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. last night, last evening</div>
  <div class='def'>2. overnight</div><b>αποβραδινός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποβραδινή, neuter αποβραδινό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(of the) evening</div><b>απογέμισμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απογεμίσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. filling up</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unloading (a weapon)</div><b>απογέρνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to incline</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to lie flat</div><b>απογίνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to become, end up</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to become worse</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀπογίνομαι, later Attic form of ἀπογίγνομαι. By surface analysis, απο- (apo-) + γίνομαι.</div><b>απογαλακτίζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be weaned</div><b>απογαλακτίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to wean (infant)</div><b>απογαλακτισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. weaning</div>
  <div class='def'>2. ablactation, drying-up</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπογαλακτισμός.</div><b>απογείωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απογειώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. takeoff</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) takeoff (large, sudden increase to prices, etc)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> από + γη (gi, “earth”)</div><b>απογειώνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to take off</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to take, go through the roof</div><b>απογειώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (transitive) to get into the air, take off</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ο πιλότος <b>απογείωσε</b> το αεροπλάνο αμέσως. - The pilot got the airplane into the air immediately.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to enhance, make successful and spectacular</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> απογει- + -ώνω, the stem from Hellenistic ἀπόγειος. Analysed as από- + γη (gi, “earth”)</div><b>απογεμίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to fill up</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to unload (a weapon)</div><b>απογερνώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to age, grow old</div><b>απογευματινός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απογευματινή, neuter απογευματινό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. afternoon (work, class, shift, etc)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>απογευματινή</b> παράσταση - matinée, afternoon performance</div>
  <div class='def'>2. evening (newspaper edition)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek. By surface analysis, απογευματ-) + -ινός.</div><b>απογιοματινός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απογιοματινή, neuter απογιοματινό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απογευματινός">απογευματινός</a></div><b>απογκρεμίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to raze, demolish, level (building, etc)</div><b>απογοήτευση</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disappointment</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From απογοητεύω + -ση (-si).</div><b>απογοητευμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απογοητευμένη, neuter απογοητευμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. disappointed</div>
  <div class='def'>2. discouraged</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of απογοητεύομαι, passive voice of απογοητεύω</div><b>απογοητευτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απογοητευτική, neuter απογοητευτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disappointing, discouraging</div><b>απογοητεύομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be disappointed</div><b>απογοητεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to disappoint, let down</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> απο- (apo-, “negation”) + γοητεύω. Calque of French désenchanter.</div><b>απογράφω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to complete a writing task</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to enumerate, catalogue, inventorise, take stock</div><b>απογραφέας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural απογραφείς)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. enumerator, census-taker</div>
  <div class='def'>2. stocktaker, cataloger, auditor</div><b>απογραφή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απογραφές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>census, inventory</div><b>απογραφικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απογραφική, neuter απογραφικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>a census, inventory, etc</div><b>απογυμνώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to strip</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to divest, to deprive</div><b>απογυρεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to seek</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to long for</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to request</div><b>απογύμνωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απογυμνώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. stripping, divestment</div>
  <div class='def'>2. deprivation, divestment</div><b>αποδάσωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποδασώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>deforestation</div><b>αποδέκτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αποδέκτες, feminine αποδέκτρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. recipient, addressee</div>
  <div class='def'>2. interlocutor</div><b>αποδέκτρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποδέκτριες, masculine αποδέκτης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. recipient, addressee</div>
  <div class='def'>2. interlocutor</div><b>αποδέλοιπος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποδέλοιπη, neuter αποδέλοιπο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>remaining (that which remains)</div><b>αποδέσμευση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποδεσμεύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. release</div>
  <div class='def'>2. deregulation, unblocking</div>
  <div class='def'>3. freeing up (of memory)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from αποδεσμεύ(ω)) + -ση (-si).</div><b>αποδέχομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to accept gladly, answer positively</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αποδέχθηκε</b> τον διορισμό του στο Υπουργείο - s/he accepted her/his appointment in the Ministry</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to agree with a view, accept, endorse</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ο Πρόεδρος δέχθηκε δυο τρεις προτάσεις από μέλη του συμβουλίου, αλλά τελικά <b>αποδέχθηκε</b> την πρόταση του Διευθύνοντος Συμβούλου - Τhe chairman received a couple or so^((two three)) of proposals by members of the Board, but in the end he accepted the CEO&#x27;s one.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀποδέχομαι, equivalent to απο- (apo-) + δέχομαι.</div><b>αποδέχτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αποδέχτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποδέκτης">αποδέκτης</a></div><b>αποδήμηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποδημήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. death, passing (euphemism)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. migration, emigration</div><b>αποδίδω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to attribute, ascribe</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to render, convey</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to input</div>
  <div class='def'>4. to administer</div>
  <div class='def'>5. to pay off, pay</div><b>αποδίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποδίδω">αποδίδω</a></div><b>αποδείξιμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποδείξιμη, neuter αποδείξιμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>demonstrable</div><b>αποδείχνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποδεικνύομαι">αποδεικνύομαι</a></div><b>αποδείχνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποδεικνύω">αποδεικνύω</a></div><b>αποδεδειγμένα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>demonstrably, provably</div><b>αποδεδειγμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποδεδειγμένη, neuter αποδεδειγμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. demonstrable, provable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. demonstrated, proven</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀποδεδειγμένος.</div><b>αποδεδειγμένως</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποδεδειγμένα">αποδεδειγμένα</a></div><b>αποδεικνύομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to be proved to be</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to be demonstrated</div><b>αποδεικνύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to prove, demonstrate</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀποδεικνύω and ἀποδείκνυμι. Morphologically, from απο- (“intensified”) + δεικνύω (“indicate”).</div><b>αποδεικτέος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποδεικτέα, neuter αποδεικτέο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be proved, to be proven, to be demonstrated</div>
  <div class='ex'>ισχυρισμός <b>αποδεικτέος</b> - a claim to be proved</div><b>αποδεικτικό</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://αποδεικτικός">αποδεικτικός</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://αποδεικτικός">αποδεικτικός</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποδεικτικά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>certificate, testimonial</div><b>αποδεικτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποδεικτική, neuter αποδεικτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>demonstrative, probative, substantiating, apodeictic</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀποδεικτικός. By surface analysis, αποδεικ(νύω)) + -τικός.</div><b>αποδεικτός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποδεικτή, neuter αποδεικτό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>may be proved, may be proven, may be demonstrated</div><b>αποδειχτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποδειχτική, neuter αποδειχτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποδεικτικός">αποδεικτικός</a></div><b>αποδεκάτισμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποδεκατίσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. decimation</div>
  <div class='def'>2. catastrophe</div><b>αποδεκατίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (historical) to decimate (Roman empire)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to inflict heavy casualties</div><b>αποδεκατισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αποδεκατισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. decimation</div>
  <div class='def'>2. catastrophe</div><b>αποδεκτός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποδεκτή, neuter αποδεκτό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>acceptable, admissible</div><b>αποδελτίωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποδελτιώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. indexing, cataloguing</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) data collection and collation</div><b>αποδελτιώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to index, list, catalogue</div><b>αποδεσμεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
