  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αποικιστές, feminine αποικίστρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>coloniser</div><b>αποικιστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποικιστική, neuter αποικιστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>relating to colonisation</div><b>αποικοδόμηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) decomposition</div><b>αποικώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to emigrate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to colonise (UK), colonize (US)</div><b>αποκάθαρση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκατάρσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>expurgation, bowdlerisation (UK), bowdlerization (US)</div><b>αποκάλυψη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκαλύψεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. revelation, disclosure</div>
  <div class='def'>2. apocalypse</div>
  <div class='def'>3. Apocalypse, Revelation (when capitalised)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀποκάλυψις. Morphologically analysed as απο- (apo-) + κάλυψη.</div><b>αποκάμνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to tire, fatigue</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to finish off, finish, bring to an end</div><b>αποκάμωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) tiredness, exhaustion, weariness</div><b>αποκάνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποκάμνω">αποκάμνω</a></div><b>αποκάτω</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>underneath</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> από + κάτω</div><b>αποκέντρωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκεντρώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>decentralisation (UK), decentralization (US)</div><b>αποκήρυξη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκηρύξεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. renunciation</div>
  <div class='def'>2. disownment</div><b>αποκαΐδι</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ember, cinder</div><b>αποκαίγομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of αποκαίομαι</div><b>αποκαίγω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποκαίω">αποκαίω</a></div><b>αποκαίω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to burn up</div><b>αποκαθήλωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκαθηλώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unnailing</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (capitalized, often) decent/deposition/removal from the Cross</div><b>αποκαθαίρω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to expurgate, bowdlerise</div><b>αποκαθηλώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to unnail</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to take down from the Cross</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) to degrade</div><b>αποκαθιστώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to repair, restore to normal</div>
  <div class='ex'>πρέπει να αποκαταστήσουμε τη βλάβη στο δίκτυο ύδρευσης (we must repair the damage to the water supply)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to provide for (financially)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (colloquial) to marry off, marry</div>
  <div class='ex'>Δεν ήθελε να νυμφευτεί ο ίδιος πριν αποκαταστήσει την αδελφή του. - He will not marry until he has married off his sister.</div><b>αποκαλυπτήρια</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. inflection of <a href="bword://αποκαλυπτήριος">αποκαλυπτήριος</a>:; feminine nominative/accusative/vocative singular</div>
  <div class='def'>2. inflection of <a href="bword://αποκαλυπτήριος">αποκαλυπτήριος</a>:; neuter nominative/accusative/vocative plural</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unveiling (a ceremony for the first public showing of something)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. revealing, exposure, uncovering, unmasking</div><b>αποκαλυπτήριος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποκαλυπτήριη, neuter αποκαλυπτήριο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. revelation, exposure (especially of wrongdoing)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (as a noun) revelation</div><b>αποκαλυπτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποκαλυπτική, neuter αποκαλυπτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>revealing, disclosing</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀποκαλυπτικός.</div><b>αποκαλύπτομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to take one&#x27;s hat off to (a sign of respect)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to take one&#x27;s hat off to, bow to superior knowledge</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to unveil</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Passive form of αποκαλύπτω.</div><b>αποκαλύπτω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to reveal; to expose, uncover</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to reveal; to unveil</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to reveal; to unmask</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀποκᾰλύπτω. By surface analysis, απο- (“un-”) + καλύπτω (“cover”).</div><b>αποκαλώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to call, name</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to characterise, label</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀποκαλῶ, contracted form of ἀποκαλεω. By surface analysis, απο- (apo-) + καλώ.</div><b>αποκαμωμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αποκαμωμένη, neuter αποκαμωμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fed up, exhausted</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect passive participle of αποκάνω / αποκάμνω, a verb without passive forms.</div><b>αποκαρδίωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκαρδιώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. discouragement</div>
  <div class='def'>2. gloom, despondency, dejection</div><b>αποκαρδιωμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποκαρδιωμένη, neuter αποκαρδιωμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>discouraged, disheartened, disconsolate</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αποκαρδιώνομαι, passive voice of αποκαρδιώνω</div><b>αποκαρδιωτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποκαρδιωτική, neuter αποκαρδιωτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disheartening, discouraging</div><b>αποκαρδιώνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be disheartened / discouraged</div><b>αποκαρδιώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to dishearten, discourage, demoralise (UK), demoralize (US)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from απο- (apo-) + καρδί(α), “heart”) + -ώνω, a calque of English dishearten.</div><b>αποκαρώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to make drowsy, induce lethargy</div>
  <div class='ex'>η ζέστη με <b>αποκάρωσε</b> - the heat has made me sleepy</div><b>αποκατάσταση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκαταστάσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. restoration, reconstruction, renovation (the process or result)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. restoration (ensure future life or quality of life)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. reinstatement, restitution</div>
  <div class='def'>4. recuperation, recovery, convalescence</div>
  <div class='def'>5. rehabilitation</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀποκατάστασις.</div><b>αποκατασταίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποκαθιστώ">αποκαθιστώ</a></div><b>αποκατινός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποκατινή, neuter αποκατινό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. lower, located below, underneath</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) of lower value</div>
  <div class='def'>3. the one below</div><b>αποκεί</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. from there</div>
  <div class='def'>2. that way</div><b>αποκεντρωτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποκεντρωτική, neuter αποκεντρωτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>decentralising (UK), decentralizing (US)</div><b>αποκεντρώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to decentralise (UK), decentralize (US)</div><b>αποκερματισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αποκερματισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>defragmentation</div><b>αποκεφάλιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκεφαλίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>beheading, decapitation, decollation</div><b>αποκεφάλισμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποκεφαλίσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>decapitation</div><b>αποκεφαλίζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be beheaded, to be guillotined</div><b>αποκεφαλίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to behead, decapitate, decollate, guillotine</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to abolish</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀποκεφαλίζω. The figurative sense, semantic loan from French décapiter. Morphologically, from απο- (apo-, “de”) + κεφάλι + -ίζω.</div><b>αποκεφαλισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αποκεφαλισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. beheading, decapitation, decollation</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) removal of a leadership</div><b>αποκεφαλιστής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αποκεφαλιστές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>headsman, executioner</div><b>αποκηρύσσω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to renounce, repudiate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to denounce, disavow, condemn</div><b>αποκηρύττω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποκηρύσσω">αποκηρύσσω</a></div><b>αποκηρύχνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποκηρύσσω">αποκηρύσσω</a></div><b>αποκλάδια</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>prunings, loppings, offcuts, cuttings</div><b>αποκλήρωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκληρώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disinheritance</div><b>αποκλήρωσης</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>genitive singular of αποκλήωση</div><b>αποκλίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to lean, lean over</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to diverge</div><b>αποκλείομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be blocked, to be excluded</div>
  <div class='ex'>Polytonic spelling: ἀποκλείομαι</div><b>αποκλείω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to block, shut out, isolate</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ο δρόμος <b>αποκλείστηκε</b> από τα χιόνια. - The road was blocked because of snow.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to ban</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ο αθλητής <b>θα αποκλειστεί</b> λόγω ντοπαρίσματος. - The athlete will be banned for doping.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to exclude, rule out</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Αποκλείω</b> το ενδεχόμενο να γίνουν εκλογές σύντομα. - I rule out the possibility of the elections happening soon.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀποκλείω. For sense &#x27;exclude&#x27;, Semantic loan from French exclure. Morphologically, from απο- + κλείω.</div><b>αποκλεισμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αποκλεισμένη, neuter αποκλεισμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. blocked, shut out</div>
  <div class='def'>2. banned</div>
  <div class='def'>3. excluded</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αποκλείομαι, passive voice of αποκλείω (“block out; exclude”). Morphologically, απο- (apo-) + κλεισμένος</div><b>αποκλεισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αποκλεισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. exclusion, elimination</div>
  <div class='def'>2. blockade, boycott</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀποκλεισμός with semantic loan from Italian blocco in the sense &#x27;blockade&#x27;. By surface analysis, αποκλείω + -μός.</div><b>αποκλειστικά</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>exclusively</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αποκλειστικός">αποκλειστικός</a></div><b>αποκλειστική</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative feminine singular of <a href="bword://αποκλειστικός">αποκλειστικός</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκλειστικές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>private nurse</div><b>αποκλειστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποκλειστική, neuter αποκλειστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>exclusive, sole</div><b>αποκλειστικότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκλειστικότητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>exclusivity, exclusiveness</div><b>αποκληρωτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποκληρωτική, neuter αποκληρωτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>relating to disinheritance</div><b>αποκληρώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to disinherit</div><b>αποκληρώσεις</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative plural of αποκλήωση</div><b>αποκληρώσεων</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>genitive plural of αποκλήωση</div><b>αποκληρώσεως</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>genitive singular of αποκλήωση</div><b>αποκλιμάκωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκλιμακώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>de-escalation</div><b>αποκλιμακώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to reduce slowly, de-escalate, scale back</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> από + κλιμακώνω</div><b>αποκοίμιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκοιμίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. getting of to sleep, lulling of to sleep</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) beguiling, lulling</div><b>αποκοίμισμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποκοιμίσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. getting of to sleep, lulling of to sleep</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) beguiling, lulling</div><b>αποκοιμάμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποκοιμιέμαι">αποκοιμιέμαι</a></div><b>αποκοιμίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to put to bed</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to beguile, lull into a false sense of security, put off one&#x27;s guard</div><b>αποκοιμιέμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to nod off, fall asleep, drop off</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το μωρό <b>αποκοιμήθηκε</b> γρήγορα. - The baby fell asleep quickly.</div><b>αποκοιμισμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποκοιμισμένη, neuter αποκοιμισμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. sleeping, asleep, dozy</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) dozy (mentally challenged)</div><b>αποκοιμιστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποκοιμιστική, neuter αποκοιμιστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. soporific</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) beguiling</div><b>αποκοιμούμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποκοιμιέμαι">αποκοιμιέμαι</a></div><b>αποκολλιέμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποκολλώμαι">αποκολλώμαι</a></div><b>αποκολλώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to unstick, unglue</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to separate, detach</div><b>αποκολλώμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to become unstuck, become unglued</div><b>αποκομίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to carry away, remove</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to carry away with me, gain</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀποκομίζω. Morphologically, from απο- (“from”) + κομίζω.</div><b>αποκομιδή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκομιδές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. removal</div>
  <div class='def'>2. collection (eg rubbish)</div><b>αποκομμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αποκομμένη, neuter αποκομμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>isolated, severed</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αποκόβομαι, passive voice of αποκόβω or of αποκόπτομαι, αποκόπτω. Morphologically, απο- (apo-) + κομμένος.</div><b>αποκοπή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) apocope</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) cutting off, amputation</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (uncountable) excommunication, anathema</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀποκοπή.</div><b>αποκορυφούμενος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποκορυφούμενη, neuter αποκορυφούμενο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>climactic, culminating</div><b>αποκορυφώνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to culminate, come to a head</div><b>αποκορυφώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to bring to a head</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to maximise (UK), maximize (US)</div><b>αποκορύφωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποκορυφώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>summit, peak, height, zenith, climax, culmination</div><b>αποκορύφωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκορυφώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>summit, peak, height, zenith, climax, culmination</div><b>αποκοσκινίδια</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>siftings, screenings</div><b>αποκοτάω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποκοτώ">αποκοτώ</a></div><b>αποκοτιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκοτιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. daring, audacity</div>
  <div class='def'>2. recklessness, foolhardiness</div><b>αποκοτώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to dare, risk, venture</div><b>αποκουμπώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to put down</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to rest on, lean on</div><b>αποκουταίνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of αποκουτιαίνομαι</div><b>αποκουταίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποκουτιαίνω">αποκουτιαίνω</a></div><b>αποκουτιαίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to soften, stupify</div>
  <div class='ex'>Τον <b>αποκούτιανε</b> ο έρωτας. - Love has made him soft.</div><b>αποκουφαίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to deafen</div><b>αποκούμπι</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκούμπια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. support, prop; armrest, headrest, footrest</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) refuge, support</div>
  <div class='def'>3. support, prop</div><b>αποκρίνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to answer, reply to, respond to</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (rare) to be excreted</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀποκρίνομαι, mediopassive of ἀποκρίνω. By surface analysis, απο- (“de-, from”) + κρίνομαι (“I am judged, chosen”).</div><b>αποκρίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(rare) to excrete</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀποκρίνω. Synchronicall analysable as απο- (“de-, from”) + κρίνω (“judge, decide”). Also see sense &quot;answer&quot; at αποκρίνομαι.</div><b>αποκραίνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποκρίνομαι">αποκρίνομαι</a></div><b>αποκρατικοποίηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκρατικοποιήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. denationalisation, privatisation (UK)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. denationalization, privatization (US)</div><b>αποκρατικοποιώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to privatise, denationalise (UK), privatize, denationalize (US)</div><b>αποκρεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to fast, prepare for a fast</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (colloquial) to celebrate carnival or mardi gras</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to eat/enjoy the last fruit of the season</div><b>αποκριάτικος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποκριάτικη, neuter αποκριάτικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>carnival</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αποκριάτικη</b> παρέλαση - carnival procession</div><b>αποκριτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποκριτική, neuter αποκριτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>responsive, answering</div><b>αποκρουστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποκρουστική, neuter αποκρουστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>repellant, abominable, repulsive, obnoxious</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Hellenistic Koine Greek ᾰ̓ποκρουστικός (“able to drive off, able to dispel”). The morden sense, a semantic loan from French répulsif.</div><b>αποκρούομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to repulsed, fended off</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to rebutted</div><b>αποκρούω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to reject, repulse, fend off</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to rebut</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to rebut; to respond (to arguments, charges, accusations)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ᾰ̓ποκρούω. For sense rebut arguments, semantic loan from French repousser. Morphologically, from απο- (“counter-”) + κρούω (“strike”).</div><b>αποκρυπτογράφηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκρυπτογραφήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>decryption, decyphering</div><b>αποκρυπτογράφος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural αποκρυπτογράφοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>decipherer, decoder (person or machine)</div><b>αποκρυπτογραφώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to decode, decipher</div><b>αποκρυστάλλωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκρυσταλλώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (figuratively) crystallisation (UK), crystallization (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. recrystallisation (UK), recrystallization (US)</div><b>αποκρυστάλλωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκρυσταλλώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (figuratively) crystallisation (UK), crystallization (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. recrystallisation (UK), recrystallization (US)</div><b>αποκρυσταλλώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to crystallise (UK), crystallize (US) (of substances, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to crystallise (of ideas, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to gell</div><b>αποκρυφισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αποκρυφισμού)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>occultism</div><b>αποκρύβομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποκρύπτομαι">αποκρύπτομαι</a></div><b>αποκρύβω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποκρύπτω">αποκρύπτω</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀποκρύβω from ἀποκρύπτω. By surface analysis, απο- (“from”) + κρύβω (“hide”).</div><b>αποκρύπτομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be concealed</div><b>αποκρύπτω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (transitive) to conceal, hide, withhold</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (transitive) to dissimulate</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀποκρύπτω. By surface analysis, απο- (“from”) + the ancient κρύπτω.</div><b>αποκτάω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποκτώ">αποκτώ</a></div><b>αποκτήνωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκτηνώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. brutalisation, dehumanisation (UK), brutalization, dehumanization (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. degradation</div><b>αποκτημένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αποκτημένη, neuter αποκτημένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>acquired, gained</div>
  <div class='ex'>also see the formal κεκτημένος (kektiménos)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αποκτώμαι &amp; αποκτιέμαι, passive voices of αποκτώ, αποκτάω (“acquire”).</div><b>αποκτηνωτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποκτηνωτική, neuter αποκτηνωτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>brutalising (UK), brutalizing (US)</div><b>αποκτηνώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to degrade</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to brutalise, dehumanise (UK), brutalize, dehumanize (US)</div><b>αποκτώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to acquire</div>
  <div class='ex'>Αποκτούσε εμπειρία κατά τη διάρκεια των πολλών πρακτικών. - She was acquiring experience during the many internships.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to gain, make, profit</div>
  <div class='ex'>Αποκτάει σημασία παγκοσμίως - It&#x27;s gaining importance worldwide</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (transitive) to create, have a child</div>
  <div class='ex'>Θα αποκτήσουμε μωρό. - We&#x27;re having a baby.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From απο- (apo-) + Byzantine Greek κτῶ, from Ancient Greek κτῶμαι, contracted form of κτᾰ́ομαι.</div><b>αποκωδικοποίηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκωδικοποιήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>decoding, deciphering, decrypting</div><b>αποκωδικοποιώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to decode, decipher, decrypt</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> απο- (apo-, “reversal”) + κωδικοποιώ</div><b>αποκόβομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (vernacular) to be weaned</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to be cut off</div>
  <div class='ex'>Alternative: αποκόπτομαι (apokóptomai) (formal)</div><b>αποκόβω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (colloquial, vernacular) alternative form of <a href="bword://αποκόπτω">αποκόπτω</a>; to cut off, sever, cut off completely</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (colloquial, vernacular) alternative form of <a href="bword://αποκόπτω">αποκόπτω</a>; to wean</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From the mediaeval Byzantine Greek ἀποκόβω, from Ancient Greek ἀποκόπτω with metaplasm in the pattern of κόπτω &gt; κόβω. Analysable as απο- (“from”) + κόβω (“cut”).</div><b>αποκόλληση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκολλήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. separation, detachment</div>
  <div class='def'>2. ungluing</div><b>αποκόμιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκομίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>acquisition, removal</div><b>αποκόπτομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be cut off</div><b>αποκόπτω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to cut off, sever</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to wean</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀποκόπτω. By surface analysis, απο- (“from”) + κόπτω (“cut”).</div><b>αποκύημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποκυήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(figuratively) product, offspring of the mind, fabrication</div>
  <div class='ex'>Οι κατηγορίες είναι <b>αποκυήματα</b> της φαντασίας του. - The accusations are products of his imagination.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Hellenistic Koine Greek ᾰ̓ποκύημα. Morphologically, from απο- (“from”) + κύημα (“foetus”).</div><b>απολάκτιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απολακτίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>rejection</div><b>απολέμητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απολέμητη, neuter απολέμητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. uncontested</div>
  <div class='def'>2. invincible</div><b>απολέπιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απολεπίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>exfoliation</div><b>απολήγω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to terminate, end</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to end up, turn out</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπολήγω.</div><b>απολίθωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απολιθώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. fossil</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>απολιθώματα</b> ζώων ή φυτών - fossils of animals or plants</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (derogatory, figuratively) dated, extinct</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) a fossil word or expression.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> First attested in 1856. From απολιθώνω + -μα (-ma, “neuter suffix”). Morphologically from από + λίθος + -μα (-ma, “suffix”). For sense fossil, calque of French pétrification. For figurative senses, calque of French fossile.</div><b>απολίθωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απολιθώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fossilisation (UK), fossilization (US); petrification</div><b>απολίνωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απολινώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ligation, ligature</div><b>απολίπανση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απολιπάνσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>degreasing, the removal of oil, fat, etc</div><b>απολίτικος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απολίτικη, neuter απολίτικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απολιτικός">απολιτικός</a></div><b>απολίτιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απολίτιστη, neuter απολίτιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. uncouth</div>
  <div class='def'>2. uncivilised (UK), uncivilized (US)</div><b>απολαβή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απολαβές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. profit, gain</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (in plural) salary, income</div><b>απολαβαίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to profit, to gain</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (colloquial) to enjoy</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> απο- (apo-, “intensified”) + λαβαίνω</div><b>απολακτίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to kick away</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to reject</div><b>απολαμβάνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to enjoy</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from mediaeval Byzantine Greek ἀπολαμβάνω, a coinciding form from the ancient verbs ἀπολαμβάνω and ἀπολαύω, with the latter supplying the past stem. By surface analysis, απο- (apo-, “intensified”) + λαμβάνω.</div><b>απολαυστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απολαυστική, neuter απολαυστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>enjoyable, pleasurable</div><b>απολαύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to profit, gain</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to enjoy (the gain)</div><b>απολείπω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to want, to need, to lack</div><b>απολείτουργα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>after the liturgy, after mass</div><b>απολειφάδι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απολειφάδια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. soap remains/stub</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) leftover</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) small weak person, squirt</div><b>απολεπίζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to flake)</div><b>απολεπίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to exfoliate, descale</div><b>απολησμονιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απολησμονιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>forgetfulness</div><b>απολησμονιάρης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural απολησμονιάρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>forgetful or absentminded person</div><b>απολησμονώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to forget completely</div><b>απολιθωμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine απολιθωμένη, neuter απολιθωμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. fossilised (UK), fossilized (US), petrified</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) petrified</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of απολιθώνομαι, passive voice of απολιθώνω</div><b>απολιθώνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to become fossilised)</div><b>απολιθώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to fossilise (UK), fossilize (US), petrify</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to petrify (with fear, etc)</div><b>απολιπαίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to degrease, remove fat or oil</div><b>απολιποπρωτεΐνη</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>apolipoprotein</div><b>απολιτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απολιτική, neuter αντιπολιτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>apolitical</div><b>απολιόρκητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απολιόρκητη, neuter απολιόρκητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unbesieged, cannot be besieged</div><b>απολλαπλασίαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απολλαπλασίαστη, neuter απολλαπλασίαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unmultipliable</div><b>απολλύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to lose (faith, virginity)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to destroy, annihilate</div><b>απολλώνιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απολλώνια, neuter απολλώνιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>apollonian</div><b>απολογήτρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απολογήτριες, masculine απολογητής)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. defender, advocate (of a policy, point of view, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (derogatory) apologist</div><b>απολογία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απολογίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. defence, justification, plea (excuse which provides support for behavior or for a belief or occurrence)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το δικαστήριο άκουσε την <b>απολογία</b> του κατηγορουμένου. - The court heard the defendant&#x27;s plea.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (literary) apologia</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπολογία, equivalent to απο- (apo-, “from”) + λόγος + -ία.</div><b>απολογητής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural απολογητές, feminine απολογήτρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. defender, advocate (of a policy, point of view, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (derogatory) apologist</div><b>απολογητικά</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://απολογητικός">απολογητικός</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>in apologetic manner</div><b>απολογητική</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>apologetics (branch of theology defending Christian faith)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπολογητική.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative feminine singular of <a href="bword://απολογητικός">απολογητικός</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπολογητική.</div><b>απολογητικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. apologetic, regretfully excusing</div>
  <div class='ex'>Μου ζήτησε συγγνώμη με <b>απολογητικό</b> ύφος και κατεβασμένο το κεφάλι. - He asked for forgiveness in an apologetic manner and (with) his head dropped.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. defence, justification (concerning an argument in support of something, mainly in legal settings)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>απολογητικό</b> υπόμνημα - defence statement</div>
  <div class='def'>3. of the branch of apologetics</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>απολογητικά</b> έργα - apologetic works</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Semantic loan from French apologétique (“apologetic: regretful; defending”) from Medieval Latin apologeticus with the same sense, from ἀπολογητικός. Also see ἀπολογία.</div><b>απολογητικώς</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>dated form of <a href="bword://απολογητικά">απολογητικά</a> (apologetically, in defence)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Older script: ἀπολογητικῶς (apologētikôs)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Byzantine Greek ἀπολογητικῶς. From ancient adjective ἀπολογητικός.</div><b>απολογισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural απολογισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>report, account, statement (of accounts)</div><b>απολογούμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to defend oneself, plea</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to excuse oneself, justify oneself, explain oneself</div>
  <div class='ex'>Δεν πιστεύω πως πρέπει να <b>απολογηθώ</b> για ό,τι έκανα, ούτε να να δικαιολογηθώ σε κανέναν! - I don&#x27;t believe I have to apologize for what I have done, or explain myself to anyone!</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (Cyprus, idiomatic) to apologize</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀπολογοῦμαι, contracted form of ἀπολογέομαι.</div><b>απολυμαίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to disinfect, sanitise (UK), sanitize (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to clean</div><b>απολυμαντήριο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απολυμαντήρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disinfection unit/facility</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>genitive masculine/neuter singular of <a href="bword://απολυμαντήριος">απολυμαντήριος</a></div><b>απολυμαντήριος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απολυμαντήρια, neuter απολυμαντήριο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disinfectant</div><b>απολυμαντής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural απολυμαντές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disinfector</div><b>απολυμαντικά</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disinfectant (with this effect)</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://απολυμαντικός">απολυμαντικός</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
