  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποσπερματίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ejaculation (of semen)</div><b>αποσπερματίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to ejaculate (semen)</div><b>αποσπερματισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αποσπερματισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ejaculation (of semen)</div><b>αποσπερνός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποσπερνή, neuter αποσπερνό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>evening</div><b>αποσπόντα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>obliquely, indirectly</div><b>αποσπόρι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποσπόρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial) lastborn, youngest (child)</div><b>αποσπώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to extort, extract</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to distract (to stop someone&#x27;s task)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to second, lend (on temporary work assignment)</div><b>αποστάζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be distilled</div><b>αποστάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to distil (UK), distill (US)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀποστάζω (“fall drop by drop”). Semantic loan from French distiller. Morphologically, from απο- (“from”) + στάζω (“drip”).</div><b>αποστάτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αποστάτες, feminine αποστάτισσα or αποστάτρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>apostate</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀποστάτης.</div><b>αποστάτισσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποστάτισσες, masculine αποστάτης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>apostate (female)</div><b>αποστάτρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποστάτριες, masculine αποστάτης)</i></div>
