  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Latin a posteriori.</div><b>αποστερώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (transitive) to rob</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (transitive) to deprive, dispossess</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀποστερῶ, contracted form of ἀποστερέω. By surface analysis, απο- (apo-) + στερώ.</div><b>αποστεωμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποστεωμένη, neuter αποστεωμένο)</i></div>
