  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to emaciate, ossify</div><b>αποστηθίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to memorise (UK), memorize (US), learn by heart</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ᾰ̓ποστηθῐ́ζω or from Mediaeval, from Hellenistic expression ἀπὸ στήθους, see από στήθους.</div><b>αποστολέας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural αποστολείς)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sender, consignor, consigner</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned, from the accusative singular ἀποστολέα of Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀποστολεύς. Semantic loan from French envoyeur and expéditeur.</div><b>αποστολή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποστολές)</i></div>
