  <div class='def'>turned to a different direction</div>
  <div class='ex'>more formal or dated: απεστραμμένος (apestramménos)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect passive participle of αποστρέφω, in the sense &quot;turn waya, avert&quot;</div><b>αποστρατεία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποστρατείες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(especially) retirement (the state and the action)</div><b>αποστρατεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to demobilise (UK), demobilize (US)</div><b>αποστρατιωτικοποίηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποστρατιωτικοποιήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>demilitarisation (UK), demilitarization (US)</div><b>αποστροφή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποστροφές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. aversion, disgust, repugnance</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (rhetoric) apostrophe</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀποστροφή from verb ἀποστρέφω &amp; semantic loan from French aversion. The sense for rhetoric, since Hellenistic period.</div><b>αποστόμωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποστομώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>silencing, enforcing silence</div><b>αποσυμφορίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποσυμφορώ">αποσυμφορώ</a></div><b>αποσυμφορώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to decongest, relieve congestion</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to decongest, relieve congestion</div><b>αποσυμφόρηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποσυμφορήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. decongestion, overcrowding relief</div>
  <div class='def'>2. decongestion</div><b>αποσυνάγωγος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποσυνάγωγη, neuter αποσυνάγωγο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. ostracised (UK), ostracized (US), excommunicated</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (Judaism) excluded from the synagogue</div><b>αποσυναρμολογώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to dismantle, disassemble, strip down</div><b>αποσυναρμολόγηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποσυναρμολογήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disassembly, dismantling, stripping down</div><b>αποσυνδέομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to disconnect yourself</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to distance yourself (from someone)</div><b>αποσυνδέω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to disconnect, sever a connection</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> απο- (“de-”) + συνδέω (“connect”). Morphologically, from απο- (“de-”) + -συν- (“con-”) + δέω.</div><b>αποσυνδεδεμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποσυνδεδεμένη, neuter αποσυνδεδεμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disconnected</div><b>αποσυνδετικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποσυνδετική, neuter αποσυνδετικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disaggregate, disorganised (UK), disorganized (US)</div><b>αποσυνθέτομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of αποσυντίθεμαι</div><b>αποσυνθέτω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to decompose, dismantle, disaggregate, to disorganise (UK), disorganize (US)</div><b>αποσυνθετικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποσυνθετική, neuter αποσυνθετικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>causing decomposition, decomposing</div><b>αποσφράγιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποσφραγήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unsealing, opening</div><b>αποσφραγίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(transitive) to unseal, remove seals</div><b>αποσχίζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to secede, break away, detach</div><b>αποσχίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to secede</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to tear, tear off</div><b>αποσχηματίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(transitive) to defrock, unfrock</div><b>αποσχηματισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αποσχηματισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>defrocking, unfrocking</div><b>αποσχισμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αποσχισμένη, neuter αποσχισμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>seceded, severed</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αποσχίζομαι, passive voice of αποσχίζω</div><b>αποσχιστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποσχιστική, neuter αποσχιστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>secessionist</div><b>αποσόβηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποσοβήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>forestalling, averting</div><b>αποσύνδεση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποσυνδέσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disconnection, log out, log off</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from Katharevousa αποσύνδεσις. By surface analysis, αποσυνδέ(ω)) + -ση (-si).</div><b>αποσύνθεση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποσυνθέσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. breakdown, decomposition</div>
  <div class='def'>2. decomposition, decay, putrefaction, putridity, rot</div>
  <div class='def'>3. disintegration, disorganisation</div><b>αποσύρομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to withdraw, stand down, retreat</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to keep one&#x27;s distance from</div><b>αποσύρω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to withdraw, retract</div><b>αποσώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to finish, finish off</div><b>αποτάσσω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to cashier, discharge</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (transitive) to dismiss, sack, discharge</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀποτάσσω.</div><b>αποτέλειωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποτελειώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>a less formal variant of <a href="bword://αποτελείωμα">αποτελείωμα</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αποτελειώ(νω), “finish”) + -μα (-ma). Compare to the learned αποτελείωμα.</div><b>αποτέλεσμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποτελέσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. result, outcome (sport, election, etc)</div>
  <div class='ex'>τα <b>αποτελέσματα</b> του τεστ - the test results</div>
  <div class='def'>2. effect</div><b>αποτέφρωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποτεφρώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>cremation, incineration</div><b>αποτίμηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποτιμήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. appraisal, assessment</div>
  <div class='def'>2. valuation</div><b>αποτίναξη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποτινάξεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>shaking off, kicking off, throwing off</div><b>αποτίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποτίω">αποτίω</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀποτίνω</div><b>αποτίω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (figuratively) to pay off</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to serve (in prison)</div><b>αποταμίευμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποταμιεύματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>savings (money or materials)</div><b>αποταμίευση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποταμιεύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. saving, thrift</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (in plural) savings</div><b>αποταμιευτής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αποταμιευτές, feminine αποταμιεύτρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>saver</div><b>αποταμιευτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποταμιευτική, neuter αποταμιευτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(relating to) saving, savings</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αποταμιευτικός</b> λογαριασμός - savings account</div><b>αποταμιεύτρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποταμιεύτριες, masculine αποταμιευτής)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>saver</div><b>αποταμιεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to save, save up</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to reserve, put to one side</div><b>αποταχύ</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>early in the morning</div><b>αποτείνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to address, apply, ask</div><b>αποτελείωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποτελειώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. completion</div>
  <div class='def'>2. annihilation</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αποτελειώνω + -μα (-ma), from Koine Greek ἀποτελειόω, hence the formal pronunciation without synizesis. Compare αποτέλειωμα.</div><b>αποτελειώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to consummate, finish off, complete</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to kill, dispatch, finish off</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀποτελειώνω, from Koine Greek ἀποτελειόω. By surface analysis απο- (apo-, “completion”) + τελειώνω.</div><b>αποτελεσματικά</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>effectively</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αποτελεσματικός">αποτελεσματικός</a></div><b>αποτελεσματικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποτελεσματική, neuter αποτελεσματικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>effective, efficient</div><b>αποτελεσματικότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) efficacy, effectiveness</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αποτελεσματικός + -ότητα. First attested 1869.</div><b>αποτελμάτωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποτελματώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>stagnation</div><b>αποτελματώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to stagnate, swamp</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to vegetate, stultify</div><b>αποτελώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to constitute, to make up</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to consist of, to be composed of, to be made up of, to comprise</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ᾰ̓ποτελῶ, contracted form of ᾰ̓ποτελέω.</div><b>αποτεφρωτήρας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αποτεφρωτήρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>crematorium, incinerator</div><b>αποτεφρώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to burn down, burn up</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to incinerate, cremate</div><b>αποτιμώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to value, assess, quantify (the financial worth of)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to assess, evaluate</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η επιτροπή συνεδρίασε για να <b>αποτιμήσει</b> το εκλογικό αποτέλεσμα. - The committee met to evaluate the election result.</div><b>αποτινάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to get rid of, shake off</div><b>αποτινάσσομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of αποτινάζομαι</div><b>αποτινάσσω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποτινάζω">αποτινάζω</a></div><b>αποτιτάνωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποτιτανώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>calcification</div><b>αποτιτανωμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αποτιτανωμένη, neuter αποτιτανωμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>calcified</div><b>αποτοίχιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποτοιχίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>wall-painting removal (for preservation)</div><b>αποτοιχίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to remove a fresco/mural</div><b>αποτολμώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to risk, dare, venture</div><b>αποτοξίνωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποτοξινώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>detoxification, detoxication</div><b>αποτοξινώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(transitive) to detoxify, detoxicate, detoxificate</div><b>αποτρέπω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to avert, ward off</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to dissuade, deter</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to stop, prevent</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned from Ancient Greek ἀποτρέπω. By surface analysis, απο- (“from”) + τρέπω (“turn”).</div><b>αποτρίχωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποτριχώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>depilation, epilation, hair removal, waxing</div><b>αποτραβάω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποτραβώ">αποτραβώ</a></div><b>αποτραβηγμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αποτραβηγμένη, neuter αποτραβηγμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>withdrawn, pulled away from</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ζει <b>αποτραβηγμένος</b> από την κοινωνία. - He lives withdrawn from society.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αποτραβιέμαι, passive voice of αποτραβώ (“I withdraw, pull back”).</div><b>αποτραβιέμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to withdraw</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to retreat, withdraw, fall back, give way</div><b>αποτραβώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to recede, withdraw, pull away</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> απο- (apo-, “from”) + τραβώ</div><b>αποτραπήκανε</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>colloquial variation of αποτραπήκαν, third-person plural simple past of <a href="bword://αποτρέπω">αποτρέπω</a></div><b>αποτρελαίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to unhinge, madden, drive mad</div><b>αποτρεπτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποτρεπτική, neuter αποτρεπτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>deterrent, preventive</div><b>αποτριχωτικό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποτριχωτικά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>hair remover, depilator, depilatory</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://αποτριχωτικός">αποτριχωτικός</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://αποτριχωτικός">αποτριχωτικός</a></div><b>αποτριχωτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποτριχωτική, neuter αποτριχωτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>depilatory, hair removing</div><b>αποτριχώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(transitive) to depilate, to remove hair</div><b>αποτροπή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποτροπές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. deterrence, dissuasion</div>
  <div class='def'>2. prevention</div><b>αποτροπιάζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to detest, hate, abhor</div><b>αποτροπιάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to disgust, repel</div><b>αποτροπιασμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αποτροπιασμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>revulsion, repugnance, abhorrence</div><b>αποτροπιαστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποτροπιαστική, neuter αποτροπιαστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abhorrent, revolting, disgusting, repulsive</div><b>αποτρυγώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to finish the vintage/grape harvest</div><b>αποτρόπαιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποτρόπαιη, neuter αποτρόπαιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. ghastly, horrid, horrible</div>
  <div class='def'>2. atrocious, revolting</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀποτρόπαιος.</div><b>αποτρώγω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to eat up, finish eating</div><b>αποτσίγαρο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποτσίγαρα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>cigarette end, butt; fag end (colloquial)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> απο- (apo-, “ex-”) + τσιγάρο</div><b>αποτυγχάνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to fail, not succeed</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to fall, fall through</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from Ancient Greek ἀποτυγχάνω; compare αποτυχαίνω.</div><b>αποτυπώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (transitive) to stamp, impress imprint; to design on cloth, words on paper etc</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (transitive) to stamp, impress imprint; to footprint, spoor, wheel track</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (transitive) to stamp, impress imprint; to express on face</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (transitive) to stamp, impress imprint; to experience into memory</div><b>αποτυφλωτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποτυφλωτική, neuter αποτυφλωτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>blinding</div><b>αποτυφλώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(transitive) to blind (go or make completely blind)</div><b>αποτυχία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποτυχίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. failure, defeat</div>
  <div class='def'>2. setback, washout</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀποτυχία from the verb ἀποτυγχάνω. By surface analysis, απο- (apo-) + τύχ(η)) + -ία. See the ancient τύχη f.</div><b>αποτυχαίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποτυγχάνω">αποτυγχάνω</a></div><b>αποτυχημένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αποτυχημένη, neuter αποτυχημένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>failed</div><b>αποτυχών</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποτυχούσα, neuter αποτυχόν)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unsuccessful</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Αποτυχόν</b> πραξικόπημα στην Τουρκία! - Unsuccessful coup d&#x27;état in Turkey!</div><b>αποτύπωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποτυπώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. imprint, impression (print left in soft material)</div>
  <div class='ex'>δακτυλικό <b>αποτύπωμα</b> - fingerprint</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) fingerprint, footprint, handprint</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) print, imprint, impression</div>
  <div class='ex'>το <b>αποτύπωμα</b> άνθρακα, το ενεργειακό <b>αποτύπωμα</b> - carbon footprint</div>
  <div class='def'>4. stamp (an indentation, imprint, or mark made by stamping)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αποτυπώνω + -μα (-ma).</div><b>αποτύπωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποτυπώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>stamping, impression, impressing</div><b>αποτύφλωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποτυφλώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>total blindness</div><b>απουσία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απουσίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>absence</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπουσία.</div><b>απουσιάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to be absent</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to absent oneself</div><b>απουσιολόγιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απουσιολόγια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>record/register of attendance, (literally, “register of absentees”)</div><b>απουσιολόγος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural απουσιολόγοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>class register taker (a student)</div><b>αποφάι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποφάγια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>leftovers, scraps, food remains</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> * απο- (apo-) + φαΐ</div><b>αποφέρω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to yield, produce</div><b>αποφαίνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to give a verdict, rule, adjudicate</div>
  <div class='ex'>το δικαστήριο <b>αποφαίνεται</b> ότι... - the court rules that...</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to express an opinion or point of view</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (impersonal, literary, rare) to seem, to appear (without attracting attention, keeping in the background); to become apparent</div>
  <div class='ex'>δεν της <b>αποφαίνεται</b> πως είναι έγκυος - Great Dictionary of the entire Greek Language</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (literary, rare) to be felt, be perceived, make an impression; to not feel/look it</div>
  <div class='ex'>Έχασε ένα εκατομμύριο στο καζίνο αλλά δεν του <b>αποφάνηκε</b>. - He lost a million in the casino but he didn&#x27;t feel it/he didn&#x27;t mind it/it didn&#x27;t make much difference to him.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀποφαίνω as in the phrase (with mediopassive form) ἀποφαίνομαι γνώμην f &quot;declare [one&#x27;s] opinion&quot; and Semantic loan from French se déclarer. Morphologically, απο- (apo-) + φαίνομαι.</div><b>αποφαντικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποφαντική, neuter αποφαντικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>assertoric</div><b>αποφασίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to decide, resolve, reach a verdict</div>
  <div class='ex'>Μερικές φορές <b>αποφασίζω</b> να μην πάρω ομπρέλα. - Sometimes I decide to not take an umbrella.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek αποφασίζω, from Koine Greek ἀπόφασις + -ίζω.</div><b>αποφασιστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποφασιστική, neuter αποφασιστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>decisive</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Calque of French décisif. First attested 1683.</div><b>αποφασιστικότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) determination, decisiveness, resoluteness</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αποφασιστικός + -ότητα. First attested 1820, in a declaration of Greece&#x27;s independence by Alexander Ypsilantis .</div><b>αποφατικά</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>negatively</div><b>αποφατικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποφατικη, neuter αποφατικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(negative) negative</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀποφατικός.</div><b>αποφευκτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποφευκτική, neuter αποφευκτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>avoidant</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀποφευκτικός, from ἀποφεύγω. By surface analysis, αποφεύγω + -τικός.</div><b>αποφευκτός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποφευκτή, neuter αποφευκτό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>avoidable (capable of being avoided)</div><b>αποφεύγω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to avoid (keep away from)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to shun, avoid (doing something)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀποφεύγω. By surface analysis, απο- (apo-) + φεύγω.</div><b>αποφθεγματικά</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>aphoristically</div><b>αποφθεγματικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποφθεγματική, neuter αποφθεγματικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>aphoristic</div><b>αποφλοίωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>peeling, stripping, debarking, flaying</div><b>αποφλοιωτήρας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αποφλοιωτήρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>peeler, debarker (equipment for doing this task)</div><b>αποφλοιωτήριο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποφλοιωτήρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>plant/place where debarking/peeling takes place</div><b>αποφλοιώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(transitive) to debark (tree), peel (fruit)</div><b>αποφοίτηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποφοιτήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. graduation</div>
  <div class='def'>2. passing out (UK)</div><b>αποφοιτήριο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποφοιτήρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>certificate of graduation etc</div><b>αποφοιτώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to graduate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to pass out</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀποφοιτῶ, contracted form of ἀποφοιτάω. By surface analysis, απο- (“de-”) + φοιτώ (“attend lessons”).</div><b>αποφορά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποφορές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>stench</div><b>αποφορτίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to discharge, remove charge</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to remove tension</div><b>αποφράδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποφράδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unlucky day, accursed/cursed day</div>
  <div class='ex'>Είκοσι εννέα Mαΐου 1453 είναι <b>αποφράδα ημέρα</b> (η άλωση της Κωνσταντινούπολης). - 29ᵗʰ May 1452 is the accursed day (the fall of Constantinople).</div><b>αποφράζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to block, (pipe, drain, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to block, barricade (road)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to brick up (doorway, etc)</div><b>αποφράσσω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποφράζω">αποφράζω</a></div><b>αποφρακτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποφρακτική, neuter αποφρακτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>obstructive</div><b>αποφυάδες</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative plural of αποφυάς or αποφυάδα</div>
  <div class='ex'>Polytonic spelling: ἀποφυάδες (apophuádes)</div><b>αποφυγή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) avoidance, evasion</div><b>αποφυλάκιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποφυλακίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>release, discharge (from prison)</div><b>αποφυλακίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(transitive) to discharge, release (prisoner)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from απο- (apo-) + φυλακίζω, a calque of French désemprisonner.</div><b>αποφυλακιστήριο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποφυλακιστήρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>release documentation/papers</div><b>αποφυλλωμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποφυλλωμένη, neuter αποφυλλωμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>defoliated</div><b>αποφόρι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποφόρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. cast off/castoff, hand-me-down (clothing)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (in plural) cast offs</div><b>αποφόρτιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποφορτίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. discharge</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) release (of emotional tension)</div><b>αποφύσεως</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>formal or dated form of απόφυσης: genitive singular of <a href="bword://απόφυση">απόφυση</a></div><b>αποφώλι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποφώλια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nest egg</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From απο- (apo-, “from”) + φώλι, from φωλι(ά), “nest”) + neuter suffix -ι (-i). Cognate with Pontic Greek πιφώλι.</div><b>αποφώλιο τέρας</b>
  <div><i>phrase</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(dated) literally: hideous monster (of criminals who committed hideous acts)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Via the Katharevousa expression ἀποφώλιον τέρας (hiderous monster), a rendering of the ancient phrase ἀποφώλιον τρέφος by Euripides, describing the Minotaur. See ἀποφώλιος</div><b>αποφώλιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποφώλια, neuter αποφώλιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>monstrous, hideous, in the dated phrase (of criminals)</div>
  <div class='ex'>αποφώλιον τέρας (apofólion téras, “hideous monster”)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀποφώλιος, in the sense: monstrous, of uncertain origin.</div><b>αποχέτευση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποχετεύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. drainage (process whereby land is drained of liquid)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. drainage, drains (system of drains)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. sewerage (network of sewer pipes that geographically transfers wastewater)</div>
  <div class='def'>4. sanitation, wastewater removal</div><b>αποχή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. abstinence (act of refraining from indulging a desire or appetite)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. abstention (act of declining to participate)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> # From Ancient Greek ἀποχή</div><b>αποχαιρετάω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποχαιρετώ">αποχαιρετώ</a></div><b>αποχαιρετίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποχαιρετώ">αποχαιρετώ</a></div><b>αποχαιρετισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αποχαιρετισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>farewell, leavetaking, goodbye</div><b>αποχαιρετιστήριος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποχαιρετιστήρια, neuter αποχαιρετιστήριο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>farewell, parting</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αποχαιρετιστήριο</b> γεύμα - a farewell dinner</div><b>αποχαιρετώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to say goodbye, bid farewell, say farewell</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> By surface analysis, απο- (apo-) + χαιρετώ.</div><b>αποχαλάω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποχαλώ">αποχαλώ</a></div><b>αποχαλίνωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) running wild, dissoluteness</div><b>αποχαλινώνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to run wild, riot</div><b>αποχαλινώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to set free, unfetter</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to run wild, riot</div><b>αποχαλνώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποχαλώ">αποχαλώ</a></div><b>αποχαλώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to destroy, ruin</div><b>αποχαρακτηρίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(transitive) to declassify</div><b>αποχαρακτηρισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αποχαρακτηρισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>declassification</div><b>αποχαυνωτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποχαυνωτική, neuter αποχαυνωτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>enervating, debilitating, torporific</div><b>αποχαυνώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to enervate, debilitate</div><b>αποχαύνωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) languour, torpor</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Back-formation from αποχαυνώνω. By surface analysis, απο- (apo-, “un-, from”) + χαύνωση. First attested 1855.</div><b>αποχείμωνα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>at the end of winter</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative plural of <a href="bword://αποχείμωνο">αποχείμωνο</a></div><b>αποχείμωνο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποχείμωνα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>winter&#x27;s end</div><b>αποχειροβίωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποχειροβίωτη, neuter αποχειροβίωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>hardworking, breadwinning</div><b>αποχειροτονία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποχειροτονίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. removal/dismissal from office</div>
  <div class='def'>2. defrocking</div><b>αποχετευτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποχετευτική, neuter αποχετευτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>drainage, drains</div><b>αποχετεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to drain, drain off</div><b>αποχουντοποίηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) removal of members and officials after the defeat of a dictatorship</div><b>αποχρέμπτομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to expectorate</div><b>αποχρεμπτικό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποχρεμπτικά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>expectorant</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://αποχρεμπτικός">αποχρεμπτικός</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://αποχρεμπτικός">αποχρεμπτικός</a></div><b>αποχρεμπτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποχρεμπτική, neuter αποχρεμπτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. expectorative</div>
  <div class='def'>2. expectorant</div><b>αποχρωμάτιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποχρωματίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>decolouration (UK), decoloration (US)</div><b>αποχρωματίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to discolour (UK), discolor (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to fade, bleach</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) to declassify</div><b>αποχρωματισμός</b>
