  <div class='def'>1. (figuratively) declassification</div>
  <div class='def'>2. discolouration (UK), discoloration (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. fading, bleaching</div><b>αποχρωστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποχρωστική, neuter αποχρωστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>decolorising (UK), decolorizing (US)</div><b>αποχρών</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποχρώσα, neuter αποχρών)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sufficient, competent</div>
  <div class='ex'>chiefly in phrase: αποχρών λόγος (apochrón lógos, “sufficient reason”)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀποχρών</div><b>αποχρών λόγος</b>
  <div><i>phrase</i></div>
  <div class='def'>rationale, sufficient reason</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ἀποχρών + λόγος</div><b>αποχτενίδι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποχτενίδια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>combings</div><b>αποχτηνώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποκτηνώνω">αποκτηνώνω</a></div><b>αποχτώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποκτώ">αποκτώ</a></div><b>αποχυμωτής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αποχυμωτές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>liquidiser (UK), liquidizer (US), juicer</div><b>αποχωρίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to separate</div><b>αποχωρητήριο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποχωρητήρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>toilet, lavatory, WC</div><b>αποχωρισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αποχωρισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>separation, parting, dissociation</div><b>αποχωριστής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αποχωριστές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>separator</div><b>αποχωρώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to leave, depart</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to withdraw, resign</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to pull out, retire</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀποχωρέω. Can be synchronically analyzed as απο- (apo-, “from”) + χωρώ. The root of the second term is the same, but it is a derived form that has the opposite meaning from the Ancient Greek.</div><b>αποχώρηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποχωρήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>withdrawal, resignation</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀποχώρησις. Can be synchronically analyzed as απο- (apo-, “from”) + χώρος + -ης (-is).</div><b>αποψίλωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποψιλώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. deforestation</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) stripping of authority</div>
  <div class='def'>3. depilation</div><b>αποψεσινός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποψεσινή, neuter αποψεσινό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (colloquial) of last night, yesterday evening, or yesterday night</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (rare) of tonight or this evening</div><b>αποψιλωτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποψιλωτική, neuter αποψιλωτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. relating to:; deforestation</div>
  <div class='def'>2. relating to:; depilation</div><b>αποψιλώνω</b>
