  <div class='def'>1. to deforest, clear ground</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to depilate</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) to strip of authority</div><b>αποψινός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποψινή, neuter αποψινό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>of this evening</div><b>αποψυκτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αποψυκτική, neuter αποψυκτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>relating to defrosting</div><b>αποψύχω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to defrost, thaw</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (rare) to freeze, refrigerate</div><b>απούλητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απούλητη, neuter απούλητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unsold</div><b>απούντο</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(idiomatic) punctually, on time</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀποῦντο, from Italian appunto with orthographic simplification of ⟨pp⟩ &lt; a punto, and see Latin punctum.</div><b>απούσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απούσες, masculine απών)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>absentee</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. nominative feminine singular of <a href="bword://απών">απών</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. accusative feminine singular of <a href="bword://απών">απών</a></div><b>απρέπεια</b>
