  <div class='def'>1. fine, unequalled (workmanship)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. insatiable (appetite)</div><b>απτέρυξ</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural απτέρυγες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>kiwi (bird)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from translingual Apteryx (literally “no-wing”).</div><b>απτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απτική, neuter απτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>tactile, tactual, haptic</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἁπτικός</div><b>απτχος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://αντιπτέραρχος">αντιπτέραρχος</a></div><b>απτόητα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>undauntedly</div><b>απτόητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απτόητη, neuter απτόητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. undeterred, undaunted, undismayed, unabashed</div>
  <div class='def'>2. dauntless</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀπτόητος</div><b>απτός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απτή, neuter απτό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. tangible, palpable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) obvious</div><b>απυρεξία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) apyrexia</div><b>απυρπόλητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απυρπόλητη, neuter απυρπόλητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unignited</div><b>απυρόβλητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απυρόβλητη, neuter απυρόβλητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>invulnerable, having cover/protection against enemy fire</div><b>απχος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://αρχιπλοίαρχος">αρχιπλοίαρχος</a></div><b>απωανατολικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απωανατολική, neuter απωανατολικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Far Eastern, from the Far East</div><b>απωθημένο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απωθημένα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>repressed emotion/impulse</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://απωθημένος">απωθημένος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://απωθημένος">απωθημένος</a></div><b>απωθημένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine απωθημένη, neuter απωθημένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. repelled</div>
  <div class='def'>2. repressed feeling</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (in plural) inhibitions</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect passive participle of απωθώ</div><b>απωθητικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απωθητική, neuter απωθητικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. repellent, repulsive</div>
  <div class='def'>2. awful, off-putting</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from the απωθη- stem of απωθώ + -τικός, a calque of French répulsif.</div><b>απωθώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to repel, repulse, push back, drive away</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to repel, disgust</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to repress</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ο ασθενής είχε <b>απωθήσει</b> τη δυσάρεστη εμπειρία. - The patient has repressed the unpleasant experience.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀπωθῶ, contracted form of ἀπωθέω. By surface analysis, απ- (από)) + ωθώ.</div><b>απωμάτιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απωμάτιστη, neuter απωμάτιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>stopperless, without a cork/stopper/cap/lid (of a container)</div><b>απωστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απωστική, neuter απωστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>repulsive (having the capacity to repel)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀπωστικός, semantically adapted to the modern meaning of άπωση.</div><b>από</b>
  <div><i>prep</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (with accusative, with genitive) from</div>
  <div class='ex'>ξεκίνησε <b>από</b> το σπίτι - started from home</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (with accusative, with genitive) from</div>
  <div class='ex'>είμαι <b>από</b> την Ελλάδα - I am from Greece</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (with accusative, with genitive) from, at, by, since</div>
  <div class='ex'>θα είμαι εδώ <b>από</b> νωρίς - I&#x27;ll be early</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (with accusative, with genitive) by, with, from</div>
  <div class='ex'>παρασύρθηκε <b>από</b> την οργή - he was carried away by anger</div>
  <div class='def'>5. (with accusative, with genitive) from</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>από</b> 25 ως 28 βαθμούς - from 25 to 28 degrees</div>
  <div class='def'>6. (with accusative, with genitive) from</div>
  <div class='ex'>έγινε <b>από</b> φιλόλογος προγραμματιστής - he changed from philologist into programmer</div>
  <div class='def'>7. (with accusative, with genitive) out of, from</div>
  <div class='ex'>προσελήφθησαν οι τρεις <b>από</b> τους πέντε υποψηφίους - three out of five applicants were taken on</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπό, from Proto-Indo-European *h₂epó (“off, away”).</div><b>από δήμαρχος κλητήρας</b>
  <div><i>phrase</i></div>
  <div class='def'>from rags to riches</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> από δήμαρχος κλητήρας</div><b>από δω κι από κει</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://από">από</a> <a href="bword://εδώ">εδώ</a> <a href="bword://και">και</a> <a href="bword://από">από</a> <a href="bword://εκεί">εκεί</a></div><b>από εδώ και από εκεί</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>from here to there, here and there, to and fro</div><b>από εδώ και στο εξής</b>
  <div><i>phrase</i></div>
  <div class='def'>from now on</div><b>από καταβολής κόσμου</b>
  <div><i>prep_phrase</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(excessive, sometimes) since the world began, since the dawn of time</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀπὸ καταβολῆς κόσμου, used in several places in the New Testament.</div><b>από κοινού</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>jointly, together</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Literally, “from common”. Compare English apo koinou.</div><b>από λεπτό σε λεπτό</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(idiomatic) any minute now</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Literally, “from minute to minute”. Compare French d&#x27;une minute à l&#x27;autre.</div><b>από μπρος</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>from the front, (from) in front</div><b>από νωρίς</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>early, early on</div><b>από πού είσαι</b>
  <div><i>phrase</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(informal) where are you from?</div><b>από πού είστε</b>
  <div><i>phrase</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(formal) where are you from?</div><b>από πού κι ως πού</b>
  <div><i>phrase</i></div>
  <div class='def'>why; for what reason (used to express strong disagreement)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Από πού κι ως πού</b> θα πρέπει το κράτος να γνωρίζει τις κινήσεις μου στο διαδίκτυο; - Why on earth should the government know what I&#x27;m doing on the Internet?</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Literally &quot;from where and until where&quot;. Calque of Turkish nereden nereye (“for some reason or other; I don&#x27;t quite know why”), literally &quot;from where to where&quot;.</div><b>από πού κρατάει η σκούφια</b>
  <div><i>phrase</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(idiomatic) (literally) from where is one&#x27;s cap retain(ed)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Από πού κρατάει η σκούφια</b> του; - What is his ancestry/background?</div><b>από σπίτι</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (indeclinable) Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see <a href="bword://από">από</a>, <a href="bword://σπίτι">σπίτι</a>.</div>
  <div class='ex'>Βρήκα ένα πιάνο <b>από σπίτι</b> παλιό. - I found a piano from an old house.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (of people) of good stock, of a good family</div>
  <div class='ex'>Αυτή είναι κορίτσι <b>από σπίτι</b> και ποτέ δε φοράει φτηνά ρούχα. - She&#x27;s a girl from a good family and she never wears cheap clothes.</div><b>από τότε</b>
  <div><i>prep</i></div>
  <div class='def'>since, from then</div><b>απόβαλμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποβάλματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>aborted foetus (UK), aborted fetus (US)</div><b>απόβαρο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απόβαρα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>tare (weight of empty container/vehicle), dead weight</div><b>απόβαση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποβάσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>landing</div><b>απόβγαλμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποβγάλματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απόβαλμα">απόβαλμα</a></div><b>απόβλητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. waste</div>
  <div class='def'>2. sewage</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://απόβλητος">απόβλητος</a></div><b>απόβλητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόβλητη, neuter απόβλητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>outcast, pariah (socially)</div><b>απόβραδο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απόβραδα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>early evening, dusk</div><b>απόβρασμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποβράσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>scum</div><b>απόβροχο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) the time just after it has rained</div><b>απόγαιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απόγειο">απόγειο</a></div><b>απόγειο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απόγεια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (figuratively) apex, acme</div>
  <div class='def'>2. apogee (in relation to the Earth)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. land breeze</div>
  <div class='def'>4. painter, mooring rope</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://απόγειος">απόγειος</a></div><b>απόγειος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόγεια, neuter απόγειο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>describing a land breeze</div><b>απόγευμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απογεύματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>afternoon</div>
  <div class='ex'>το <b>απόγευμα</b> - in the afternoon</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> από + γεύμα.</div><b>απόγκρεμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόγκρεμη, neuter απόγκρεμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>steep, sheer, rugged, craggy</div><b>απόγνωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) despair, desolation</div>
  <div class='ex'>φέρνω σε <b>απόγνωση</b> - I am desolate</div><b>απόγονος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural απόγονοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. descendant, progeny</div>
  <div class='def'>2. child, offspring</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπόγονος. Morphologically, from από- + γόνος.</div><b>απόγραφο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απόγραφα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>authenticated copy, official copy (of a document)</div><b>απόδ.</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://απόδοση">απόδοση</a>: apodosis</div><b>απόδειξη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποδείξεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. proof</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η <b>απόδειξη</b> του θεωρήματος βρίσκεται στη σελίδα 35. - The proof of the theorem can be found on page 35.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (mainly) evidence</div>
  <div class='ex'>Δεν υπήρχαν αρκετές <b>αποδείξεις</b> για την καταδίκη του. - There was not enough evidence to convict him.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. receipt</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ξέχασα την <b>απόδειξη</b> στο εστιατόριο. - I forgot the receipt in the restaurant.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Classical Greek ἀπόδειξις.</div><b>απόδειπνο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απόδειπνα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. compline, evening service or prayer</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) time after supper</div><b>απόδημος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόδημη, neuter απόδημο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>migrant, migratory, emigrant</div><b>απόδοση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποδόσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. imputation, attribution</div>
  <div class='def'>2. performance, yield, efficiency</div>
  <div class='def'>3. rendering, rendition, a free translation</div>
  <div class='ex'>also see μετάφραση f (metáfrasi, “translation”), ερμηνεία f (ermineía, “interpretation”)</div>
  <div class='def'>4. apodosis</div><b>απόδραση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποδράσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>escape (act of leaving a restricted facility, actual or figurative)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπόδρασις.</div><b>απόδυση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποδύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. undressing</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) carry out a difficult task</div><b>απόζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to stink, smell, smell bad</div><b>απόηχος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural απόηχοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>reverberation, echo</div><b>απόθεμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποθέματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. store, reserve (of goods)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (in plural) reserves</div>
  <div class='def'>3. deposit, savings</div>
  <div class='def'>4. deposit, sediment, silt, loess</div><b>απόθεση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποθέσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. putting down, setting down, laying down</div>
  <div class='def'>2. putting aside, saving</div>
  <div class='def'>3. deposition</div><b>απόκειμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>only used in <a href="bword://απόκειται">απόκειται</a></div><b>απόκειται</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (impersonal) to it depends upon</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (impersonal) to it&#x27;s up to</div><b>απόκεντρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόκεντρη, neuter απόκεντρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>out of the way</div><b>απόκληρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόκληρη, neuter απόκληρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. disinherited</div>
  <div class='def'>2. disinherited</div><b>απόκλιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκλίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. declination</div>
  <div class='ex'>μαγνητική <b>απόκλιση</b> - magnetic declination</div>
  <div class='def'>2. deviation</div>
  <div class='ex'>τυπική <b>απόκλιση</b> - standard deviation</div>
  <div class='def'>3. declination</div>
  <div class='def'>4. divergence</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From από- + κλίση.</div><b>απόκομμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποκόμματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. clipping, cutting, shaving (a small piece cut from a larger piece)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>απόκομμα</b> εφημερίδας - newspaper cutting</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (colloquial) weaning</div><b>απόκοντα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>closely behind, on the heels of</div><b>απόκοσμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόκοσμη, neuter απόκοσμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>uncanny, weird, unearthly, eerie</div><b>απόκοτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόκοτη, neuter απόκοτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. daring, audacious</div>
  <div class='def'>2. reckless, foolhardy</div><b>απόκρημνος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόκρημνη, neuter απόκρημνο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>steep, craggy</div>
  <div class='ex'>Δεν πρέπει να υποτιμήσουμε πόσο <b>απόκρημνο</b>, πετρώδες και δύσκολο θα είναι το μονοπάτι. - We should not underestimate just how steep, stony and difficult the path is going to be.</div><b>απόκριμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποκρίματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>secretion</div><b>απόκριση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκρίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. answer, response (to letter, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. reaction</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (rare) excretion</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀπόκρισις, from the ancient Ancient Greek ἀπόκρισις. By surface analysis, απο- (apo-, “from”) + κρίση.
For the medical sense, learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀπόκρισις from the sense &quot;excretion or secretion, separation&quot;.</div><b>απόκρουση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκρούσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. push back, repulse</div>
  <div class='def'>2. rejection (of an offer)</div><b>απόκρυφος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόκρυφη, neuter απόκρυφο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. occult</div>
  <div class='def'>2. secret, concealed</div><b>απόκρυψη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκρύψεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. hiding, concealment</div>
  <div class='def'>2. dissimulation</div><b>απόκτημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποκτήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. acquisition, addition</div>
  <div class='def'>2. purchase bargain</div><b>απόκτηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποκτήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>acquisition, addition</div><b>απόλ.</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://απόλυτος">απόλυτος</a>: cardinal</div><b>απόλαμπρα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>after Easter</div><b>απόλαυση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απολαύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. pleasure, enjoyment, delight</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (in plural) sensual pleasure</div><b>απόλεμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόλεμη, neuter απόλεμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unblooded, untried in battle</div><b>απόληξη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απολήξεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ending, termination</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>απολήξεις</b> νεύρων - nerve endings</div><b>απόληψη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απόληψεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. withdrawal (cash from bank, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. yield (of a production process)</div><b>απόλυση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απολύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>dismissal, release, discharge, layoff</div><b>απόλυτα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>absolutely, completely, altogether</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://απόλυτος">απόλυτος</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative plural of <a href="bword://απόλυτο">απόλυτο</a></div><b>απόλυτη αιθανόλη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) absolute alcohol</div><b>απόλυτο</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://απόλυτος">απόλυτος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://απόλυτος">απόλυτος</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απόλυτα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(rare) the absolute, fundamental</div><b>απόλυτο μηδέν</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) absolute zero</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το <b>απόλυτο μηδέν</b> ορίζεται ως ακριβώς −273.15 °C. - Absolute zero is defined as −273.15 °C exactly.</div><b>απόλυτοι αριθμοί</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/vocative plural of <a href="bword://απόλυτος">απόλυτος</a> <a href="bword://αριθμός">αριθμός</a></div><b>απόλυτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόλυτη, neuter απόλυτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. absolute, complete, total</div>
  <div class='def'>2. absolute</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>απόλυτο</b> μηδέν - absolute zero</div>
  <div class='def'>3. cardinal</div>
  <div class='ex'><b><b>απόλυτ</b>ος</b> αριθμός, <b>απόλυτο</b> αριθμητικό - cardinal number</div>
  <div class='def'>4. absolute (as in ablative absolute)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπόλυτος, from ἀπολύω.</div><b>απόλυτος αριθμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural απόλυτοι αριθμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>cardinal number</div><b>απόλυτου μηδενός</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>genitive of <a href="bword://απόλυτο">απόλυτο</a> <a href="bword://μηδέν">μηδέν</a></div><b>απόμακρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόμακρη, neuter απόμακρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>remote, far-off, distant</div><b>απόμαχος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόμαχη, neuter απόμαχο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. veteran, retirement</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ναυτικό Απομαχικό Ταμείο - Merchant Seamen&#x27;s Fund</div>
  <div class='def'>2. pensioner, retiree, veteran</div><b>απόμερος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόμερη, neuter απόμερο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. secluded, remote</div>
  <div class='def'>2. out of the way</div><b>απόμπευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόμπευτη, neuter απόμπευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>has not been ridiculed or pilloried</div><b>απόνερα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. wastewater</div>
  <div class='def'>2. wake (behind a ship)</div><b>απόνετος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόνετη, neuter απόνετο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. painless</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) heartless, unfeeling</div><b>απόντιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόντιστη, neuter απόντιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not submerged, unsunk</div><b>απόξενος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόξενη, neuter απόξενο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>totally alien/ foreign</div><b>απόξεση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποξέσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. abrasion, scraping</div>
  <div class='def'>2. curettage</div><b>απόξεσμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποξέσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>scrapings (material removed by scraping)</div><b>απόξυση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποξύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απόξεση">απόξεση</a></div><b>απόξω</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απέξω">απέξω</a></div><b>απόπαιδο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απόπαιδα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αποπαίδι">αποπαίδι</a></div><b>απόπασχα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>after Easter</div><b>απόπατος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural απόπατοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. toilet (room)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. latrine, earth closet, privy</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) dirty place</div><b>απόπειρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απόπειρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>attempt, try; go (informal)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Κάθε ανταγωνιστής επιτρέπεται τρεις <b>απόπειρες</b>. - Each competitor is allowed three attempts.</div><b>απόπιμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποπίματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απόπιομα">απόπιομα</a></div><b>απόπιομα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποπιόματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>remains, residuum (drink left in a glass)</div><b>απόπληκτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόπληκτη, neuter απόπληκτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>apoplectic</div><b>απόπληχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόπληχτη, neuter απόπληχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απόπληκτος">απόπληκτος</a></div><b>απόπλυμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποπλύματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. rinsings, dishwater</div>
  <div class='def'>2. pigswill, hogwash</div><b>απόπλυση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποπλύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. washing away, leaching</div>
  <div class='def'>2. rinsing</div><b>απόπνοια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) exhalation</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively, uncountable) exude</div><b>απόπτυση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποπτύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>spitting, expectoration</div><b>απόπτυσμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποπτύσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>spit, phlegm, expectoration</div><b>απόπτωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποπτώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. apoptosis</div>
  <div class='def'>2. exfoliation</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (literary) defoliation, moulting leaffall</div><b>απόρθητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόρθητη, neuter απόρθητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>impregnable, untaken, secure, invincible</div>
  <div class='ex'>το <b>απόρθητο</b> κάστρο - the impregnable castle</div><b>απόρρητο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απόρρητα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>secret</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://απόρρητος">απόρρητος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://απόρρητος">απόρρητος</a></div><b>απόρρητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόρρητη, neuter απόρρητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>secret, confidential</div>
  <div class='ex'>άκρως <b>απόρρητο</b> - top secret</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπόρρητος.</div><b>απόρριγμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απορρίγματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abortus, product of an abortion, dead foetus (UK), fetus (US)</div><b>απόρριμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απορρίματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απόρριμμα">απόρριμμα</a></div><b>απόρριμμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απορρίμματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. a piece of trash or rubbish</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (in plural) rubbish, refuse</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπόρριμμα, from ἀπορρίπτω.
Compare typologically German Ausschuss, Russian отбро́с, see απορρίμματα for more.</div><b>απόρριψη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απορρίψεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. rejection, dismissal</div>
  <div class='def'>2. fly-tipping</div>
  <div class='def'>3. jettison</div>
  <div class='def'>4. overruling</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Nominal formation from απορρίπτω.</div><b>απόρροια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απόρροιες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>consequence, outcome</div><b>απόσβεση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποσβέσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>amortisation (UK), amortization (US), payment, write-off, depreciation</div><b>απόσειση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) shaking off</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) disproving, refutation</div><b>απόσκεπος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόσκεπη, neuter απόσκεπο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>covered, protected</div><b>απόσκιο</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://απόσκιος">απόσκιος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://απόσκιος">απόσκιος</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural απόσκια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. shade, shady spot/place</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) somewhere where it is difficult to see</div><b>απόσκιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόσκια, neuter απόσκιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>shady</div><b>απόσπαση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποσπάσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>secondment, detachment</div>
  <div class='ex'>είμαι με <b>απόσπαση</b> - I&#x27;m on detachment</div><b>απόσπασμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποσπάσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. detachment, squad, detail</div>
  <div class='def'>2. excerpt, citation, quotation</div><b>απόσταγμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποστάγματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. distillate, condensate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. extract, essence</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) quintessence</div><b>απόσταμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποστάματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial, literary) weariness, tiredness, fatigue, exhaustion</div><b>απόσταξη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποστάξεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>distillation</div><b>απόσταση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποστάσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. distance (between two points)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. length (distance between the ends of an object)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. duration (time between the start and finish of an event)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀπόστασις.</div><b>απόστημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποστήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. abscess</div>
  <div class='def'>2. apothem</div><b>απόστολος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural απόστολοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>apostle (follower of Jesus Christ)</div>
  <div class='ex'>ο Απόστολος Παύλος (Paul the Apostle)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀπόστολος.</div><b>απόστρατος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απόστρατη, neuter απόστρατο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>retired, ex-service</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural απόστρατοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ex-service person, ex-serviceman</div><b>απόστροφος</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απόστροφοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>apostrophe, the character ’</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀπόστροφος, substantivised feminine of the ancient adjective with sense: &quot;turning away from, averted&quot;, from verb ἀποστρέφω. From ἀπό + στροφ- of verb στρέφω + ending -ος (-os).</div><b>απόσυρση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποσύρσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>withdrawal (an act of withdrawing: money, by an army, from sale, psychologically, etc)</div><b>απόσχιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποσχίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>secession, breakaway</div><b>απότακτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απότακτη, neuter απότακτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. cashiered, dishonorably discharged</div>
  <div class='def'>2. dismissed</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀπότακτος for which, see words ἀποτάσσσω, τακτός &amp; τάσσω</div><b>απόταξη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποτάξεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. cashiering, discharge</div>
  <div class='def'>2. dismissal, sacking</div><b>απότιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποτίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. serving (sentence)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. paying (tribute)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. paying off (debt)</div><b>απότιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απότιστη, neuter απότιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unwatered, not watered</div><b>απότοκος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απότοκη, neuter απότοκο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (figuratively) resulting from, born of</div>
  <div class='def'>2. child object</div><b>απότομα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>suddenly</div><b>απότομος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απότομη, neuter απότομο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (of cliffs) steep, sheer, abrupt</div>
  <div class='def'>2. abrupt, sudden</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (of speech) short, brusque, curt</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀπότομος, with semantic loan from French brusque.</div><b>απόφανση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποφάνσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. assertion</div>
  <div class='def'>2. court judgement</div><b>απόφαση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποφάσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>decision, ruling, verdict, judgement, resolution</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀπόφαση from Ancient Greek ᾰ̓πόφᾰσῐς, ἀπο- (apo-, “away, from, off”) + φᾰ́σῐς, from ἀποφαίνω, root verb φαίνω from Proto-Hellenic *pʰáňňō, from Proto-Indo-European *bʰeh₂- (“to shine”). Only partially cognate to Latin apophasis, English apophasis, from the identical form ᾰ̓πόφᾰσῐς, root *bʰeh₂- (“to say”) via root verb φημί.</div><b>απόφθεγμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποφθέγματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. apophthegm (UK), apothegm (US), adage, saying, maxim, aphorism</div>
  <div class='def'>2. motto</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπόφθεγμα.</div><b>απόφοιτος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural απόφοιτοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>graduate, alumnus, alumna</div><b>απόφραξη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποφράξεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>obstruction, stoppage</div><b>απόφυγα</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>rare colloquial variant of απέφυγα, first-person singular simple past of <a href="bword://αποφεύγω">αποφεύγω</a></div><b>απόφυση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποφύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. outgrowth, excrescence</div>
  <div class='def'>2. vermiform appendix</div>
  <div class='ex'>σκωληκοειδής <b>απόφυση</b> - appendix outgrowth</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀπόφυ(σις)) + -ση (-si).</div><b>απόχη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απόχες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. landing net (used in fishing)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. hand net, dip net, scoop net (used to catch small fish and invertebrates)</div><b>απόχρεμμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποχρέμματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>phlegm, spittle</div><b>απόχρεμψη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποχρέμψεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>expectoration (process, action)</div><b>απόχρωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποχρώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. colour (UK), color (US), shade of colour</div>
  <div class='def'>2. hue, tint, nuance</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀπόχρωσις + the modern suffix -ση (-si), from ἀπό- + the root underlying χρώς + -σις (-sis), with semantic loan from French coloration.</div><b>απόχτημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αποχτήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απόκτημα">απόκτημα</a></div><b>απόχτηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποχτήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απόκτηση">απόκτηση</a></div><b>απόψε</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. tonight, this evening</div>
  <div class='ex'>Θα δω τους φίλους μου <b>απόψε</b>. - I&#x27;ll see my friends tonight.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (of immediate past events) last night</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Απόψε</b>, είδα ένα πολύ τρομακτικό όνειρο. - I had a very frightening dream last night.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀπ’ ὀψέ.</div><b>απόψυξη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αποψύξεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>defrosting, deicing, thawing</div>
  <div class='ex'>αυτόματη <b>απόψυξη</b> - automatic defrosting</div><b>απύθμενος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απύθμενη, neuter απύθμενο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abysmal, bottomless</div><b>απύλωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απύλωτη, neuter απύλωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(figuratively) gateless (of a chatterbox)</div>
  <div class='ex'>έχει <b>απύλωτο</b> στόμα - he has a loose tongue</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπύλωτος</div><b>απύραυλος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απύραυλη, neuter απύραυλο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>missile free</div><b>απύρετος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απύρετη, neuter απύρετο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>feverless, apyretic</div><b>απύρηνος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απύρηνη, neuter απύρηνο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (of fruit, etc) without seed, stone, etc</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (of a cell) anucleate (without a nucleus)</div><b>απύρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απύρωτη, neuter απύρωτ)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fireproof</div><b>απώθηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απωθήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. repulsion, repulse, repression</div>
  <div class='def'>2. repulsion</div><b>απώλεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural απώλειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>loss (of an object)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Όσο πιο σημαντική είναι η <b>απώλεια</b>, τόσο πιο έντονο είναι το πένθος. - The more significant the loss, the more intense the mourning.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀπώλεια.</div><b>απώλητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απώλητη, neuter απώλητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unsold</div><b>απών</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απούσα, neuter απόν)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>absent</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek, the present participle ἀπών of the verb ἄπειμι &quot;I am absent&quot;.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural απόντες, feminine απούσα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>absentee</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek, the present participle ἀπών of the verb ἄπειμι &quot;I am absent&quot;.</div><b>απώτατος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απώτατη, neuter απώτατο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>most distant: farthest, remotest</div><b>απώτερος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine απώτερη, neuter απώτερο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>farther, ulterior, remoter</div><b>αρά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(literary) curse</div><b>αράγιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αράγιστη, neuter αράγιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. uncracked (china, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) solid, reliable, unbreakable</div><b>αράδα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>one after another (continuously or non-stop)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Γεννούσε <b>αράδα</b> παιδιά. - She was having babies one after the other.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Etymology unknown.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αράδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. line, queue (straight sequence of people or objects)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Υπήρχαν δύο <b>αράδες</b> γι’ αυτούς που πλήρωσαν και γι’ αυτούς που αγόραζαν εισιτήριο στην πόρτα. - There were two queues, for those that paid and for those buying a ticket at the door.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) place, spot (in a line or queue)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Φίλε, που πας; Κάτσε στην <b>αράδα</b> σου! - Where are you going, mate? Stay in your spot / get back in line!</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Etymology unknown.</div><b>αράδιασμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αραδιάσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. lining up, arranging in rows</div>
  <div class='def'>2. marshalling, heaping up</div><b>αράζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to anchor, moor</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το πλοίο <b>άραξε</b> στο λιμάνι. - The ship docked at the harbour.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (colloquial) to park</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Άραχ’</b> το αυτοκίνητο να πάμε να πιούμε κανέναν καφέ. - Park the car and let&#x27;s go for a coffee.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (colloquial) to lie down and relax at one place, stay at one place for long</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Αράζω</b> στον καναπέ και βλέπω τηλεόραση. - I lie on the couch and watch television.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀράζω form the Ancient Greek ἀράσσω from past tense: ‑αξα to present: ‑άζω, in the pattern of στάζω, ἔσταξα.</div><b>αράθυμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αράθυμη, neuter αράθυμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>irritable, tetchy</div><b>αράντιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αράντιστη, neuter αράντιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unsprinkled, unsprayed</div><b>αράπης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αράπηδες, feminine αραπίνα or αράπισσα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (colloquial, ethnic, offensive, slur) nigger (black person)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ήταν ένας <b>αράπης</b> στην παραλία που πούλαγε CD. - There was a nigger selling CDs on the beach.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (archaic, colloquial, ethnic, slur) Arab</div>
  <div class='def'>3. A type of supernatural boogeyman-type being that appears in several forms: as a guardian of households who enriches the owner (but eats greedy persons); as a dark guardian of hidden treasures; or as a brawny opponent to the hero of the story, whom Arapis serves after he is defeated by him. Often used in previous times to scare small children</div>
  <div class='ex'>Φάε το φαΐ σου, γιατί θα φωνάξω τον <b>αράπη</b>! - Eat your food or I&#x27;ll call Arapis!</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from Ottoman Turkish عرب (Arap), from Arabic عَرَب (ʕarab).</div><b>αράπικα φιστίκια</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>plural of αράπικο <a href="bword://φιστίκι">φιστίκι</a></div><b>αράπικο φιστίκι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αράπικα φιστίκια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>peanut</div><b>αράπικος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αράπικη, neuter αράπικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(offensive) Arab, negro</div><b>αράπισσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αράπισσες, masculine αράπης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(offensive) female nigger</div><b>αράχνη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αράχνες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. spider (predatory arthropod of the order Araneae)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) cobweb, spiderweb</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀράχνη.</div><b>αρένα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρένες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. arena</div>
  <div class='def'>2. bullring</div><b>αρέσκεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) liking, satisfaction</div><b>αρέσκω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αρέσω">αρέσω</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ᾰ̓ρέσκω.</div><b>αρέσω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(intransitive) to be liked by somebody, to be pleasing to someone.</div>
  <div class='ex'>Μου αρέσει το παγωτό<b></b> - I like ice cream ~ Ice cream pleases me.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀρέσω, from Ancient Greek ᾰ̓ρέσκω.</div><b>αρίγωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρίγωτη, neuter αρίγωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unlined, unruled (paper, &amp;c)</div><b>αρίδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρίδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. drill, auger, bit</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (humorous) leg/foot</div><b>αρίθμηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αριθμήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. counting, numeration</div>
  <div class='def'>2. numbering, pagination</div><b>αρίστευση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αριστεύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>superb performance, high achievement</div><b>αρίφνητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρίφνητη, neuter αρίφνητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(literary) countless, innumerable</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀρίφνητος, from Byzantine Greek ἀναρίφνητος, from Ancient Greek ἀναρίθμητος replacing consonant cluster [θm] with [fn] and the prefix ἀνα- (ana-) with ἀ- (a-).</div><b>αραίωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αραιώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>thinning out, dilution, watering</div><b>αραίωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αραίωσες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>thinning out, dilution, watering</div><b>αραβίδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αραβίδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>rifle</div><b>αραβικά</b>
