  <div class='def'>1. oxcart</div>
  <div class='def'>2. araba (Eastern Mediterranean horsedrawn carriage)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (humorous) a very slow vehicle or other land-based mode of transportation</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ottoman Turkish عربه (araba, “two-wheeled carriage”), of ultimately unknown origin. See Turkish araba (“car, carriage”) for further discussion on etymology.</div><b>αραμπατζής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αραμπατζήδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>carter, cart owner</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from Ottoman Turkish عربهجی.</div><b>αραξοβόλι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αραξοβόλια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. anchorage, harbour, haven, cove</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) refuge</div><b>αραούγια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αραούγιες)</i></div>
