  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from translingual Araujia.</div><b>αραπίνα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αραπίνες, masculine αράπης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (colloquial, ethnic, slur) negress, nigger (black woman)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (archaic, colloquial, ethnic, slur) Arab woman</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ottoman Turkish عرب (arab,arap, “Arab”), from Arabic عَرَب (ʕarab).</div><b>αραπιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (colloquial) Arabia, the Arab countries, their peoples</div>
