  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αραβόσιτος">αραβόσιτος</a>: maize</div><b>αραποσίτι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αραποσίτια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αραβόσιτος">αραβόσιτος</a> (sweet corn)</div><b>αραποσιτιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αραποσιτιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>maize plant</div><b>αραποσυκιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αραποσυκιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>prickly pear (plant)</div><b>αραπόσταρο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αραπόσταρα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αραποσίταρο">αραποσίταρο</a></div><b>αραχνίδια</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>The Arachnida.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Calque of translingual Arachnida.</div><b>αραχνιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αραχνιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>cobweb, spiderweb (web spun by a spider)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η σοφίτα είναι γεμάτη <b>αραχνιές</b>. - The attic is full of cobwebs.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αράχνη + -ιά.</div><b>αραχνιάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (intransitive) to become covered in cobwebs, fill with cobwebs (usually through disuse or abandonment)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το σπίτι έμεινε άδειο τον χειμώνα και <b>αράχνιασε</b>. - The house stayed empty during the winter and filled with cobwebs.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to become dull, become boring, have enough of</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Αραχνιάσαμε</b> μέσα στο σπίτι. Πάμε βόλτα! - We&#x27;ve had enough of being in the house. Let&#x27;s go for a walk!</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀραχνιάζω, from Ancient Greek ἀραχνιόω, ἀραχνιῶ) + -άζω.</div><b>αραχνιασμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αραχνιασμένη, neuter αραχνιασμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (literally) covered with cobwebs, full of cobwebs</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η αποθήκη είναι γεμάτη μούχλα κι <b>αραχνιασμένη</b>. - The cellar is full of mould and covered with cobwebs.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively, idiomatic) out-of-date, outdated</div>
  <div class='ex'>Δυστυχώς, ο παππούς μου είναι γεμάτος <b>αραχνιασμένες</b> απόψεις. - Unfortunately, my grandfather is full of outdated opinions.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect passive participle of αραχνιάζω, a verb with no passive forms.</div><b>αραχνοΰφαντος</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. finely spun or woven, diaphanous, like gossamer</div>
  <div class='def'>2. flimsy</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> By surface analysis, αράχνη + υφαίνω + -τος (-tos), literally “spiderwoven”.</div><b>αραχνοειδής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αραχνοειδής, neuter αραχνοειδές)</i></div>
