  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρμαντίλλα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>armadillo</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from Spanish armadillo, diminutive of armado (“armored”), in reference to its protective plates.</div><b>αρμαντίλο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρμαντίλα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αρμαντίλλο">αρμαντίλλο</a> (armadillo)</div><b>αρματαγωγά πλοία</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>plural of <a href="bword://αρματαγωγό">αρματαγωγό</a> <a href="bword://πλοίο">πλοίο</a></div><b>αρματαγωγό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρματαγωγά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>landing craft for tanks</div><b>αρματαγωγό πλοίο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρματαγωγά πλοία)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>landing craft for tanks</div><b>αρματηλάτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρματηλάτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>charioteer</div><b>αρματηλασία</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρματηλασίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>charioteering</div><b>αρματικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρματική, neuter αρματικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>armoured (UK), armored (US)</div><b>αρματοδρομία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρματοδρομίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>chariot race, chariot racing</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἁρματοδρομία</div><b>αρματοδρόμος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρματοδρόμοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>charioteer</div><b>αρματολίκι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρματολίκια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (historical) a region protected from outlaws armatoli in Ottoman times.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (historical) a unit of armatoli</div><b>αρματολός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρματολοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>armatole, man-at-arms (under Ottoman rule)</div><b>αρματομαχία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρματομαχί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>tank battle</div><b>αρματωλός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρματωλοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αρματολός">αρματολός</a></div><b>αρματωμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αρματωμένη, neuter αρματωμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>armed</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αρματώνομαι, passive voice of αρματώνω</div><b>αρματωσιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρματωσιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. armour (UK), armor (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. rigging, gear</div><b>αρματώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to arm, equip</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to fit out (a ship)</div><b>αρμενίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (intransitive) to sail (to travel aross water)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (of the mind) to wander</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek αρμενίζω. By surface analysis, άρμεν(ο)) + -ίζω.</div><b>αρμενικά</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Armenian (the language of Armenia and its people)</div><b>αρμενικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρμενική, neuter αρμενικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Armenian (relating to Armenia or its people or language)</div><b>αρμεξιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρμεξιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(dialectal, regional) the product of a milking</div><b>αρμογή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρμογές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>joint, connection</div><b>αρμοδίως</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (formal) competently</div>
  <div class='ex'>Δε μπορώ να μιλήσω <b>αρμοδίως</b> σ’ αυτό το θέμα. - I cannot speak competently on this matter.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (formal) from/by the powers that be, from/by the authorities</div>
  <div class='ex'>Δηλώθηκε <b>αρμοδίως</b> ότι τα σχολεία θα κλείσουν. - It was stated by the powers that be that the schools will close.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἁρμοδίως.</div><b>αρμοδιότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρμοδιότητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. province, domain, competence, purview (power or right to exercise authority)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Αυτό το ζήτημα είναι εκτός της <b>αρμοδιότητάς</b> μου. - This issue is outside of my domain.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. jurisdiction, competence (legal authority to deal with a matter)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το δικαστήριο δεν έχει <b>αρμοδιότητα</b> να εκδικάσει την υπόθεση. - The court does not have the jurisdiction to try the case.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἁρμοδιότης, equivalent to αρμόδιος + -ότητα.</div><b>αρμοκάλυπτο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρμοκάλυπτα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αρμοκάλυπτρο">αρμοκάλυπτρο</a></div><b>αρμοκάλυπτρο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρμοκάλυπτρα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. decorative trim or moulding:; casing bead</div>
  <div class='def'>2. decorative trim or moulding:; bead, beading, moulding</div><b>αρμολογώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to point, to joint</div><b>αρμολόγημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρμολογήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αρμολόγηση">αρμολόγηση</a></div><b>αρμολόγηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρμολογήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>pointing, jointing, grouting (act and effect)</div><b>αρμονία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρμονίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. harmony, accord</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unity, concord, symmetry</div>
  <div class='def'>3. harmony, tune</div><b>αρμονικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρμονική, neuter αρμονικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. harmonious</div>
  <div class='ex'>Οι βιολιστές παράγουν αρμονικούς ήχους.<b></b> - The violinists produce a harmonius sound.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. symmetrical</div>
  <div class='def'>3. harmonic</div>
  <div class='ex'>απλή <b>αρμονική</b> ταλάντωση - simple harmonic motion</div><b>αρμονικότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρμονικότητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>harmoniousness</div><b>αρμοστής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρμοστές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. governor, commissioner</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ύπατος <b>Aρμοστής</b> των HΕ - High Commissioner of the UN</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (historical) harmost (Sparta)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἁρμοστής</div><b>αρμοστεία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρμοστείες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. governorship, commissionership (office, position)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. residency (building)</div><b>αρμπαρόρριζα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρμπαρόρριζες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sweet-scented pelargonium</div><b>αρμπεντές</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρμπεντέδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. racket, commotion</div>
  <div class='def'>2. revolution</div>
  <div class='def'>3. massacre, slaughter</div>
  <div class='ex'>ο μεγάλος <b>αρμπεντές</b> - the great massacre</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from Ottoman Turkish عربده (ʼarbede).</div><b>αρμπουρέτο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρμπουρέτα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>topmast</div><b>αρμυρήθρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρμυρήθρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>samphire, glasswort (Salicornia europaea)</div><b>αρμυρίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αλμυρίζω">αλμυρίζω</a></div><b>αρμυρίκι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρμυρίκια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αλμυρίκι">αλμυρίκι</a></div><b>αρμυρούτσικος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρμυρούτσικη, neuter αρμυρούτσικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αλμυρούτσικος">αλμυρούτσικος</a></div><b>αρμυρός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρμυρή, neuter αρμυρό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αλμυρός">αλμυρός</a></div><b>αρμόδιοι</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. nominative masculine singular of <a href="bword://αρμόδιος">αρμόδιος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. vocative masculine plural of <a href="bword://αρμόδιος">αρμόδιος</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>powers that be (holders of power or the authorities in a given situation)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Οι <b>αρμόδιοι</b> δεν ενδιαφέρονται για τους φτωχούς. - The powers that be don&#x27;t care about the poor.</div><b>αρμόδιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρμόδια, neuter αρμόδιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>qualified (by an authority to judge, decide, or handle a situation)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Δεν είμαι <b>αρμόδιος</b> να κρίνω. - I&#x27;m not qualified to judge.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἁρμόδιος, from ἁρμόζω. Also substantivised.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρμόδιοι, feminine αρμόδια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>in charge, responsible (answerable for an act performed or for its consequences)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ποιος είναι ο <b>αρμόδιος</b> για την ασφάλεια; - Who is the Director/Assistant/Chief for safety?</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἁρμόδιος, from ἁρμόζω. Also substantivised.</div><b>αρμόζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to be proper, to suit, to befit, to be suitable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to fit</div><b>αρμόνικα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρμόνικες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>harmonica; mouth organ</div><b>αρμόνιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρμόνια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. harmonium</div>
  <div class='def'>2. organ</div><b>αρμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. joint, union</div>
  <div class='def'>2. seam</div>
  <div class='def'>3. gap</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἁρμός.</div><b>αρμύρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρμύρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αλμύρα">αλμύρα</a></div>
  <div class='ex'>Σκέπασε <b>αρμύρα</b> το γυμνό κορμί σου,
Σου ’φερα απ’ τους Δελφούς γλυκό νερό. - Your naked body was covered with salt,
I brought you fresh water from Delphi.</div><b>αρνάδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρνάδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>female lamb</div><b>αρνήτρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρνήτριες, masculine αρνητής)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>denier, denialist, negationist, refusenik, rejecter</div><b>αρνί</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρνιά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. lamb (farm animal or meat)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) meek or gentle person</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀρνί(ν)), from Ancient Greek ἀρνίον, diminutive or hypocoristic form of ἀρήν, from Proto-Hellenic *warḗn, from *wr̥h₁ḗn (“lamb”). Cognate with Mariupol Greek арны́.</div><b>αρνίσιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρνίσια, neuter αρνίσιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>lamb</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το προϊόν έχει κατασκευαστεί με φυσικό 90% <b>αρνίσιο</b> μαλλί. - The product is made with 90% natural lamb&#x27;s wool.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αρνί + -ίσιος.</div><b>αρνησίθεος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ήη)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. atheist</div>
  <div class='def'>2. atheist</div><b>αρνησίθρησκος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρνησίθρησκοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>apostate, renegade</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρνησίθρησκη, neuter αρνησίθρησκο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>apostatical</div><b>αρνησίπατρι</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>accusative/vocative singular of <a href="bword://αρνησίπατρις">αρνησίπατρις</a></div><b>αρνησίπατρις</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρνησιπάτριδες, feminine αρνησιπατρία)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>renegade/traitor: someone who denies/renounces their nationality or homeland</div><b>αρνησιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρνησιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. oblivion, forgetfulness</div>
  <div class='def'>2. rejection, abandonment</div><b>αρνησιδικία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρνησιδικίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>denial of justice</div><b>αρνησιθρησκία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρνησιθρησκίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>apostasy</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αρνησι- (arnisi-) + θρησκεία</div><b>αρνησιθρησκεία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρνησιθρησκείες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αρνησιθρησκία">αρνησιθρησκία</a></div><b>αρνησικυρία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρνησικυρίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>veto</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αρνησι- (arnisi-) + κυρία</div><b>αρνησιπατρία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρνησιπατρίες, masculine αρνησίπατρις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>renegade/traitor: someone who denies/renounces their nationality or homeland</div><b>αρνητ.</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://αρνητικός">αρνητικός</a>: negative, undesirable, disapproving</div><b>αρνητής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρνητές, feminine αρνήτρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>denier, denialist, negationist, refusenik, rejecter</div><b>αρνητικά</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αρνητικός">αρνητικός</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>negatively</div><b>αρνητικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρνητική, neuter αρνητικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. disapproving, undesirable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (negative) negative</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀρνητικός. The contemporary scientific senses are a semantic loan from French négatif.</div><b>αρνητισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρνητισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>negativism, negativity</div><b>αρνιέμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αρνούμαι">αρνούμαι</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from the mediaeval Byzantine Greek ἀρνιέμαι.</div><b>αρνιούμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αρνούμαι">αρνούμαι</a></div><b>αρνούμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to deny, reject, turn down</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀρνοῦμαι, contractive form of ἀρνέομαι. The variant αρνιέμαι, inherited from the mediaeval ἀρνιέμαι.</div><b>αροτριώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to plough (UK), plow (US), till, cultivate</div><b>αροτριώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αροτριώ">αροτριώ</a></div><b>αρουραίος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρουραίοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. rat (rodent)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) mouse, vole</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) devious and evil person</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀρουραῖος, via the phrase ἀρουραῖος μῦς, with the adjective adopting the core &quot;rodent&quot; sense via linguistic ellipsis, similar to the process seen with ποντίκι.</div><b>αρπάγη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρπάγες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. hook, grappling iron, grasping tool</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αρπάγη</b> του Αρχιμήδη - the claw of Archimedes</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) grip</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἁρπάγη.</div><b>αρπάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to snatch, grab, steal</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to whisk away</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to catch hold of</div>
  <div class='def'>4. to quarrel easily</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἁρπάζω.</div><b>αρπάχνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αρπάζω">αρπάζω</a></div><b>αρπάχτρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρπάχτρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>grabber, snatcher (a grasping ot predatory person)</div><b>αρπίστας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρπίστες, feminine αρπίστρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>harpist, harper</div><b>αρπίστρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρπίστριες, masculine αρπιστής or αρπίστας)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>harpist, harper</div><b>αρπίχορδο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρπίχορδα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>harpsichord</div><b>αρπα-κόλλα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>willy-nilly</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) slapdash work</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (slang, uncountable) cut and paste work</div><b>αρπαγή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρπαγές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. plundering, theft, looting</div>
  <div class='def'>2. plunder, booty, loot</div>
  <div class='def'>3. abduction (the wrongful, and usually forcible, carrying off of a human being)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἁρπαγή.</div><b>αρπακολλατζής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρπακολλατζήδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial) a sloppy, slipshod worker</div><b>αρπακτικό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρπακτικά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. bird of prey</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) predator</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἅρπα.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://αρπακτικός">αρπακτικός</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://αρπακτικός">αρπακτικός</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἅρπα.</div><b>αρπακτικό πτηνό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρπακτικά πτηνά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>bird of prey</div><b>αρπακτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρπακτική, neuter αρπακτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>predatory, rapacious</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἅρπα.</div><b>αρπακτικότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) rapacity, ravening, predacity, predatoriness</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἅρπα: αρπακτικός + -ότητα. First attested 1881.</div><b>αρπακόλλα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of αρπα-<a href="bword://κόλλα">κόλλα</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. alternative form of αρπα-<a href="bword://κόλλα">κόλλα</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. genitive singular of αρπακόλλας</div><b>αρπαχτά</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>hurriedly, in haste</div><b>αρπιστής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρπιστές, feminine αρπίστρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>harpist, harper</div><b>αρρίζωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρρίζωτη, neuter αρρίζωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. rootless, unrooted (plant)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) rootless, ungrounded</div><b>αρραβωνιάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (transitive) to engage, betroth, affiance</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to pledge</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀρραβωνίζω, from Ancient Greek ἀρραβών.</div><b>αρραβωνιάρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρραβωνιάρες, masculine αρραβωνιάρης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fiancée, betrothed, intended</div><b>αρραβωνιάρης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρραβωνιάρης, feminine αρραβωνιάρα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fiancé, betrothed, intended</div><b>αρραβωνιαστικιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρραβωνιαστικιές, masculine αρραβωνιαστικός)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fiancée</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Feminine form of αρραβωνιαστικός.</div><b>αρραβωνιαστικός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρραβωνιαστικοί, feminine αρραβωνιαστικιά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fiancé, betrothed, intended</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αρραβώνας.</div><b>αρραβώνας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρραβώνες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. betrothal (promise of marriage)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. engagement ring</div>
  <div class='def'>3. pledge</div>
  <div class='def'>4. deposit, earnest money</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀρραβών, itself from Biblical Hebrew עירבון / עֵרָבוֹן.</div><b>αρραβώνιασμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρραβωνιάσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. engagement, betrothal</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (in plural) betrothal ceremony</div><b>αρραγής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρραγής, neuter αρραγές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unbreakable</div><b>αρρεβωνιάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αρραβωνιάζω">αρραβωνιάζω</a></div><b>αρρενογονία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρρενογονίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>male birth (used mainly in phrases)</div><b>αρρενοπρέπεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρρενοπρέπειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>masculinity, virility</div><b>αρρενοπρεπής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρρενοπρεπής, neuter αρρενοπρεπές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>manly, virile, masculine</div><b>αρρενωπά</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αρρενωπός">αρρενωπός</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>in a manly fashion, virilely</div><b>αρρενωπός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρρενωπή, neuter αρρενωπό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>manly, virile, masculine</div><b>αρρενωπότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρρενωπότητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>masculinity</div><b>αρριβίστας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρριβίστες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αριβίστας">αριβίστας</a></div><b>αρριβιστής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρριβιστές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αριβίστας">αριβίστας</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From French arriviste.</div><b>αρρυθμία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρρυθμίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. absence of rhythm, absence of symmetry</div>
  <div class='def'>2. arrhythmia, cardiac dysrhythmia</div><b>αρρυμοτόμητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρρυμοτόμητη, neuter αρρυμοτόμητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αρυμοτόμητος">αρυμοτόμητος</a></div><b>αρρυμούλκητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρρυμούλκητη, neuter αρρυμούλκητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>untowed, not towed</div><b>αρρυτίδωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρρυτίδωτη, neuter αρρυτίδωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unwrinkled, unlined</div>
  <div class='def'>2. fresh (complexion)</div><b>αρρωσταίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to become ill</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to sicken, get sick</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> άρρωστος + -αίνω</div><b>αρρωστημένα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>in a sickly manner</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αρρωστημένος">αρρωστημένος</a></div><b>αρρωστημένος</b>
  <div><i>verb, masculine (feminine αρρωστημένη, neuter αρρωστημένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. beyond normal, healthy boundaries, pervert</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το <b>αρρωστημένο</b> του μυαλό, η <b>αρρωστημένη</b> του φαντασία, τον οδήγησαν στο έγκλημα. - His sick mind, his sick imagination, led him to the crime.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (rare) sick</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (of plants) sickly</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect passive participle of αρρωσταίνω or αρρωστώ, a verb without passive voice forms.</div><b>αρρωστιάρης</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρρωστιάρα, neuter αρρωστιάρικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sickly, weak, ailing, wan, unhealthy</div><b>αρρωστιάρικος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρρωστιάρικη, neuter αρρωστιάρικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sickly, weak, ailing, wan, unhealthy</div><b>αρρωστομανής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρρωστομανής, neuter αρρωστομανές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>suffering from nosomania</div><b>αρρωστομανία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αρρωστομανίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) nosomania</div><b>αρρωστώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αρρωσταίνω">αρρωσταίνω</a></div><b>αρρύθμιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρρύθμιστη, neuter αρρύθμιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unregulated, irregular, not arranged</div>
  <div class='def'>2. untuned</div><b>αρρύπαντος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρρύπαντη, neuter αρρύπαντο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. pure, undefiled, unsoiled</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) flawless</div><b>αρρώστια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρρώστιες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>malady, sickness, illness, disease</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀρρωστία.</div><b>αρσ.</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://αρσενικός">αρσενικός</a>: masculine</div><b>αρσακειάδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρσακειάδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. a student of Arsakeio</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) excessively modest</div><b>αρσενικοθήλυκος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρσενικοθήλυκη, neuter αρσενικοθήλυκο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. hermaphrodite</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) having contradictory properties</div><b>αρσενικό</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. inflection of <a href="bword://αρσενικός">αρσενικός</a>:; neuter nominative/accusative/vocative singular</div>
  <div class='def'>2. inflection of <a href="bword://αρσενικός">αρσενικός</a>:; masculine accusative singular</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> See the etymology of the corresponding lemma form.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) arsenic</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀρσενικόν.</div><b>αρσενικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρσενική or αρσενικιά, neuter αρσενικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>masculine</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀρσενικός.</div><b>αρσενοκοίτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρσενοκοίτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. sodomite</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) gay man, pederast</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀρσενοκοίτης.</div><b>αρσιβαρίστας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρσιβαρίστες, feminine αρσιβαρίστρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>weightlifter</div><b>αρσιβαρίστρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρσιβαρίστριες, masculine αρσιβαρίστας)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>weightlifter</div><b>αρτέμονας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρτέμονες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>jib</div><b>αρτίδιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρτίδια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>bread roll, roll, bun</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀρτίδιον, diminutive of ἄρτος. By surface analysis, άρτος + -ίδιο.</div><b>αρτίστας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρτίστες, feminine αρτίστα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>artist, performer</div><b>αρτίωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αρτιώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) perfection, refinement (the action or result)</div><b>αρταίνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to break your fast</div><b>αρταίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to eat forbidden food during a religious fast</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to stop fasting</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to make food more tasty</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Ultimately from Ancient Greek ἀρτύω, related to ἀραρίσκω.</div><b>αρτεμισία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρτεμισίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>artemisia (genus of aromatic flowering plants)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀρτεμισία, from Ἄρτεμις.</div><b>αρτεργάτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρτεργάτες, feminine αρτεργάτρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>bakery worker, baker</div><b>αρτεργάτρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρτεργάτριες, masculine αρτεργάτης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>bakery worker, baker</div><b>αρτεσιανά φρέατα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>plural of αρτεσιανό <a href="bword://φρέαρ">φρέαρ</a></div><b>αρτεσιανό φρέαρ</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρτεσιανά φρέατα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>artesian well</div><b>αρτεσιανός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρτεσιανή, neuter αρτεσιανό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. artesian</div>
  <div class='def'>2. artesian spring/well</div><b>αρτζι-μπούρτζι</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. topsy-turvy, higgledy-piggledy, disordered</div>
  <div class='def'>2. without logic</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀρτζιβούριος, borrowed from Old Armenian առաջաւորաց (պահք), “pre-lenten fast”), from առաջաւոր, whence also Old Georgian ალაჯორი.</div><b>αρτζιμπούρτζι</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of αρτζι-μπούρτζι</div><b>αρτηρία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρτηρίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. artery (blood vessel)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) arterial or main road</div>
  <div class='ex'>H πόλη έχει τρεις βασικές οδικές <b>αρτηρίες</b>. - The city has three arterial roads.</div><b>αρτηριακός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρτηριακή, neuter αρτηριακό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>arterial</div><b>αρτηριοπάθεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αρτηριοπάθειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) arteriopathy</div><b>αρτηριοσκλήρυνση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αρτηριοσκληρύνσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) arteriosclerosis</div><b>αρτηριοσκλήρωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αρτηριοσκληρώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) arteriosclerosis</div><b>αρτηριοσκληρωτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρτηριοσκληρωτική, neuter αρτηριοσκληρωτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>arteriosclerotic</div><b>αρτιγέννητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρτιγέννητη, neuter αρτιγέννητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. newborn, newly born</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) newly formed</div><b>αρτιγενής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρτιγενής, neuter αρτιγενές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. newborn, newly born</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) newly formed, newly created, nascent</div><b>αρτιμέλεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρτιμέλειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fitness</div><b>αρτιμελής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρτιμελής, neuter αρτιμελές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>able-bodied, sound of limb</div><b>αρτισύστατος</b>
