  <div class='def'>completeness, wholeness</div><b>αρτιώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to complete, to perfect, to accomplish</div><b>αρτοβιομηχανία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αρτοβιομηχανίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) bread making industry</div><b>αρτοκλασία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αρτοκλασίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) breaking bread</div><b>αρτοποίηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αρτοποιήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) breadmaking</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀρτοποίησις. By surface analysis, άρτος + ποίηση.</div><b>αρτοποιΐα</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αρτοποιία">αρτοποιία</a></div><b>αρτοποιία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αρτοποιίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable, usually) bread making</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable, usually) bakery</div><b>αρτοποιείο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρτοποιεία)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>bakery, baker&#x27;s shop</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> άρτος + -ποιείο</div><b>αρτοποιητής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρτοποιητείς)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>breadmaker (person or machine)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀρτοποιητής. By surface analysis, αρτοποίηση + -τής.</div><b>αρτοποιός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural αρτοποιοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>baker</div><b>αρτοπωλείο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρτοπωλεία)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>bakery, bread shop</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> άρτος + πωλώ + -είο</div><b>αρτοπώλης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρτοπώλες, feminine αρτοπώλισσα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>baker</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἄρτος.</div><b>αρτοπώλισσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρτοπώλισσες, feminine αρτοπώλης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>baker</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἄρτος.</div><b>αρτοσκεύασμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρτοσκευάσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. item produced by baker</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (plural normally) pastries, bakery products</div><b>αρτοφόριο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρτοφόριες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>pyx, tabernacle, monstrance</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀρτοφόριον</div><b>αρτυμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρτυμένη, neuter αρτυμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. non-fasting (food not eaten during a fast)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. non-fasting (of a person who is not fasting)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αρταίνομαι, passive voice of αρταίνω</div><b>αρτύζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αρταίνω">αρταίνω</a></div><b>αρτύνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αρταίνω">αρταίνω</a></div><b>αρτύσιμος</b>
