  <div class='def'>2. chief butler</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (historical) symposiarch</div><b>αρχιφύλακας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρχιφύλακες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>a non-commissioned officer (a sergeant) in the police</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αρχι- (archi-) + φύλακας.</div><b>αρχιχρονιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αρχιχρονιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) New Year&#x27;s Day (first day of a year)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Traditional song, Κάλαντα Πρωτοχρονιάς
Αρχιμηνιά κι αρχιχρονιά
ψηλή μου δεντρολιβάνια
Month&#x27;s beginning and year&#x27;s beginning
my tall rosemary</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αρχι- (archi-, “start”) + χρονιά.</div><b>αρχιψάλτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρχιψάλτες, feminine αρχιψάλτρια)</i></div>
