  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρχοντικά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. the house of the lord, manor house</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) mansion</div><b>αρχοντικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρχοντική, neuter αρχοντικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>aristocratic, noble, lordly</div><b>αρχοντογυναίκα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρχοντογυναίκες, masculine αρχοντάνθρωπος)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>gentlewoman</div><b>αρχοντολόι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρχοντολόι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>the nobility</div><b>αρχοντοξεπεσμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρχοντοξεπεσμένη, neuter αρχοντοξεπεσμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>genteel and poor, shabbily genteel</div><b>αρχοντοπιάνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to put on airs, to have genteel pretensions</div><b>αρχοντοπούλα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρχοντοπούλες, masculine αρχοντόπουλο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>young noblewoman, aristocrat&#x27;s daughter</div><b>αρχοντοχωριάτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρχοντοχωριάτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. a nouveau riche, snob</div>
  <div class='def'>2. country squire</div><b>αρχοντόπουλο</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρχοντόπουλα, feminine αρχοντοπούλα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>young nobleman, aristocrat&#x27;s son</div><b>αρχοντόσπιτο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρχοντόσπιτα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. noble family, wealthy family</div>
  <div class='def'>2. country house</div>
  <div class='def'>3. mansion</div><b>αρχόμενος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρχόμενη, neuter αρχόμενο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>incipient</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αρχόμενο</b> έκλος - incipient ulcer</div><b>αρχόντισσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρχόντισσες, masculine άρχοντας)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. ruler, noblewoman</div>
  <div class='def'>2. magistrate</div>
  <div class='def'>3. rich woman</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From άρχοντας + -ισσα (-issa), ultimately from Ancient Greek ἄρχων.</div><b>αρχύτερα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(in phrase) earlier</div>
  <div class='ex'>μια ώρα <b>αρχύτερα</b> - one hour earlier</div><b>αρωγή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρωγές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>aid, help, assistance, relief</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀρωγή</div><b>αρωγός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρωγοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>aider, helper</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀρωγός.</div><b>αρωματίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (transitive) to (add) scent, perfume</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to flavour (UK), flavor (US)</div><b>αρωματικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρωματική, neuter αρωματικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. perfumed, scented</div>
  <div class='def'>2. aromatic</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το βενζόλιο είναι <b>αρωματική</b> οργανική ένωση. - Benzene is an aromatic organic compound.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. aromatic (flavourful substance)</div><b>αρωματοποιΐα</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αρωματοποιία">αρωματοποιία</a></div><b>αρωματοποιία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρωματοποιίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>perfumery (action, craft and industry)</div><b>αρωματοποιός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρωματοποιοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>perfumer (perfume maker)</div><b>αρωματοπωλείο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αρωματοπωλεία)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>perfume shop</div><b>αρωματοπώλης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αρωματοπώλες, feminine αρωματοπώλισσα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>perfumer (seller)</div><b>αρωματοπώλισσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αρωματοπώλισσες, masculine αρωματοπώλης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>perfumer (seller)</div><b>αρωματώδης</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρωματώδης, neuter αρωματώδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>perfumed, scented</div><b>αρόσιμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρόσιμη, neuter αρόσιμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>arable, cultivable, tillable</div><b>αρύπαντος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρύπαντη, neuter αρύπαντο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αρρύπαντος">αρρύπαντος</a></div><b>αρύς</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αριά, neuter αρύ)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sparse, rare</div><b>αρώτητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αρώτητη, neuter αρώτητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unasked</div><b>ασ&#x27;</b>
  <div><i>prep</i></div>
  <div class='def'>contraction of άσε</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Άσ’</b> την ήσυχη. - Leave her alone.</div><b>ασάλευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασάλευτη, neuter ασάλευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. still, firm, stationary, unmoved</div>
  <div class='def'>2. immovable</div><b>ασάλιωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασάλιωτη, neuter ασάλιωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not salivating</div><b>ασάρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασάρωτη, neuter ασάρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unswept</div><b>ασάφεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural ασάφειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) vagueness, ambiguity</div><b>ασέβεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ασέβειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. disrespect, disrespectfulness, contempt, impiety, impiousness</div>
  <div class='ex'>Του επιβλήθηκε πρόστιμο για <b>ασέβεια</b> προς το δικαστήριο. - He was fined for contempt of court.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. impiety</div>
  <div class='def'>3. an insulting behaviour or word</div>
  <div class='ex'>Αυτό που είπες ήταν μεγάλη <b>ασέβεια</b>, ντροπή σου! - What you said was a huge insult, shame on you!</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ᾰ̓σέβειᾰ.</div><b>ασέβημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (usually uncountable, plural ασεβήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) disrespect, impiety</div><b>ασέλγεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ασέλγειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. lewdness, lechery (vulgar overindulgence in sexual activity)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η <b>ασέλγεια</b> του δεν περιγράφεται. - His lechery can&#x27;t be described.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) indecent assault, molestation (unwanted sexual contact with another person, short of rape)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Κατηγορείται ότι διέπραξε <b>ασέλγεια</b> εις βάρος ανηλίκου. - He is accused of having committed indecent assault against a minor.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀσέλγεια, of uncertain origin.</div><b>ασέληνος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασέληνη, neuter ασέληνο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>moonless (night)</div><b>ασέλωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασέλωτη, neuter ασέλωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>saddleless</div><b>ασήκωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασήκωτη, neuter ασήκωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unliftable, unlifted</div>
  <div class='def'>2. overweight</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) unbearable</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ασήκωτος</b> καημός - an unbearable heartache</div>
  <div class='def'>4. uncleared</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το τραπέζι είναι ακόμα <b>ασήκωτο</b>. - The table is not cleared yet.</div><b>ασήμαντος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασήμαντη, neuter ασήμαντο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unimportant, trivial, negligible, insignificant</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀσήμαντος.</div><b>ασήμι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ασήμια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. silver</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (in plural) silverware</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἄσημον, substantivized neuter form of ἄσημος.</div><b>ασήμωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ασημώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. silver-plating, silver-plate</div>
  <div class='def'>2. gift of money</div>
  <div class='def'>3. crossing palm with silver</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (in plural) used in supplication: effigies of limbs or objects</div><b>ασίγαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασίγαστη, neuter ασίγαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unquenched, unappeased, unquenchable, unsilenced, unsilenceable</div><b>ασίγητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασίγητη, neuter ασίγητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unsung</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unsilenced, unsilenceable, incessant</div><b>ασίκης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ασίκηδες, feminine ασίκισσα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial) bold/strapping/strong man</div><b>ασίκικος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασίκικη, neuter ασίκικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. Levantine</div>
  <div class='def'>2. describes a brave lad</div><b>ασίκισσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ασίκισσες, masculine ασίκης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial) bold/strapping young woman</div><b>ασίτευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασίτευτη, neuter ασίτευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fresh, not gamey (of meat)</div><b>ασαβάνωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασαβάνωτη, neuter ασαβάνωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unshrouded</div><b>ασαβούρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ανερμάτιστη, neuter ανερμάτιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unballasted, without ballast, out of ballast</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) waste of space, worthless</div><b>ασαγήνευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασαγήνευτη, neuter ασαγήνευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unseduced, unenchanted</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unmoved</div><b>ασαμάρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασαμάρωτη, neuter ασαμάρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unsaddled, saddleless (without a saddle)</div>
  <div class='ex'>γαϊδούρι <b>ασαμάρωτο</b> - a saddleless donkey</div><b>ασανσέρ</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(indeclinable) lift (UK), elevator (US)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from French ascenseur.</div><b>ασαπούνιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασαπούνιστη, neuter ασαπούνιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not washed, especially not with soap</div><b>ασαράντιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασαράντιστη, neuter ασαράντιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>less than forty days (from birth or death)</div><b>ασατίριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασατίριστη, neuter ασατίριστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not satirical, unsatirised (UK), unsatirized (US)</div><b>ασατύριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασατύριστη, neuter ασατύριστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>misspelling of <a href="bword://ασατίριστος">ασατίριστος</a></div><b>ασαφήνιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασαφήνιστη, neuter ασαφήνιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unclear, obscure</div><b>ασαφής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασαφής, neuter ασαφές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ambiguous, vague, obscure, unclear</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀσαφής. By surface analysis, α- (a-) + σαφής.</div><b>ασβέστης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) lime, quicklime, whitewash</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) lime, hydrated calcium oxide, calcium hydroxide</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ασβέστης m, from ασβέστιν n, itself a diminutive of Ancient Greek ἄσβεστος f.</div><b>ασβέστιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (usually uncountable, plural ασβέστια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) calcium</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἄσβεστος.</div><b>ασβέστωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ασβεστώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>whitewashing</div><b>ασβεστάδικο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ασβεστάδικα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>lime works, lime kiln</div><b>ασβεστίτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ασβεστίτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>calcite</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> By surface analysis, ασβέστιο + -ίτης.</div><b>ασβεστοκάμινο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ασβεστοκάμινα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. lime kiln</div>
  <div class='def'>2. accusative/vocative singular of <a href="bword://ασβεστοκάμινος">ασβεστοκάμινος</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Ultimately from ασβέστης m + καμίνι n</div><b>ασβεστοκάμινος</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ασβεστοκάμινοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ασβεστοκάμινο">ασβεστοκάμινο</a></div><b>ασβεστοκονίαμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ασβεστοκονιάματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>lime mortar</div><b>ασβεστολιθικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασβεστολιθική, neuter ασβεστολιθικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>calcarious, chalky</div><b>ασβεστοποίηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural ασβεστοποιήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) calcination, lime burning</div><b>ασβεστοποιία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural ασβεστοποιίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable, usually) lime production, lime burning</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable, usually) calcination</div><b>ασβεστούχος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασβεστούχη, neuter ασβεστούχο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>calciferous (containing calcium)</div><b>ασβεστόγαλα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural ασβεστόγαλες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) limewater</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> άσβεστος + γάλα</div><b>ασβεστόλακκος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ασβεστόλακκοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>lime pit, limepit</div><b>ασβεστόλιθος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (usually uncountable, plural ασβεστόλιθοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) limestone</div><b>ασβεστόνερο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (usually uncountable, plural ασβεστόνερα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable, usually) limewater</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable, usually) pickling lime</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (colloquial, uncountable, usually) whitewash</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> άσβεστος + νερό</div><b>ασβεστόπετρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural ασβεστόπετρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) limestone</div><b>ασβεστώδης</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασβεστώδης, neuter ασβεστώδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>calcareous, like lime, containing lime</div><b>ασβεστώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to limewash, whitewash, lime</div><b>ασβολερός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασβολερή, neuter ασβολερό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(rare) dark, with sooty, black color/colour</div><b>ασβόλη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ασβόλες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>soot</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἄσβολος f</div><b>ασβός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ασβοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. badger</div>
  <div class='def'>2. timid person</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Proto-Slavic *jаzvъ (“badger”). Compare Bulgarian я́зовец.</div><b>ασεβής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασεβής, neuter ασεβές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. disrespectful</div>
  <div class='def'>2. impious</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ᾰ̓σεβής.</div><b>ασεβώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to show disrespect for everything sacred, holy or revered</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ᾰ̓σεβέω / ᾰ̓σεβῶ.</div><b>ασεβώς</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(formal) disrespectfully, with contempt</div>
  <div class='ex'>in polytonic script: ἀσεβῶς</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Hellenistic Koine Greek ᾰ̓σεβῶς.</div><b>ασεισμικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασεισμική, neuter ασεισμικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>no seismic activity</div><b>ασελγής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασελγής, neuter ασελγές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>lewd, lecherous, lascivious, libidinous (driven by lust and unethical or vulgar)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Δεν θέλω να ακούσω για τις <b>ασελγείς</b> λεπτομέρειες, με αηδιάζει. - I don&#x27;t want to hear the lewd details, it disgusts me.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Ancient Greek ἀσελγής, of uncertain origin.</div><b>ασελγαίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to assault, to be unruly</div><b>ασελγώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to assault sexually, indecently assault.</div>
  <div class='ex'>Αποπειράθηκε να <b>ασελγήσει</b> σε ανήλικο. - He attempted to indecently assault a minor.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Koine Greek ἀσελγῶ, ancient form ἀσελγαίνω of uncertain origin.</div><b>ασελιδοποίητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασελιδοποίητη, neuter ασελιδοποίητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unpaged, unpaginated</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ασελιδοποίητο</b> δοκίμιο - galley proof</div><b>ασετιλίνη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ασετυλίνη">ασετυλίνη</a></div><b>ασετυλίνη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) acetylene, ethyne (IUPAC name)</div><b>ασετόν</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(indeclinable) acetone</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from French acétone.</div><b>ασημάδευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασημάδευτη, neuter ασημάδευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unmarked</div>
