  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασούρωτη, neuter ασούρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unstrained, undrained</div>
  <div class='ex'>Mην αφήσεις <b>ασούρωτα</b> τα μακαρόνια. - Don&#x27;t leave the spaghetti unastained</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unpleated, uncreased</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) sober, not drunk</div><b>ασούφρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασούφρωτη, neuter ασούφρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. uncreased, unwrinkled</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (colloquial, figuratively) not stolen, not pilfered, not half-inched</div><b>ασπάζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to greet, hail</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (literary) to kiss</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) to embrace, espouse (theories, ideals)</div><b>ασπάλαθος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ασπάλαθοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. a species of broom:; Calicotome spinosa, thorny broom, spiny broom</div>
  <div class='def'>2. broom, furze, gorse</div>
  <div class='def'>3. a species of broom:; Calicotome villosa, hairy thorny broom, spiny broom</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀσπάλαθος</div><b>ασπάλακας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ασπάλακες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (literary) mole (mammal)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) A mentally blinded man.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (rare) dormouse</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀσπάλαξ.</div><b>ασπέδιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασπέδιστη, neuter ασπέδιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unhobbled (horse)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) unfettered, unrestricted</div><b>ασπίδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ασπίδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. shield, buckler (for personal protection)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) shield, protection</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from the Ancient Greek ἀσπίς, as in the accusative singular ἀσπίδα.</div><b>ασπίλωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασπίλωτη, neuter ασπίλωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://άσπιλος">άσπιλος</a></div><b>ασπίτωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασπίτωτη, neuter ασπίτωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(rare) homeless</div><b>ασπαραγίνη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) asparagine</div><b>ασπαραγινικού οξέος</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>genitive singular of ασπαρτικό <a href="bword://οξύ">οξύ</a></div><b>ασπαργάνωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασπαργάνωτη, neuter ασπαργάνωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not swaddled, unswaddled</div><b>ασπαρτικό οξύ</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>aspartic acid</div><b>ασπασμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ασπασμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>kiss, hug</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀσπασμός</div><b>ασπαστός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασπαστή, neuter ασπαστό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>acceptable, accepted</div><b>ασπιδοφόρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασπιδοφόρος or ασπιδοφόρη, neuter ασπιδοφόρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. shield-bearing</div>
  <div class='def'>2. shield-bearer</div><b>ασπιρίνη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ασπιρίνες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>aspirin (analgesic)</div><b>ασπλαχνία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural ασπλαχνίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) ruthlessness, mercilessness, cruelty</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀσπλαγχνία</div><b>ασπλαχνιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural ασπλαχνιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ασπλαχνία">ασπλαχνία</a></div><b>ασπούδαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασπούδαστη, neuter ασπούδαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>uneducated, untaught</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀσπούδαστος</div><b>ασπούδαχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασπούδαχτη, neuter ασπούδαχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ασπούδαστος">ασπούδαστος</a></div><b>ασπράγκαθο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ασπράγκαθα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>name of various thorny plants such as Xanthium spinosum (spiny cocklebur), Scolymus hispanicus (common golden thistle),Calicotome villosa (hairy thorny broom), Cirsium acarna (soldier thistle), or Ptilostemon stellatum</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From ασπρ- (aspr-, “white”) + αγκάθι.</div><b>ασπράδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural ασπάδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) whiteness</div><b>ασπράδι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ασπράδια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. egg white</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (colloquial) sclera; the white of the eye</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀσπράδιον.</div><b>ασπρίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (transitive) to whiten, whitewash</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (intransitive) to turn white, whiten</div><b>ασπρίλα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural ασπρίλες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) whiteness</div><b>ασπραγκαθιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ασπραγκαθιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ασπράγκαθο">ασπράγκαθο</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From ασπρ- (aspr-, “white”) + αγκάθι + -α (-a).</div><b>ασπριδερός</b>
