  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ασπρολούλουδα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. white flower</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (especially) daisy</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ασπρο- (aspro-) + λουλούδι</div><b>ασπρομάλλα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ασπρομάλλες, masculine ασπρομάλλης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>white-haired woman</div><b>ασπρομάλλης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ασπρομάλληδες, feminine ασπρομάλλα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>white-haired man</div><b>ασπροντυμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασπροντυμένη, neuter ασπροντυμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>dressed in white</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ασπρο- (aspro-) + ντυμένος</div><b>ασπροπρόσωπος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασπροπρόσωπη, neuter ασπροπρόσωπο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>white-faced</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ασπρο- (aspro-) + πρόσωπο</div><b>ασπροσκούληκο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ασπροσκούληκα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>cockchafer</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From ασπρο- (aspro-, “white”) + σκουλήκι.</div><b>ασπρουδερός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασπρουδερή, neuter ασπρουδερό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ασπριδερός">ασπριδερός</a></div><b>ασπρουλιάρης</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασπρουλιάρα, neuter ασπρουλιάρικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>whitish, pale</div><b>ασπρουλιάρικος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασπρουλιάρικη, neuter ασπρουλιάρικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>whitish, pale</div><b>ασπροφορεμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασπροφορεμένη, neuter ασπροφορεμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>dressed in white</div><b>ασπρόμαυρο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ασπρόμαυρα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>black-and-white color/colour (literally: white and black)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Neuter of the adjective ασπρόμαυρος.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://ασπρόμαυρος">ασπρόμαυρος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://ασπρόμαυρος">ασπρόμαυρος</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Neuter of the adjective ασπρόμαυρος.</div><b>ασπρόμαυρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασπρόμαυρη, neuter ασπρόμαυρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>of black-and-white color/colour</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ασπρόμαυρη</b> ταινία, τηλεόραση, φωτογραφία - literally white and black (black-and-white) film, television, photograph</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From ασπρο- (aspro-, “white”) + μαύρος. Also see the medieval verb ἀσπρομαυρίζω.</div><b>ασπρόρουχο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ασπρόρουχα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. white goods; underwear, underclothes</div>
  <div class='def'>2. white goods; bedlinen, sheets, pillowcases</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ασπρο- (aspro-) + ρούχο</div><b>ασπρόχωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ασπροχώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>potters&#x27; clay, argil, white clay</div><b>ασπρόψαρο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ασπρόψαρα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Various species of leuciscines (Leuciscinae).</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From άσπρος + -ψαρο (-psaro, “fish”).</div><b>ασπόνδυλα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>invertebrates</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://ασπόνδυλος">ασπόνδυλος</a></div><b>ασπόνδυλος</b>
