  <div class='def'>(historical, obsolete) assassin</div><b>ασσυριακός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασσυριακή, neuter ασσυριακό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Assyrian (relating to Assyria or its people or language)</div><b>αστάθεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αστάθειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. instability, unsteadiness</div>
  <div class='def'>2. inconstancy</div><b>αστάθμητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αστάθμητη, neuter αστάθμητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (literally) not weighable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) imponderable</div><b>αστάρι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αστάρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>primer, undercoat</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from Ottoman Turkish آستر (astar), from Classical Persian آستر.</div><b>αστάρωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ασταρώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>priming, (paint: the action and effect)</div><b>αστάρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αστάρωτη, neuter αστάρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unprimed, not undercoated</div><b>αστέγαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αστέγαστη, neuter αστέγαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. roofless</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (person) homeless</div><b>αστέγνωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αστέγνωτη, neuter αστέγνωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>undried, damp</div><b>αστέρας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αστέρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. star</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αστέρας</b> νετρονίων - neutron star</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (of star polygons) star (a flat figure with projecting points)</div>
  <div class='ex'>πεντάκτινος <b>αστέρας</b>, εξάκτινος <b>αστέρας</b> - five-pointed star, six-pointed star</div>
  <div class='def'>3. star (quality scoring system)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το ξενοδοχείο μας είναι πέντε <b>αστέρων</b>, επισήμανε ο εκπρόσωπος τύπου. - Our hotel is five-star, the spokesperson pointed out.</div>
  <div class='def'>4. star</div>
  <div class='ex'>διάσημος κινηματογραφικός <b>αστέρας</b> - famous film star</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀστέρας, from the ancient singular accusative τὸν ἀστέρα of Ancient Greek ἀστήρ. The modern senses, semantic loan from English star.</div><b>αστέρευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αστέρευτη, neuter αστέρευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αστείρευτος">αστείρευτος</a></div><b>αστέρι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αστέρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. star</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (informal) star (a flat figure with projecting points)</div>
  <div class='ex'>πεντάκτινο <b>αστέρι</b>, εξάκτινο <b>αστέρι</b> - five-pointed star, six-pointed star</div>
  <div class='def'>3. star</div>
  <div class='ex'>τ’ <b>αστέρια</b> του Χόλιγουντ - the stars of Hollywood</div>
  <div class='def'>4. a brilliant person</div>
  <div class='ex'>Αυτό το παιδί είναι <b>αστέρι</b> στα μαθηματικά. - This child is a star at maths.</div>
  <div class='def'>5. star (quality scoring symbol, especially for hotels)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀστέριν, from Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀστέριον, diminutive of the Ancient Greek ἀστήρ, from Proto-Indo-European *h₂stḗr.</div><b>αστέρινος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αστέρινη, neuter αστέρινο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>of the stars or star material, starry</div><b>αστέριωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αστέριωτη, neuter αστέριωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unfixed</div><b>αστή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αστές, masculine αστός)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>townswoman</div><b>αστήρικτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αστήρικτη, neuter αστήρικτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unsupported, unpropped</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) indefensible</div><b>αστήριχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αστήριχτη, neuter αστήριχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αστήρικτος">αστήρικτος</a></div><b>αστίατρος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural αστίατροι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>municipal medical officer, municipal doctor</div><b>αστίλβωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αστίλβωτη, neuter αστίλβωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unpolished, unvarnished</div><b>ασταθής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασταθής, neuter ασταθές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unstable, unsteady</div>
  <div class='def'>2. changeable, fickle, volatile</div><b>αστακός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αστακοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>lobster</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀστακός.</div><b>ασταμάτητα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unstoppably, unrelentingly; continuously</div><b>ασταμάτητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασταμάτητη, neuter ασταμάτητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unstoppable, unrelenting; continuous</div><b>ασταρώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to undercoat, to prime</div><b>ασταύρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασταύρωτη, neuter ασταύρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not crucified</div><b>αστεΐζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αστειεύομαι">αστειεύομαι</a></div><b>αστεία</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>in a funny way</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>στ’ αστεία</b> - jokingly</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. nominative/accusative/vocative feminine singular of <a href="bword://αστείος">αστείος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αστείος">αστείος</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative plural of <a href="bword://αστείο">αστείο</a></div><b>αστείο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αστεία)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>joke</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From the Ancient Greek ἀστεῖον.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://αστείος">αστείος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://αστείος">αστείος</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From the Ancient Greek ἀστεῖον.</div><b>αστείος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αστεία, neuter αστείο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. funny, amusing, comical, comic</div>
  <div class='def'>2. trivial</div>
  <div class='def'>3. laughable</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀστεῖος.</div><b>αστείρευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αστείρευτη, neuter αστείρευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>inexhaustible, without limit</div><b>αστεγία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (countable and uncountable, plural αστεγίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(countable, rare, uncountable) homelessness; houselessness</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Attested as ἀστεγία since 1889. From άστεγ(ος), “homeless”, literally “roofless”) + -ία. The modern usage, calque of English homelessness.</div><b>αστειεύομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to joke, to tell a joke, to crack a joke</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) to be jesting, to not being serious</div><b>αστειολόγημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αστειολογήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>jest, joke, banter, jesting, joking</div><b>αστειολόγος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αστειολόγοι)</i></div>
