  <div class='def'>1. ungathered, uncollected</div>
  <div class='def'>2. not mustered, not assembled</div><b>ασύνδετος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασύνδετη, neuter ασύνδετο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unconnected, disconnected, not linked, uncoupled</div>
  <div class='def'>2. asyndeton (a sentence without conjunctions)</div><b>ασύνειδος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασύνειδη, neuter ασύνειδο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>of the unconscious</div><b>ασύνετος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασύνετη, neuter ασύνετο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unwise, thoughtless</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀσύνετος</div><b>ασύνορος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασύνορη, neuter ασύνορο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>borderless, frontierless, unbounded</div><b>ασύντακτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασύντακτη, neuter ασύντακτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ασύνταχτος">ασύνταχτος</a></div><b>ασύνταχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασύνταχτη, neuter ασύνταχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. badly composed</div>
  <div class='def'>2. asyntactic, not syntactical</div><b>ασύντμητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασύντμητη, neuter ασύντμητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unabbreviated, cannot be abbreviated</div><b>ασύρματος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασύρματη, neuter ασύρματο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. wireless, radio</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (literally) wireless, without wires</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ασύρματοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>wireless, radio (transceiver, transmitter, receiver)</div><b>ασύστατος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασύστατη, neuter ασύστατο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. untrue, groundless</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unrecommended, without references</div><b>ασύστολος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασύστολη, neuter ασύστολο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. shameless, brazen</div>
  <div class='def'>2. promiscuous</div><b>ασύχαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασύχαστη, neuter ασύχαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>incessant, in constant motion</div><b>ασύχναστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασύχναστη, neuter ασύχναστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>remote, secluded, unfrequented</div><b>ασώματος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασώματη, neuter ασώματο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>disembodied, bodiless, immaterial</div><b>ασώπαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ασώπαστη, neuter ασώπαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>describes: a chatterbox, someone who talks continuously</div><b>ατάιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατάιστη, neuter ατάιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unfed</div><b>ατάκα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ατάκες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. catch phrase, pick-up line</div>
  <div class='def'>2. retort, immediate response</div>
  <div class='def'>3. continuing piece</div><b>ατάλαντος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατάλαντη, neuter ατάλαντο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>talentless, untalented (lacking in talent)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Νομίζει ότι είναι σπουδαίος στο πιάνο αλλά είναι εντελώς <b>ατάλαντος</b>. - He thinks he&#x27;s great on the piano but he&#x27;s completely talentless.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀτάλαντος, equivalent to α- (a-, “un-”) + τάλαντο. Modern sense has completely displaced the Koine Greek sense of “isobaric, straight”.</div><b>ατάραχος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατάραχη, neuter ατάραχο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unruffled, tranquil, composed</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀτάραχος. See the verb ταράσσω.</div><b>ατάσθαλος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατάσθαλη, neuter ατάσθαλο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. immoral, indecent</div>
  <div class='def'>2. untidy</div><b>ατέκμαρτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατέκμαρτη, neuter ατέκμαρτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unknown, unclear, obscure</div><b>ατέλεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ατέλειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. defect, defectiveness</div>
  <div class='def'>2. imperfection</div>
  <div class='def'>3. exemption (from duty or tax)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀτέλεια</div><b>ατέλειωτα</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://ατέλειωτος">ατέλειωτος</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>endlessly, unendingly, ceaselessly</div>
  <div class='ex'>Δρόμοι παλιοί που αγάπησα και μίσησα <b>ατέλειωτα</b>. - Old roads that I loved and hated endlessly.</div><b>ατέλειωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατέλειωτη, neuter ατέλειωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>a less formal variant of <a href="bword://ατελείωτος">ατελείωτος</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀτελείωτος, morphologically α- (a-, “un-, a-, not”, privative) + τελειώ(νω), “I finish”) + -τος (-tos). Shift of stress backwards dates from Medieval era. Compare to the learned borrowing ατελείωτος.</div><b>ατέντωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατέντωτη, neuter ατέντωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unstretched</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) relaxed</div><b>ατέρμονας</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατέρμονη, neuter ατέρμονο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>endless, interminable</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural +~)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. worm</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ατέρμονας</b> κοχλίας - worm screw</div>
  <div class='def'>2. jib (sail)</div><b>ατέρμων</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατέρμων, neuter ατέρμον)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>endless, interminable</div><b>ατίθασος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατίθαση, neuter ατίθασο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. insubordinate, rebellious, undisciplined</div>
  <div class='def'>2. intractable, untameable, untamed</div><b>ατίμασμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (usually uncountable, plural ατιμάσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) dishonour (UK), dishonor (US), disgrace</div><b>ατίμητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατίμητη, neuter ατίμητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unhonoured (UK), unhonored (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. priceless, inestimable</div><b>ατίμωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ατίμωσιες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>dishonour (UK), dishonor (US), disgrace</div><b>ατίναχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατίναχτη, neuter ατίναχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unshaken</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unbeaten (carpet)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. not blown up (bridge, etc)</div><b>αταίριαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αταίριαστη, neuter αταίριαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>incongruous, ill-matched, dissimilar</div><b>αταίριαχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αταίριαχτη, neuter αταίριαχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αταίριαστος">αταίριαστος</a></div><b>αταβάνωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αταβάνωτη, neuter αταβάνωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ceilingless, unceilinged, without a ceiling</div><b>αταβισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (countable and uncountable, plural αταβισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(countable, uncountable) atavism</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from French atavisme.</div><b>αταβιστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αταβιστική, neuter αταβιστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>atavistic</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from English atavistic.</div><b>ατακτοποίητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατακτοποίητη, neuter ατακτοποίητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>untidy, disorganised (UK), disorganized (US)</div><b>ατακτώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to misbehave</div><b>αταλάντευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αταλάντευτη, neuter αταλάντευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unswayed, firm</div>
  <div class='def'>2. immobile</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀταλάντευτος.</div><b>αταλαιπώρητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αταλαιπώρητη, neuter αταλαιπώρητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>having not suffered</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀταλαιπώρητος.</div><b>αταξία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αταξίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. ataxia</div>
  <div class='def'>2. disorder, disorderliness</div>
  <div class='def'>3. confusion</div>
  <div class='def'>4. irregularity</div>
  <div class='def'>5. mischief</div><b>αταξίδευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αταξίδευτη, neuter αταξίδευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>untravelled (UK), untraveled (US)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From α- (a-, alpha privative) + ταξιδεύ(ω), “to travel”) + -τος (-tos).</div><b>αταξικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αταξική, neuter αταξικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. classless</div>
  <div class='ex'>Οι μαρξιστές πιστεύουν σε μια <b>αταξική</b> κοινωνία. - Marxists believe in a classless society.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unclassified</div><b>αταξινόμητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αταξινόμητη, neuter αταξινόμητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>uncategorised (UK), uncategorized (US), unclassified</div><b>αταπείνωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αταπείνωτη, neuter αταπείνωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not humbled</div><b>αταρίχευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αταρίχευτη, neuter αταρίχευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unembalmed</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unsalted (fish)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀταρίχευτος.</div><b>αταραξία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) ataraxia</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) composure, equanimity</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀταραξία.</div><b>ατασθαλία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ατασθαλίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. irregularity, foul play</div>
  <div class='def'>2. immorality, indecency</div>
  <div class='def'>3. untidiness</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀτασθαλία, from ἀτάσθαλος.</div><b>αταχτώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ατακτώ">ατακτώ</a></div><b>αταχυδρόμητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αταχυδρόμητη, neuter αταχυδρόμητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unmailed, unposted</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αταχυδρόμητη</b> επιστολή - unmailed letter</div><b>αταύτιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αταύτιστη, neuter αταύτιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unidentified, unidentifiable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unmatched</div><b>ατείχιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατείχιστη, neuter ατείχιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unwalled, unfortified</div><b>ατεκνία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural ατεκνίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) childlessness</div><b>ατελέσφορος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατελέσφορη, neuter ατελέσφορο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fruitless, ineffective</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>ατελέσφορη</b> διαπραγματευτική τακτική - fruitless negotiating tactics</div><b>ατελής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατελής, neuter ατελές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>imperfect, incomplete</div><b>ατελείωτα</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://ατελείωτος">ατελείωτος</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>endlessly, unendingly, ceaselessly</div><b>ατελείωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατελείωτη, neuter ατελείωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. endless, unending, never-ending (never ending or seeming to end)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Με αυτό τον άνθρωπο έχω <b>ατελείωτες</b> ιστορίες! - I have endless dealings with this man!</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unfinished, incomplete (not having ended properly)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Έφυγε και άφησε τις σπουδές της <b>ατελείωτες</b>. - She quit and left her studies unfinished.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀτελείωτος, morphologically α- (a-, “un-, a-, not”) + τελειώνω.</div><b>ατελεσφόρητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατελέσφορη, neuter ατελέσφορο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ατελέσφορος">ατελέσφορος</a></div><b>ατελεύτητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατελεύτητη, neuter ατελεύτητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>endless, never-ending</div><b>ατελιέ</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(indeclinable) studio, atelier</div><b>ατελώνιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατελώνιστη, neuter ατελώνιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. uncleared through customs</div>
  <div class='def'>2. imported duty-free</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (broadly) smuggled</div><b>ατελώς</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>tax exempt, postage free</div><b>ατεμάχιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατεμάχιστη, neuter ατεμάχιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>whole: uncut, not cut up</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From τεμαχίζω</div><b>ατενής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατενής, neuter ατενές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fixed, intent, blank (glare/stare)</div><b>ατενίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to stare, to glare</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀτενίζω</div><b>ατερμάτιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατερμάτιστη, neuter ατερμάτιστος)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>endless, interminable</div><b>ατετραγώνιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατετραγώνιστη, neuter ατετραγώνιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not squared</div>
  <div class='ex'>ο κύκλος είναι <b>ατετραγώνιστος</b> - the circle cannot be squared</div><b>ατεχνία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ατεχνίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>incompetence, clumsiness</div><b>ατζέμ πιλάφι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) pilaf with stewed meat</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from Ottoman Turkish عجم پلاوی, from عجم and پلاو.</div><b>ατζέντα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ατζέντες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (US) diary</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (UK) agenda (schedule of business for a meeting)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from English agenda.</div><b>ατζέντης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ατζέντηδες, feminine ατζέντισσα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. shipping broker</div>
  <div class='def'>2. actors&#x27; theatrical agent</div><b>ατζέντισσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ατζέντισσες, masculine ατζέντης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. actors&#x27; theatrical agent</div>
  <div class='def'>2. shipping broker</div><b>ατζαμής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ατζαμήδες, feminine ατζαμού)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>botcher, bungler, cowboy (incompetent, slapdash worker)</div><b>ατζαμίδικος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατζαμίδικη, neuter ατζαμίδικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>botched, bungled (done in an incompetent manner)</div><b>ατζαμίστικος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατζαμίστικη, neuter ατζαμίστικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>clumsy, inept, inexpert, bungling</div><b>ατζαμοσύνη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (countable and uncountable, plural ατζαμοσύνες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (countable, uncountable) botched job</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (countable, uncountable) ineptitude, clumsiness</div><b>ατηγάνιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατηγάνιστη, neuter ατηγάνιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unfried, not fried</div><b>ατηγάνιτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατηγάνιτη, neuter ατηγάνιτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ατηγάνιστος">ατηγάνιστος</a></div><b>ατημέλεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural ατημέλειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ατημελησία">ατημελησία</a></div><b>ατημέλητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατημέλητη, neuter ατημέλητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unkempt, bedraggled</div>
  <div class='def'>2. slovenly</div><b>ατημελησία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural ατημελησίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) negligence, carelessness</div><b>ατιθάσευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατιθάσευτη, neuter ατιθάσευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ατίθασος">ατίθασος</a></div><b>ατιμάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. disgrace</div>
  <div class='def'>2. rape, ravish</div><b>ατιμία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (countable and uncountable, plural ατιμίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (countable, uncountable) disgrace, dishonour (UK), dishonor (US), atimia</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (countable, uncountable) dishonesty</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (countable, uncountable) fraud</div><b>ατιμασμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (usually uncountable, plural ατιμασμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) dishonour (UK), dishonor (US), disgrace</div><b>ατιμαστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατιμαστική, neuter ατιμαστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>dishonouring (UK), dishonoring (US) (contributing to)</div><b>ατιμολόγητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατιμολόγητη, neuter ατιμολόγητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unpriced</div>
  <div class='def'>2. not invoiced</div><b>ατιμωρησία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural ατιμωρησίες)</i></div>
