  <div><i>noun, masculine (countable and uncountable, plural αττικάρκες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(countable, uncountable) chief of police in Attica</div><b>αττικίζουσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αττικίζουσες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(of language) Atticizing (language), written in Attic style</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀττῐκῐ́ζουσα, feminine of the participle ἀττικίζων. For the language, substantivised, by ellipsis of γλώσσα f.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative feminine singular of αττικίζων</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek ἀττῐκῐ́ζουσα, feminine of the participle ἀττικίζων. For the language, substantivised, by ellipsis of γλώσσα f.</div><b>αττικίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to Atticise (UK), Atticize (US)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀττικίζω.</div><b>αττικισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αττικισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Atticism, imitation of an Attic style</div><b>αττικιστής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural μιμητές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Atticist</div><b>αττικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αττική, neuter αττικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Attic, relating to Attica or Athens.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> See Αθήνα.</div><b>ατυράγνιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατυράγνιστη, neuter ατυράγνιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ατυράννιστος">ατυράννιστος</a></div><b>ατυράννητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατυράννητη, neuter ατυράννητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ατυράννιστος">ατυράννιστος</a></div><b>ατυράννιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατυράννιστη, neuter ατυράννιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not tortured, untormented, without suffering</div><b>ατυχής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατυχής, neuter ατυχές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unlucky, unfortunate, ill-fated</div><b>ατυχία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ατυχίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. misfortune, bad luck, ill-fortune, adversity</div>
  <div class='def'>2. misfortune, accident (physical event)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀτυχία. By surface analysis, α- (a-) + τύχ(η)) + -ία.</div><b>ατυχώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be unlucky, to have bad luck</div><b>ατυχώς</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unluckily, unfortunately</div><b>ατόνηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural ατονήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) weakening, attenuation, decline</div><b>ατόνιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατόνιστη, neuter ατόνιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unaccented, unstressed</div><b>ατόπημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ατοπήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>slip, blunder, faux pas</div><b>ατόρνευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατόρνευτη, neuter ατόρνευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unturned</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unmachined (loosely)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) coarse, uncultivated</div><b>ατός</b>
  <div><i>pron, masculine (feminine ατή, neuter ατό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://απατός">απατός</a></div><b>ατός μου</b>
  <div><i>pron, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>myself</div><b>ατός σου</b>
  <div><i>pron, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>yourself</div><b>ατόφιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατόφια, neuter ατόφιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>solid, complete, whole, pure</div><b>ατύλιχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατύλιχτη, neuter ατύλιχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. not rolled up, not swaddled</div>
  <div class='def'>2. not wrapped/wrapped up</div>
  <div class='def'>3. unrollable</div><b>ατύπωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ατύπωτη, neuter ατύπωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unpublished, unprinted</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) imprint, remember</div><b>ατύχημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ατυχήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>accident, mishap</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Hellenistic Koine Greek ἀτύχημα. Morphologically, α- (a-) + τύχη + -μα (-ma, “suffix for neuters”).</div><b>αυγά μάτια</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative plural of <a href="bword://αυγό">αυγό</a> <a href="bword://μάτι">μάτι</a> (fried eggs)</div><b>αυγάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(literary) to shine, to illuminate</div><b>αυγή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αυγές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. dawn, sunrise, daybreak</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) beginning, start</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From the Ancient Greek αὐγή, from Proto-Indo-European *h₂ewg- (“to increase, to enlarge”).</div><b>αυγατίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αβγατίζω">αβγατίζω</a></div><b>αυγαταίνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αβγαταίνω">αβγαταίνω</a></div><b>αυγερινός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυγερινή, neuter αυγερινό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. seen at dawn, dawn rising</div>
  <div class='def'>2. Morning Star</div><b>αυγινός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυγινή, neuter αυγινό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>dawn</div><b>αυγοθήκη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αυγοθήκη)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αβγοθήκη">αβγοθήκη</a></div><b>αυγοκομμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αυγοκομμένη, neuter αυγοκομμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>a different spelling of of <a href="bword://αβγοκομμένος">αβγοκομμένος</a></div><b>αυγοκόβω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αβγοκόβω">αβγοκόβω</a></div><b>αυγολέμονο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative spelling of <a href="bword://αβγολέμονο">αβγολέμονο</a></div><b>αυγοσαλάτα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αυγοσαλάτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>egg salad</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αυγό + σαλάτα</div><b>αυγοτάραχο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αυγοτάραχα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. fish roe</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (especially) bottarga</div><b>αυγουστίνειος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυγουστίνεια, neuter αυγουστίνειο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Augustinian</div><b>αυγουστιάτικος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυγουστιάτικη, neuter αυγουστιάτικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. August</div>
  <div class='def'>2. the hottest days of August</div><b>αυγό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αυγά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αβγό">αβγό</a></div><b>αυγό μάτι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αυγά μάτια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αβγό">αβγό</a> <a href="bword://μάτι">μάτι</a></div><b>αυγότσουφλο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αυγότσουφλα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αβγότσουφλο">αβγότσουφλο</a></div><b>αυθάδεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (countable and uncountable, plural αυθάδειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(countable, uncountable) insolence, cheek, impudence, sauciness</div><b>αυθάδης</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυθάδης, neuter αυθάδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>insolent, saucy, cheeky, impudent</div><b>αυθάδικος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυθάδικη, neuter αυθάδικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>insolent, saucy, cheeky, impudent</div><b>αυθέντης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αυθέντες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. authority, master</div>
  <div class='def'>2. ruler, overlord</div><b>αυθαίρετα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. arbitrarily</div>
  <div class='def'>2. without official authorization</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αυθαίρετ(ος)) + -α (-a).</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αυθαίρετος">αυθαίρετος</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αυθαίρετ(ος)) + -α (-a).</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative plural of <a href="bword://αυθαίρετο">αυθαίρετο</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αυθαίρετ(ος)) + -α (-a).</div><b>αυθαίρετο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αυθαίρετα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. illegal, unauthorised (UK), unauthorized (US) building, usually house, built in violation of regulations</div>
  <div class='def'>2. arbitrariness</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> short for αυθαίρετο σπίτι or οικοδόμημα: nominalization of αυθαίρετος, substantivised neuter, by Ellipsis of σπίτι, or οικοδόμημα n, or, as an abstract sense.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://αυθαίρετος">αυθαίρετος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://αυθαίρετος">αυθαίρετος</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> short for αυθαίρετο σπίτι or οικοδόμημα: nominalization of αυθαίρετος, substantivised neuter, by Ellipsis of σπίτι, or οικοδόμημα n, or, as an abstract sense.</div><b>αυθαίρετος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυθαίρετη, neuter αυθαίρετο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unauthorised (UK), unauthorized (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. arbitrary (without logic)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek αὐθαίρετος, from αὐθ- (auth-), form of αὐτο- (auto-) + αἱρετός &lt; verb αἱρέω.</div><b>αυθαδιάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be insolent/saucy/cheeky, to cheek</div><b>αυθαιρεσία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αυθαιρεσίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abuse of power, arbitrariness</div><b>αυθαιρετώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to abuse power, to behave arbitrarily</div><b>αυθεντία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αυθεντίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. authority, overlordship, power (property)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. authority, overlord (status)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. authority</div>
  <div class='ex'>Είναι <b>αυθεντία</b> σε εξέλιξη. - He is an authority on evolution.</div><b>αυθεντικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυθεντική, neuter αυθεντικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>authoritative, reliable, valid, genuine</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek αὐθεντικός.</div><b>αυθεντικότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αυθεντικότητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) authenticity, validity, genuineness</div><b>αυθημερόν</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>on the same day, on the actual day</div><b>αυθορμησία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αυθορμησίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) spontaneity</div><b>αυθορμητισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (countable and uncountable, plural αυθορμητισμός)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (countable, uncountable) spontaneity</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (countable, uncountable) impulsiveness</div><b>αυθυπαρξία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αυθυπαρξίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) self-existence</div><b>αυθυποβάλλομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be autosuggestive, to delude oneself</div><b>αυθυποβολή</b>
  <div><i>noun</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) autosuggestion</div><b>αυθυπόστατος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυθυπόστατοςη, neuter αυθυπόστατο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>self-existent, independent</div><b>αυθωρεί</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(literary) at once, immediately</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αυθωρεί</b> και παραχρήμα - immediately</div><b>αυθόρμητα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>spontaneously</div><b>αυθόρμητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυθόρμητη, neuter αυθόρμητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. spontaneous</div>
  <div class='def'>2. instinctive</div>
  <div class='def'>3. impulsive</div>
  <div class='def'>4. unsolicited</div><b>αυθύπαρκτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυθύπαρκτη, neuter αυθύπαρκτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. self-existent</div>
  <div class='def'>2. self-contained, self-sufficient</div><b>αυθύπαρχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυθύπαρχτη, neuter αυθύπαρχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αυθύπαρκτος">αυθύπαρκτος</a></div><b>αυλάκι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αυλάκια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. irrigation ditch</div>
  <div class='def'>2. rifling, rifle groove</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek αὐλάκιν, from Koine Greek αὐλάκιον, from a diminutive of Ancient Greek αὖλαξ).</div><b>αυλάκιασμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αυλακιάσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αυλάκιασσμα">αυλάκιασσμα</a></div><b>αυλάκιασσμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αυλακιάσσματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>grooving, the making of a groove</div><b>αυλάκωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αυλάκωσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. groove; grooving (the process)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. groove; rifling</div><b>αυλάρχης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αυλάρχες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>chamberlain (usually a position in royal court)</div><b>αυλή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αυλές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. courtyard</div>
  <div class='def'>2. back garden, backyard</div>
  <div class='def'>3. court, courtiers (those near and working for a monarch)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek αὐλή.
Compare Mariupol Greek авлы́.</div><b>αυλαία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. a heavy curtain that separates the stage of a theatre from the auditorium</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) the end of a theatrical act, when the curtain is lowered</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (broadly) the beginning of a theatrical act, when the curtain is raised</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (figuratively) the end of an affair or situation</div>
  <div class='def'>5. (figuratively) the beginning of developments in a case or situation</div>
  <div class='def'>6. the shutter of a film camera</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek αὐλαία, from αὐλή</div><b>αυλακίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αυλακώνω">αυλακώνω</a></div><b>αυλακιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αυλακιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. furrow</div>
  <div class='def'>2. groove</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αυλάκι n.</div><b>αυλακιάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αυλακώνω">αυλακώνω</a></div><b>αυλακωτός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυλακωτή, neuter αυλακωτό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. rifled, grooved</div>
  <div class='ex'>η <b>αυλακωτή</b> κάννη όπλου - the rifled barrel of a gun</div>
  <div class='def'>2. furrowed</div>
  <div class='def'>3. rutted, corrugated, fluted</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αυλακωτές</b> λαμαρίνες - corrugated sheets</div><b>αυλακώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to plough (UK), plow (US), to furrow</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to groove</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to corrugate</div><b>αυλαρχία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αυλαρχίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>chamberlainship (position and period of office)</div><b>αυλαρχείο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αυλαρχεία)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>chamberlain&#x27;s office (place of work)</div><b>αυλητής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αυλητές, feminine αυλητρίδα or αυλήτρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. flautist, flutist</div>
  <div class='def'>2. piper</div><b>αυλικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυλική, neuter αυλικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>courtly, of the court, of a courtier</div><b>αυλοκολακεία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αυλοκολακείες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) flattery, servility (to power, at court)</div><b>αυλοκόλακας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αυλοκόλακες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. obsequious person (especially at court):; toady, flatterer, lickspittle, bootlicker</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (vulgar) obsequious person (especially at court):; brown noser, arse-kisser</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αυλή and κόλακας</div><b>αυλωτός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυλωτή, neuter αυλωτό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>tubular</div><b>αυλόγυρος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αυλόγυροι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>courtyard wall</div><b>αυλόδουλος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυλόδουλη, neuter αυλόδουλο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. servile, slavish, flattering (at court)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. toady, flatterer (to royalty)</div><b>αυλόθυρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αυλόθυρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>entrance, gate (to courtyard)</div><b>αυλόπορτα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αυλόπορτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>gate (especially in a wall or courtyard)</div><b>αυλός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αυλοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. pipe, flute, fife (any wind instrument played by blowing)</div>
  <div class='ex'>«Ο Μαγικός <b>Αυλός</b>» - The Magic Flute (1791 opera by Mozart)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. floghera or souravli (Greek folk instruments)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. bellows&#x27; pipe (used by blacksmith)</div>
  <div class='def'>4. the tubular part of any hollow organ eg intestines.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek αὐλός, from Proto-Indo-European *h₂ewlos (“tube”).
Cognates include Lithuanian aulas, Norwegian aul, Hittite [script needed] (auli-, “tube-shaped organ in the neck”), and perhaps also Latin alvus, Old Church Slavonic улица (ulica, “small lane, narrow street”), and Old Armenian ուղ, ուղի.</div><b>αυνανίζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to masturbate</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Back-formation from αυνανισμός: αυναν- (avnan-, “to masturbate”) + -ίζομαι.</div><b>αυνανισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) masturbation, onanism (manual erotic stimulation of the genitals or other erotic regions)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Παλιά, έλεγαν ότι ο <b>αυνανισμός</b> προκαλεί τύφλωση. - In the past, they used to say that masturbation causes blindness.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Αυνάν + -ισμός, a calque of French onanisme. First attested 1777.</div><b>αυνανιστής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αυνανιστές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>masturbator</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Back-formation from αυνανισμός: αυναν- (avnan-, “to masturbate”) + -ιστής.</div><b>αυνανιστικός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) masturbatory, onanistic (relating to the manual erotic stimulation of the genitals or other erotic regions)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Back-formation from αυνανισμός.</div><b>αυξάνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (transitive) to increase, raise, put up</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (transitive) to augment</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek αὐξάνω.</div><b>αυξίνη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αυξίνες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>auxin, plant-growth regulator</div><b>αυξητικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυξητική, neuter αυξητικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>augmentative, upward</div><b>αυξομείωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αυξομειώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fluctuation</div><b>αυξομειωμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αυξομειωμένη, neuter αυξομειωμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>increased and decreased, which has fluctuated</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αυξομειώνομαι, passive voice of αυξομειώνω (“increase and decrease”).</div><b>αυξομειώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(transitive) to fluctuate</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from the Hellenistic Ancient Greek αὐξομειῶ, contracted form of αὐξομειόω, with metaplasm + -ώνω. By surface analysis, αυξάνω + μειώνω</div><b>αυριανός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυριανή, neuter αυριανό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. tomorrow&#x27;s, of tomorrow (of or relating to the day after the present day)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) tomorrow&#x27;s, of tomorrow (of or relating to some point in the future)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αύρι(ο)) + -ανός.</div><b>αυστηρός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυστηρή or αυστηρά, neuter αυστηρό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. strict, severe, harsh</div>
  <div class='def'>2. austere</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek αὐστηρός.</div><b>αυστηρότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αυστηρότητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. severity, strictness</div>
  <div class='def'>2. austerity</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek αὐστηρότης, equivalent to αυστηρός + -ότητα.</div><b>αυστηρώς</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. strictly, harshly</div>
  <div class='def'>2. austerely</div><b>αυστραλέζικος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυστραλέζικη, neuter αυστραλέζικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Australian (relating to Australia or its people)</div><b>αυστραλιανός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυστραλιανή, neuter αυστραλιανό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Australian (relating to Australia or its people)</div><b>αυστριακός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυστριακή, neuter αυστριακό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Austrian (relating to Austria or its people)</div><b>αυτ.</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://αυτόθι">αυτόθι</a>: ibid.</div><b>αυτά</b>
  <div><i>det</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αυτός">αυτός</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>pron</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (personal, pronoun, strong) they (3rd person neuter plural, nominative)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (personal, pronoun, strong) them (3rd person neuter plural, accusative)</div><b>αυτά μου φαίνονται κινέζικα</b>
  <div><i>phrase</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(idiomatic) it&#x27;s all Greek to me (literally, “this seems Chinese to me”)</div><b>αυτάδελφος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αυτάδελφοι, feminine αυταδέλφη or αυταδέλφισσα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(rare) brother-german, full-brother</div><b>αυτάρεσκος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυτάρεσκη, neuter αυτάρεσκο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>smug, self-satisfied, vain</div><b>αυτάρκεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) self-sufficiency, independence; autarky, autarchy</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek αὐτάρκεια.</div><b>αυτάρκης</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυτάρκης, neuter αύταρκες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>self-sufficient</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek αὐτάρκης. By surface analysis, αυτ- (αυτο-) (aft- (afto-)) + αρκώ, αρκ- + -ης (-is)</div><b>αυτή</b>
  <div><i>det, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative feminine singular of <a href="bword://αυτός">αυτός</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek αὐτή.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>pron</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (personal, pronoun, strong) she (3rd person feminine singular, nominative)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. alternative form of αυτήν</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek αὐτή.</div><b>αυτή τη στιγμή</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>right now, at the moment, on the spot</div><b>αυτήκοος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυτήκοη, neuter αυτήκοο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. overheard (especially by oneself), earwitnessed</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αυτήκοος</b> μάρτυρας - eye witness</div>
  <div class='def'>2. earwitness</div><b>αυτί</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αυτιά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αφτί">αφτί</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> See αφτί.</div><b>αυταδέλφη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αυταδέλφες, masculine αυτάδελφος)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(rare) sister-german, full-sister</div><b>αυταδέλφισσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αυταδέλφισσες, masculine αυτάδελφος)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(rare) sister-german, full-sister</div><b>αυτανάφλεξη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (countable and uncountable, plural αυταναφλέξεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(countable, uncountable) autoignition, spontaneous combustion</div><b>αυταπάρνηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αυταπαρνήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable, usually) self-denial, self-abnegation</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable, usually) altruism</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from αὐταπάρνησις (Katharevousa)</div><b>αυταπάτη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αυταπάτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>self-deception, delusion</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αυτό + απάτη</div><b>αυταπατώμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be deluded/fooled</div><b>αυταπόδεικτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυταπόδεικτη, neuter αυταπόδεικτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>self-evident, axiomatic</div><b>αυταπόδειχτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυταπόδειχτη, neuter αυταπόδειχτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αυταπόδεικτος">αυταπόδεικτος</a></div><b>αυταρέσκεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αυταρέσκειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable, usually) smugness, pride, vanity</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable, usually) self-satisfaction, self-complacency</div><b>αυταρχία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αυταρχίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. absolute sovereignty, independence, autarky</div>
  <div class='def'>2. autarchy, autocracy, absolutism, despotism, authoritarian rule</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek αὐταρχία, partially a semantic loan from French autocratie via Ancient Greek αὐτοκρατής.</div><b>αυταρχικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυταρχική, neuter αυταρχικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>autocratic</div><b>αυταρχικότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(indeclinable) bossiness, imperiousness</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αυταρχικός + -ότητα. First attested 1892.</div><b>αυταρχισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αυταρχισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>autocracy, despotism</div><b>αυτασφάλεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αυτασφάλειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) self-insurance</div><b>αυτασφάλιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αυτασφάλισες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) self-insurance</div><b>αυτενέργεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αυτενέργειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>self-action, self-motion, self-activity</div><b>αυτενεργός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυτενεργή, neuter αυτενεργό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. self-acting, self-activating</div>
  <div class='def'>2. automatic</div><b>αυτενεργώ</b>
