  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://αυτόματος">αυτόματος</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative plural of <a href="bword://αυτόματο">αυτόματο</a></div><b>αυτόματες ταμειακές μηχανές</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative plural of αυτόματη ταμειακή <a href="bword://μηχανή">μηχανή</a></div><b>αυτόματες ταμειολογιστικές μηχανές</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative plural of αυτόματη ταμειολογιστική <a href="bword://μηχανή">μηχανή</a></div><b>αυτόματη ταμειακή μηχανή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αυτόματες ταμειακές μηχανές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>automated teller machine, automatic teller machine</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αυτόματος + ταμειακός + μηχανή.</div><b>αυτόματη ταμειολογιστική μηχανή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αυτόματες ταμειολογιστικές μηχανές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of αυτόματη ταμειακή <a href="bword://μηχανή">μηχανή</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From αυτόματος + ταμείο + λογιστικός + μηχανή.</div><b>αυτόματο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αυτόματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>automatic weapon, machine gun</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. accusative masculine singular of <a href="bword://αυτόματος">αυτόματος</a></div>
  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://αυτόματος">αυτόματος</a></div><b>αυτόματος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυτόματη, neuter αυτόματο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>automatic</div><b>αυτόμολος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυτόμολη, neuter αυτόμολο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (dated) describing a defector or their actions</div>
  <div class='def'>2. a defector, a deserter</div><b>αυτόνομος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυτόνομη, neuter αυτόνομο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. autonomous, self-governing</div>
  <div class='def'>2. standalone</div><b>αυτόπτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural αυτόπτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>eyewitness</div><b>αυτός</b>
  <div><i>det, masculine (demonstrative determiner, feminine αυτή, neuter αυτό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(demonstrative, determiner) this (masculine singular, nominative)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek αὐτός.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>pron</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (demonstrative, pronoun) this</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αυτό</b> εδώ - this one</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (personal, pronoun) he (3rd person masculine singular, nominative)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (demonstrative, pronoun) that</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αυτό</b> εκεί - that one</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek αὐτός.</div><b>αυτόφυτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυτόφυτη, neuter αυτόφυτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. self-sown, volunteer</div>
  <div class='def'>2. natural, wild</div><b>αυτόφωρο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αυτόφωρα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>all day special court sitting, proceeding trial, of persons caught in the act</div><b>αυτόφωρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυτόφωρη, neuter αυτόφωρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>flagrant, caught in the act</div><b>αυτόφωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυτόφωτη, neuter αυτόφωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. self-illuminated, self-illuminous, with intellectual light of one&#x27;s own</div>
  <div class='def'>2. not relying on external influences</div><b>αυτόχειρας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural αυτόχειρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>suicide (the person)</div><b>αυτόχθονας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural αυτόχθονες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. autochthon, an early inhabitant of a country</div>
  <div class='def'>2. an indigenous person, native</div>
  <div class='def'>3. an indigenous animal or plant</div>
  <div class='def'>4. a person born and living in the place of his ancestors</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek αὐτόχθων, from αὐτός + χθών.</div><b>αυτόχθων</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυτόχθων, neuter αυτόχθον)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>indigenous, native, aboriginal</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek αὐτόχθων.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural αυτόχθονες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. autochthon, an early inhabitant of a country</div>
  <div class='def'>2. an indigenous person, native</div>
  <div class='def'>3. an indigenous animal or plant</div>
  <div class='def'>4. a person born and living in the place of his ancestors</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek αὐτόχθων.</div><b>αυτόχρημα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>literally, altogether, positively</div><b>αυτώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (colloquial) to do (in general, which the speaker doesn&#x27;t know or as a placeholder term)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Όλη μέρα καθαρίζει, μαγειρεύει, <b>αυτώνει</b>, δεν σταματάει καθόλου. - All day she cleans, cooks, does God-knows-what, she doesn&#x27;t stop at all.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (colloquial, euphemistic) as a euphemism for <a href="bword://γαμώ">γαμώ</a> or other vulgar verbs</div>
  <div class='ex'>Την <b>αύτωσε</b> κι έφυγε. - He you-know-whatted her and left.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αυτό + -ώνω.</div><b>αυχάριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυχάριστη, neuter αυχάριστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αχάριστος">αχάριστος</a></div><b>αυχένας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αυχένες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. nape of neck</div>
  <div class='def'>2. saddle, col (between two hills)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From the Ancient Greek αὐχήν.</div><b>αυχενικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυχενική, neuter αυχενικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>cervical, relating to the nape/neck</div><b>αυχμηρός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αυχμηρή, neuter αυχμηρό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (archaic) harsh, rough</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (archaic) parched, arid</div><b>αφ&#x27;</b>
  <div><i>prep</i></div>
  <div class='def'>contraction of <a href="bword://από">από</a></div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αφ’</b> ενός … <b>αφ’</b> ετέρου … - on the one hand … on the other …</div><b>αφάγωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφάγωτη, neuter αφάγωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. fasting (being without food)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. uneaten</div><b>αφάνα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αφάνες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>broom (plant)</div><b>αφάνεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αφάνειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable, usually) obscurity</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable, usually) oblivion</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀφάνεια</div><b>αφάνταστα</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>neuter nominative/accusative/vocative plural of <a href="bword://αφάνταστος">αφάνταστος</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unimaginably</div><b>αφάνταστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφάνταστη, neuter αφάνταστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unimaginable</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Koine Greek ἀφάνταστος. By surface analysis, α- (a-) + φάντασ-) + -τος (-tos).</div><b>αφάσκιωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφάσκιωτη, neuter αφάσκιωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unswaddled</div><b>αφέγγαρος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφέγγαρη, neuter αφέγγαρο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial) moonless (lacking moonlight)</div><b>αφέλεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αφέλειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. naivety, innocence</div>
  <div class='def'>2. childishness</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (in plural) fringe (UK), bang (US)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀφέλεια.</div><b>αφέντης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αφέντες or αφεντάδες, feminine αφέντρα or αφέντισσα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. master, boss</div>
  <div class='def'>2. ruler, prince</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀφέντης, from Ancient Greek αὐθέντης.</div><b>αφέντισσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αφέντισσες, masculine αφέντης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>boss, mistress</div><b>αφέντρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αφέντρες, masculine αφέντης)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>boss, mistress</div><b>αφέτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αφέτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>starter (person who starts a race)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀφέτης, from ἀφίημι.</div><b>αφέψημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αφεψήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>herbal, chamomile or other tea</div>
  <div class='ex'>Σερβίρουμε χαμομήλι και άλλα αφεψήματα. - We serve chamomile and other herbal teas.</div><b>αφή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αφές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>touch (sense and sensation)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἁφή, from ἅπτω.</div><b>αφήγημα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αφηγήματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>narrative (the systematic recitation of an event or series of events)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀφήγημα with semantic loan from French récit. By surface analysis, αφήγη-) + -μα (-ma).</div><b>αφήγηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αφηγήσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>narration, account</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀφήγησῐς, from Ancient Greek ἀφηγέομαι, from ἀφ- (aph-) + ἡγέομαι.</div><b>αφήλιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αφήλια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>aphelion</div><b>αφήνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to leave, allow, let, let go, let go of, drop, drop off, abandon</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>άφησε</b> το μολύβι του να πέσει στο πάτωμα - he let the pencil fall to the floor</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From the mediaeval Byzantine Greek ἀφήνω, a metaplasm of the ancient aorist ἄφησα of ἀφίημι.</div><b>αφίδρωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αφιδρώσηεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sweat, perspiration</div><b>αφίλευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφίλευτη, neuter αφίλευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not shown hospitality, not treated</div><b>αφίλητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφίλητη, neuter αφίλητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unkissed, not kissed</div><b>αφίλιωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφίλιωτη, neuter αφίλιωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unreconciled</div>
  <div class='def'>2. irreconcilable, unreconcilable (rare)</div><b>αφίμωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφίμωτη, neuter αφίμωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>not muzzled, unsilenced</div><b>αφίππευση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αφιππεύσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>dismounting</div><b>αφίσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αφίσες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>poster, bill</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αφίσα</b> θεάτρου - theatre poster</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From French affiche.</div><b>αφίσσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αφίσσες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αφίσα">αφίσα</a></div><b>αφίσταμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to distance (oneself), to stand away</div><b>αφαίμαξη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αφαίμαξες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (dated) blood-letting, bleeding</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) draining a resource</div><b>αφαίρεση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αφαιρέσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. subtraction</div>
  <div class='def'>2. removal, elimination, withdrawal</div>
  <div class='def'>3. abstraction</div><b>αφαγία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αφαγίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. fasting, dieting</div>
  <div class='def'>2. starvation</div><b>αφαιμάσσω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to bleed to draw blood</div><b>αφαιμαξομετάγγιση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αφαιμαξομεταγγίσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>exchange transfusion (exsanguination followed by transfusion)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> αφαίμαξη + μετάγγιση</div><b>αφαιρέτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αφαιρέτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>subtrahend (to be removed)</div><b>αφαιρεμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφαιρεμένη, neuter αφαιρεμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. absent minded</div>
  <div class='def'>2. abstract</div><b>αφαιρετέος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφαιρετέα, neuter αφαιρετέο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>subtrahend (to be removed)</div><b>αφαιρετική</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αφαιρετικές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(ablative) ablative</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αφαιρετική</b> πτώση - ablative case</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀφαιρετική.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative feminine singular of <a href="bword://αφαιρετικός">αφαιρετικός</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀφαιρετική.</div><b>αφαιρετικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφαιρετική, neuter αφαιρετικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. abstract</div>
  <div class='def'>2. subtractive</div><b>αφαιρετός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφαιρετή, neuter αφαιρετό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to be removed, removable</div>
  <div class='def'>2. subtrahend</div><b>αφαιρώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to subtract, reduce, remove</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to deprive</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to cut someone off, interrupt (prevent someone from speaking further)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Κύριε Σμιθ, σας <b>αφαιρώ</b> το λόγο. - Mr. Smith, I&#x27;m going to interrupt you.</div>
  <div class='def'>4. to subtract</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀφαιρέω. Morphologically αφ- (af-) + αιρώ.</div><b>αφακέλωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφακέλωτη, neuter αφακέλωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unfiled, undocumented</div>
  <div class='def'>2. without a record or file with the security services</div><b>αφαλάτωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αφαλατώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>desalination</div><b>αφαλατώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to desalinate</div><b>αφαλοκόβω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (colloquial) to cut the umbilical cord</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (colloquial, figuratively) to rupture myself (lifting a heavy weight)</div><b>αφαλός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αφαλοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (colloquial) navel</div>
  <div class='def'>2. hub (of wheel)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ὀμφαλός, from Proto-Indo-European *h₃m̥bʰ-, a variant of *h₃nebʰ-. Doublet of ομφαλός.</div><b>αφανάτιστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφανάτιστη, neuter αφανάτιστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>dispassionate, not fanatical</div><b>αφανέρωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφανέρωτη, neuter αφανέρωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unseen, undisclosed, unrevealed</div><b>αφανής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφανής, neuter αφανές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>invisible</div><b>αφανίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(transitive) to annihilate, to destroy, to eradicate (to reduce to nothing; to cause to cease to exist)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀφανίζω.</div><b>αφανισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αφανισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. destruction, devastation</div>
  <div class='def'>2. extermination, extinction</div><b>αφανιστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφανιστική, neuter αφανιστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>destructive</div><b>αφαρπάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to blow away, to tear off</div><b>αφασία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αφασίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable, usually) aphasia, dysphasia</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable, usually) speechlessness</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively, uncountable, usually) with unpredictable reactions</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἀφασία</div><b>αφατρίαστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφατρίαστη, neuter αφατρίαστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>impartial, unbiased</div><b>αφγανικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφγανική, neuter αφγανικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Afghan, Afghani (relating to Afghanistan or its people)</div><b>αφεαυτού</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial) of one&#x27;s own accord</div><b>αφεγγής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφεγγής, neuter αφεγγές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://άφεγγος">άφεγγος</a></div><b>αφειδής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφειδής, neuter αφειδές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>generous, lavish, profuse</div><b>αφειδία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (countable and uncountable, plural αφειδίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(countable, literary, rare, uncountable) generosity, abundance</div><b>αφειδώλευτα</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>generously, unsparingly</div><b>αφειδώλευτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφειδώλευτη, neuter αφειδώλευτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>generous, lavish, profuse</div><b>αφειδώς</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(Katharevousa) lavishly</div><b>αφελής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφελής, neuter αφελές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>naive</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἀφελής.</div><b>αφελληνίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to dehellenise (UK), dehellenize (US)</div><b>αφελληνισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (usually uncountable, plural αφελληνισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) dehellenisation (UK), dehellenization (US)</div><b>αφεντάδικος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφεντάδικη, neuter αφεντάδικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial) bossy</div><b>αφεντάνθρωπος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αφεντάνθρωποι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(obsolete) nobleman</div><b>αφεντεύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to command, to control</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to rule</div><b>αφεντιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αφεντιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>eminence, nobility</div><b>αφεντικό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αφεντικά, feminine αφεντικίνα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. owner, master (someone who has control over something or someone)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το <b>αφεντικό</b> του σκύλου αυτού είναι ο αδερφός μου. - This dog&#x27;s owner is my brother.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. boss (person who oversees and directs the work of others)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το <b>αφεντικό</b> με βάζει πάντα να δουλεύω παράξενες ώρες. - The boss always makes me work odd hours.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (dated) boss, master (the head of a household particularly with regards to servants)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το <b>αφεντικό</b> έχει προσλάβει νέες υπηρέτριες. - The master has hired new maids.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀφεντικός, from Ancient Greek αὐθεντικός, from αὐθέντης.</div><b>αφεντικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφεντική, neuter αφεντικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>referring to the master, mistress or lord</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial, ironic) the boss</div><b>αφενός</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(literary) on the one hand</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned univerbation of αφ’ (af’) + ενός, genitive of ένας. Calque of French d&#x27;une part.</div><b>αφερέγγυος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφερέγγυα, neuter αφερέγγυο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. insolvent</div>
  <div class='ex'>, also see χρεωκοπημένος (chreokopiménos, “bankrupt”, participle)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. untrustworthy, unreliable</div><b>αφερεγγυότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (countable and uncountable, plural αφερεγγυότητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(countable, uncountable) insolvency</div><b>αφετέρου</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(literary) on the other hand</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from αφ’ (af’) + ἑτέρου, genitive of Ancient Greek ἕτερος. Calque of French d&#x27;autre part.</div><b>αφετηρία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αφετηρίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. startline, starting line</div>
  <div class='def'>2. point of departure, terminus</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) the start of something new</div><b>αφεύκτως</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>certainly, inescapably, inevitably, unavoidably</div><b>αφηγήτρια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αφηγήτριες, masculine αφηγητής)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>narrator, storyteller (one providing narrative) (chiefly in media contexts)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η <b>αφηγήτρια</b> πρέπει να έχει σταθερή και ζωντανή φωνή. - The narrator must have a calm and lively voice.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀφηγέομαι, from ἀφ- (aph-) + ἡγέομαι. First attested 1888.</div><b>αφηγημένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αφηγημένη, neuter αφηγημένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncommon) narrated, recounted</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αφηγούμαι, a verb only in the passive form.</div><b>αφηγηματικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφηγηματική, neuter αφηγηματικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>narrative</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αφηγηματικό</b> ποίημα - narrative poem</div><b>αφηγητής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αφηγητές, feminine αφηγήτρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>narrator, storyteller (one providing narrative) (chiefly in media contexts)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ο ταλαντούχος <b>αφηγητής</b> ζωνταντεύει το ντοκιμαντέρ. - The talented narrator brings the documentary to life.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ἀφηγητής, from Ancient Greek ἀφηγέομαι, from ἀφ- (aph-) + ἡγέομαι.</div><b>αφηγητικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφηγητική, neuter αφηγητικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. narratorly (in that style/fashion)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. narrative</div><b>αφηγούμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to tell, recount, relate</div><b>αφηνίαση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αφηνιάσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. rampage, fury</div>
  <div class='def'>2. bolting (horses)</div><b>αφηνιάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to bolt, to run away (horse, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to rampage, to run amok</div><b>αφηνιασμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αφηνιασμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. rampage, fury</div>
  <div class='def'>2. bolting (horses)</div><b>αφηρ.</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://αφηρημένος">αφηρημένος</a>: abstract</div><b>αφηρημάδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αφηρημάδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>absent-mindedness</div><b>αφηρημένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφηρημένη, neuter αφηρημένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. abstract</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αφηρημένη</b> τέχνη - abstract art</div>
  <div class='def'>2. absent-minded, preoccupied</div><b>αφθαρσία</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (usually uncountable, plural αφθαρσίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) indestructibility, imperishability</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἀφθαρσία.</div><b>αφθονία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) plenty, abundance, profusion</div><b>αφθονώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be plentiful or abundant, abound, teem</div><b>αφθονών</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφθονούσα, neuter αφθονόν)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abundant, plentiful</div><b>αφθόνητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφθόνητη, neuter αφθόνητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unenviable</div><b>αφθόνως</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abundantly, plentifully</div><b>αφθώδης</b>
