  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀφοπλισμός.</div><b>αφοπλιστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφοπλιστική, neuter αφοπλιστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (figuratively) disarming</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>αφοπλιστικό</b> χαμόγελο - disarming smile</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (literally) disarming</div>
  <div class='def'>3. unrigging</div><b>αφορά</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (intransitive, literary, transitive) to be concerning, to be about; [with <a href="bword://σε">σε</a> (se)]</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η διάσκεψη <b>αφορά σε</b> πολλά θέματα, κυρίως στην οικονομική κατάσταση. - The conference is about many issues, mainly about the economical situation.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (without <a href="bword://σε">σε</a> (se) ) to be concerning, to be about</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η διάσκεψη <b>αφορά</b> πολλά θέματα, κυρίως την οικονομική κατάσταση. - The conference is about many issues, mainly the economical situation.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (transitive) to concern</div>
  <div class='ex'>Δεν με <b>αφορά</b>! - It is none of my concern!</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Third persons from Ancient Greek ἀφοράω, ἀφορῶ. Morphologically, from αφ- (απο-) (prefix, here emphasizing) + the ancient ὁράω, ὁρῶ. Semantic loan from French regarder or concerner (en ce qui concerne)</div><b>αφορία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αφορίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(literary, uncountable, usually) infertility, unfruitfulness</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek αφορία.</div><b>αφορίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to excommunicate</div><b>αφορισμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αφορισμένη, neuter αφορισμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>excommunicated</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αφορίζομαι, passive voice of αφορίζω</div><b>αφορισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αφορισμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. aphorism</div>
  <div class='def'>2. excommunication</div><b>αφοριστικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφοριστική, neuter αφοριστικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. aphoristic</div>
  <div class='def'>2. excommunicative</div><b>αφορμάριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφορμάριστη, neuter αφορμάριστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. amorphous, shapeless, unformed</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unformatted</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) unfit (physically, metally)</div><b>αφορμή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αφορμές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. pretext, cause, reason, motive, excuse, occasion (surface/trigger event or circumstance)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Με <b>αφορμή</b> την εισβολή της Πολωνίας, η Βρετανία κήρυξε πόλεμο στην Γερμανία. - On the pretext of the invasion of Poland, Britain declared war on Germany.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. grudge, complaint (long-term animosity or ill will about something or someone)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Δεν έχω <b>αφορμή</b> μαζί του. - I have no grudge against him.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἀφορμή, from ἀφ’ (aph’) / ἀπό + ὁρμή.</div><b>αφορμίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to fester, to become septic</div><b>αφορολόγητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>duty-free goods</div><b>αφορολόγητο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural αφορολόγητα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>tax exemption or relief</div><b>αφορολόγητος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφορολόγητη, neuter αφορολόγητο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>untaxed, tax-free, duty-free</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From α- (a-, “not”) + φορολογώ. See φορολογία for more.</div><b>αφορώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>only used in <a href="bword://αφορά">αφορά</a> (occurs in 3rd person, also impersonal)</div><b>αφοσίωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αφοσιώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>devotion, faithfulness, dedication</div><b>αφοσιωμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αφοσιωμένη, neuter αφοσιωμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. devoted</div>
  <div class='def'>2. faithful, attached</div>
  <div class='def'>3. absorbed (in doing something)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect participle of αφοσιώνομαι, a verb with passive forms only.</div><b>αφοσιώνομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to devote oneself (+<a href="bword://σε">σε</a>: to)</div><b>αφουγκράζομαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (colloquial) to listen attentively</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (colloquial) to eavesdrop</div><b>αφουγκράστρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αφουγκράστρες, masculine αφουγκραστής)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>evesdropper</div><b>αφουγκραστής</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural αφουγκραστές, feminine αφουγκράστρα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>evesdropper</div><b>αφού</b>
