  <div class='def'>1. after (having done something)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. since</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἀφοῦ, from Koine Greek ἀφ’ (aph’) and οὗ, from Ancient Greek ἀπό and οὗ.</div><b>αφούντωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφούντωτη, neuter αφούντωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. bare, unleafy, not leafy (tree, plant)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. not blazing (lamp, light)</div><b>αφράτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφράτη, neuter αφράτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>soft, frothy, foamy</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek ἀφράτος, from the ancient ἀφρ(ός), “foam”) + -άτος.</div><b>αφρίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to foam, to froth, to fizz</div><b>αφρεσκάριστος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφρεσκάριστη, neuter αφρεσκάριστο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unfreshened, ungroomed</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unrefreshed</div><b>αφρικάανς</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(indeclinable) Afrikaans (a language of South Africa)</div><b>αφρικάνικος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφρικάνικη, neuter αφρικάνικο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://αφρικανικός">αφρικανικός</a></div><b>αφρικανικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφρικανική, neuter αφρικανικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>African, relating to Africa.</div><b>αφρικανός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine αφρικανή, neuter αφρικανό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(rare) African (pertaining to Africa, its people or languages)</div><b>αφρισμένος</b>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine αφρισμένη, neuter αφρισμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. foamy</div>
  <div class='ex'>τα <b>αφρισμένα</b> κύματα της θάλασσας, <b>αφρισμένη</b> θάλασσα - the foamy waves of the sea, foamy sea</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) foaming, frenzied</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Perfect passive participle of αφρίζω, a verb with no passive forms.</div><b>αφρογέννητος</b>
