  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Back-formation from the plural αφτιά, extracted from article &amp; noun τ’ αφτιά, from Byzantine Greek τά ἀφτία), from Koine Greek τά ὠτία), diminutive of Ancient Greek τᾰ̀ ὦτᾰ), through a regular phonological development of
: /ta.uˈti.a/ → (*/tavˈti.a/) → /tafˈti.a/ and αφτιά /aˈftça/, singular αφτί /aˈfti/.
Ultimately from Proto-Indo-European *h₂ṓws.
Etymology according to Georgios Hatzidakis, accepted by Babiniotis. Other linguists support the spelling αυτί from τ’ αυτιά through /tawˈti.a/ - /tafˈti.a/. Similar case is the spelling of αβγό or αυγό.</div><b>αφτιάζομαι</b>
