  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Byzantine Greek ἀψιθία with synizesis of /ia/ to avoid hiatus, from Koine Greek ἀψινθία f with assimilation of [nθ] &gt; [θθ] and simplification [θθ] &gt; [θ]. Also see ἀψίνθιον.</div><b>αψιθυμία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αψιθυμίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) irascibility, irritability, tetchiness</div><b>αψιλία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural αψιλίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(colloquial, uncountable, usually) pennilessness, lack of money</div><b>αψιμαχία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural αψιμαχίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>skirmish, a low-level engagement</div><b>αψιμαχώ</b>
