  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural βανίλιες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. vanilla (food flavouring)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. vanilla (orchid)</div><b>βανίλλια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural βανίλλιες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://βανίλια">βανίλια</a></div><b>βανδαλίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>To vandalise.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> By surface analysis, βάνδαλος + -ίζω.</div><b>βανιλίνη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural βανιλίνες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>vanillin</div><b>βαπτίζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to baptise (UK), baptize (US), christen</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek βαπτίζω.</div><b>βαπτιστικός</b>
