  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) biochemistry (biological chemistry)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From French biochimie. By surface analysis, βίος + χημεία.</div><b>βιοχημικός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural βιοχημικοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>biochemist</div><b>βιρύλλιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>misspelling of <a href="bword://βηρύλλιο">βηρύλλιο</a></div><b>βισμούθιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) bismuth</div><b>βιταμίνη</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural βιταμίνες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>vitamin</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>βιταμίνη</b> C - vitamin C</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> French vitamine</div><b>βιτρίνα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural βιτρίνες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. shop window</div>
  <div class='def'>2. showcase, display cabinet</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) showcase (event carefully arranged to give good impression)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From French vitrine (“display cabinet, shop window”).</div><b>βιωσιμότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) sustainability, viability</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From βιώσιμος + -ότητα. Calque of English viability.</div><b>βιόλα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural βιόλες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. viola</div>
  <div class='def'>2. gillyflower, wallflower</div>
  <div class='ex'>μαραμένα τα γιούλια κι οι <b>βιόλες</b>. - Withered violets and gillyflowers.</div><b>βιόσφαιρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural βιόσφαιρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>biosphere</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from French biosphère from bio- &lt; Ancient Greek βιο- + -sphère &lt; Ancient Greek σφαῖρα Morphologically, from βιο- + -σφαιρα.</div><b>βιώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(transitive) to experience</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from Ancient Greek βι(ῶ)) + -ώνω, with semantic loan from German erleben.</div><b>βιώσιμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine βιώσιμη, neuter βιώσιμος)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>viable</div>
