  <div class='def'>(rare) colon ( : )</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> διπλή + στιγμή</div><b>διπλή τελεία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural διπλές τελείες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(rare) colon ( : )</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> διπλή + τελεία</div><b>διπλανή</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative feminine singular of <a href="bword://διπλανός">διπλανός</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural διπλανές, masculine διπλανός)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>next-door neighbour (who lives on either side of me)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Οι <b>διπλανές</b> κάνουν πάρτι. - The neighbours are having a party.</div><b>διπλανός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine διπλανή, neuter διπλανό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>next, next-door, adjacent, adjoining, neighbouring (being on the left or right)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Ο <b>διπλανός</b> τοίχος είναι από ατσάλι. - The adjoining wall is made of steel.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> δίπλα + -νός.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural διπλανοί, feminine διπλανή)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>next-door neighbour (who lives on either side of me)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Οι <b>διπλανοί</b> καβγαδίζουν πάλι. - The neighbours are quarreling again.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> δίπλα + -νός.</div><b>διπλασιάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to double</div><b>διπλασιασμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural διπλασιασμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. doubling (multiply by two)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. gemination</div><b>διπλογραφία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural διπλογραφίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>double-entry book keeping</div><b>διπλοκατοικία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural διπλοκατοικίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>duplex</div><b>διπλοσάγονο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural διπλοσάγονα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>double chin</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From διπλός + σαγόνι with διπλ(ός)) + -ο- (-o-) + σαγόν(ι)) + -ο (-o).</div><b>διπλοσάϊνο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural διπλοσάϊνα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>northern goshawk (Astur gentilis)</div><b>διπλωματία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. diplomacy (the art and practice of conducting international relations)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. diplomacy (tact and subtle skill in dealing with people so as to avoid or settle hostility)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from French diplomatie with -ία suffix.</div><b>διπλόποδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>The Diplopoda, the diplopods or millipedes.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from translingual Diplopoda.</div><b>διπλόποδο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural διπλόποδα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>diplopod, millipede</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Back-formation from διπλόποδα, from translingual Diplopoda.</div><b>διπλός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine διπλή, neuter διπλό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>twofold, double, dual, dual purpose</div>
