  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative plural of <a href="bword://δίπλωμα">δίπλωμα</a> οδήγησης</div><b>διπλώνεται</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>third-person singular present indicative of διπλώνομαι, the passive of <a href="bword://διπλώνω">διπλώνω</a></div><b>διπλώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to fold, to fold in two, to fold over (bend (any thin material) over so that it comes in contact with itself)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From διπλός + -ώνω.</div><b>διπροσωπία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural διπροσωπίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>duplicity</div><b>δις</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>twice</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek δίς, from Proto-Hellenic *dwís, from Proto-Indo-European *dwís.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>abbreviation of <a href="bword://δεσποινίς">δεσποινίς</a>: Miss, Ms</div><b>δισδιάστατος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine δισδιάστατη, neuter δισδιάστατο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>two-dimensional</div><b>δισεκατομμύριο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural δισεκατομμύρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. billion, thousand million (10⁹)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (British, obsolete) billion, million million (10¹²)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Exact calque of French billion, with the wrong bi- (“bi-, twice”) corresponding to δίς and million to εκατομμύριο. Thus literally &quot;two million&quot;. The mathematically correct formation would be χίλια + εκατομμύριο. Attested in 1871. Compare to the ancient δισχίλιος and δισμύριος”).</div><b>δισκέτα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural δισκέτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>floppy disk</div><b>δισκίο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural δισκία)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>tablet, pill, caplet</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Diminutive of δίσκος.</div><b>δισκοβόλος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural δισκοβόλοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>discus thrower</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek δισκοβόλος.</div><b>δισκογραφία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural δισκογραφίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>discography</div><b>δισκοπρίονο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural δισκοπρίονα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>circular saw (disk shaped power saw)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> δίσκος + πριόνι</div><b>διστάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to hesitate, waver, pause</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek διστάζω.</div><b>δισταγμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural δισταγμοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>hesitation</div><b>διστακτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine διστακτική, neuter διστακτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>hesitant, timid</div>
