  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ημερολόγια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. calendar (system for calculating days of the year)</div>
  <div class='ex'>σεληνιακό ημερολόγιο, Γρηγοριανό ημερολόγιο, κλπ (lunar calendar, Gregorian calendar, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. calendar (wall chart showing months day-by-day)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. diary, journal (personal daily record of someone&#x27;s life)</div>
  <div class='def'>4. ledger, journal (daily record of financial transactions)</div>
  <div class='ex'>το ημερολόγιο της Άννας Φρανκ (the diary of Anne Frank)</div>
  <div class='def'>5. ship&#x27;s log</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> By surface analysis, ἡμέρα + -ο- (-o-) + -λόγιο.</div><b>ημερομίσθιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ημερομίσθια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. a day&#x27;s pay</div>
  <div class='def'>2. low pay</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (broadly) a day&#x27;s work</div><b>ημερομίσθιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>relating to day labourer (UK), day laborer (UK)</div><b>ημερομηνία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ημερομηνίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>date (a specific day)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Since 1833 as ἡμερομηνία at the Greek codices From ημερο- (imero-) + μήν(ας))) + -ία, possibly modeled after the ancient νουμηνία.</div><b>ημερονύκτιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ημερονύκτια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>24 hours, a day and a night</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From ημέρα + νύχτα.</div><b>ημερονύχτιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ημερονύχτια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ημερονύκτιο">ημερονύκτιο</a></div><b>ημερόβιος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ημερόβιη, neuter ημερόβιο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. ephemeral, short-lived</div>
  <div class='def'>2. lasting one day</div><b>ημερότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) gentleness, tameness</div><b>ημερώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to domesticate, tame, break in</div><b>ημιαστέρας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ημιαστέρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>quasar</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ημι- (imi-, “quasi-”) + αστέρας, calque of English quasar, from quasi-stellar radio source</div><b>ημιεπαγγελματικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ημιεπαγγελματική, neuter ημιεπαγγελματικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>semi-professional</div><b>ημιευθεία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ημιευθείες)</i></div>
