  <div class='def'>heroism</div><b>ηρωοποιώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to heroise (UK), heroize (US)</div><b>ησυχάζω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to settle down, quieten down</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to calm down, appease (someone)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek ἡσυχάζω.</div><b>ησυχία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) calm, peace, quiet (absence of trouble or problems)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Θέλω να κάτσω με την <b>ησυχία</b> μου και να διαβάσω. - I want to sit in peace and read.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) quiet, silence (absence of noise)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Επιτέλους <b>ησυχία</b> τώρα που τελείωσε αυτή η παρέλαση. - Finally, there&#x27;s peace now that the parade is over.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἡσυχία.
Cognate with Mariupol Greek йих (jix).</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>intj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>quiet, silence, be quiet</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Ησυχία</b>, παρακαλώ, αρχίζει η παράσταση. - Quiet, please, the show is starting.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἡσυχία.
Cognate with Mariupol Greek йих (jix).</div><b>ηττοπάθεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (usually uncountable, plural ηττοπάθειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable, usually) defeatism</div>
