  <div class='def'>2. property</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η <b>ιδιοκτησία</b> είναι κλοπή. - Property is theft.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned formation from ιδιο- (idio-) + -κτησία, formed as a calque of German Eigenbesitz.</div><b>ιδιομορφία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ιδιομορφίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. particularity, peculiarity, singularity (the state of being particular, peculiar, singular, distinct)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. particularity, peculiarity, specific feature (a distinctive characteristic or quality)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from ιδιόμορφ(ος)) + -ία.</div><b>ιδιοσυγκρασία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ιδιοσυγκρασίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. idiosyncrasy, distinctive characteristic, temperament</div>
  <div class='def'>2. idiosyncrasy (personal physiological properties)</div><b>ιδιοτέλεια</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ιδιοτέλειες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>selfishness, self-interest</div><b>ιδιοτελής</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ιδιοτελής, neuter ιδιοτελές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>selfish, self-seeking</div><b>ιδιοφυής</b>
