  <div class='def'>1. private, intimate, personal</div>
  <div class='def'>2. private (not public, e.g. of a school, etc.)</div><b>ιδιωτικότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ιδιωτικότητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>privacy</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From ιδιωτικ(ός), “private”) + -ότητα.</div><b>ιδιόμορφος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ιδιόμορφη, neuter ιδιόμορφο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. particular, peculiar, singular (distinctive; characteristic of a specific person or thing)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Near-synonyms: ιδιόρρυθμος (idiórrythmos), ιδιότυπος (idiótypos)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. idiomorphous</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ἰδιόμορφος.</div><b>ιδιότητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ιδιότητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. property, quality, characteristic; a feature or attribute common to members of the same class</div>
  <div class='ex'>Οι φυσικές και χημικές <b>ιδιότητες</b> των σωμάτων.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (of persons) capacity, status, role from which rights, duties, or authority derive</div>
  <div class='ex'>Μίλησε με την <b>ιδιότητα</b> του εκλεγμένου αντιπροσώπου.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἰδιότης. By surface analysis, ίδιος + -ότητα.</div><b>ιδιώτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ιδιώτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. private individual</div>
  <div class='def'>2. person with learning difficulties, mentally handicapped person</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἰδιώτης. Sense 2 is a semantic loan from French idiot.</div><b>ιδρυτής</b>
