  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to be established, founded</div><b>ιδρύω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to found, establish (a city, society, institution)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncommon) to erect (a building of importance)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἱδρύω.</div><b>ιδρώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to sweat, to perspire</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Cf. ιδρώτας, Ancient Greek ἱδρόω, ἱδρώς.</div><b>ιδρώτας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ιδρώτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sweat, perspiration</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Byzantine Greek ἱδρώτας, from Ancient Greek ἱδρώς.</div><b>ιεράκιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ιεράκια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>hawkweed (Hieracium)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek ἱερᾱ́κῐον, with a semantic loan from translingual Hieracium.</div><b>ιεράρχης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ιεράρχες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. a high priest</div>
  <div class='def'>2. hierarch</div>
