  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ιερός + -άρχης from Hellenistic Koine ἱεράρχης</div><b>ιερέας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural ιερείς, feminine ιέρεια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. clergyman (any rank in the Orthodox Church)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. priest or minister (of any religion)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ἱερεύς.</div><b>ιερακοτρόφος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ιερακοτρόφοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>falconer</div><b>ιεραρχία</b>
