  <div class='def'>1. drone (male bee)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (figuratively) parasite, freeloader</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From the Ancient Greek κηφήν.</div><b>κι έζησαν αυτοί καλά κι εμείς καλύτερα</b>
  <div><i>phrase</i></div>
  <div class='def'>they lived happily ever after (used at the end of fairy tales)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Literally, “and they lived happily, and we, even better”</div><b>κι αν</b>
  <div><i>phrase</i></div>
  <div class='def'>even if, whatever</div><b>κι η κουτσή Μαρία</b>
  <div><i>phrase</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(idiomatic) everyone and their mother, the whole world and his dog (everyone)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το ότι απατά τη γυναίκα του το ξέρει <b>κι η κουτσή Μαρία</b>. - Everyone and their mother knows that he is cheating on his wife.</div><b>κιάλι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. scope, telescope, spyglass, field glass; a portable optical instrument containing a lens used for magnification to see distant objects</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (in plural) See κιάλια.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from Italian occhiali (“eyeglasses”), the apheresis perhaps resulting via crasis of article το (to) with an earlier Byzantine Greek ὀκκιάλιν.</div><b>κιβωτός</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural κιβωτοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. ark, Ark (Ark of the Covenant)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. ark, Ark (Noah&#x27;s Ark)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. ark (something affording protection, especially to a spiritual tradition)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek κιβωτός with biblical senses from Koine Greek.</div><b>κιβώτια ταχυτήτων</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative plural of <a href="bword://κιβώτιο">κιβώτιο</a> ταχυτήτων</div><b>κιβώτιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural κιβώτια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. box, crate, case, container</div>
  <div class='def'>2. trunk</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from Ancient Greek κιβώτιον.</div><b>κιβώτιο ταχυτήτων</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural κιβώτια ταχυτήτων)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>gearbox</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Calque of French boîte de vitesses.</div><b>κιγκλίδωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural κιγκλιδώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. railing</div>
  <div class='def'>2. guardrail</div>
  <div class='def'>3. balustrade</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from κιγκλίδ(α)) + -ωμα (-oma), a loose calque of French grillage.</div><b>κιθάρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural κιθάρες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>guitar</div>
