  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek μέλισσα.
Compare Mariupol Greek мелы́ш, милиш.</div><b>μέλλον</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural μέλλοντα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. the future</div>
  <div class='ex'>στο εγγύς <b>μέλλον</b> - in the near future</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (broadly) a promising future</div>
  <div class='ex'>Αυτή η εφεύρεση έχει <b>μέλλον</b>. - This invention has a future.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Originally the neuter gender of the adjective μέλλων.</div><b>μέλλοντας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural μέλλοντες)</i></div>
