  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural μέλλοντες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(dated, formal) older form of <a href="bword://μέλλοντας">μέλλοντας</a>: &quot;future (tense)&quot;</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek μέλλων. Present participle of μέλλω, see 3rd person μέλλει. The masculine and neuter μέλλον, also substantivised.</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>participle, masculine (feminine μέλλουσα, neuter μέλλον)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>future, forthcoming, to-be</div>
  <div class='ex'>οι <b>μέλλουσες</b> γενεές - the future generations</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek μέλλων. Present participle of μέλλω, see 3rd person μέλλει. The masculine and neuter μέλλον, also substantivised.</div><b>μέλος</b>
