  <div class='def'>mentor (friendly adviser)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek Μέντωρ.</div><b>μένω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (intransitive) to stay, reside, live (somewhere)</div>
  <div class='ex'>δε <b>μένω</b> πια εδώ - I don&#x27;t live here anymore</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (copulative) to stay, remain (in a condition)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>μένω</b> ανύπαντρος - I remain single</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (intransitive) to remain, be left over see: μένει (3rd person, impersonal)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Δε <b>μένει</b> τίποτα να πούμε. - There is nothing left to be said.</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (transitive) to fail (examination)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Ancient Greek μένω, from Proto-Indo-European *men-.</div><b>μέρα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural μέρες)</i></div>
