  <div class='def'>fatalism</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from μοιρολάτρ(ης)) + -ία.</div><b>μοιρολατρικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine μοιρολατρική, neuter μοιρολατρικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fatalistic</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from μοιρολάτρ(ης)) + -ικός.</div><b>μοιρολογώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to mourn, wail</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to sing a lament</div><b>μοιρολόγι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural μοιρολόγια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://μοιρολόι">μοιρολόι</a></div><b>μοιρολόι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural μοιρολόγια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>lament, dirge (a mournful poem or piece of music composed or performed as a memorial to a dead person)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Inherited from Byzantine Greek μοιρολόγιον, from μοιρολογ(ώ)) + -ιον (-ion).</div><b>μοιχεία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural μοιχείες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>adultery</div><b>μολ</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (indeclinable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(indeclinable) mole (the SI unit quantifying matter)</div><b>μολδαβικά</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter plural</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Moldovian (language)</div><b>μολδαβικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine μολδαβική, neuter μολδαβικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Moldovan, Moldavian (relating to Moldova or its people or language)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Μολδαβία + -ικός.</div><b>μολογάω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://ομολογώ">ομολογώ</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From the mediaeval Byzantine Greek μολογῶ, from Koine Greek ὁμολογῶ, contracted form of ὁμολογέω.</div><b>μολογήθηκα</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of ομολογήθηκα</div>
  <div class='ex'>first-person singular simple past of μολογιέμαι (mologiémai), the passive of μολογάω (mologáo) and μολογώ (mologó)</div><b>μολογιέμαι</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
