  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://μολυβδαίνιο">μολυβδαίνιο</a></div><b>μολυβδαίνιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) molybdenum</div><b>μολυσίτης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (countable and uncountable, plural μολυσίτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(countable, uncountable) ferric chloride</div><b>μολυσματικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine μολυσματική, neuter μολυσματικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. infectious (caused by an agent that enters the host&#x27;s body)</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>μολυσματική</b> αρρώστια - infectious disease</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (rare) infectious (able to infect others; capable of transmitting pathogens)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from the μολυσματ- stem of μόλυσμα + -ικός, adapted to the meaning of μόλυνση.</div><b>μολόγησα</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of ομολόγησα</div>
  <div class='ex'>first-person singular simple past of μολογάω (mologáo) and μολογώ (mologó): &quot;I confessed, I admitted, I said&quot;</div><b>μολύβι</b>
