  <div class='def'>2. eyeliner</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (colloquial) bullets</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From a derivative of Ancient Greek μόλυβδος.</div><b>μονάδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural μονάδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. unit of measurement, charge unit</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unit</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Μονάδα</b> Εντατικής Θεραπείας - Intensive Care Unit</div>
  <div class='def'>3. point (in scoring)</div>
  <div class='def'>4. lowest grade</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek μονάς.</div><b>μονάρχης</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural μονάρχες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>monarch</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek μονάρχης; equivalent to μόνος + -άρχης.
Compare Mariupol Greek мона́рхус.</div><b>μονή</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural μονές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>monastery, nunnery, convent</div>
