  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://μόνιμα">μόνιμα</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek μονί̆μως.</div><b>μοναδικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine μοναδική, neuter μοναδικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>unique, sole</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek μοναδικός, from μονάς.</div><b>μοναξιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural μοναξιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. loneliness (.U.K.), lonesomeness (U.S.) (feeling of depression resulting from being alone or from having no companions)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Με πεθαίνει η <b>μοναξιά</b> εδώ. - The loneliness here is killing me.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. solitude, seclusion, solitariness (condition or state of being alone or having no companions)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Μ’ αρέσει η <b>μοναξιά</b>. - I like my solitude.</div>
  <div class='def'>3. (figuratively) lonely person</div>
  <div class='ex'>Μύριες χαμένες <b>μοναξιές</b> με σένα σμίγανε,
Φεύγαν καράβια μα πριν φύγουν σου σφυρίζανε. - Myriads of lost lonely ones had romances with you,
Boats would leave but before they did they would whistle at you.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek μοναξία, from Ancient Greek μονάξ, from μόνος.</div><b>μοναρχία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural μοναρχίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>monarchy</div>
  <div class='ex'>συνταγματική <b>μοναρχία</b> - constitutional monarchy</div><b>μοναστήρι</b>
