  <div class='def'>1. one-sided, single-sided</div>
  <div class='def'>2. unilateral</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek μονόπλευρος with semantic loan from French unilatéral and English one-sided. By surface analysis, μονό- + -πλευρος (-plevros).</div><b>μονός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine μονή, neuter μονό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. single, with one part or element</div>
  <div class='def'>2. odd</div>
  <div class='ex'>μονά ή ζυγά (odds or evens)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek μόνος.</div><b>μονότονος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine μονότονη, neuter μονότονο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. monotonous, flat</div>
  <div class='def'>2. dull, boring</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> μονός + τόνος</div><b>μοριακά βάρη</b>
