  <div class='def'>supporter, follower, fan, devotee, (of political party, sports, etc)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ὀπαδός.</div><b>οπερέτα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural οπερέτες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. operetta (lighter version of opera)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Οι Γκίλμπερτ και Σάλιβαν ήταν διάσημοι για τις <b>οπερέτες</b> τους. - Gilbert and Sullivan were famous for their operettas.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (attributive, colloquial, derogatory, figuratively) joke, shambles (an event or thing lacking seriousness or only ostensibly serious)</div>
  <div class='ex'>Η Ελλάδα έχει καταντήσει πλέον κράτος <b>οπερέτα</b>. - Greece has ended up as a joke state.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Borrowed from Italian operetta.</div><b>οπερατικός</b>
