  <div class='def'>gunsmith</div><b>οπλοποιός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural οπλοποιοί, feminine οπλοποιία)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>gunsmith</div><b>οπλουργία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural οπλουργίες, masculine οπλουργός)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>armourer (UK), armorer (US)</div><b>οπλουργός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural οπλουργοί, feminine οπλουργία)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>armourer (UK), armorer (US)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ὁπλουργός, from ὅπλον + -ουργός; equivalent to όπλο + -ουργός.</div><b>οποία πέτρα κι αν σηκώσεις, τον βρίσκεις από κάτω</b>
  <div><i>proverb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Of people who are ubiquitous, who have many connections and seem to be everywhere.</div><b>οποίος</b>
  <div><i>pron, masculine (feminine οποία, neuter οποίο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. who, which, that</div>
  <div class='ex'>το βιβλίο το <b>οποίο</b> έχετε διαβάσει - the book which you have read</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (without article) what, such</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Οποία</b> έκπληξη! - What a surprise!</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ὁποῖος, morphologically ο- (o-) + ποιος (poios).</div><b>οποιοσδήποτε</b>
  <div><i>pron, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (pronoun, universal) whoever, whatever</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (pronoun, universal) whosoever, whatsoever (dated)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Koine Greek ὁποιοσδήποτε, in turn from the pronoun ὁποῖος + -δήποτε.</div><b>οποτεδήποτε</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. whenever (at whatever time)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. whenever (every time)</div><b>οπουδήποτε</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>wherever, anywhere</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek ὁπουδήποτε, itself a calque of Latin ubicumque.</div><b>οπτικά</b>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative neuter plural of <a href="bword://οπτικός">οπτικός</a></div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>optically</div><b>οπτική</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. optics</div>
  <div class='def'>2. vision, view (way of viewing or understanding something)</div>
  <br/><br/>
  <div><i>adj</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative feminine singular of <a href="bword://οπτικός">οπτικός</a></div><b>οπτικοί σαρωτές</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/vocative plural of <a href="bword://οπτικός">οπτικός</a> <a href="bword://σαρωτής">σαρωτής</a></div><b>οπτικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine οπτική, neuter οπτικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. optical</div>
  <div class='def'>2. visual</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ὀπτικός.</div>
