  <div class='def'>to pasteurise (UK), pasteurize (US)</div><b>παστινάκη</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural παστινάκες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>parsnip</div><b>παστινάκι</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural παστινάκια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://παστινάκη">παστινάκη</a></div><b>παστού βοδινού</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>genitive singular of παστό <a href="bword://βοδινό">βοδινό</a></div><b>παστό βοδινό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (uncountable) corned beef, bully beef</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (uncountable) salted beef</div><b>παστός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine παστή, neuter παστό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>salted, preserved with salt, corned</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>παστό</b> χοιρινό - salt pork</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek παστός, from πάσσω, from Proto-Indo-European *kʷeh₁t- (“to shake”).</div><b>πασχαλίτσα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural πασχαλίτσες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>ladybird, ladybug</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From πασχαλιά + -ίτσα.</div><b>πασχαλιά</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural πασχαλιές)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. lilac</div>
  <div class='def'>2. Eastertide, Eastertime (usually with initial capital letter)</div><b>πασχαλινά αβγά</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative plural of πασχαλινό <a href="bword://αβγό">αβγό</a></div><b>πασχαλινό αβγό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural πασχαλινά αβγά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>Easter egg</div><b>πασχαλινός</b>
