  <div class='def'>alternative form of <a href="bword://τακτοποιώ">τακτοποιώ</a></div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From τακτ(ός), “arranged, fixed, set”) + -ο- + -ποιώ. First part from the ancient τάξη/τάσσω and suffix from the ancient ποιέω / ποιῶ. First attested in 1855, a calque of French mettre en ordre.</div><b>ταχυαρρυθμία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) tachyarrhythmia</div><b>ταχυδακτυλουργία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ταχυδακτυλουργίες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>sleight of hand, prestidigitation</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From ταχυ- (tachy-, “fast”) + δάκτυλο + -ία, calque of French prestidigitation. First attested 1872.</div><b>ταχυδακτυλουργός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural ταχυδακτυλουργοί)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>magician, prestidigitator (performer of tricks)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From ταχυ- (tachy-, “fast”) + δάκτυλο + -ουργός, calque of French prestidigitateur. First attested 1874.</div><b>ταχυδρομείο</b>
