  <div><i>noun, neuter</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative plural of ταχυδρομικό <a href="bword://κιβώτιο">κιβώτιο</a></div><b>ταχυδρομικές θυρίδες</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/accusative/vocative plural of ταχυδρομική <a href="bword://θυρίδα">θυρίδα</a></div><b>ταχυδρομική θυρίδα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ταχυδρομικές θυρίδες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. post office box, PO box</div>
  <div class='def'>2. letterbox, mailbox</div>
  <div class='def'>3. letterbox, pillar box (UK)</div><b>ταχυδρομικοί κώδικες</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>nominative/vocative plural of <a href="bword://ταχυδρομικός">ταχυδρομικός</a> <a href="bword://κώδικας">κώδικας</a></div><b>ταχυδρομικό κιβώτιο</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ταχυδρομικά κιβώτια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(Cyprus) post office box, PO box, letterbox, mailbox, pillar box (UK)</div><b>ταχυδρομικός</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ταχυδρομική, neuter ταχυδρομικό)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>postal, post, mail</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from ταχυδρομ(είο)) + -ικός.</div><b>ταχυδρομικός κώδικας</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ταχυδρομικοί κώδικες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>postcode (UK), zip code (US)</div><b>ταχυδρομικώς</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>by mail, by post</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from ταχυδρομικ(ός)) + -ώς.</div><b>ταχυδρομώ</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>to post (a letter)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Morphologically, from ταχυδρομ(είο) n, “post office”) or older ταχυδρομ(εῖον)) + -ώ or as a learned borrowing from Koine Greek ταχυδρομῶ in the sense of modern ταχυδρόμος. The expected form of 1888 ταχυδρομίζω is obsolete.</div><b>ταχυδρόμος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine or feminine (plural ταχυδρόμοι)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. postwoman, postman, letter-carrier (UK)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. mailwoman, mailman, letter-carrier (US)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ταχυ- (tachy-, “fast”) + δρόμος.</div><b>ταχυκαρδία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) tachycardia</div><b>ταχυστέγνωτος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ταχυστέγνωτη, neuter ταχυστέγνωτο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>quick-drying</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> By surface analysis, ταχυ- (tachy-, “quick”) + στεγνώνω + -τος (-tos, adjectival suffix).</div><b>ταχυφαγείο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ταχυφαγεία)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fast food outlet</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> ταχυ- (tachy-, “fast”) + φαΐ + -είο.</div><b>ταχύρρυθμος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ταχύρρυθμη, neuter ταχύρρυθμο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>fast-paced, rapid</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly from ταχυ- (tachy-) + ρυθμ(ός)) + -ος (-os) with duplication of -ρ- as seen also in απορρυθμίζω.</div><b>ταχύς</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ταχεία, neuter ταχύ)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. fast, rapid</div>
  <div class='def'>2. sudden</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ταχύς.</div><b>ταχύτητα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural ταχύτητες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. speed, velocity</div>
  <div class='ex'>Το αυτοκίνητο έτρεχε με <b>ταχύτητα</b> 50 χιλιόμετρα την ώρα. - The car was travelling with a speed of 50 kilometres per hour.</div>
  <div class='def'>2. swiftness, alacrity</div>
  <div class='def'>3. speed, gear</div>
  <div class='ex'>Έβαλε την πρώτη <b>ταχύτητα</b> και ξεκίνησε. - He put it into first gear and set off.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ταχυτής, with stress shift. Equivalent to ταχύ- + -ύτητα.</div><b>ταψί</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural ταψιά)</i></div>
