  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ottoman Turkish تپسی (tepsi, “tray”).</div><b>ταύρος</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (plural ταύροι, feminine αγελάδα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. bull</div>
  <div class='def'>2. Taurus</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek ταῦρος, from Proto-Indo-European *táwros.</div><b>ταώς</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (archaic, obsolete, uncountable) the constellation Pavo or the peacock</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (archaic, obsolete, uncountable) peacock</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Ancient Greek ταώς.</div><b>ταὐτομετάβατος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine ταὐτομετάβατος, neuter ταὐτομετάβατον)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(archaic, obsolete, reflexive) reflexive</div>
  <div class='ex'>, Hellenistic Koine αὐτοπαθής (autopathḗs)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> A rare Katharevousa compound, constructed as an alternative for the Hellenistic grammar term αὐτοπαθής.
Compound from the ancient ταὐτός ταὐτο- + Hellenistic Koine μεταβατός, from μεταβαίνω. From μετα- (meta-, “meta-”) μετά + βατός &lt; βαίνω.</div><b>τείνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (transitive) to stretch (string, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (intransitive) to stretch, extend, hold out (hand, etc)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. to approach, tend towards</div>
  <div class='ex'>Όταν το x <b>τείνει</b> προς το 0, τότε το 1/x <b>τείνει</b> προς το άπειρο. - As x approaches 0, 1/x tends to infinity.</div>
  <div class='def'>4. (followed by να (na) ) tend to</div>
  <div class='ex'><b>Τείνω</b> να τον πιστέψω. - I tend to believe him.</div>
  <div class='def'>5. (followed by να (na) ) intend to, aim to</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learnedly, from Ancient Greek τείνω. Stems with vowel gradation τεν-, τα-, τον-</div><b>τείχος</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural τείχη)</i></div>
