  <div class='def'>2. nominative/accusative/vocative neuter singular of <a href="bword://τεθωρακισμένος">τεθωρακισμένος</a></div><b>τεθωρακισμένος</b>
  <div><i>adj, masculine (feminine τεθωρακισμένη, neuter τεθωρακισμένο)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. armoured (UK), armored (US)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (dated) ironclad</div><b>τεκίλα</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural τεκίλες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>tequila</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from English tequila, from Mexican Spanish tequila.</div><b>τεκμήριο</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural τεκμήρια)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. evidence, argument, proof (in support of an assertion)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. evidence, testimony (in court)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek τεκμήριον.</div><b>τεκμηρίωση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural τεκμηριώσεις)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. documentation, paperwork (supporting material for a taken position)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. documentation (software manual etc)</div><b>τεκμηριώνω</b>
  <div><i>verb</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. to substantiate, document</div>
  <div class='def'>2. to prove</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek τεκμηρῐόω, from τεκμήριον, from τεκμαίρομαι, from Proto-Hellenic *kʷekmə́řřomai, from *kʷékmər, from Proto-Indo-European *kʷéḱ-mr̥.</div><b>τεκνοποίηση</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine</i></div>
  <div class='def'>childbearing</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Koine Greek τεκνοποίησις with -ση (-si). By surface analysis, τέκνο + -ο- (-o-) + -ποίηση.</div><b>τεκνό</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural τεκνά)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. (colloquial) gifted or attractive boy</div>
  <div class='def'>2. (slang) gay man, homosexual</div><b>τεκνό της βιολέτας</b>
  <div><i>phrase</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(Kaliarda) gay prostitute</div><b>τεκτονική</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) tectonics</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Reborrowing from English tectonics, from Ancient Greek τεκτονικός.</div><b>τεκτονισμός</b>
  <div><i>noun, masculine (uncountable)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(uncountable) freemasonry</div><b>τελεία</b>
  <div><i>noun, feminine (plural τελείες)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>A full stop or period ⟨.⟩.</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From Ancient Greek τελεία, from τέλος + -εια (-eia, “-ness”).</div><b>τελείωμα</b>
  <div><i>noun, neuter (plural τελειώματα)</i></div>
  <div class='def'>1. finishing, ending (the act of completing something)</div>
  <div class='def'>2. finish (a protective coating given to wood or metal and other surfaces)</div>
  <div class='def'>3. finish (shot on goal, especially one that ends in a goal)</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> Learned borrowing from Ancient Greek τελείωμα.</div><b>τελείως</b>
  <div><i>adv</i></div>
  <div class='def'>(emphatic, intensifier) completely, totally</div>
  <div class='etym'><b>Etymology:</b> From τέλειος + -ως (-os).</div><b>τελειομανής</b>
